window.AKK_DIRECTED_INNER_VOICE_CHAPTERS=(window.AKK_DIRECTED_INNER_VOICE_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":501,"title":"Chapter 501: One of Our Own, Who Can Escape","paragraphs":["The moment he finished speaking, the women around him began to wail again.","\"System, did these people know we were coming? This is too much of a coincidence!\"","[Host, if I weren't absolutely certain they couldn't possibly know our schedule, I'd suspect it too!]","The system was just as dumbfounded as its host. All it could say was that this was way too coincidental!","The crowd of onlookers grew larger and larger. They stood motionless—no talking, no crying, no leaving. They just stood there, occasionally glancing up at the sky.","It was enough to make Yue Fuguang feel a little uneasy.","But the eyes of these Southern Yue commoners were empty, wooden—like dry wells, like parched riverbeds.","\"Big brother, didn't Kohana just say it? The goddess is Dà Yǎn's goddess, not our Southern Yue's goddess. Why would she come here to bring rain?\"","\"Weicheng, Fengcheng, and then later Yucheng—didn't they all get rain? Why can't we have it too?!\"","At first listen, that seemed to make sense, but a moment's thought revealed it to be completely without logic.","So Yue Fuguang was now utterly speechless. Equally speechless, aside from herself and the system and Zheng Chunying and the other two, was the young woman referred to as \"Third Sister-in-law.\"","Yue Fuguang even caught a glimpse of her rolling her eyes just a little. \"Big brother, have you forgotten whose hands Weicheng, Fengcheng, and Yucheng are in now?\"","The young man glanced around, and only when he saw no government officials did he chime in, \"Yeah, big brother, Kohana's right. Those three cities... they're under Dà Yǎn's jurisdiction now.\"","But this area here was barely any distance from the capital and still belonged to Southern Yue. How could it be compared?","There was something else very strange too: the officials who usually roamed the streets grabbing people and beating them—not a single one was to be seen today. The entire main street had only commoners, no officials at all.","By all logic, with this many people gathered, officials should have already come to disperse the crowd. The fact that there wasn't a single one was quite odd.","\"But if the goddess is an immortal, shouldn't immortals be compassionate and full of virtue? The goddess is the goddess of all the people under heaven—she shouldn't limit herself to just one city or one place!\"","Kohana frowned, instinctively feeling that her brother-in-law, who couldn't even read a handful of characters, shouldn't be able to say something that sounded so reasonable but was actually inciting.","Just as Kohana was about to say something else, an old man leaning on a cane walked over. At the sight of him, the crying gradually quieted down.","\"Get up, all of you. Go home.\" His voice was flat. He said this, then slowly turned and started back the way he came. After a few steps, he paused, looked back once, and continued on.","\"If the heavens refuse to give us a way to live... we'll find our own.\" It sounded like he was talking to himself. His voice was so soft that it scattered in the wind.","\"Father, I won't get up. I want to beg the goddess! Beg the goddess to look at us too, to save us!\"","\"A Quan, it's no use. We're still Southern Yue people. The goddess of Dà Yǎn can't see us.\"","Zhao Quan was still crouched on the ground, holding his head in both hands. \"I don't believe it. I don't believe it. Why does she send rain to them but not to us? It must be that we haven't begged hard enough!\"","\"Father, my husband is right!\" The woman who had been sobbing with her head down suddenly looked up, and Yue Fuguang finally got a clear look at her face—sallow and dry, she looked to be only around twenty years old.","She had stopped crying by now. Her voice was hoarse. \"If the goddess doesn't send rain, it must be because she's angry that our offerings have been too little.\"","She abruptly reached behind her and pulled forward a little girl of three or four. \"As long as the goddess is willing to send rain, I, this humble woman, am willing to offer our Dani to the goddess!\"","Hearing someone offer up a living human sacrifice to her—and her own biological daughter at that—Yue Fuguang, sitting in her flying carriage, felt like ten thousand horses were stampeding through her mind.","\"Little Zhu, what would I even do with her little girl? Raise her for free?\"","[Master, this family's situation is off. They're clearly targeting you.]","Heshui Town sat on the main road leading to the capital, Gancheng. It was a large town, and merchants from north and south passed through in especially great numbers.","Although less than a tenth of the usual merchants were active due to the drought, wherever these people went, news followed.","\"It should be a play staged by the Southern Yue court.\" The goal was still to dilute the narrative that \"the emperor lacks virtue, and heaven has sent disaster upon Southern Yue.\"","If they wanted to use her reputation to whitewash Gan Sheng's name, they'd better check whether she agreed!","\"Zhao's wife is righteous!\" The surrounding people, who had been numb and expressionless, suddenly came alive and began praising the woman.","That no one found anything wrong with her offering up her own daughter as a sacrifice was deeply unsettling.","\"The drought demon runs rampant, and as a deity, the goddess ought to save the world. This humble woman is merely contributing a meager effort—I don't deserve everyone's praise!\"","Only Kohana and her husband pulled the little girl aside, strongly disapproving of her actions. \"Sister-in-law, Dani is still little. How can you offer her as a sacrifice?!\"","The Southern Yue people were deeply influenced by Nanzhao, and like them, they worshiped unorthodox sacrificial practices above all. Every year, for all sorts of reasons, many boys and girls were sacrificed. Those children were sent to the altar to die while still too young to understand the world. What had those children ever done wrong?!","\"Yeah, sister-in-law, Dani is still little!\"","\"Didn't the goddess say that torrential rain would soon fall across all of Southern Yue? Then we'll have water to drink!\"","Hearing her brother-in-law's words, the woman exchanged a glance with her husband. Zhao Quan's face immediately grew even more bitter. \"A Qun, don't forget—the goddess did say there would be rain, but she also said the heavy rains would bring floods!\"","The woman nodded repeatedly as well. \"We just want to kneel and beg the goddess to send less rain upon our Southern Yue. We just want to live. What wrong have we done?!","If the goddess truly pours down heavy rain day after day, how can we possibly survive? Does the goddess really want to watch us innocent people die?\"","[Master, isn't their attempt to shift the blame a little too obvious?] Whoever was behind this, coming up with a plan to wage a war of public opinion—they were clever.","\"Obvious? But obvious is enough to steer public opinion!\" Most commoners didn't understand much reasoning. When they heard everyone around them saying the same thing, they'd start to believe it was true.","If Southern Yue really managed to divert their internal conflicts outward, their court might buy itself a little more breathing room amidst these successive natural disasters.","\"Didn't everyone say the emperor lacks virtue and heaven sends great disasters? The drought and the floods are because the emperor lacks virtue. What does that have to do with a goddess from another country?\"","\"That's right. I heard our disasters are all because the emperor lacks virtue. Nanzhao's drought is because of the drought demon, and the floods are because the imperial heirs are unfilial. Meanwhile, Dà Yǎn's goddess is kind and benevolent, giving us all an early warning!\"","\"Exactly, exactly. If we manage to survive this time, we should be sure to thank Goddess Yue properly! Once we become Dà Yǎn citizens, we'll be under the goddess's protection even more!\"","\"Little Zhu, saying something like that in front of so many people—does he not want to live?\" The Zhao family could put on this kind of performance, which meant someone nearby had to be watching to review the results!","These people were speaking up for her and criticizing the emperor's lack of virtue—they'd definitely suffer for it.","[Master, don't worry. These people are all spies bribed by Dà Yǎn. They're our own. They can get away.]","[Performances like the Zhao family's aren't the first. The Dà Yǎn agents stationed here have long since worked out ways to handle it.]"]},{"number":502,"title":"Chapter 502: Entering the Hall","paragraphs":["Zhao Qun disagreed with his brother and sister-in-law, instead finding the villagers' words more sensible. \"Brother, sister-in-law, this is no time for arguing. Let's head home quickly, pack up, and get to the mountains!\"","Zhao Quan shook his head. \"Go to the mountains? I'm not going. Up there there's no food or water, not even a place to shelter from the wind and rain. I'm not putting myself through that misery!\"","His wife chimed in, \"The head of the household is right. Going up there is too miserable. Our family isn't leaving, and neither should you. Staying home is far more comfortable.\"","Hearing this from the older brother and his wife, Kohana was so angry she laughed, no longer caring about saving face for them. \"You know full well why there's no shelter, brother and sister-in-law! Qun-ge found a cave we could hide in, but sister-in-law gave it to her own family! If we'd gone up two days earlier, we could have built a simple shack, but no—you kept stopping the whole family from going to the mountains. Are you trying to get everyone killed?\"","At Kohana's words, the woman's face darkened. \"Sister-in-law, are you blaming us? Everyone says that story about the goddess isn't to be trusted. Look at the blazing sun in the sky—does it look like rain is coming?\"","Hearing the argument below, Yue Fuguang shook her head and flew the vehicle further away, hoping only that the younger couple would stay firm in their resolve and make it up the mountain soon.","The flying vehicle traveled through the air for another half hour. Yue Fuguang, who had been resting with her eyes closed, heard the system's excited cry: [Master, look, we're here!]","Yue Fuguang opened her eyes while reaching up to rub her ear. \"Little Zhu, we're here, that's all—why must you be so worked up?\" So undignified, she thought. Where was the ethereal aura befitting a divine artifact?","[Master, we arrived just in time—caught Prince Cheng making his move! How could Little Zhu not be excited? In all my thousands of years, I've never witnessed a palace coup!]","The system spoke with such genuine emotion about living thousands of years that if Yue Fuguang hadn't been so focused on looking down, she might have noticed something off. As it was, she assumed it was just putting on another show.","Below them lay the capital of Southern Yue—Gan City. The city was eerily quiet; even though it was broad daylight, all the citizens had their doors and windows shut, not a single person on the streets.","Yet through the alleys and streets, fully armored soldiers of the Southern Yue army marched in patrol, weapons in hand.","Especially on Xihua Street, where the wealthy and powerful resided, there were thousands of soldiers keeping close watch on every official residence.","It was the afternoon, and Yue Fuguang guessed that the Southern Yue officials were all trapped in their government offices. The people in their homes served as leverage and hostages.","\"So all these officials were just doing their jobs when—boom—their boss suddenly changes. What a tragicomedy of human life.\"","[Master, it's not over yet. Whether the boss changes, and to whom, is still up in the air!]","\"What do you mean? The whole capital is in Prince Cheng's hands and he still can't take the throne? Is he really that useless?\"","[Isn't it obvious? Several of his men have already been bought off, and the fool doesn't even know it!]","Yue Fuguang's eyes lit up. \"Little Zhu, Prince Cheng must take the throne—I've decided, and no one's changing that!\"","Useless was good. A useless ruler would help Dayan take Southern Yue faster. If they got another cunning emperor like Gan Sheng on the throne, it'd be a headache for Dayan, and she might have to intervene with targeted strikes herself.","Those who sat on the throne all carried a bit of destiny with them. The less she had to act directly, the better.","[Understood. Rest assured, Master—today, no matter who dies, Prince Cheng will come out fine!]","Feng Tang silently gave the two bosses a thumbs-up. He too thought that the somewhat dimwitted Prince Cheng ascending the throne best served Dayan's interests.","\"So this is Southern Yue's imperial palace? It looks quite similar to Dayan's.\" It had its own style, but the foundations were clearly the same.","[It's all from one nation split apart. Even after two or three hundred years, the heritage left by their ancestors isn't so easily changed.]","The palace was even more heavily garrisoned—squads of armored soldiers patrolled between the halls, and like the common homes outside, every palace gate was shut tight, not a single eunuch or maid in sight.","\"Little Zhu, where are the emperor and Prince Cheng now?\"","[Master, look at the grand hall right below us—that's Yuchen Hall, where Emperor Gan Sheng is resting.] As the system's words faded, the flying vehicle also turned invisible and landed at the entrance of Yuchen Hall.","Hearing faint voices from inside, Yue Fuguang made a silencing gesture to Shen Chunying and the other two.","Then she pressed an invisibility talisman onto each of them and casually stepped off the flying vehicle.","Shen Chunying and the others tried to stop her but it was too late; they hurried to follow, flanking Yue Fuguang on either side to keep her in the middle, while Feng Tang lingered three steps behind in a defensive stance.","\"We pay our respects to Your Majesty!\" The words were spoken, but there was no kneeling—not even a slight bow.","It was at this moment that Yue Fuguang, through the wooden lattice window, saw a stalwart man in full armor walking step by step toward the dragon bed.","Compared to the gaunt emperor on the bed, Prince Cheng was in the prime of his life, just past forty. His face was square and broad, his short beard neatly trimmed, and his narrow eyes held a sharp glint. The corners of his mouth turned downward in a naturally stern expression.","He came to a stop in the center of the hall, and four armored guards filed in behind him, positioned on both sides, hands resting on their sword hilts, eyes sharp as eagles. The eunuchs, palace maids, concubines, and physicians in the hall had all long turned pale with terror, huddled into corners, scarcely daring to breathe.","As for the officials present—they all bowed their heads, trying to make themselves invisible.","In their view, this was the royal family's private affair. As outside ministers, it was not their place to intervene.","Yue Fuguang: Just say you're afraid of dying! Who was it that said there are no private matters for the royal family?!","Prince Cheng's gaze swept over everyone in the hall. He was satisfied with the responses.","A faint smile tugged at his lips. His eyes finally came to rest on the dragon bed. He slightly raised his clasped hands in a perfunctory gesture and spoke in a flat tone, \"Nephew, long time no see. Your uncle was worried about you. How's your health? You look worse than when I left?\"","His words were concerned, but the smile at the corners of his mouth could not be contained.","On the dragon bed, Emperor Gan Sheng lay weakly within the bright yellow brocade blankets, his face as pale as the potted ice plant in the corner of the hall.","His cheekbones jutted out sharply, his eyes sunken into dark sockets. Only when his eyes moved did one realize that his wasted body still held a flicker of life.","He was all of twenty-eight years old, yet he looked like a man at death's door.","At this moment, he was too weak even to sit up, forced to watch helplessly as Prince Cheng barged into his bedchamber and hurled insults at him.","Gan Sheng felt an emperor being mocked by a subject—an overwhelming wave of fury and humiliation enveloped him, further weakening his already failing body.","Brought up under the loving favor of the late emperor, Gan Sheng had never known such humiliation. But reality was what it was. As much as he raged, all he could do was glare with venomous eyes at the Prince Cheng who approached step by step."]},{"number":503,"title":"Chapter 503: The day is about to change, and the master is about to be replaced.","paragraphs":["Gazing at the imperial uncle before him, Gan Sheng’s throat bobbed a few times before he managed to squeeze out a single sentence, “Imperial Uncle... to enter the palace with armed guards without being summoned, for what purpose?” As for the grave crime of abandoning his post and entering the capital without orders, in the struggles of the past two days, despite holding the moral high ground as emperor, he had not gained the slightest advantage.","Gan Sheng cast a wary glance at the man behind Prince Cheng, then quickly averted his eyes.","Prince Cheng stood with his hands clasped behind his back. Because of his armor, his stance was especially straight, like a blade drawn from its sheath.","He did not answer immediately, but tilted his head slightly to glance at the empress beside the couch.","The empress met his gaze, calmly setting down the medicine bowl, rising, and folding her hands in a proper bow, her posture impeccable and beyond reproach. “Your nephew’s wife pays respects to the Imperial Uncle!”","Prince Cheng nodded, then met the murderous look from the frail, ailing emperor, and did not mince words. He said bluntly, “My dear nephew, you can see from this outfit of your uncle’s what I’m here for! It’s not that your uncle is forcing your hand, it’s that your own body simply won’t cooperate! Don’t blame your uncle for being heartless. For the sake of our Gan family’s empire, I’m afraid I have to put you through some hardship!”","He swept his gaze over the others in the bedchamber. “You wouldn’t want the empire our Gan ancestors fought so hard to build to one day fall into the hands of outsiders, would you?”","Prince Cheng sat down on the low stool beside the bed. Aside from their childhood encounters, this was the closest the uncle and nephew had been in over a decade.","Gan Sheng closed his eyes. He truly did not want to see Prince Cheng’s face right now, that look of a victor already assured of triumph, gazing with pity upon him lying in bed, unable even to move as he pleased—the countenance of the strong looking down on the weak.","He had long heard the rumors circulating in the capital about himself and had prepared countermeasures. But even shifting the blame onto Yue Fuguang could not save his throne or his life!","Because the emperor’s health was poor, only two basins of ice had been placed in the vast Yuchen Hall. It should have been somewhat warm, but with Prince Cheng’s arrival, everyone present could not help but shiver.","By the bedside, the empress had already picked up the medicine bowl again and stood at the foot of the dragon couch. The medicinal liquid, once scalding hot, had cooled somewhat due to Prince Cheng’s sudden intrusion—just the right temperature for drinking. Her gaze fell upon the dark brown liquid, her nostrils filled with the nauseating bitter smell of medicine, her expression as indifferent as if she were watching a grand play that had nothing to do with her.","Standing outside the hall, watching the drama unfold, Yue Fuguang took in everyone’s expressions. Only the empress’s expression puzzled her.","The empress had no son. The current crown prince was the eldest son born to the emperor and his favored concubine. From this, it was clear that the relationship between emperor and empress was not as harmonious as rumor suggested. But then again, Gan Sheng was exactly the type to put on a good show on the surface.","Yet the fleeting flash of hatred in the empress’s eyes made her think the discord between emperor and empress was not simply because of a favored concubine wedged between them.","There was hatred in those eyes, yet it was hidden. Surely there was something deeper going on!","Just as Prince Cheng was pressing Gan Sheng harder and harder, a sound of urgent footsteps suddenly came from behind Yue Fuguang and her companions—not the quick, shuffling steps of eunuchs, but the clashing of armor, the heavy thud of leather boots stomping on white marble bricks. Dull, orderly, carrying a chilling killing intent.","It was the patrol squad under Prince Cheng’s command. They deliberately kept their distance from Yuchen Hall, which gave certain people an opportunity.","Yue Fuguang watched as a short, small eunuch quietly opened a door and squeezed through it in a flash.","“Hurry, let’s follow and get front-row seats to the drama!”","The people inside the great hall also heard those footsteps heavy with murderous intent. The empress’s hand holding the medicine bowl paused slightly, then returned to normal—she did not even twitch an eyebrow.","The stagnant atmosphere of the hall was broken by the arrival of a single person. The foster son of Zhao Quan’an, the emperor’s chief eunuch—Little Anzi—scrambled and crawled his way into the inner chamber.","Before he could even see the situation inside, he threw himself to his knees with a thud, his voice shaking uncontrollably. “Your... Your Majesty, the palace gate... the palace gate has already... been surrounded by Prince Cheng’s troops! This servant cannot get out!”","Before he could finish, Zhao Quan’an’s scolding voice rang out from inside the hall, “Little Anzi, this is none of your business. Go wait outside!”","“Yes!” Little Anzi did not dare lift his head, and quickly obeyed, hurrying out. But Yue Fuguang and her group of four, who had followed in behind Little Anzi’s footsteps, remained inside, finding a prime spot from which to enjoy the drama, and stood there awaiting the developments to come.","Watching the hall doors close again, Prince Cheng let out a derisive snort. “My dear nephew, your uncle already told you—the entire palace is in my hands. Why bother struggling further? Wouldn’t it be better to just listen to your uncle obediently?” His voice was booming, full of vigor, piercing through layers of curtains and reaching every corner of the inner hall—a stark contrast to the ailing Gan Sheng, who could barely even speak properly.","“You...” Gan Sheng’s voice was as hoarse as rough stone scraped by sandpaper. “How many men have you... brought into the palace? How is... how is my mother the Empress Dowager?”","Prince Cheng laughed heartily at the question. “My dear nephew, your uncle sees no harm in telling you. This time I entered the palace with three thousand elite armored soldiers under my command, with another five thousand outside the imperial city. Just outside this very hall, there are three hundred warriors.”","At a single command from him, they could rush in at any moment and take the emperor’s life.","Prince Cheng patted the edge of the bed triumphantly, the phoenix-tail patterned nanmu dragon couch letting out muffled thumping sounds. “Let me give you another piece of news. My fifty thousand troops have all entered the city through Desheng Gate today.”","Desheng Gate—he had specifically chosen this gate of entry to secure a favorable omen, for the name meant “victory.”","“Wei Guang, he...!”","“Don’t blame Minister Wei. He did his best!” Best at putting on a show, without letting anyone see that he had long since become Prince Cheng’s man.","“Not blame him? Not blame him for defecting to the Imperial Uncle?” Gan Sheng, thinking that Wei Guang had likely opened the city gates without any resistance to let Prince Cheng’s army in, felt as if a heavy hammer had struck his chest.","At this moment, because his chest was filled with immense hatred, Gan Sheng suddenly felt a surge of strength in his body. He let out a roar. “Treacherous ministers have ruined me!”","He slowly struggled to sit up, and Zhao Quan’an quickly fetched several soft pillows to prop behind his back.","“Master, what did you do to Gan Sheng?”","“Give him a little strength. A quarrel is only interesting when both sides are evenly matched. A one-sided crushing is no fun to watch at all.”","How else could they lure out the others? Without chaos, how could they deplete their strength? Plant seeds of suspicion in everyone’s hearts, make them doubt one another, and they could never band together on the same ship.","Seeing the emperor’s sudden improvement, everyone in the hall felt a stir of hope—except Prince Cheng and a few others.","Gan Sheng reclined against the soft pillows and rested for a moment, a bitter curve tugging at the corner of his mouth.","Wei Guang had let Prince Cheng’s army into the city. The imperial guards must not have offered much resistance either, otherwise he would have received some warning before Prince Cheng entered the hall.","Where had Dai Ping’an gone? The commander of the imperial guards, Fang Huaying, was recommended by Dai Ping’an. That man had either already been bought off, or had hidden away out of fear of Prince Cheng’s power, or had concluded that the times were changing and it was time to switch masters."]},{"number":504,"title":"Chapter 504: Forcing the Palace","paragraphs":["Just then, Little Anzi's report suddenly came from outside the door, \"Your Majesty! The Crown Prince requests an audience!\" Through the palace door, Gan Sheng was first taken aback, a flicker of complex emotion quickly passing through his eyes, while Consort Shu, standing in the corner playing the part of a wooden post, gave a slight shudder.","The hand holding the brocade handkerchief instantly clenched tight. Shouldn't her royal son be hiding himself away at this moment? What was he doing here!","Consort Shu inwardly blamed the Crown Prince, then cursed everyone around him as well, but most of all she regretted having played the virtuous woman—pushing the Empress aside to come tend to the Emperor herself.","\"Absolutely not!\" Before she could say more, Prince Cheng laughed and said, \"Nephew's wife, what words are these? The Crown Prince has arrived at an opportune moment—it just so happens I haven't seen my grand-nephew in a long while. Today is a fine day to meet him!\"","\"Let him enter.\" Gan Sheng let out a long sigh inwardly, his hand beneath the brocade quilt gripping the hem of his robes tightly. The first child he had with his beloved—was even this one to be lost?","Zhao Quan'an kowtowed, rose, and backed out of the inner hall. Before long, the sound of armor clinking came from beyond the hall, heavy footsteps growing nearer. The curtains were swept open by eunuchs on either side, and a hot wind rushed in, carrying a mixture of iron rust and blood, scattering the medicinal fragrance throughout the hall.","Crown Prince Gan Minghao stepped into the hall, accompanied by a tall, burly young officer—one of Prince Cheng's trusted men.","He strode in behind the Crown Prince, his gleaming armor reflecting a faint cold light in the dim hall. His cloak, originally dark in color, was now stained with patches of darker blotches, and the smell of rust came from there.","The sword at his waist had not been removed, its scabbard striking against his outer thigh with each step, making a dull, heavy sound.","\"Your subordinate Qian Tu pays respects to His Highness!\" Qian Tu did not even glance at the Emperor lying on the dragon bed, only offering his salute to Prince Cheng.","His voice was neither servile nor rushed, yet carried the fierce vigor befitting a warrior commander, and his respect toward Prince Cheng was extraordinary.","Gan Sheng on the dragon bed narrowed his eyes at him, and when his gaze fell upon an unremarkable ornament hanging at the man's waist, a sharp light suddenly burst forth from those sickly, clouded eyes—like the last moment of clarity in a dying man before his final breath.","His palms were sweaty, his heart felt like it might leap into his throat, but he bit his lip hard and put on an angry expression.","Prince Cheng, however, did not look at him. Instead, he turned a benevolent smile upon the Crown Prince. \"Grand-nephew, do you still remember me?\"","The Crown Prince, who appeared to be around ten years old, instinctively flinched at Prince Cheng's smile. He looked up at his father's pale face, then at his mother standing in the corner, before stepping forward respectfully to bow. \"Minghao greets Sixteenth Grand-uncle!\"","Prince Cheng nodded with a satisfied smile. \"Good lad!\"","He then turned to Gan Sheng and said, \"Grand-nephew, what do you say to me sending Minghao to Lingbao Mountain?\"","\"No!\" Before Gan Sheng could respond, Consort Shu's shrill voice cut through in refusal.","Prince Cheng's expression showed clear displeasure at her words. Frowning at the Empress, he said, \"Empress, you are the nation's Empress, the master of this palace. You allow a concubine to behave with such impropriety before an elder—how are you managing the harem as Empress?\"","The Empress did not even glance at Consort Shu, only replying calmly to Prince Cheng, \"It is this niece's failure in discipline. Please forgive us, Uncle.\"","Her expression was serene, showing neither alarm nor anger, and even carrying a faint trace of... detachment.","Prince Cheng gave a slight nod, his gaze lingering on her face for a moment before turning back to Gan Sheng on the dragon bed. \"Grand-nephew, it is not your uncle's place to scold you, but no matter how much you dote on a palace concubine, she is still a concubine. Even if she has borne you an heir and that child has been named Crown Prince, she cannot be set above the legitimate wife.\"","The corner of his mouth curled upward, revealing a mocking smile. \"Don't follow in Father's footsteps.\"","That remark—\"Don't follow in Father's footsteps\"—was a blatant slap in the face to Gan Sheng's line. After all, Gan Sheng himself had risen to power when his legitimate elder brother and mother had died, relying on his own father's favor. And Consort Shu was now walking the very path the late Empress Dowager had once taken.","The only difference was that the former Empress had had the Crown Prince at her side and her maternal family's backing, while Empress Dowager Jiang Wan, during her lifetime, had only been the first among the Four Concubines, never even attaining the rank of Guifei.","Gan Sheng's pale face flushed a livid purple. Clenching his teeth, he looked at Prince Cheng and said, \"What Uncle says is right!\"","He then weakly waved a hand toward Consort Shu, who was still wiping tears but inwardly seething with hatred for Prince Cheng. \"Shu'er, withdraw for now.\"","\"Your Majesty!\" Consort Shu was deeply unwilling. It could only be said that even at this moment, she had yet to see reality clearly.","Gan Sheng's face turned cold. \"Withdraw!\"","Yue Fuguang had been watching the imperial family drama throughout, and seeing the Empress's reaction only confirmed that there was more to this story.","[Host!] The system's electronic voice almost cracked.","[I think I've found a clue about the Pen Mountain lair!]","\"Really? Where? Can we raid it?\" Yue Fuguang asked excitedly in rapid succession.","Among all her missions, everything had gone smoothly except for eliminating Pen Mountain. Only Pen Mountain, which truly lived up to its name—had been as hard as rock to uproot.","[I don't know the exact location yet, but if we can capture the key leader, we should be close to finding out where their lair is!]","\"A key leader—who is it?\" Yue Fuguang's gaze swept one by one across everyone in the bedchamber.","From the Emperor, Prince Cheng, the several adults, the Empress and Consort Shu, to the eunuchs and palace maids—and even the ten-year-old Crown Prince—she even harbored a small suspicion of him.","While Yue Fuguang was searching for someone here, Prince Cheng was not idle either. Clearly feeling that the preliminaries had gone on long enough, his words were now beginning to show his true hand.","\"The Emperor has been gravely ill for a long time, the court has fallen into neglect, and the realm is unsettled. This Prince has come for the sake of the dynasty, for the ancestral foundation.\"","He paused, his voice deepening. \"Originally, with Your Majesty in the prime of life, you could still bear the weight of our Gan family's heritage. But now...\" He looked at Gan Sheng's face, which clearly showed signs of impending death. \"If one day... Your Majesty ascends to heaven, tell me—how can a young Crown Prince truly inherit the throne and secure the realm?\"","The words were so blunt as to be almost cruel.","The air in the hall seemed to freeze. Although Gan Sheng had designated an heir, he had six sons and four daughters in total, and the eldest, the son of Consort Shu who had been named Crown Prince, Gan Minghao, was only ten years old this year.","As for Prince Cheng—he was the late Emperor's younger brother. Though not born of the Empress, as a princely member of the imperial clan, he held command of a hundred and fifty thousand troops on the northern front, eighty thousand of whom were his personal loyalists, with additional support from certain quarters in the court...","A morbid flush spread across Gan Sheng's pale face. He gasped for breath, and his voice, though weak, still carried the final dignity of a Son of Heaven. \"I... have my own plans! Why is Uncle so impatient?\"","\"Impatient?\" Prince Cheng suddenly laughed, the sound echoing through the vast hall with a trace of derision. \"Your Majesty, I have garrisoned the northern front for five years, clashed with the Dayan forces numerous times, and have walked through the gates of death more than once.","And in the court? Treacherous ministers hold sway, and eunuchs meddle in affairs.\" At this point, he deliberately swept a pointed glance at Zhao Quan'an. \"Your Majesty presently lies ill, having not held court for over a month.\""]},{"number":505,"title":"Chapter 505: I Want the Imperial Jade Seal in Your Majesty's Hands","paragraphs":["He stepped forward, the clatter of his armor ringing out. \"Your Majesty, Dayan is already at our doorstep. Nanyue has lost four cities in a row, and floods are imminent. I am not impatient, but the people of this realm cannot afford to wait!\"","\"Does Uncle also believe Yue Fuguang's nonsense?\" Gan Sheng looked at Prince Cheng in disbelief, suspecting that he too had become a follower of that person.","Prince Cheng let out a scoff. \"Nonsense? Who told Your Majesty it was nonsense?\" He pointed at Zhao Quan'an. \"Your Majesty should listen to people outside your inner circle, not just those beside you. Sometimes, those voices are the true ones, the honest ones!\"","He sat down with an air of authority, pouring himself a cup of water. \"Even if Your Majesty is bedridden with illness, surely you have sent spies into Dayan's territory to see for yourself? Yue Fuguang does indeed have the power to control rain, and truly performs divine deeds in a mortal body!\"","\"Your Majesty, if you cannot even see this, or simply refuse to acknowledge it, then does the rain in heaven only favor Dayan's lands?\"","He drained the cup in one gulp, as if a thought had just struck him. \"Ah, I nearly forgot—how did the war between our Nanyue and Dayan even begin? If Your Majesty did not believe in the Divine Maiden's abilities, why would you have gone against the will of heaven to forcibly summon her? Your Majesty believes more than anyone. Why deceive yourself here?\"","At Prince Cheng's mockery, Gan Sheng's pale face flushed red. \"Your Majesty cares only for his own reputation, not the lives of his people. That is not the way of a wise sovereign.\"","\"Your Majesty, rest assured. Even if I take the throne, I will take good care of the people of Nanyue and... of your wife and children!\"","(System, is it the kind of 'taking care' I think it is?)","[Host, no need to doubt—it is exactly that kind of taking care! Also, this Prince Cheng’s estate has one principal consort, two secondary consorts, plus over twenty concubines and nameless bed servants. His harem rivals the emperor’s.]","\"So many wives—how does he manage? Isn't he afraid of dying in bed?\" He had sounded almost respectable when dressing down Gan Sheng, but at the end, he had turned beastly again!","[Host, you actually hit the mark. Originally, Prince Cheng's fate was to die in the bed of a favored concubine.]","\"Is there something suspicious about that?\"","[Naturally, Gan Sheng orchestrated it. He wanted to seize military power from Prince Cheng, who refused, so he had him killed.]","\"Isn't this karmic retribution? Now it's Prince Cheng's turn to watch Gan Sheng die.\"","Creak—the hall doors were suddenly pushed open with force from outside. Several ministers were \"invited\" in by Prince Cheng's men. Their faces were pale, and their legs trembled as they walked.","(Judging by their official robes, these are the true heavyweights of Nanyue, aren't they?) She had thought the ones already in the hall were weaklings—none of them had dared to let out a single fart after Prince Cheng entered.","At the front were Prime Minister Li Jie, Minister of Works Zhou Wenbi, Minister of Personnel Liu Yu, Minister of Rites Wei Zhao, Minister of Revenue Fei Yongxing, and several other senior officials who had been attending to the emperor in his illness.","They had already known something was gravely wrong when the armored guards \"invited\" them here. Now, with grim faces, they stood in the hall, neither advancing nor retreating, like startled birds.","[Master, they don't look much better than the ones already in here.]","Minister of Works Zhou Wenbi, well past sixty and a veteran of three reigns, stepped forward unsteadily, clasping his hands in salute. \"Prince Cheng, entering the palace with armed men without summons violates ancestral law. His Majesty is unwell. If there is urgent business, perhaps we should discuss it at court tomorrow...\"","\"Lord Zhou.\" Prince Cheng did not so much as glance at him, cutting him off flatly. \"I do not like being interrupted while I am speaking.\"","Before the words had even faded, one of the armored guards at Prince Cheng's side drew his blade half an inch. The flash of steel was biting cold.","Zhou Wenbi's face changed instantly. His lips trembled a few times, but in the end, he fell silent and shrank back into the ranks of officials.","Gan Sheng took all of this in, his chest heaving violently. He suddenly found it ironic—these ministers who daily shouted \"Long live the Emperor\" could not even finish a single sentence now.","The so-called might of the Son of Heaven was nothing more than a sheet of thin paper, torn at the slightest poke.","\"What does Uncle want? Say it plainly.\" Gan Sheng's voice suddenly grew calm, as if he had resigned himself to fate.","Prince Cheng gave him a long, hard look, then unbuckled the sword at his waist. He planted it on the ground still in its sheath, producing a dull thud.","He swept his gaze across the room—over the trembling imperial concubines, the ashen-faced ministers, the unmoved empress—and finally rested his eyes on the emperor upon the dragon bed.","\"What I ask for,\" he said, each word deliberate, \"is the Imperial Jade Seal in Your Majesty's hand.\"","The entire hall was struck dumb. Though Prince Cheng had hinted at it and then said it outright upon entering, the words still made Gan Sheng's body tremble when he actually heard them.","Everyone had guessed the answer, but when those four words were spoken so bluntly, they still landed like a thunderclap over every head.","Fei Yongxing dropped to his knees with a thud, crying shrilly, \"Your Highness! His Majesty still lives! What is the meaning of this? This is high treason!\"","Prince Cheng finally turned to look at him, his gaze as flat as if he were regarding an ant. \"Lord Fei Yongxing, when I was defending the northern border, did you ever send me a single grain of rations? Nanyue has lost four cities in a row, and Dayan is already at our doorstep. With an emperor like this, how can he govern the realm or repel the enemy?\" Fei Yongxing was struck speechless, kneeling and shaking all over.","\"And now you speak to me of rebellion?\" Prince Cheng laughed coldly. \"I am of the imperial clan; the blood of the late emperor runs in my veins. The name of this dynasty will not change. Unlike you lot, I want this dynasty to stand for a thousand, ten thousand years!\"","[Master, has he forgotten that two of the four cities Dayan took were lost on his watch?]","(Good thing he's forgotten. Once he takes the throne, it won't be cities he gives away—it'll be the entire kingdom!)","Shen Chunying, still hidden and having retreated further into a corner after the ministers arrived, heard the two ancestors' banter and could not help but curl her lips into a faint smile.","They were all pleased here, but across the room, Gan Sheng lying on the bed felt as though a invisible hand were gripping the broken heart in his chest—aching, suffocating.","He forced the words out with difficulty. \"The jade seal... is in my hands... If I refuse to pass it on, even if Uncle takes it, it would be... an act of usurpation, would it not?\"","Prince Cheng sneered, taking up the thread without missing a beat. Unhurriedly, he produced a roll of bright yellow silk from his sleeve, unfolded it, and laid it before Gan Sheng. \"Your Majesty, the abdication edict has already been drafted. It only awaits the jade seal.\"","Gan Sheng looked down. The calligraphy on the silk was bold and forceful—unmistakably Prince Cheng's own hand. The gist was this: the emperor was gravely ill and unable to govern, no crown prince had been established, and the young princes were too immature to bear the burden—therefore, following precedent of abdication by virtuous rulers of old, the throne was to pass to his uncle, Prince Cheng...","\"No crown prince established? My crown prince...\" Gan Sheng caught the phrase, his pupils constricting. \"I have already named my eldest son as Crown Prince!\"","Prince Cheng smiled, and in the flickering candlelight, that smile was laden with meaning. \"Your Majesty will not have one soon. The eldest son born of Consort Shu is too young and unfit for the position. As of today, his title as Crown Prince is revoked.\"","\"How dare you!\"","\"Your Highness, you cannot!\""]},{"number":506,"title":"Chapter 506: The Queen","paragraphs":["Pfft! Gan Sheng was so enraged that a mouthful of blood sprayed out, staining the brocade quilt crimson, especially the golden dragon embroidered with gold thread on the quilt, now marked with splotches of blood all over its body.","Prince Cheng merely glanced sideways at him, and the look in his eyes was unmistakable—'Do you dare test me?'","Seeing that Gan Sheng hadn't been infuriated to death outright, he made no effort to hide his disappointment.","He continued, \"Furthermore, I hereby bestow upon him the title of Marquis of Anguo, with a fief of a thousand households, hereditary in perpetuity. As for Your Majesty...\" He paused. \"Your Majesty may move to Yong'an Palace to spend your remaining years in comfort, with all provisions maintained as before.\"","Spending his remaining years in comfort? Anyone with eyes could see that even if Prince Cheng didn't lift a finger, the Emperor didn't have many days left.","But the unspoken threat in Prince Cheng's words was also clear: write the abdication edict obediently, and your son will live a life of wealth and honor.","If you refuse... Gan Sheng clutched the bedding beneath him, his knuckles turning white from the force.","He suddenly thought of the late Crown Prince, his elder brother, and thought that if his only son had grown up safely, he would be thirteen years old by now.","Unfortunately, the Late Empress had not been able to protect her grandson, nor had she been able to protect her own life.","He abruptly lifted his head to look at the Empress seated at the foot of the bed. This woman had not spoken a single word from beginning to end, nor had her expression changed even once. She just sat there quietly, as if everything happening in this hall had nothing to do with her.","She should have been one of the most alarmed people. If the Son of Heaven were deposed, her position as Empress would vanish into thin air as well.","But she didn't care.","Gan Sheng thought of when she had changed, and his heart sank. It seemed he suddenly understood the reason—she must hate him!","He and the Empress had never shared much affection. Their marriage was a political alliance; the Empress's father was the patriarch of the Chen clan, a great family in the south, and she had been made Empress solely to win over the southern gentry.","And Gan Sheng, like his own father, truly doted not on his Empress but on others. The late Emperor had favored his mother, Consort Jiang, while he himself favored Consort Shu the most.","Chen Yuli, who had not known what palace life would be like before entering it, had tried to win the Emperor's heart after she did. In her twelve years within the palace, her relationship with Gan Sheng had gone from mutual respect to mutual indifference—and it wasn't just because of Consort Shu and the other concubines.","Chen Yuli had performed her duties as Empress flawlessly.","Unfortunately, she and Consort Shu had been pregnant at the same time. Consort Shu gave birth to the eldest prince safely and was promoted to Noble Consort, while the Empress miscarried at five months—and it had been a prince.","Two years later, the Empress became pregnant again and gave birth to a son, but the child was frail and sickly, it was said that he had been poisoned while still in the womb.","The Fourth Prince died before reaching his first birthday.","The Empress lost two of her own flesh and blood in succession, yet Gan Sheng only punished a few palace maids and called it done.","The Empress had once treated Gan Sheng sincerely, but she was clever and had long seen that she shared the same fate as the Late Empress. After that, she merely played the part of a bodhisattva, letting the others scheme as they pleased.","Now, looking at the bodhisattva-like Empress, Gan Sheng felt uneasy. He suspected that she might have learned the truth about the loss of her two sons!","\"Empress,\" Gan Sheng suddenly spoke, his voice so hoarse it was barely audible. \"Do you... have nothing to say?\"","The gazes of everyone in the hall turned to the Empress.","The Empress slowly raised her eyes, glanced at Gan Sheng, then at Prince Cheng. A faint smile curved at the corners of her lips, carrying a meaning that was hard to decipher.","She stood up, smoothed her sleeves, and spoke unhurriedly, \"This concubine is but a woman; matters of state are not for me to meddle in.\"","After a pause, she added another sentence, her voice as soft as if she were mentioning something utterly trivial. \"It's just that... Yong'an Palace is stifling and airless in the summer. His Majesty dislikes the heat. I would ask the Imperial Uncle to add more ice braziers.\" The moment these words were spoken, everyone in the hall was stunned.","No plea for mercy. No angry rebuke. No tearful complaint. Just a request for more ice braziers.","Gan Sheng stared at her blankly, then suddenly laughed. \"Empress, Minghao and the others are also your children. You...\"","Empress Xu suddenly smiled—a beautiful smile, yet tinged with bitterness, and a thick, unshakeable sorrow spread through her eyes. \"Has Your Majesty forgotten? This concubine lost one son ten years ago, and another eight years ago!\"","Her gaze swept over Gan Sheng's detestable face before landing on Consort Shu, who was as radiant as a flower but now pale as paper. \"You may all have forgotten, but this concubine has not!\"","\"My sons are gone. What do the children of others have to do with me?\"","If killing members of the royal family wouldn't have brought disaster upon her mother's clan, she would have taken action a month ago to send this pair of faithless man and wicked woman down to meet her two wrongfully killed children!","Even if Prince Cheng took the throne, what of it? In this game of chess, she had already prepared an escape route for herself.","The Chen clan's power lay in the south, and no matter who became Emperor, they would need the Chen family's support. Perhaps that was also the reason her two sons hadn't survived.","On the surface, it seemed Consort Shu had done the deed, but behind it all, there must have been the Emperor's tacit approval, even his support. The fact that she had managed to erase all traces, leaving her unable to find evidence for so many years despite her investigations, made that clear.","If Gan Sheng hadn't fallen so ill that he couldn't get out of bed, she truly might never have uncovered the truth. So she hated Consort Shu, who had done the deed, but she hated Gan Sheng even more—the one who had tacitly approved, even encouraged it. He was her true debtor!","\"Like they say, even a fierce tiger won't eat its own cubs. But an emperor is different!\" Having watched plenty of dramas and movies, Yue Fuguang saw the situation even more clearly than Chen Yuli herself.","[So that's why emperors call themselves 'the lonely one.' No matter how much they scheme and calculate, life is but a few short decades.]","They weren't truly immortals, but in terms of lifespan, they also enjoyed a kind of extended existence. Each mission world was a performance with no rehearsals and no retakes. Though they lived what seemed to be another's life, they were truly alive.","As long as one was alive, there were infinite possibilities.","That was what the system thought, and it was what Gan Sheng thought too. He knew he didn't have long to live, but his children still had a chance, so they had to live well.","Prince Cheng naturally noticed the rift between the Emperor and Empress. He glanced at Empress Chen, a glimmer of satisfaction passing through his eyes, appreciating her intelligence and her sense of timing.","Prince Cheng nodded slightly. \"Rest assured, Empress. Yong'an Palace's ice and charcoal will not run out as long as my dear nephew is still there.\" Of course, whether he would live long enough to use the charcoal was another question.","The Empress performed a graceful bow, then sat back down. Picking up the bowl of herbal medicine that had long gone cold, she resumed swirling it slowly with a silver spoon, as if everything happening in this hall truly had nothing to do with her.","Just then, from outside the hall came an old but authoritative shout of fury, \"Prince Cheng! How dare you!\"","The curtains were thrown open violently, and Empress Dowager Jiang, supported by an elderly palace maid, strode quickly into the hall, followed by guards who had tried but failed to stop her.","The Empress Dowager was a woman nearing fifty, with only a few threads of white in her hair, showing how well she usually maintained herself.","Her gaze swept sharply across the assembled people in the bedchamber like a hawk's, emanating the imposing aura of one who had long held a position of supreme power.","She wore a deep purple robe, and though she had arrived in haste, not a single part of her appearance was out of place."]},{"number":507,"title":"Chapter 507: You are a treacherous minister who usurped your nephew's throne","paragraphs":["Prince Cheng saw the Empress Dowager and his brow furrowed almost imperceptibly. He raised his hand to dismiss the two squads of guards who had followed him in, then greeted the Empress Dowager with a hint of a smile that did not reach his eyes, cupping his hands in a gesture of respect. \"How fortunate that the Imperial Sister-in-law has arrived!\"","The Empress Dowager was his elder sister-in-law, and now, technically, his elder as well.","Because of the Late Empress, Prince Cheng had never held Empress Dowager Jiang in much regard. When the late Emperor and the Late Empress were still alive, this woman Jiang had merely been a favoured consort of the emperor.","Thanks to the late Emperor's favour, aside from the deceased Empress and her son, who in the imperial harem was not overshadowed by mother and son alike?","She had never been a mentor to Prince Cheng, nor did he owe her any filial deference.","The Empress Dowager did not even glance at him. She walked straight toward the dragon couch.","Gan Sheng upon the couch saw his mother and his eyes suddenly reddened. His throat worked several times, like a drowning man finally seizing a piece of driftwood. In a hoarse voice he called out, \"Mother...\"","The Empress Dowager sat down at the edge of the couch and reached out to grasp Gan Sheng's withered hand. It was icy to the touch, his knuckles stiff, like gripping a bundle of dry firewood.","Her own eyes reddened as well, but she forced herself not to weep. She simply pressed her son's hand tightly within both of hers, as if she could pour her life into him that way.","\"Mother is here,\" she said softly, her voice as steady as a mountain. \"Don't be afraid, Sheng'er.\"","Then she slowly turned her head, her gaze like a blade, cutting toward Prince Cheng, who was watching their display of mother-son affection with that faintly mocking smile.","Prince Cheng, the late Emperor treated you well. After ascending the throne, His Majesty did not make things difficult for you either—he entrusted you with important responsibilities, enfeoffed you as a prince of the first rank, and granted you military command. Is this how you repay us, mother and son?","The Empress Dowager's voice was not loud, but every word carried the weight of a thousand pounds, each syllable forced out between clenched teeth. \"The Emperor is still alive, and you, his uncle, do not think of helping us hold the Gan family's realm, but instead conspire with outsiders to force the palace at this moment—is it not a little too hasty?\"","Prince Cheng's expression did not change. He merely rotated the sword resting on the ground slightly in his grip. \"You speak too harshly, Imperial Sister-in-law. What I do, I do for the sake of my Gan family's domain and ancestral legacy!\"","\"Domain and ancestral legacy?\" The Empress Dowager let out a cold laugh, dripping with scorn. \"You dare to speak of such words? You lost two cities on the northern front! Those were cities founded by our ancestors—did you hold them? You shrank from battle and lost them, and for that, you are a sinner of the Southern Yue!\"","The Empress Dowager slapped the edge of the bed in fury. \"When the court ordered you to fight to the death, you paid lip service and did otherwise. When it came to taxes, you withheld them for your own use. Do you think I don't know?\"","\"Now you see the Emperor gravely ill, and you cannot wait to abandon Jialing City, rushing back to seize your nephew's throne! Prince Cheng, your scrambling is far too ugly to watch!\"","Prince Cheng's face finally darkened. He had never liked this Consort Jiang, so favoured by his elder brother. After the Crown Prince died and the Empress followed, this woman's son had taken the throne, she had become Empress Dowager, and in due course, an elder to the imperial kin.","Now being lectured by her before the entire court, even with his deep scheming and broad mind, his composure cracked.","\"Imperial Sister-in-law,\" his voice turned cold, \"I respect you as Empress Dowager, as my elder, but I bid you choose your words carefully!","Calling me a coward who shrinks from battle? A sinner of Southern Yue? On the northern front I fought against the Dayan army—has the court any idea how far their weaponry has advanced?","Their firearms make my Southern Yue soldiers nothing but cannon fodder! Have any of you seen that?\"","He cast a cold glance at Gan Sheng on the bed. \"Why did Dayan send troops against Southern Yue? It is because of your fine son, our beloved Emperor, who laid hands on someone he should not have!","When he harboured improper thoughts toward that Goddess, he should have foreseen the consequences.","To blaspheme a deity is to invite Heaven's wrath!\"","He stepped forward, his armour clanking, and his voice suddenly rose. \"Drought not yet ended, and now floods! All because of the Emperor's lack of virtue!\"","With one stroke he nailed Gan Sheng in place. If what Prince Cheng said were true, not only would Gan Sheng have to yield the realm to him, but even after death he would earn no good reputation—at best, a posthumous name of ill repute.","A man's legacy before and after death—how could the Empress Dowager and Gan Sheng bear that?","\"Prince Cheng! All five nations suffer from drought. Why blame the emperor alone? She tried to bind that girl of Dayan, but only acting on rumours—she did it for the sake of Southern Yue's people! What crime is that?","You say all this now, but it is nothing more than an excuse for your seizure of the throne!","And the heavy rains have not yet come—the floods have not yet happened. Yet you are so certain in the words of a little girl from Dayan—aren't you inviting mockery?\"","[Master, this Empress Dowager simply will not be convinced until disaster hits! Wait till the rain comes in three days—then she'll have something to cry about!]","\"Little Pearl, whether she believes is not important. What matters is that the inaction of Southern Yue's court officials in this matter—we should help spread word of it far and wide!\"","Feng Tang's eyes lit up. The Grand Tutor was thinking of a war of public opinion—to sow discord among the people of Southern Yue, so that when Dayan conquered them, winning over the hearts of the people might go more smoothly!","Not to mention that at the very least, the people of both nations shared one thing in common: belief in the Goddess.","If Yue Fuguang knew what Feng Tang was thinking at this moment, he would surely be astonished—this fellow's mind turned faster than anyone's!","\"Imperial Sister-in-law says Lady Yue's warning is a joke?\" Prince Cheng took a deep breath, tamping down his surging emotions. His gaze swept over the Empress Dowager, over Gan Sheng, over every cowering figure in the hall.","\"Is that how all of you think? Is that why you wouldn't let the people leave the city? What if there really is heavy rain in three days?","What if the rain lasts a full month—what will you do then? Do you have any plan?\"","\"Well...\" The Empress Dowager and the Emperor were silent. Li Jie and the other officials exchanged glances. All their policies had been made to cope with drought. As for flooding, they did not entirely disbelieve it, but any suggestion of preparing for it had been shot down by the Empress Dowager herself.","They understood how she thought. If they acknowledged Lady Yue's words, they would be confirming the rumor that the Emperor had lost Heaven's favour and brought disasters upon the people.","Still, as for suppressing the commoners and refugees, they had their methods.","Prince Cheng saw the looks on their faces and gave a derisive snort. His voice returned to calm, but it was colder than ever. \"Imperial Sister-in-law, I will not argue with you. Whether the floods come, we will know in three days.","But what happens here today is already settled. If Your Majesty can bow to Heaven's will and the people's hearts, I will act with all due courtesy. If not...\"","He did not finish the sentence, but his hand went to the hilt of his sword.","The Empress Dowager rose to her feet abruptly. Her neatly arranged hair came loose at the edges from the sudden movement, but she paid it no mind. She straightened her back and glared at Prince Cheng. \"If not, then what? Kill me? Kill the Emperor? Kill the Crown Prince? And then kill every last minister?\"","She drew everyone to her side with one sentence. \"And then what? The voices of all under heaven—can you silence them? The historians with their upright brushes—can you blot them out? Prince Cheng, even if you sit on that throne, you will still be a traitor and usurper!","For a thousand generations, the histories will record what you did this day! Your descendants will remember that you stole the throne from your nephew!\"","These words rang out with force, startling the entire court. Li Jie, Zhou Wenbi, and the others felt their blood surge, and a few young officials could not help but straighten their backs."]},{"number":508,"title":"Chapter 508: Heaven Wants Him Dead: Southern Yue","paragraphs":["Prince Cheng was silent for a moment, then suddenly laughed, the smile full of mockery. \"History books?\"","He repeated the words coldly, then looked around the hall, his voice neither loud nor low, pitched to reach every ear present clearly. \"History is written by the victors, Sister-in-law. Surely you understand this principle.\"","The Empress Dowager trembled all over, her face changing drastically.","Prince Cheng paid her no further heed, turning instead toward the dragon bed, drawing the edict scroll from his sleeve and spreading it open once more, placing it before Gan Sheng.","Then, he unfastened an emblem token from his waist and cast it to the ground, the crisp sound ringing out.","\"Your Majesty, my soldiers have secured the entire imperial palace. The palace gates, the city gates, and the imperial guard barracks — all are under my control.\"","His voice remained calm, yet every word he spoke was chilling. \"Whether Your Majesty signs or not, the outcome will not change. If you sign, we can all keep our dignity. If not...\"","A smile tugged at the corner of his lips as his gaze fell upon Consort Shu, trembling in the corner, and the Crown Prince cradled in her arms.","Consort Shu's eyes brimmed with tears. The ten-year-old Crown Prince, long aware of their family's dire predicament, buried his head in his mother's embrace.","He feigned cowardice, careful not to let Prince Cheng see the hatred and penetrating awareness in his eyes.","\"Little Zhu, in the original timeline, what became of this Crown Prince?\" Gan Tang had seized Gan Sheng's position before the latter could even think clearly, and in both lifetimes, this prince had never been destined for the throne. Such was fortune's fickleness!","[In the original timeline, Gan Minghao was never named Crown Prince. With the support of the You family and Ling Yuanhang, Gan Tang's rise to power was far smoother than Prince Cheng's current path.]","[However, this Gan Minghao did not live to see Gan Tang ascend the throne. By the Da Yan calendar, he fell ill and died in the tenth year of Yuankang. Otherwise, given Gan Sheng's fondness for this mother and son, the position of Crown Prince would have been his sooner or later.]","\"Died of illness? Genuinely ill, or something else?\" Yue Fuguang detected the scent of poison in this.","[It started as genuine illness, but the medicine used to treat him was altered behind his back, and before long, it killed him.]","\"Who did it?\" Asking this aloud, her eyes unconsciously flickered between Consort Shu and the Empress.","[You must have guessed by now, Master. It was the Empress who struck. As for why — of course, to avenge her two sons. Though her loss of two children was tacitly approved by the Emperor, it was Consort Shu's people who had acted. Once the Empress lost her sons, she certainly wasn't about to watch her enemy's child grow to adulthood and seize the throne. She took her revenge on Consort Shu, and she did not forgive the Emperor either.","Gan Tang's smooth ascent to power owed much to the Empress's covert support.]","So that was it.","Yue Fuguang reflected — one should never underestimate a mother. Consort Shu, for the sake of her own child, had instigated the deaths of the Empress's two sons in succession.","And the Empress, in turn, could lie in wait for over a decade, avenging her sons and herself, even willing to hand the realm of Gan Sheng's bloodline into another's hands.","Yue Fuguang caught the Empress's gaze pausing briefly on Consort Shu and her child — a surge of raw murderous intent flashing through it that instant. So she already knew who her enemy was at this point.","Perhaps she had suspected long ago, merely lacking solid proof.","\"If you refuse to sign,\" Prince Cheng's voice arose once more, feather-light, \"I cannot guarantee that within these palace walls, some accident might not befall...\"","It was open, naked threat.","The Empress Dowager's face turned deathly pale. She opened her mouth to speak, but Gan Sheng pulled at her sleeve, silencing her.","Gan Sheng lay upon the bed, gazing at the scroll of yellow silk before him, at the bold, vigorous calligraphy inscribed upon it, and felt the whole scene was utterly absurd.","He was the late Emperor's most beloved son — not the eldest, but the one his father had marked as heir from the very beginning.","So what if his elder brother had been made Crown Prince? In the end, the throne fell into his own lap.","He had never needed to scheme for that seat, never had to fight tooth and nail for it the way his brothers had, cracking heads and drawing blood.","He simply devoted himself to being his father's most dutiful, filial son, never grabbing or scrambling. His eldest brother died, his legitimate uncle died, and his father pushed him into the position of Crown Prince. The path he had walked had been far too smooth.","In the early days of his reign, he had harbored grand ambitions — to govern with diligence, lay strategies across every front, and swallow up the geographically richest land of Da Yan, annexing it into Nan Yue, forging a mighty empire.","Everything had gone splendidly at first. The kingdom was peaceful at home, and Da Yan, just as he had wished, had been riddled through with his infiltration like a sieve.","Only a few more years and it would have been time to reap the harvest. But heaven did not comply. His nemesis — Yue Fuguang — had appeared.","Who could have imagined that this young girl's arrival would mark the beginning of his downfall?","He was merely twenty-eight years old, and the ambitions in his heart had yet to be realized — and now he was going to die, poisoned, no less.","Just like his elder brother and legitimate maternal uncle, succumbing to the same poison. Heaven's cycle of retribution was merciless after all.","He suddenly recalled his father's dying words: \"Beware of your little sister, and your uncle... a man who will never amount to much, but one who can certainly ruin things.\"","These years, that little imperial sister had remained quiet enough. When his brother and the former Empress died, she had still been a child, and he had paid her no particular suspicion, raising her alongside his own princesses.","He had never imagined that he would ultimately die at her hands. As for the kingdom itself — his gaze shifted to Prince Cheng — it would fall into the hands of this fool who would never amount to anything.","Heaven truly was betraying Nan Yue.","Yue Fuguang was unaware that within a few brief breaths, Gan Sheng's inner turmoil had been so rich — not only crediting her as the root cause of his ruin.","But also, as if at death's very door, retracing all twenty-eight years of his life.","Gan Sheng thought of resisting to the death, but he knew the ranks of officials filling this chamber were beyond helping him. Some, no doubt, were already quietly lining up behind Prince Cheng.","His edicts would never leave the palace; his orders would be carried out by no one. He was a dying man, and no one now cared that he was still the one sitting upon the dragon throne.","Dai Ping'an... at the very moment he needed him most, the man was nowhere to be seen. Not a trace of movement from him this entire time.","Either dead, or gone over to the enemy.","Having worked all of this through, Gan Sheng slowly extended his emaciated hand, the tips of his fingers brushing the edge of the silken scroll.","\"Your Majesty!\" Fei Yongxing knelt prostrate, tears and mucus streaming down his face. Every official in the court knew he was the Emperor's trusted confidant — if the Emperor fell, his entire household would follow.","Thus, Fei Yongxing's weeping came from a true place, and his words carried genuine sincerity. \"Your Majesty, you cannot! The foundations laid by our ancestors must not be handed away! Your subjects swear to live and die with Your Majesty!\"","His voice echoed through the bedchamber. No one answered.","The colleagues around him, who moments before had been stirred to fervor by the Empress Dowager's words, now stood like clay effigies, utterly still.","Li Jie and the others thought: This performance thing — you clearly don't grasp it. Emotional support is given because it is given; who actually takes it seriously!","What Fei Yongxing did not know was that the men behind him, though appearing statue-still, were in truth watching him with complex expressions, lips pressed tight — not in silence, but in observation, in calculation, waiting for a safe moment to choose sides.","Gan Sheng did not look at them. His gaze settled upon the Crown Prince, held in Consort Shu's arms — the ten-year-old boy trembling in his mother's embrace, shoulders quivering, seemingly terrified out of his wits."]},{"number":509,"title":"Chapter 509: Isn't this a little too late","paragraphs":["Originally, this son could have followed in his footsteps, and he would have done as his own father had done, letting the child of the woman he loved most inherit his empire.","But alas, heaven had other plans — a divine maiden descended from the Great Yan and utterly upended his grand design!","Gan Sheng closed his eyes.","If he refused, Prince Cheng would truly lay hands on this child. Putting himself in Prince Cheng's shoes, if he, Gan Sheng, were in that position, he would act even more ruthlessly than Prince Cheng.","There was a benefit to the man being simple-minded: Prince Cheng's soft-heartedness was the only lifeline his children had.","Otherwise, before the Great Yan forces even broke through the gates, all his sons would have died of \"sudden illness\" — wasn't that exactly how he had dealt with his late imperial uncle's only heir?","He opened his eyes and looked at Prince Cheng. The uncle and nephew stared at each other for a long moment, until Gan Sheng finally spoke, his voice weak yet clear: \"Imperial Uncle, I have three conditions.\"","Prince Cheng raised an eyebrow slightly. \"Your Majesty, pray speak!\"","\"First, the eldest prince shall be created Marquis of Anguo, with a fief of a thousand households, hereditary in perpetuity, and never subject to prosecution.\"","Prince Cheng nodded. \"Granted.\" This had been the place he'd already arranged for the crown prince — but as for \"never subject to prosecution\"... if the man fell ill or got hurt, that had nothing to do with him.","Prince Cheng's gaze flickered toward someone in the corner. He didn't even need to act personally; the man behind him would take care of the cleanup.","\"Second, the Grand Dowager shall move to Ciming Palace, with all her provisions doubled and her treatment at court never diminished.\"","Prince Cheng hesitated a moment, then said, \"Granted.\"","That old woman was already advanced in years — she didn't have many years left, and how much could she really use up anyway?","\"Third,\" — Gan Sheng's gaze suddenly turned sharp, a flame burning with the light of a dying man's final rally — \"I require the Imperial Uncle to swear before heaven that, for as long as he lives, he shall never harm the Grand Dowager or the princes. If he breaks this oath, may men and gods alike forsake him, may the state collapse, and may he die without a place to be buried!\"","The hall fell silent. Everyone turned to look at Prince Cheng.","Prince Cheng was silent. The final rays of the setting sun streamed through the window lattice, falling across his armor and casting shifting, uncertain light and shadow.","His expression revealed nothing — neither joy nor anger. Only his narrow, elongated eyes narrowed slightly, as if weighing something in his mind.","At last, he raised his right hand, faced the hall's entrance into the dying sunlight, and spoke in a low, solemn voice: \"Let Heaven and Earth above bear witness: I swear before Heaven that, for as long as I live, I shall never raise my hand against the Grand Dowager or the princes. Should I break this oath, may men and gods forsake me, may the state collapse, and may I die without a place to be buried.\"","As the oath settled over the hall, complete silence reigned.","Gan Sheng listened, and a bleak smile crept across his lips.","Slowly, he sat up — a motion that drained nearly all his remaining strength — then extended his trembling hand and took up the Imperial Jade Seal.","The seal was heavy. Holding it in both hands, it felt like clasping a mountain.","This seal had passed from his father's hands to his own, and now it was to pass from his hands to another's.","What it represented was not power, but a death warrant. A throne without the strength to protect it was nothing but a road to ruin.","He held the seal over the blank imprint space left on the edict, suspended, undropped.","Everyone in the hall held their breath.","The Grand Dowager turned her head away, unable to look. Empress Xu finally paused in her stirring of the medicine broth, her gaze lifting slightly to fix upon the jade seal, light flickering on and off in her eyes.","Even Prince Cheng's breathing unconsciously grew shallower. His fingers tightened slightly, the scales of his armor whispering against one another.","Gan Sheng suddenly raised his head one last time, taking in the palace he had lived in for twenty-eight years.","Carved beams, painted rafters, glorious and resplendent — not a single corner lacked some trace of him.","This palace had once belonged to his father, then to him, and now it was about to welcome a new master.","Suddenly, he felt a sense of release.","With a heavy, muffled thud, the seal fell.","The cinnabar seal paste left a scarlet imprint on the yellow silk: \"Receiving the Mandate from Heaven, May It Prosper Forever.\" Eight characters, red as if written in blood — so bright it dazzled the eye.","Gan Sheng's hands fell limp, his whole body drained of all strength, collapsing softly against the backrest.","His eyes were half-open, half-closed, his chest rising and falling faintly — a lamp on its last flicker of oil.","Seeing the matter settled, Yue Fuguang could not help but grow anxious. \"System, Prince Cheng is about to get exactly what he wants. What about the high-level figures of Panshan you mentioned? Those who side with the Emperor and the Crown Prince, those who side with Prince Cheng — where are they all?\"","Her gaze swept across every face in the room. At several junctures, she had expected someone to leap out and intervene, but from beginning to end — over several chapters by now — aside from one Fei Yongxing, everyone's role had been played entirely by three generations of the royal family.","\"Host, don't be impatient! The real show is just beginning!\"","No sooner had the system finished speaking than the tightly shut doors to the hall creaked open once more.","In came a procession of people. At the head was a young general in full armor, a sword at his waist, followed by two soldiers, and behind them a gaggle of elegantly dressed women and children — likely Gan Sheng's consorts and offspring. Behind them came a few more armored guards.","The women were of varied figures, each beautiful in her own way, and the children appeared to be Gan Sheng's sons and daughters.","They filed in, instantly drawing the attention of everyone in the bedchamber.","\"System, what's going on here? The edict of abdication has already been sealed. Why has Prince Cheng brought in all of his little wives and children? If it's meant to be a threat, isn't it a little too late?\"","\"It is too late. Host, didn't you notice? While Prince Cheng was facing off against the Grand Dowager earlier, he was unobtrusively glancing at the doorway several times.\"","\"His men are useless! They took so long that by the time they finally arrived with the hostages, the deed was already done.\"","\"Host, is it possible they did it on purpose?\"","\"What do you mean by that? Is this the 'real show' you mentioned?\"","\"Aren't you the one who's been looking for the head of Panshan? Well, look — that person is right there in this crowd.\"","\"Which one, which one?\" Since no one could see her, Yue Fuguang shamelessly let her eyes wander over every person in the group, thinking everyone looked suspicious, and yet no one looked like the Panshan leader.","Prince Cheng, who had just picked up the edict to scrutinize it — his gaze lingering especially long on the fresh red seal — was examining it.","Why hadn't he simply seized it and stamped it himself? Why go through the convoluted process of making Gan Sheng do it by hand?","Merely for the sake of \"legitimacy.\" Of course, such tricky maneuvering was not his own idea — it had come from his good strategist.","Left to his own temper, he would have had his men handle it long ago. There would have been no need to argue with the Emperor and his mother for all this time, or to drag in so many ministers as witnesses and hostages!","Just as he was thinking of his hostages, Prince Cheng's good mood from receiving the abdication edict soured a little. His brow knit. He had been about to look at his strategist and ask what they should do next, when the doors opened.","The man he had been waiting for all this time — Xiao Qi — had finally brought the people in.","Useless fool! By the time he got here, everything was already done... But then Prince Cheng's eyes landed on Gan Sheng's gathered consorts, and they lit up suddenly.","Xiao Qi grinned proudly at Prince Cheng. He knew he had fumbled the original task, but with such beauties in hand, his lord's punishment would be light.","Xiao Qi clasped his fist in salute to Prince Cheng. \"Your Highness, the people have been brought!\"","Before Gan Sheng could even say a word, the Grand Dowager exploded first: \"Prince Cheng! The edict has long since been sealed. The oath you swore had barely been made a moment ago — do you mean to renege already?\"","She slapped the bed frame hard, clearly enraged to the core."]},{"number":510,"title":"Chapter 510: People of Panshan Personally Come Down to Give Birth to Gan Sheng's Child","paragraphs":["It wasn't that she begrudged the emperor's consorts, but rather that she worried for her own grandchildren—these were the only offspring her son had left in this world, so of course she valued them more.","Prince Cheng rubbed his nose. He had originally intended to bring everyone over to threaten the emperor, but who knew his subordinates would be inefficient and arrive too late!","That was the situation, but he certainly couldn't say it that way. \"Royal sister-in-law is overthinking things. I merely heard that my eldest nephew was ill and hadn't seen the children in many days, so I specially had my men bring them over for my eldest nephew to see, and for him to enjoy a bit of family happiness one last time. This is also my sincerity as his uncle.\"","Although they had arrived late, letting Gan Sheng see them more was still good—it would prevent him from doing something foolish without considering their lives.","\"Your Majesty!\"","\"Father!\"","Wife and children rushed to the bedside together, fussing over Gan Sheng with concern.","[Host, have you figured out which one is the head of Panshan yet?]","\"Is it one of Gan Sheng's consorts?\"","[Don't forget, Prince Cheng also has support from the Panshan faction.]","\"That middle-aged man behind Prince Cheng, the only one not wearing armor? He's playing the role of military advisor, isn't he?] It's a pity he's missing a feather fan—not enough style.","[Master, look at that consort in white, and the matron behind her.]","Speaking of wanting to wear mourning clothes, among all the beautifully dressed consorts, the only woman wearing white stood out like a single patch of white in a garden of blossoms—beautiful and eye-catching.","\"Gan Sheng is about to die, and she wears that outfit? Not afraid of the Empress Dowager scolding her?\"","Sure enough, no sooner had Yue Fuguang's words fallen than the Empress Dowager's scolding began. She had been furious at Prince Cheng with nowhere to vent, and now her son's throne was gone, and he was about to lose his life too.","The hatred in her heart!","Seeing Consort Liang dressed in white again, she lashed out, \"Shen Lingqin, haven't I told you that you're not allowed to wear white before the Emperor recovers? Did you stuff my words into a dog's stomach?\"","Everyone silently lowered their heads at the Empress Dowager being driven to such crude language—if they were in her position, they probably couldn't maintain their composure either.","\"Forgive me, Empress Dowager. This concubine... this concubine was so focused on His Majesty that I came in a hurry, without time to dress properly, and forgot to change my clothes. I beg the Empress Dowager and His Majesty to forgive me.\"","Yue Fuguang swept her eyes over her face and her ornaments from head to toe. [System, do you really think Consort Liang didn't dress up? I think this looks more like a no-makeup makeup look!]","Her naturally delicate beauty was further enhanced by the white outfit, making her appear even more soft and fragile. Among all the consorts, each beautiful in her own way, she was particularly eye-catching—the type that makes men want to protect her, especially suited to an emperor like Gan Sheng.","\"Consort Liang, dear sister, stop crying. His Majesty is still ill, and with that outfit and your tears, isn't that bad luck!\"","Consort Shu had been keeping a close eye on her rival Consort Liang ever since the consorts entered. If she had to name her greatest enemy in the harem, it wasn't Her Majesty the Empress—it was this Consort Liang, who held a special place in the Emperor's heart.","Now that her son's position as Crown Prince was taken away, that didn't mean the competition was over.","The resources and wealth in the hands of the Emperor and the Empress Dowager belonged to her and her son, so naturally she had to find ways to make the Empress Dowager and Emperor detest Consort Liang.","Consort Liang's tears welled up in her eyes. \"Sister Consort Shu, it's my fault.\"","She then apologized to the Emperor and Empress Dowager, \"It's all this concubine's fault. From now on...\"","Prince Cheng had been watching the show with great interest, especially when the beautiful woman in white shed tears—truly like pear blossoms in rain, delicate and pitiful. He couldn't take his eyes off her. It was precisely at this moment, with his eyes dazzled, that Prince Cheng failed to notice danger approaching.","\"Little Zhu, protect Prince Cheng's life!\"","\"Your Highness, watch out!\"","Whoosh!","Bang!","\"Xiao Qi, how dare you!\"","\"Your Highness, you're injured!\"","\"No! The sword is poisoned!\"","\"Xiao Qi, you traitor! Not only do you wound His Highness, but you dare to use poison! I'll fight you to the death!\"","The young general who had been escorting the ministers raised his weapon and clashed with Xiao Qi.","Chaos broke out in an instant. Everyone watched the two fight in the relatively spacious bedchamber and scrambled to back away.","Meanwhile, Prince Cheng, whose arm was dripping dark red blood, was shielded by the military-advisor-looking man and several subordinates.","\"Xiao Qi, go to hell!\"","\"Fei Dashan, you're no match for me!\"","In the midst of the flashing blades and daggers, all eyes were drawn to them. [Master, beware of Consort Liang and her maid!]","\"What, is the problem her? Would she also move against Prince Cheng?] If it hadn't been for the system using its power to shove Prince Cheng at the last moment, his wound would have been to the heart rather than the arm.","\"Little Zhu, could Consort Liang be the head of Panshan planted inside the palace?\"","If she was, when the system performed a soul search on her later, should she have it go a bit easier?","This thought had just surfaced in her mind when Yue Fuguang suppressed it.","[Master, Consort Liang does hold a high position, but she's not the top leader. She...]","Before the system could finish its sentence, Prince Cheng and his group had retreated to a position between Consort Liang and the princes and princesses.","\"Die!\" A nondescript young eunuch whipped out a dagger gleaming with cold light and lunged at Prince Cheng from an extremely tricky angle.","\"Protect His Highness!\"","Bang!","The seemingly harmless middle-aged military advisor reacted in time when the dagger was just an inch from Prince Cheng's lower abdomen—he blocked it with his hand and kicked the attacker away in one motion.","\"Take him down!\"","Yue Fuguang glanced at where Prince Cheng was wounded. This man, before even ascending the throne, had nearly lost his kidney!","\"Little Zhu, is there more? Why isn't it Consort Liang doing the attacking?\"","[Master, do you know who that eunuch is?]","Nonsense—she had only been in the Southern Yue palace for one day, even seeing the Emperor for the first time. How would she know some random eunuch!","\"Little Zhu, do you think your master would know some eunuch from an enemy country?\"","[Hehehe, don't be angry, master. Little Zhu was just asking casually. Master, let me tell you—that eunuch is part of Consort Liang's group.","Within Panshan, he serves as a guard. He's currently by Consort Liang's son's side, taking orders from her.","See that kid in the blue brocade clothes among the children? That's Consort Liang's son, the candidate that part of Panshan wants to push onto the throne.]","\"Panshan people personally gave birth to Gan Sheng's child and then escort him all the way to the throne? That's even more grand an arrangement than Emperor Mingxi's.\"","Yue Fuguang glanced at the terrified former Crown Prince Gan Minghao. \"So in the original timeline, the Crown Prince died simply because he wasn't the heir Panshan wanted? Did Gan Sheng know about this?\"","[Exactly. Even if the Crown Prince weren't deposed now, he'd still be destined to die of illness. Not because he wasn't the heir Panshan favored, but because the faction behind him lost to Consort Liang's group.]","\"This Panshan faction is really complicated—so many people placing their bets?\""]},{"number":511,"title":"Chapter 511: Even You Want to Kill Me, Your King","paragraphs":["Mount Pan is not a monolith. Gan Sheng certainly doesn't know Consort Liang's true identity. He still thinks the Crown Prince can replicate his own path to power. Little does he know, the one truly replicating his rise is Consort Liang's son, the Third Prince, Gan Mingyu. Both their paths were orchestrated by certain figures in Mount Pan!","As for the \"grand occasion\" the master mentioned, if Gan Sheng knew, he might not want it. This Consort Liang is Mount Pan's third-in-command stationed in Nanyue.","\"What about first and second-in-command? Is there a fourth? Are they all in the imperial palace?\" If so, Gan Sheng's harem isn't much better than Dayan's. He's desperately planting spies in Dayan, unaware that his own home has been stolen right from under him.","Master, look at the elderly maid who's always sticking close to Consort Liang. She's the true top boss of Mount Pan's Nanyue operation. She only arrived at the palace recently—and she's here to seize the throne. As for second-in-command, isn't he right by Prince Cheng's side? That kick he gave his own man—not a shred of loyalty in it.","\"So, what about Xiao Qi, who made the move? Is he also from Mount Pan?\"","He's not. He was just bought off by Mount Pan. At best, he's a half-member.","\"Half? What does that mean?\"","Xiao Qi fell for a honey trap. That's the work of the eunuch Zhao Quan'an by Gan Sheng's side. He's also Mount Pan's man—he's been with Gan Sheng since before the late emperor, the late empress, and the late Crown Prince died. He and the person behind Consort Liang originally came from the same faction, but then someone developed selfish ambitions, and that's how Consort Liang and her son came to be.","\"A honey trap? Low cost, high reward. Brilliant strategy!\"","Xiao Qi wants to marry the man's adopted daughter, so of course he has to earn his keep for the emperor. Prince Cheng's life is the bride price for that marriage.","\"Judging by this man, he seems quite favored by Prince Cheng. He should be a trusted confidant, no? How did he let Prince Cheng barge into the imperial palace? If he truly cared for the emperor, he should have struck halfway or tipped him off in advance. Look at the emperor now—he seems completely unprepared.\"","That's where you have to hand it to the strategist by Prince Cheng's side. He knows how to keep secrets. Out of the entire army, only he and Prince Cheng knew the attack would happen today. Everyone else's orders were to stand by.","\"Your Majesty, since you've made a move against me, don't blame me for breaking our agreement!\" Prince Cheng said through gritted teeth at the emperor.","He was not only angry, but also in pain. The wound on his waist wasn't deep, and although the gash on his arm was wide, he could still bear it. But add poison to the mix, and it became hard to endure.","\"Uncle, look at me. I'm in this state—where would I find the strength to arrange assassins to harm you?\" Gan Sheng acted perfectly calm, even distancing himself from any involvement. \"You know the one I trust most is Dai Ping'an. He's not here right now. What men do I have at my disposal?\"","\"Uncle, is Dai Ping'an... dead, or did he defect?\"","\"He told me that he owed you a debt of gratitude for recognizing his talent. He said he'd go down first to wait for you—so you wouldn't be a stranger in the underworld.\"","What a phrase—\"a stranger in the underworld.\" As if anyone could claim experience there!","The System: I do!","Gan Sheng closed his eyes. He knew, at this point, that Dai Ping'an's failure to appear could only mean he was gone.","\"Don't worry. Though he wouldn't serve me, I admire loyal men. I gave him an honorable end.\"","His gaze shifted to Xiao Qi, still locked in combat. \"But the disloyal—everyone has the right to strike them down!\"","Fei Dashan was gradually losing ground, but when he heard Prince Cheng's words, it was like he'd been injected with new spirit. \"Brothers, charge together! Traitors deserve no courtesy!\"","\"Nephew, Xiao Qi and this young eunuch—if they're not your men, whose are they? Tell me, who else could command them?\"","His eyes settled on Gan Mingyu. When he'd first entered, he'd seen this eunuch trailing the boy.","\"You—come here!\" He pointed straight at Gan Mingyu. \"If I recall correctly, you should be the third prince, right? Come, tell me—what's the meaning of this eunuch? Are you trying to kill me?\"","\"It wasn't me! It wasn't me!\" Gan Mingyu retreated a few steps. His siblings instinctively distanced themselves, afraid of being implicated.","\"Uncle, the Third Prince is only eight years old. He knows nothing. How could he possibly harbor any intention to harm you?\"","Consort Liang put on an air of frailty, gracefully supported by the old maid as she drifted toward Prince Cheng. She wasn't weeping, but her off-puttingly elegant, hesitant demeanor created an entirely different spectacle.","\"Shameless!\" The Grand Empress Dowager, irritated by the display, swiftly rolled her prayer beads between her fingers, wishing she could strike herself blind.","The ministers in the background had been doing their best to stay invisible from the start. Except for Fei Yongxing, whose barely-contained excitement was written all over his face, everyone else kept their heads down in silence.","Prince Cheng, on the other hand, was staring openly at Consort Liang the moment she appeared—his gaze stuck like a fool.","Yue Fuguang saw this look and decided this worthless man's life absolutely had to be saved. If Nanyue fell into his hands, conquering it would cost Dayan far fewer soldiers.","\"Little Zhu, this lecher—has he forgotten he's still poisoned?\"","Master, people from Mount Pan know their poisons. Just now I saw the strategist give Prince Cheng a pill. It should be an antidote.","\"An antidote? Then why is black blood still oozing from his arm?\"","Feng Tang and the others looked—sure enough. If you paid close attention, you could also see that Prince Cheng's face and lips had a faint blue tinge.","If Prince Cheng's poison couldn't be resolved, the question was whether their deputy commander would eventually step in to save him.","Master, do you think mortals' antidote pills can compare to ours? They need time to work.","\"Little Zhu, is Consort Liang's group about to make their move? Prince Cheng can't croak here! You...\"","Before Yue Fuguang could even finish giving the order to the System, the System took the initiative on its own. The moment Consort Liang raised her sleeve to strike, it launched the lovesick Prince Cheng flying back with a blast.","To any outside observer, it looked like Consort Liang herself had sent him flying—even she nearly believed she'd somehow mastered extraordinary martial arts on the spot.","\"Consort Liang! You too! You want me dead!\" Once safely on the ground, Prince Cheng naturally spotted the delicate dagger hidden in Consort Liang's sleeve.","Consort Liang glanced at Gan Sheng. \"For His Majesty, your servant would die willingly!\"","And there it was—even at this moment, Consort Liang refused to reveal her true allegiances.","\"Seize her!\" Prince Cheng barked the order. A squad of soldiers, who had finally arrived to investigate the commotion, finally had something useful to do.","\"And the old maid beside her! Also all the eunuchs and palace maids in Consort Liang's quarters, and everyone in the Third Prince's residence! Arrest them all—not one left behind! Throw them all in the dungeon!\"","After being assassinated back-to-back, Prince Cheng finally grew a brain and took action before Mount Pan's #1 could, cuffing them all first.","With the imperial edict now in hand, Prince Cheng remembered that staying there any longer was unwise. Turning on his heel, he strode toward the palace gates.","\"A few of you, come help our dear emperor... relocate.\" He planned to occupy this place. He couldn't let Gan Sheng die here—that would be too inauspicious.","Halting at the doorway, he spoke without turning back: \"When you reach Yong'an Palace, His Majesty may rest easy recovering. All provisions for Yong'an Palace will be arranged by me.\"","A pause, and his voice drifted back from beyond the hall, muted by the evening wind: \"As for today's events, I will investigate until I find the truth!\""]},{"number":512,"title":"Chapter 512: This Death Is Very Un-Imperial","paragraphs":["His peripheral vision swept over the bound Xiao Qi and the blood-spitting eunuch, then back to Consort Liang and her son, who had lost all trace of their earlier composure.","Just now, he had felt something push him, but it clearly wasn't Consort Liang, because she had obviously been about to make a move against him.","\"Could it be that I truly carry the Mandate of Heaven?\" Prince Cheng muttered to himself. His dark cloak fluttered behind him as the sounds of his armor grew fainter in the distance.","\"What a confident one, this fellow!\"","Prince Cheng was gone, but the three hundred armored guards outside the hall did not withdraw. They still surrounded the emperor's bedchamber, watertight.","[Master, do we stay or follow Consort Liang and the others? Whose memory should we search first?]","Prince Cheng's departure took the life of the hall with him. The emperor's bedchamber suddenly fell quiet. What remained were the emperor's mother and his wives and concubines—many people, but all silent. Not a single one dared to speak.","\"Let's watch the ending before we leave. Isn't there still Zhao Quan'an? By the look of it, he didn't manage to find an antidote for the emperor.\"","[Exactly. Even the two most skilled poison masters of this age, Du Zhongxian and Li Sanming, could only shake their heads when faced with the poison 'Red Medicine.'","This thing was designed from the very beginning to kill. There simply is no antidote.]","But judging by how Gan Sheng was still clinging to life, he must have taken some kind of palliative medicine.","At this moment, a whole room full of women, yet it was utterly silent. Seeing that Consort Liang, with whom they had struggled their entire lives, had been taken away, the various concubines felt joy in their hearts. But with the throne lost, they no longer had the will to keep fighting.","In the face of an emperor about to die, everyone chose silence by mutual consent.","The Empress Dowager slowly walked to the edge of the couch, took Gan Sheng's hand, and finally let her tears fall.","The tears silently traced the wrinkles on her face and dripped onto the bright yellow bedding, leaving dark stains.","\" Sheng'er...\" Her voice choked. \"It's your mother's fault. I couldn't save you, and I couldn't protect your throne either!\"","Gan Sheng forced his eyes open. Looking at his mother's face, usually so well-maintained but now looking ten years older, he suddenly felt a pang of bitterness in his heart.","He wanted to say something, but found his throat blocked, as if something were stuck there. The confrontation just now had used up all his strength, and now he could not say a single word.","His throne had originally been seized through schemes, and now it had been taken from him the same way... He shook his head slightly, reached out, and gently squeezed his mother's hand.","The Empress stood up, handed the bowl of long-cold medicinal broth to the palace maid beside her, and said in a flat tone, \"The medicine has gone cold. Have another bowl brewed.\"","Her voice was calm, her movements and etiquette flawless, as if nothing had happened at all.","Several imperial consorts, though they had lost the heart to compete for favor, could not help but sob softly at the thought of their uncertain futures. How much of that weeping was for the emperor's fate, and how much for their own unknown destinies, only they themselves knew.","Consort Shu, holding Gan Minghao's hand, trembled slightly with a look of panic and despair, all trace of her former pride as the first favorite concubine of Southern Yue gone. Only her darting eyes hinted that she was still scheming about something.","Gan Sheng watched all of this and quietly closed his eyes. He was too tired and needed to sleep.","The court officials who had been taken away by Prince Cheng were released at the palace gates. The great deed was done—the entire capital was in his hands—and he was not afraid they could stir up any trouble.","What mattered most was that he needed these people to get to work, preparing for his coronation ceremony.","Zhou Wenbi, Li Jie, and the others paused at the palace gate, glanced back in the direction of the imperial palace, then shook their heads with long sighs—whether sighing for the emperor or for themselves, no one could tell.","The setting sun cast their hunched silhouettes against the palace walls beyond. Their footsteps were as heavy as if they were carrying the fate of the entire dynasty on their backs, and they slowly faded away into the twilight.","\"Little Pearl, time to get to work!\"","[Master, just you wait and see!]","Yue Fuguang didn't know how many broken hearts were in that evening's glow, but at least none of them were hers.","This trip to Southern Yue, for her, was not just about watching a good show. She had also uncovered several big fish that Panshan had planted in Southern Yue.","They stayed in Southern Yue for three days. During those three days, the system went through—took care of—each of Panshan's key operatives in Southern Yue, and through careful analysis, calculated the location of Panshan's headquarters.","[Too bad. That Grand Chief covers himself too well every time he appears. We can't even tell if it's a man or a woman!]","\"It doesn't matter. First, we take out their stronghold, then we empty their treasury. Once we've arrested everyone we know about, we won't have to worry about that person not showing themselves!\"","[Then when do we go treasure hunting?] Judging from the memories of the old nanny beside Consort Liang, Panshan's treasury could be described as wealth to rival a nation—that was no exaggeration.","\"Not so fast. Let's deal with what's right in front of us first!\"","Yue Fuguang stretched out her hand and caught a drop of rain. The heavy rains of Southern Yue had arrived right on schedule. All the slander and disbelief in the world turned to panic in that single moment.","The common people rushed home to pack their belongings and prepare to take refuge in the mountains.","News of the downpours in Southern Yue and Nanzhao spread across the six kingdoms within days. By this time, the Grand Yan army's southern campaign had finished its rest and resupply. The army arrived outside the walls of Suicheng, and the great battle was about to break out.","Upon hearing this news, both Beili and Western Qiang—who had been on the verge of war over the incident at Mount Chengping—set aside their differences and began peace talks in the face of the mighty Dayan.","[Master, the plague in Dongyi is basically under control. This is a perfect time for Dayan to swoop in and claim the spoils.]","\"Yesterday I received a letter from the emperor; the naval forces stationed along the eastern coast should have finished assembling. The eastern campaign is a matter of a day or two.\"","Now that the system has given such concrete intelligence, Emperor Mingxi will surely stop hesitating or trying to find the perfect moment to strike.","[Master! The Empress of Nanzhao has passed away!]","Yue Fuguang was still thinking about the Dongyi situation when suddenly the system's death knell rang in his ears. \"What? Lan Xuan'er's mother is dead? When did that happen?\"","\"That shouldn't be— the southern rains in Nanzhao and Nanyue only lasted five or six days; a flood is still some way off. Even if there were flood damage, how would it affect a reigning monarch?\"","[Because she didn't die a natural death— she died of 'illness'!]","\"Illness? A real illness or a fake one? Don't tell me she was poisoned again? Damn it, Gan Sheng is still alive and well, so why is she gone first?\"","[She died this morning. Master, have you been busy these past few days? Today is Prince Cheng's enthronement ceremony. On the very same day— one person ascends as emperor while the neighboring kingdom's ruler dies. What a coincidence.","But you've guessed wrong this time, Master. In the early stages, the Empress was indeed genuinely sick. Because someone with malicious intent switched her medicine, a minor cold dragged on into typhoid fever. Her body was already weak, and what with her ungrateful sons and daughters provoking her day after day, this morning she coughed up blood and died!]","\"Killed by her own children's anger? That's hardly a death befitting an emperor!\"","Yue Fuguang slapped his forehead lightly. \"Oh right, I almost forgot— today is the day Prince Cheng ascends the throne! And also the Empress's death anniversary!\"","[And those aren't the only big events today. Suicheng has been successfully taken by Dayan. The moment Prince Cheng takes power, he inherits half the realm.]"]},{"number":513,"title":"Chapter 513: The Title of 'Hundred-Day Emperor'","paragraphs":["Yue Fuguang smiled faintly. “Perhaps he may even become the emperor who presides over Nanzhao’s downfall—the shortest-reigning emperor in Nanzhao’s history.”","【If Lords Xu and Wei put in some effort, maybe Prince Cheng could earn the title of a 'Hundred-Day Emperor'.】","\"Speaking of the throne, now that the Empress of Nanzhao is gone, which of her children will take the throne?\"","【I saw that the Empress left behind a decree, passing the throne to Lan Xuan'er, but she won't have the chance to succeed.】","\"Why? Is someone planning to move against her?\"","【Exactly. The Second Prince, in league with the Empress's close attendant, trusted ministers, and the Marquis of Jing'an, forged a decree, passing the throne to the Second Prince, and ordering the other children to leave for their fiefs in ten days. As for Lan Xuan'er, still staying in Dayan, she is accused of colluding with the enemy and betraying the state—she is to be given the death penalty!】","\"System, this plot feels awfully familiar!\"","【Host, of course it's familiar—these are all leftovers from the games your ancestors back home played!】","Yue Fuguang's eyes twinkled, \"Little Zhu, will Lan Xuan'er go to her death obediently?\" In history, there was only ever one well-behaved royal darling, and it remains to be seen how Lan Xuan'er will choose.","She has no troops and no power in her hands; the question is whether she has the courage to defy imperial authority.","\"She's in Dayan. As long as she doesn't want to die, no one can force her to.\" Yue Fuguang believed that with Dayan's current national strength, it wasn't something a small Nanzhao could dictate.","Besides, ordering the execution of his own daughter—Emperor Mingxi himself would first suspect the decree was a forgery.","\"What? Someone is questioning Mother Empress's decree?\"","While Yue Fuguang was discussing Nanzhao matters with the system, the Nanzhao court was busier than ever due to the Empress's sudden death.","Meanwhile, the future emperor of Nanzhao, the Second Prince Lan Xuancheng, heard his subordinate's report and slammed his teacup onto the floor with a loud crash.","The tea splashed onto the Minister of Rites's official robe. He didn't bother to wipe it off, instead bowing to the Second Prince Lan Xuancheng seated above him, \"Second Prince, what arrangements would you have for His Majesty's funeral?\"","Outside the hall, the rain poured in torrents; inside the hall, a storm was brewing.","The funeral bells announcing the Empress's death still echoed over the Nanzhao imperial palace, and within a short half hour, the Empress's children had already clashed several times over the succession.","In theory, the funeral rituals for a deceased emperor had established precedents, and the Minister of Rites could have simply followed the standard procedure. But these were troubled times!","It wasn't that he, as Minister of Rites, was incompetent—it was that Nanzhao at this moment truly was, like the weather outside, on the verge of collapse.","The entire court had been busy preparing against potential floods and calming the already restless populace, when suddenly, the core of the nation—the Emperor—was gone. Who wouldn't be distressed?","\"The heavy rain has already fallen for six consecutive days. Many people's homes have collapsed, and large areas are flooded. If we still follow the original funeral protocol...\"","Then all the high-ranking officials would be attending the Emperor's funeral, leaving too few people to handle the relief work!","\"Also, with His Majesty's sudden death, the entire kingdom must go into mourning and wear white. But since more than half the populace has fled into the mountains, it's difficult to notify everyone in time.\"","Before Lan Xuancheng could respond, the Minister of Rites Xia Wenqi had already moved himself to tears. If His Majesty's funeral were to be simplified, as a veteran minister, he would feel terrible about it—but circumstances demanded it...","\"In your opinion, Lord Xia, what should be done?\" Lan Xuancheng kicked the ball right back.","Xia Wenqi cursed a hundred times in his heart, but what came out of his mouth was, \"Your Highness is the new sovereign who will ascend the throne. Your word is law. Your humble servant will defer entirely to Your Highness!\"","He phrased his allegiance euphemistically, kicking the ball back just as skillfully.","Lan Xuancheng glanced at his adoptive father, the Marquis of Jing'an, seated below. Seeing him nod, Lan Xuancheng cleared his throat, and his eyes instantly turned red. \"While Mother Empress was alive, she always advocated frugality. Now that state affairs are complicated, with troubles both at home and abroad, and she loved her people like her own children, she surely would not want her funeral to delay the rescue of the afflicted.\"","\"Your Highness, please do not grieve too deeply, lest you harm your health—the late Emperor would worry!\" Eunuch Fu, the Empress's close attendant, dutifully offered Lan Xuancheng a silk handkerchief. \"Your Highness should focus on matters of state. The late Emperor's funeral arrangements can be entirely entrusted to Lord Xia and the other princes.\"","No one in the hall spoke up about Eunuch Fu's sudden interjection—they didn't even raise an eyelid. This man's current standing was even more favored than during the Empress's lifetime.","Sure enough, Lan Xuancheng heeded his words and nodded repeatedly. \"What Eunuch Fu says is reasonable. My siblings are all Mother Empress's biological children, and they will surely put in more effort than others.","Just now, the Eldest Princess was so grief-stricken over Mother Empress's passing. It would be fitting to entrust the funeral arrangements to them—a way for them to fulfill their final filial duty to our mother.\"","Eunuch Fu immediately led the chorus, \"Your Highness is most wise!\"","Xia Wenqi and the six ministers of the ministries, along with a host of high officials, exchanged glances and all bowed in unison, \"Your Highness is most wise!\"","\"Let me in! I want to see Lan Xuancheng!\" Amid the chorus of \"Your Highness is most wise,\" a commotion arose outside the hall—the Eldest Princess was causing a scene.","She and her siblings had received news of their mother's death barely an hour ago. And now Lan Xuancheng, who had supposedly been granted the throne but had yet to formally ascend it, was already starting his covert moves against them.","When it came to discussing state affairs with the ministers, even the princes and princesses who had already taken part in politics were excluded—such small-mindedness truly ran in the blood of his biological father, that concubine-born son of the Yue family.","“Eldest Princess, the Second Prince is inside deliberating with the ministers, and without summons, you cannot enter!” The guard blocked the way with his halberd, trying to talk the cluster of princes and princesses back.","Blue Xuanting, never one for patience, flared up at the word “summons.” “Lan Xuancheng has not yet succeeded the throne—what right does he have to issue decrees? Does he dare touch the imperial seal now?”","“Indeed. Though Second Brother is the heir apparent, until the day of his coronation, he may not use the imperial seal without authorization.” The Third Prince, standing behind the Eldest Princess, also stepped forward. “Our mother the Empress has barely grown cold—as her children, we should show her due respect!”","“Third Brother speaks truly.” The Fourth Prince’s lips curled into a cold smirk. “This one recalls that Mother’s imperial seal was always kept under Eunuch Fu’s watch. And now, given how close Eunuch Fu is with Second Brother, one cannot help but wonder.”","“Fourth Brother, wonder about what?” the Fifth Princess couldn’t help but ask.","“Dear Fifth Sister, naturally one wonders whether someone has secretly used the imperial seal—and the succession edict...” The Fourth Prince stopped there, leaving it to the imagination. But everyone around him—everyone except the siblings themselves—broke out in a cold sweat.","Was this something they were hearing for free just by standing in the front row? They hadn’t asked to be first in line for this!","“Fourth Brother, you exaggerate!” The doors to the council hall opened from within, and Lan Xuancheng stood at the threshold, hands clasped behind his back. Behind him trailed Eunuch Fu, the Marquis of Jing’an, and a host of high-ranking officials robed in purple and crimson.","The Fourth Prince absently fingered the jade pendant at his waist, one eyebrow raised. “Second Brother, whether I exaggerate or not—outsiders may not know, but the siblings among us certainly do.”","He turned toward the Eldest Princess. “Eldest Sister, don’t you agree your brother here speaks the truth?”","The Eldest Princess stepped forward, lightly patting the Fourth Prince’s arm. “Fourth Brother is right. Mother doted on every one of us, and as for Little Sixth being accused of colluding with the enemy and sentenced to death—I for one refuse to believe it.”"]},{"number":514,"title":"Chapter 514: Sibling Quarrel","paragraphs":["It wasn’t because she and the Sixth Princess had such a close relationship. Rather, she was using it as an excuse. As long as there was any doubt about the part of the edict ordering Lan Xuan’er’s death, then even the claims that the throne had been passed to Lan Xuancheng could be false.","Hearing the pointed, loaded remarks from the others, the Second Prince’s expression darkened, and his eyes grew colder. “You don’t believe me? Elder Sister, why don’t you go ask Mother herself whether she truly passed the throne to me?”","The Eldest Princess couldn’t help tightening her grip on the exquisite riding crop in her hand. Her beautiful face turned icy as she glared sharply at her younger brother. “Lan Xuancheng, are you threatening me?”","Lan Xuancheng brushed at a speck of nonexistent dust on his clothes and clasped his hands behind his back. “What do you think, Elder Sister?”","Then he changed tack. “Mother has shown me such great favor by entrusting me with this heavy responsibility. I am, of course, filled with trepidation.”","He pointed behind him. “Mother is in the Anning Palace. Aren’t you afraid of disturbing her peace? You came here without first paying your respects to Mother, and instead brought baseless rumors to make trouble for me. Is that how a child should behave? Is that how a subject should act?”","The Fifth Princess stepped forward and linked her arm through the Eldest Princess’s. “Second Brother, naturally we will pay our respects to Mother. But right now, we are talking about Sixth Sister.”","She looked straight at the Second Prince. “Second Imperial Brother, everyone in the court knows that Mother dotes on Sixth Sister above all others. How could she bear to order her death?","“As for treason and selling out the country, do you have any actual evidence?”","Lan Xuancheng let out a mocking laugh. “Fifth Sister, if I remember correctly, among the six of us siblings, you and Sixth Sister have always had the worst relationship.","“And now you’ve come here to question me. Is this truly because of your deep sisterly affection?”","“Besides, I wasn’t the one who accused her of treason and betraying the country. It was written in the edict. Why don’t you go ask Mother, along with Elder Sister, why she was so certain?”","Lan Xuancheng refused to take the bait, and naturally, the Fifth Princess refused to take his. “So, Second Imperial Brother, you have no evidence, do you?”","“Second Brother, that isn’t fair. Normally, when Fifth Sister and Sixth Sister quarrel over jewelry, clothes, or Mother’s favor, those are merely childish squabbles.","“But this concerns life and death. Fifth Sister came to ask you about it precisely because they are sisters born of the same mother. You shouldn’t question her intentions.”","The Third Prince, who had the closest relationship with the Fifth Princess, stepped forward to defend her.","The imperial siblings stood before the palace, trading words one after another. The palace maids and eunuchs, the guards and ministers, and even the storm raging outside the palace all became mere background to their argument.","Yue Fuguang only learned from the system two days later that the Lan siblings had quarreled several times. In the end, because of the flooding, the Empress’s funeral was held as simply as possible.","Other than Lan Xuancheng, who was to ascend the throne, the other princes and princesses would depart for their fiefs later. Their departure was postponed until the torrential rain stopped. Lan Xuancheng had agreed to this mainly because the rain had continued for eight days, and the water in the streets had already risen above people’s calves. Even if he wanted to drive them away to their fiefs, they couldn’t leave.","As for Lan Xuan’er’s charge of treason, it was temporarily set aside due to insufficient evidence. After Lan Xuancheng ascended the throne, he would send people to investigate and deal with her accordingly.","However, the edict summoning Lan Xuan’er back to the kingdom had already been sent out.","“So, by keeping everything simple, Lan Xuancheng can ascend the throne sooner?”","[Exactly. Although everyone has already acknowledged him as the new ruler, the formal ceremony hasn’t been completed. Without the proper legitimacy, even sitting on the throne makes Lan Xuancheng feel uneasy.]","“What happened to Lan Xuan’er? Would Lan Xuancheng really let go so easily of the younger sister who poses the greatest threat to him? Somehow, I don’t believe it.”","A Crown Prince who had been deposed never ended well after the new ruler took the throne. Lan Xuan’er had even been personally named by the Empress as her successor. Would Lan Xuancheng really keep her alive?","[The incident happened less than three days ago, so Lan Xuan’er hasn’t yet received news of the Empress’s death. But just as you predicted, Lan Xuancheng has agreed publicly to punish her only after solid evidence is found.","[In reality, he has already secretly sent people to Great Yan. They plan to ambush and kill her on the way back.]","“He wants to dispose of Lan Xuan’er in secret, then pin the blame on Great Yan? Killing two birds with one stone!”","Seated outside the flying carriage, Feng Tang and Dai Yuxing exchanged a glance. Dai Yuxing had gradually recovered from the excitement of riding in a flying carriage for the first time.","He had begun thinking about how to get the news to the capital as quickly as possible. Great Yan was not going to take the blame for killing another country’s princess.","[There are people from Southern Yue behind Lan Xuancheng. They hope that Nanzhao will help Southern Yue tie down part of Great Yan’s army.]","“So they plan to use Lan Xuan’er’s death as a pretext to declare war on Great Yan? If they want to fight, they could just do it. Why go through all these twists and turns?”","[That’s Southern Yue’s plan. Whenever a war is launched, one needs a justifiable cause to calm the people at home, doesn’t one? Unfortunately, they never expected Lan Xuancheng to betray them once he had crossed the river. They had never encountered anyone who moved as quickly as he did.]","“What do you mean? Lan Xuancheng has other plans?”","[Master, Lan Xuancheng has also realized that Southern Yue is probably doomed this time. So he doesn’t dare confront Great Yan at all. He only wants to use Lan Xuan’er’s death to negotiate peace with Great Yan. He hopes that after Great Yan conquers Southern Yue, it will spare Nanzhao.]","Lan Xuancheng: Great Yan, once you’ve swallowed Southern Yue, you can’t eat me too, right?","“He... is rather clever! What a shame that all his efforts will be in vain!”","[Master, do you think he’ll end up like Gan Chengyuan, King of Cheng? Before he’s even had time to warm his seat on the throne, he’ll become the ruler of a fallen kingdom!]","“That’s true. But by then, their deaths will be recorded as deaths in office rather than ordinary deaths, and they’ll still have a page in the history books.”","Lan Xuancheng and Gan Chengyuan: If that’s the kind of place you’re offering us in the history books, you can keep it!","Suddenly, Cuizhu pointed down below and said to Yue Fuguang, “Miss, look! We’ve reached Feng City!”","Yue Fuguang had met up with the escort team in Xuzhou. Aside from Feng Tang, who remained with her, Dai Yuxing and Cuizhu had replaced the other two passengers in the carriage. The group then hurried all the way toward Feng City.","After eight consecutive days of rain, Feng City had become a vast expanse of water when viewed from above. The mountains outside the city were crowded with people, and even the high peaks were covered with refugees.","“Dad, when will the rain stop? I’m cold. I’m hungry!” A seven- or eight-year-old boy huddled in his thin father’s arms as the family gazed outside through the opening of a makeshift shelter.","“Soon. It’ll stop soon. Just hold on a little longer, Shanzai. When the rain stops, your mother will make you a nice hot meal.”","He pulled his son closer and didn’t forget to look toward his wife and little daughter, who were huddled farther inside.","“Wife, has our daughter’s fever gone down?” The only blanket they had brought with them had been given to their sick daughter.","They had assumed that, with the weather so hot, it wouldn’t be too cold even if it rained. Who could have imagined that the rain would grow more and more violent? The air was nothing but damp and cold.","Fortunately, they had brought a thin blanket up the mountain. It had been made only two years earlier, and his wife had been reluctant to ruin it, which was why they had brought it along. Now that their five-year-old daughter was sick, it had become her only protection against the cold.","“It’s gone down. Thankfully, you brought medicine up the mountain, or our daughter would have suffered terribly.” Their village had only one doctor, and no one knew where he was hiding from the rain now. Finding a doctor was simply impossible.","“Husband, do you think the rain will really be like the Divine Maiden said...?”","The woman’s face was full of worry. Beneath the dim shelter, she gazed sorrowfully at her sleeping daughter and the son clinging tightly to his father. The concern in her eyes quickly turned into tears, which fell drop by drop onto the damp earth beneath them."]},{"number":515,"title":"Chapter 515: This Is Spring Water","paragraphs":["The man looked toward the best spot in the small shack, where a little table stood with a statue of Yue Fuguang on it.","He gently nudged the son in his arms. \"Shanzai, come, it's time to offer incense to the Divine Maiden.\"","His family had only one able-bodied worker, and there wasn't much they could carry up the mountain. Besides food, the most precious things were the statue of the Divine Maiden and the incense and candles used to worship her.","\"Dad, this time Shanzai will pray hard to the Divine Maiden, so the rain outside will stop soon, and sister's illness will get better!\"","The man looked at his son's innocent face and patted his head. \"Good child! Dad believes the Divine Maiden will hear you.\"","At this moment, among those caught in the heavy rain, there were many, many people like the man and his family, devoutly offering incense and praying to Yue Fuguang, making wishes.","Because she was close by, she didn't even need to focus to hear the faint prayers of her believers.","[Host, has your power grown stronger again?] The system was green with envy.","They were both borrowing shells, so why could its host grow without limit, while it was bound hand and foot by those damn rules?","\"As you can see, I have indeed grown a little stronger lately.\" Yue Fuguang stepped out of the flying carriage, and lotuses bloomed beneath her feet. She walked leisurely through the raging storm, the lotuses underfoot shining like lamps in the dark night.","This light was quickly spotted by the common folk on the ground, who kept glancing at the sky.","No one knew who shouted first, \"Look, the Divine Maiden has come! The Divine Maiden has come to save us!\" The last words came out as a cracked shriek.","\"Divine Maiden, it really is the Divine Maiden!\"","\"Father, mother, come out quickly and see the Divine Maiden!\"","\"We beg the Divine Maiden to save us!\"","\"We beg the Divine Maiden to save us!\"","Many people rushed out of their hiding places in caves and shacks, heedless of the violent rain.","Yue Fuguang lifted her hand gently, and the sky, which had been howling with wind and pouring with rain, suddenly grew still. The sky was still dark, and the black clouds overhead had not dispersed, but the rain had indeed stopped, and the wind that had been bending trees had vanished without a trace.","\"We bow in gratitude to the Divine Maiden!\"","\"We bow in gratitude to the Divine Maiden!\"","The people of Feng City had originally thought they would have to plead with the Divine Maiden for a long time before she might take pity on them and let the deadly wind and rain stop.","They never expected that the moment the Divine Maiden appeared, the wind stopped and the rain ceased!","\"Rise, all of you!\" Yue Fuguang stood on the lotus platform, only a few hundred meters above the ground. The divine manifestation behind her filled nearly half the sky, visible to people within a hundred miles.","\"Since you are now subjects of Dayan, I will naturally look after you.\"","The people who had been kowtowing ceaselessly were stunned for a moment, then responded with a chorus of agreement. \"The Divine Maiden speaks truly! We are Dayan subjects, believers of the Divine Maiden!\"","\"Yes, yes, we are all Dayan subjects now, believers of the Divine Maiden!\"","\"Father, mother, are we now citizens of the same nation as the Divine Maiden?\"","An innocent little girl tugged at her parents' sleeves, her eyes curving into crescents with joy. Though her face was sallow, thin, and frail, her smile at that moment was bright and full of life.","Her mother nodded. \"That's right, little one. Our family is also citizens of the same nation as the noble Divine Maiden now!\"","Her father smiled too. \"From now on, we can serve the Divine Maiden without having to do it in secret anymore!\"","Such conversations were unfolding in many places. Yue Fuguang, standing on the lotus, heard them all clearly — not only from Feng City, but also from Wei City.","Her true body was in Feng City, but that didn't stop her divine manifestation from appearing in Wei City, two hundred miles away.","The people of Wei City saw the divine manifestation, saw the wind and rain cease the moment it appeared, and also heard the Divine Maiden officially confirm that they too were now citizens of Dayan.","Looking at the sea of kneeling citizens of Wei City, the Dayan officers on the city walls felt the stones in their hearts finally drop back into place.","\"Sir, now that the Junior Preceptor has appeared, we no longer need to worry about the people of Wei City and the surrounding areas rebelling because of the floods!\"","A man in his forties, wearing a blue robe, Cai Xin, the new prefect of Wei City, stroked his beard and smiled. \"General Qin is right. With the Junior Preceptor's single statement, the people of Wei City now identify themselves as Dayan subjects — that's more effective than my month of appeasement efforts!\"","If the Junior Preceptor hadn't appeared in time, and they had delayed any longer, the people of Wei City might have stormed the prefectural office.","He had received intelligence reports that someone was spreading rumors among the people, stirring up conflict between the citizens and the government.","\"Where are the prefect and all the officials?\"","Just as Cai Xin and Wei City's garrison commander Qin Guangyuan were speaking, Yue Fuguang's voice came again from the sky — this time summoning the Dayan officials.","Qin Guangyuan, Cai Xin, and all the other officials stepped forward the moment her words fell, bowing deeply toward the manifestation in the sky. \"Wei City Prefect Cai Xin greets the Junior Preceptor!\"","\"Wei City Garrison Commander Qin Guangyuan greets the Junior Preceptor!\"","\"Wei City...\"","\"Feng City...\"","The common folk called Yue Fuguang the Divine Maiden, but the Dayan officials habitually addressed her as the Junior Preceptor, because it seemed more intimate, marking their relationship as something special.","Yue Fuguang nodded. \"The court's disaster relief grain is already on its way and should arrive in two or three days.","You must ensure that this life-saving grain is used for the people!\"","Hearing that relief grain was coming, the people within the range of both cities wept with joy, prostrating themselves on the ground. They truly had hope now!","It was good to be Dayan subjects — drought brought the Divine Maiden, torrential rain brought the Divine Maiden, and now food shortages were also on the court's mind!","They were finally being treated as human beings, not ignored like weeds.","Her brows lowered slightly, her expression appearing deeply compassionate. \"If any wrongdoing occurs, regardless of who is involved, you should keep a bodhisattva's heart but act with thunderous measures.\"","The crowd was startled for a moment, then shouted in unison, \"Yes! We will follow your orders, act with integrity, and faithfully protect the people of this land!\"","Among the people, some eyes flickered nervously, while others shouted praise with excitement. At this moment, their hearts truly settled.","Yue Fuguang's gaze swept over the gaunt, sallow-faced people, passed over the forests, and finally landed on the flood-damaged river embankment in the distance. There, torrents of floodwater raged, and all kinds of debris floated to the surface.","\"The flood has submerged fertile fields and drowned countless livestock and wild animals. After a great disaster, one must guard against a great epidemic! You must clean up all corpses as soon as possible.","Strictly follow the Dayan epidemic prevention guidelines in everything, and make sure to educate the people thoroughly!\"","Hearing about disease, both officials and civilians felt a chill of dread. All their joy in that moment turned into fear and worry about epidemics.","Yue Fuguang waved her wide sleeve, and countless petal-sized flowers drifted down from the sky. \"Mother, look, how beautiful!\"","\"The Divine Maiden sent me flowers!\"","\"A rain of petals?\"","The young girls who reached out to catch the petals quickly discovered that what lay in their palms was not petals at all, but drops of clear water — droplets rolling in their hands, tinged with a faint green hue.","\"This is Spring Water. It strengthens the body and improves health, and will help you get through this calamity.\""]},{"number":516,"title":"Chapter 516: When will the Dayan Army reach our area","paragraphs":["Upon hearing that it could strengthen the body and improve health, the men who had been maintaining their reserve sprang into action immediately. Fortunately, there was no woman who didn't love beauty—even the older women had been captivated by the drifting petals, unable to resist catching a few themselves.","Otherwise, they wouldn't have stood a chance against the men.","\"You hag, give me what you've got in your hands!\"","The petal rain stopped quickly. Some had caught more, some fewer, and so the greedy ones couldn't help but reach out toward their own daughters and wives.","\"Third daughter-in-law, you and that good-for-nothing girl of yours don't deserve something this fine. Hand it over so my son and grandsons can enjoy it!\"","\"Girl, you've got no use for this. Give it to your older brother and younger brother!\"","\"Eldest, your younger brother needs his wits about him for his studies. Give him your family's share—once he makes something of himself, he won't forget his big brother and sister-in-law.\"","\"You're the eldest son, so it's only right that you yield to your younger siblings. A brother who is eldest is like a father...\"","Yue Fuguang's ears were filled with all kinds of discordant voices. The corner of her mouth curled into a sneer. See—this was precisely why she hadn't simply sent down spiritual rain directly.","Because some people simply didn't deserve to have anything of hers!","\"Greedy!\"","\"Noisy!\"","Once all the ugliness had been laid bare, Yue Fuguang acted without hesitation. She raised her hand and swept it downward, and the beads in some people's hands suddenly flew up into the air and burst apart.","The Divine Maiden's sacred form radiated an unspoken authority. She lifted her eyes lightly, and those with guilty consciences all felt that the Divine Maiden was looking straight at them.","But her gaze no longer held compassion—it was as if she were looking down at a swarm of ants.","\"Divine Maiden, forgive me! This humble one was wrong!\"","\"Divine Maiden, spare me! This old man dares not do it again!\"","\"Divine Maiden, be merciful! This old woman knows she has sinned!\"","Those who had tried to steal and lost everything throwe themselves to the ground, their heads knocking against the earth with heavy thuds. Moments before, with such treasures before them, they had instinctively revealed their true natures, momentarily forgetting that the Divine Maiden was still watching from above.","If only they had held back, waited until the Divine Maiden had left...","Yue Fuguang let them knock their heads bloody, but she did not send down another thing. They knew they were wrong?","A leopard cannot change its spots. Even wearing the skin of the Divine Maiden, she could not instantly alter their dispositions.","The evil in human nature—it was not something that disappeared so easily!","Ignoring the crowd below, whose joys and sorrows were worlds apart, Yue Fuguang formed hand seals. The cloud-riding technique she had practiced for days was executed so swiftly that her fingers blurred into afterimages.","The darkened sky began to show light. The crowd looked up and saw the heavy black clouds overhead slowly shifting, drifting off into the distance. At last, a sliver of sunlight broke through behind the clouds.","\"Is the Divine Maiden moving the rain clouds away?\"","They wouldn't get rain overhead for a while, but that didn't mean the rain was gone for good. As long as the clouds lingered, the rain couldn't escape.","But now—the clouds were being moved by the Divine Maiden, and they no longer had to worry about more rain!","\"Mother, the Divine Maiden is so amazing!\"","\"Mother, does this mean we'll have hot water to drink soon?\"","\"Mother, I want porridge!\"","They watched as the sky grew brighter and brighter, sunlight spilling down, slowly warming the land.","Yue Fuguang, the cloud-wrangler, did not return to the carriage. Instead, she moved as if walking on wind, guiding the rain clouds rapidly toward the direction of Dayan.","Inside the flying carriage, Dai Yuxing had witnessed the entire scene. His mouth had been hanging open in shock the whole time.","With stars in his eyes as he gazed at Yue Fuguang's distant figure, \"This is our lady for you—solves every problem the moment she makes a move!\"","Moreover, since she had begun managing the drought, the lady no longer seemed to hide her abilities deliberately.","One display of divine power after another, without even bothering to come up with excuses.","\"Of course—the lady is the Divine Maiden descended to earth, capable of anything!\" Cuizhu's admiration for Yue Fuguang was even more unshakable than Dai Yuxing's.","Feng Tang waved his hand against the wind. \"For this world to have encountered our lady is fortune for Dayan, fortune for all its people!\"","As he spoke, Feng Tang began to recite again: \"Scorched earth stretching a thousand li, blazing sun like fire, wells dry and smoke rising. The Divine Maiden lowers her gaze from the azure heavens. Her fair hands part the clouded valleys, soft thunder bears the rain along. Ten thousand acres of withered seedlings regain their green, streams swell full overnight. Village elders lean on canes and speak of her grace. May the mountains and rivers live long, ever guarding the jade-bright court.\"","The moment he finished, Dai Yuxing chimed in: \"The sky like a boiling cauldron, grain about to turn to ash. Suddenly the Divine Maiden strikes her thunder drums, the downpour quenches the summer's torment. Grace poured upon countless beings, green returns to the southern shores. From this day, temple halls welcome new swallows, incense smoke rises morning and dusk.\"","Yue Fuguang, who had overheard their conversation and the verses those literati had written to sing her praises, felt the lotus petals beneath her feet involuntarily curl closed a little!","And so it went, time and again. Yue Fuguang moved rain clouds from Weicheng, Fengcheng, Yucheng, Jialing City, and Suicheng, one after another, into Dayan's territory.","The unending rainfall finally alleviated Dayan's drought and also put an end to the flooding in the five newly conquered cities.","This news spread like it had grown wings, reaching the ears of every nation.","The first to learn of it was, of course, Yecheng, which lay only a hundred li from Suicheng.","\"Scholar Zhang, you're telling the truth? The rain in Suicheng has really stopped?\"","An old man stood on a mountaintop, tears in his eyes, gazing down at the direction of his village—the house he had spent most of his life building, and his few meager plots of land, all destroyed by the endless downpour.","Scholar Zhang looked at the old man before him, then at his own parents, who wore similar expressions. \"Uncle, according to my schoolmate, it's not just Suicheng—even Yucheng and Jialing City nearby, everywhere Dayan has taken over, the rain has stopped!\"","The old man stopped looking at the fields below and turned to fix his gaze on Scholar Zhang, who looked barely past twenty. \"Are you saying that as long as Dayan takes over, the rain stops?\"","\"Uncle, it's not that the rain stops just because Dayan took over.\" Scholar Zhang's face stiffened, then he paused before nodding firmly. \"It's the Divine Maiden—she moved all the rain away! She said that since they are all now people of Dayan, the Divine Maiden would look after them!\"","That last line was the Divine Maiden's exact words—he wasn't making anything up!","\"Well then...\" Old Man Zhang looked around in every direction. He wanted to ask when this land of theirs would finally fall into Dayan's hands.","But when he looked, he was taken aback—the mountaintop, which had been nearly empty just moments ago, was now packed with people. Not just from their village, but from the neighboring ones too.","Why weren't they all staying inside to avoid the rain? Why had they all come up here?","Daqing Mountain was indeed the tallest in the area, but the fact that they'd all braved the rain to come here was something Old Man Zhang hadn't expected. The words caught in his throat.","\"Scholar Zhang—when do we get to become people of Dayan?\" A young man blurted out the question on everyone's mind without a care. He was young and bold, without the caution of his elders—he just wanted this damned rain to stop.","Seeing someone break the ice, the others decided there was no point in holding back. A buzz of discussion erupted:","\"Yeah, Scholar Zhang, you've read so much and seen the world. Tell us—when will our land end up in Dayan's hands like neighboring Suicheng?\"","\"When will the Dayan army reach us?\"","\"That won't be easy—the roads are flooded everywhere. They'll have a hard time getting here.\"","\"Ugh! This wretched rain is just getting in the way of everything!\""]},{"number":517,"title":"Chapter 517: Do you think its host would mind if they found out about it","paragraphs":["Scholar Zhang said, \"If I knew when the Dayan Army was coming, would I still be standing here waiting?\"","\"The defender of Ye City is the new emperor's confidant, so he'll definitely defend the city to the death.\" Staring at the vast expanse of water, he still couldn't help sharing the rumors he'd heard with the villagers.","\"Uncles and elders, if it weren't for this rain, we might all have been dragged off to defend the city walls!\"","\"Making us take swords and blades for them? Damn them!\"","\"If they try to drag me into defending the city, the moment I see the Dayan Army, I won't even wait for them to attack — I'll open the gates myself!\" A young man proclaimed his brilliant idea with smug pride.","The brothers around him nodded in agreement one after another. \"Old Seven's right, that's exactly what we should do!\"","Smack!","Old Seven Zhang's head was knocked sideways by his father's palm. \"Always so clever, aren't you? Opening the city gates for the Dayan Army — you tired of living?\"","\"Yeah, swords and arrows have no eyes. The first thing the military inspector does is execute anyone who turns coat.\"","The fathers began scolding their impulsive sons one by one, until Scholar Zhang said, \"According to my old classmate, the common folk in those captured cities have already started receiving relief grain shipped in by Dayan.\"","One sentence from Scholar Zhang silenced every father who had been lecturing his son. Seeing everyone staring at him wide-eyed, he felt he hadn't gone far enough, so he threw more fuel on the fire: \"I hear it's distributed by full measure, not a grain short — even babies still nursing get their ration.\"","\"Scholar Liu, are you telling the truth?\"","\"How could it be false? My classmate has family living in Sui City.\"","Old Seven's father traded the slap for a pat, smoothing out his son's wrinkled clothes with tender care. \"Old Seven's right! If they really try to make us defend the city, the moment we see the Dayan Army, we open the gates!\"","Over in Zhang Family Village, they were only talking — but somewhere else, people were already planning to actually do it.","\"Chief, we'll follow whatever you say. Tell us what to do and we'll do it!\"","\"That's right, Chief, we're all with you! My youngest son's been sick for days. Because of this cursed rain, the medicine for him got soaked through, and he just isn't getting better!\"","\"My little girl hasn't had a full meal in days. We're just waiting to become Dayan citizens and get the relief rations!\"","In a small duty room among Ye City's garrison troops, a squad of soldiers huddled together, whispering among themselves. The topic was simple: they were waiting for the Dayan Army to arrive so that those responsible for guarding the city could quietly open the gates and let the Dayan forces in.","For these common soldiers — who barely had a meal today, whose families didn't even have that — surrendering carried not a shred of guilt.","The Dayan Army didn't loot when entering a city, and they didn't kill those who surrendered. These facts had already been proven by the five cities that fell before.","It was from this point onward that Yue Fuguang's strict discipline codes for the Dayan Army's city entries began to bear fruit.","The defenders of Ye City were waiting for the Dayan Army to besiege the city so they could open the gates and welcome the righteous army. In the other cities, both military morale and civilian spirit were shattered as word spread of the Divine Maiden's descent, the ceaseless rain finally stopping, the Dayan Army's arrival, and the delivery of disaster relief grain.","Southern Yue was like this, and Southern Zhao — whose empress had just died — was no different. In the towns and villages surrounding Flower City, which was closest to Southern Zhao, refugees crossing the border from Southern Zhao could be seen almost every day.","Yue Fuguang watched the rain clouds beneath her feet turn to water and fall across the lands of Lian Province and He Province. Yet on the other side of the river, Northern Li, and beyond the mountain, Western Qiang, were so dry that a single spark might set the whole country ablaze.","「System, Northern Li and Western Qiang have already started falling into chaos internally. Do you think they'll lash out and try to shift their internal conflicts outward?」 What could be more inciting than launching a war and invading a country that had water and food?","【Host, haven't you noticed that both countries are reinforcing their border garrisons? According to the intelligence I've received, they're planning to take advantage of Dayan's focus on the war with Southern Yue to launch a sneak attack on Lian and He Provinces.】","「Do the emperor and his ministers already know?」","【Zheng Feng's spies caught wind of their movements early on. The Dayan Army is also secretly mobilizing. When the great battle comes, the Three Forks region will bear the brunt of it!】","「We saw this coming, didn't we? Thank heavens the Ministry of Works has been reliable — gunpowder supplies are sufficient. If soldiers from those two countries dare cross the border, they'll get a taste of what black powder can do!」","Dayan was taking on three kingdoms at once. Without the great equalizer of gunpowder, things would indeed be precarious — the soldiers of those three nations were no pushovers.","Before Yue Fuguang arrived, the fighting strength of Northern Li and Western Qiang had actually been slightly superior to Dayan's.","Just then, the system began a bout of left-brain-versus-right-brain combat — or rather, a data collision between the Gossip System and the Merit System.","【Host, won't this be too much bloodshed?】 This time, the Merit System had the upper hand.","「System, didn't you say that as long as we're completing the mission and the main system verifies it, the karmic consequences won't be counted against us?」","【That's true, but we Merit System hosts usually don't kill more than double digits during missions. You, though — you're talking about killing tens of thousands. Isn't that too many?】","「Then aren't the people I saved even more? Hundreds of thousands, millions — how do you count those?」 Yue Fuguang planted her hands on her hips and lifted her chin. 「Besides, it's not like I did the killing myself. I just provided a bit of technology. It's like a blacksmith forging a blade. If someone takes that blade and kills a man with it, can you blame the blacksmith? No matter how you argue it, there's no logic in that!」","【Right, the host is correct. No matter how you argue it, we have right on our side!】 This time, the Gossip System had beaten the Merit System.","The system seemed to have been poisoned, slapping its own face and immediately switching sides, flipping its stance so fast that Yue Fuguang was momentarily dazed. 「What the heck? System, whose side are you on anyway?」","【I... I'm obviously on the host's side!】","「System, be honest — are you infected with a virus or something? If you're sick, we can spend some points to fix you right away! Don't let a small problem turn into a big one.」","「You systems have doctors, right? Super programmers?」","【Host, I'm not sick. Just now... just now I lost the fight and let the Merit System take the upper hand!】","「Aren't you the Merit System?」","Could her system be developing a split personality, just like a human? Or was it because of the dual-core single-body design? Could it be that she'd used the Gossip System so much that the system's data had inevitably crashed?","「System, whatever you do, don't crash! We're almost there — just two more years and we'll make it!」","【Host, don't worry, I'm never going to crash!】","In the system space, the system had curled itself into a little ball. After hesitating for a long time, it decided to come clean about the tiny bit of information it had learned.","【Host, I have a system friend. It ran into a little problem and doesn't know whether to tell its host.】","Yue Fuguang narrowed her eyes, then took a casual sip of tea and a bite of pastry, responding in a relaxed tone, 「What kind of problem? Let's hear it. It's been a while since I had some good gossip. We can just take it as entertainment.」","The system felt that its host hadn't caught on to its little scheme, so it boldly continued, 【Host, suppose — just suppose — my friend is like you right now, living through a borrowed shell. Do you think its host would be disgusted by it if they found out?】"]},{"number":518,"title":"Chapter 518: Have These Two Brothers Joined Forces","paragraphs":["“Use someone else’s shell, just like me?”","【Yes!】","“My case is legal. I signed a contract with the System Group! Is its situation legal?”","【That...】","Yue Fuguang’s heart sank. She thought bitterly, I’m still so young, yet I’ve already had to experience death and be reborn once. Now I even have to worry about being scammed by my system.","What on earth had she done in her previous lives to deserve this?","The hand holding her teacup trembled almost imperceptibly, but she continued asking in a casual tone, “Let’s put that aside for now. Is the task contract it signed with its host legal?","“Is its host-tasker status legitimate and compliant? Were its tasks authorized by the Main System?”","【There definitely shouldn’t be any problems with those. The system my friend recently moved into was legally manufactured and compliant. Only a small portion of its data was edited into that system.","“Although it found the host itself, the employment contract was signed with the Main System, and the tasks were issued by the Main System.”】","In the end, the system concluded firmly, 【Everything is reasonable, compliant, and legal!】 Except for the system itself.","Only then did Yue Fuguang’s worried heart finally settle. As for that small portion of data, it was probably the Gossip System.","The system had seemed perfectly normal before. Yue Fuguang had even suspected at one point that it possessed some extraordinary identity, especially since the Main System treated it rather differently.","It had only started acting strangely in the past few months. Could it really be related to absorbing too much incense power and repairing its data too quickly?","“Since that’s the case, the problem shouldn’t be too serious, right?” At least there shouldn’t be much of a problem with her status as a tasker.","【Not too serious?】 Most of the Gossip System’s functions had been locked. It couldn’t recover as it had expected—not even to seventy or eighty percent of its original state.","“There’s something else. Seventh, you said your friend borrowed a shell like I did. But I only took over this body after its original owner had completely died.","“What happened to the system whose shell your friend borrowed?”","The Gossip System had occupied the Merit System, but what had happened to the original Merit System? These systems were intelligent systems with thoughts and consciousness of their own. From Yue Fuguang’s perspective, systems were practically half-human.","【Host, systems like us are different from humans. In the beginning, we’re all controlled by our data cores. My friend has completely fused with the original system core.】","“Completely fused? So they’ve become one? Then what is it afraid of? Can the Main System discover that something is different?”","Her understanding was that the two sets of data had devoured each other and become one entity, with the Gossip System’s data merely occupying the dominant consciousness.","【That... It isn’t entirely sure either. But my friend has only just begun to slowly remember some of the original system’s affairs. Because its share of the data was too small at the beginning of the fusion, it was in a state of complete amnesia, much like a human being reincarnated!】","I see, Yue Fuguang thought, now that she understood the situation.","Her system couldn’t exactly be considered completely illegal. It was merely... not entirely legal.","“If the Main System discovers a situation like this, what will happen?”","【Uh... Maybe, possibly, it’ll be sent back to the factory and reformatted?】 Still, the system had a feeling that, in this case, the Main System hadn’t remained completely unaware.","After all, how had such a small amount of Gossip data managed to survive within the vast sea of data, then successfully fuse with the data of a newly created system? Although its functions had been suppressed, it was obvious that its control over the data had taken the dominant position.","This system’s thoughts and actions were still primarily guided by it.","“Since that’s the case, my advice is for your friend to keep itself hidden and avoid letting the Main System discover any clues.","“As for its host, it’s best not to tell her for now.”","【Why?】","“Have you never heard that the more you know, the more dangerous it is? Even if the Main System discovers everything one day, an uninformed tasker cannot be accused of covering anything up. Keeping her in the dark is also a way of protecting her.","“Since her identity is legitimate, she only needs to focus on completing her tasks. There’s no need to say anything until all of you have grown stronger.”","At the very least, they should wait until she had rebuilt her own body. If things went wrong then, she could still run.","It seemed that she would have to complete this world’s tasks as perfectly as possible. The higher the task rating, the more generous the points would be.","【That makes sense. Then I’ll... I’ll go talk to my friend!】","The system left, then returned again. Only a few minutes had passed. Clearly, it had put on an act, but not entirely committed to it.","【Master, I have some fresh gossip for you.】","Hearing that the system was ready to get to work, Yue Fuguang immediately perked up. “What is it? Hurry up and tell me.”","【Master, do you remember Chancellor Wei? Wei Qingyi’s father.】","“Of course I remember him. What happened?”","【Have you forgotten? Chancellor Wei’s beloved from his youth was the Empress of Nanzhao. Now that the Empress is dead, the old man learned of the news and is making a fuss about going to Nanzhao to pay his respects.】","“Pay his respects? Leaving aside whether he can even get there with the heavy rains and flooding in Nanzhao, even if he does make it, aren’t the Empress’s funeral rites being kept as simple as possible?","“By the time he arrives, the Empress will have been buried long ago.”","Wei Qingyi’s mother seemed to still be alive. If the old man pulled a stunt like this, where would that leave his legitimate wife’s dignity?","“Besides, would that old Emperor of Northern Ji agree?”","【Of course he wouldn’t. He’s jealous! The army originally assembled at the border was supposed to be commanded by members of the Zhuang family. But now, because Chancellor Wei wanted to go see his beloved from the past, Northern Ji’s emperor became so furious that he temporarily replaced the commanding general with Wei Qingyi.","“With a battle about to break out at the front, Chancellor Wei doesn’t dare leave now—not with his son’s life at stake.】","“Wei Qingyi? Wasn’t he a civil official? Why would they put him in command? Does Northern Li have a tradition of sending civil officials to lead armies as well?”","Northern Li was clearly determined to bring about its own destruction.","It wasn’t that civil officials could never command troops. The problem was that civil officials with the talent to serve as true military commanders were exceedingly rare.","【He is indeed a civil official, but the Wei family was once involved in the military as well. After Northern Ji’s emperor came to power, their influence gradually withdrew from the armed forces, but their connections remained. Wei Qingyi himself is quite capable, so there’s no problem with him taking command.】","“How many troops does Wei Qingyi have under his control?”","【A force of one hundred and fifty thousand!】","“Does Bei Ye know that his old flame has become the commander of an army?”","【That’s precisely what I wanted to tell you. Bei Ye has already received the news and has secretly left the capital, heading for the border between the two countries.】","“He found out quickly. It seems he planted quite a few people in Northern Li. And what does ‘secretly’ mean? Northern Ji didn’t stop him or Beiyue from returning home. Why does he need to sneak back into his own country?”","【Master, guess why he’s doing that!】","“He’s planning something? Is it for the one hundred and fifty thousand troops under Wei Qingyi’s command?”","【Correct! That was also the result of a discussion he and Beiyue had throughout the night. Bei Ye is secretly returning to Northern Li. He plans to find a way to stay by Wei Qingyi’s side and seize control of the army when the opportunity arises.】","“The two brothers have joined forces?”"]},{"number":519,"title":"Chapter 519: Did the defenders of Yecheng open the city gates and surrender","paragraphs":["【They had joined forces long ago. Their common enemies were their own father and younger brother. The two cannon-fodder characters wanted to save themselves, so naturally they had to work together.","Bei Ye was responsible for dealing with Wei Qingyi, while Beiyue remained in Dayan to cover for him and create the illusion that Bei Ye was still there.】","「Does Emperor Mingxi and the Director of the Court of State Ceremonies, You Mingmin, know that Bei Ye has fled?」","【Of course they do. They even secretly sent people to escort him the entire way, making absolutely sure he reached the border safely!】","Yue Fuguang rubbed her chin. So the emperor and his ministers also wanted to use this opportunity to stir things up!","「I just don’t know whether Wei Qingyi’s feelings for Bei Ye will be enough to make him hand over the military power he holds.","After all, the favored consort is his maternal aunt, and the emperor’s chosen heir is his cousin.」","【The master probably doesn’t know this yet, but she has already been made Imperial Noble Consort Rong, practically the empress in all but name.】","「What... Bei Ji isn’t hiding them anymore?」","【He wanted to, but over the past year, the mother and son have suffered so many covert attacks that they can’t even count them all on both hands. If he hadn’t given them enough guards, the two of them would have been dead long ago.】","「Were those attacks carried out by Beiyue or Bei Ye?」","【Both of them took part. And it wasn’t only the two of them. Every prince who harbored even the slightest ambition for the throne got involved.","That’s also why, even though Bei Ji knew who was responsible, he didn’t punish anyone.】","「He’s letting them off because there are too many offenders? When did he become so protective of his other sons?」 He either treated them as cannon fodder and set them up as targets, or watched indifferently while his sons were poisoned.","【He has so many sons that losing one or two wouldn’t matter. But when seven or eight of them all got involved, he couldn’t bear to sacrifice the others just for the sake of one.","So Bei Ji decided to stop hiding them. He brought the mother and son into the open in order to protect them and build up their faction.】","「Build up their faction? If the Eighth Prince and Imperial Noble Consort Rong truly gain power, Bei Ji himself should be the first person unable to sit still!」","【The master is right. Others may not know it, but Chancellor Wei certainly thinks so. That’s why, even now, he remains unmoved by the “overtures” from Imperial Noble Consort Rong and her son. To outsiders, he appears to be a staunch supporter of the emperor!】","「What an old fox! The question is whether Bei Ji believes him.」","【One is the genuine article, and the other is a counterfeit. When facing the two of them, his intelligence is bound to drop a little. But no secret can remain hidden forever. Perhaps Bei Ji will learn the truth through some other channel.】","The system glanced outside the carriage. It seemed to remember that Zheng Zicheng’s spies had already sent someone close to Bei Ji.","「Little Zhu, if Bei Ji learns the truth, do you think he’ll move against the Wei family? And in the end, who will the fifteen hundred thousand troops under Wei Qingyi’s command obey?」","The Wei family, the mother and son, Bei Ji, and Bei Ye—all of them were locked in a contest of schemes and power. In the end, it would be best if they all suffered losses. That way, Dayan could reap the benefits.","While Yue Fuguang was discussing the affairs of Beili, far away in the capital, the emperor and his ministers were also making detailed plans as they studied a vast map showing the directions of Beili and Xiqiang.","“Lord Zheng, where has that boy Bei Ye reached?” Emperor Mingxi’s gaze wandered back and forth over the enormous map hanging on the wall. His mouth asked about Bei Ye’s itinerary, but his eyes were fixed on the movements of Yue Fuguang that Qian Gui had reported to him an hour earlier.","His eyes settled on the border between Lian and He Prefectures. Fuguang must have sensed that a great battle was approaching and was worried about the Yue army stationed at Sancha.","He had originally not intended to send the Yue army into the vanguard, but Feng Tang had relayed Fuguang’s rejection of that arrangement.","She had said that young soldiers yearned for military achievements. They had sweated through countless days for this very moment—to distinguish themselves, earn noble titles, and prepare themselves for positions of power. No one had the right to stand in their way.","Zheng Zicheng stepped forward and bowed. “Your Majesty, according to the information this subject received yesterday, Bei Ye has already reached Wanqian County in He Prefecture.” That was already the territory granted to the Grand Preceptor.","Emperor Mingxi lightly tapped Wanqian County twice with his finger before ordering Zheng Zicheng, “Tell your people that once they confirm Bei Ye has entered Wei Qingyi’s military camp, the men planted beside Bei Ji may make their move.”","Zheng Zicheng nodded solemnly. “Yes, Your Majesty. Bei Ye is expected to reach the border in three days. We will take action five days from now.”","Emperor Mingxi nodded. “Make sure everything is done cleanly. Leave no trace connecting us to it!” Bei Ji was an old fox and would not be easy to deceive.","Fortunately, all the information they had released was true. If Bei Ji truly put his mind to investigating, he would definitely be able to uncover traces of Chancellor Wei’s contact with Imperial Noble Consort Rong.","“Lord Huo, how much longer do you estimate the war in Nanyue will last?”","“Your Majesty, I have just received a battle report from the front. Our army has already captured Ye City. Once we take Suiye City, we can concentrate our forces and seize Gan City.","“However, the heavy rains in Nanyue will slow the army’s movements.”","“So at the earliest, it will still take another three or four months to conquer all of Nanyue.” By the time the new year arrived, Dayan would certainly have complete control over Nanyue’s territory.","Emperor Mingxi accepted the latest victory report from Huo Ying and quickly read through it. His expression became exceptionally vivid as he fought back a smile. He casually passed the letter to the Crown Prince, Huo Ying, and several other important ministers for them to read.","“Minister Huo, is this really true? It says that the defenders of Ye City opened the gates and surrendered?” Cai Xian looked utterly incredulous after reading the letter.","He finally understood why the emperor had worn that expression moments earlier!","“This... This is simply unbelievable. Ye City is separated from Gan City by only Suiye City. The emperor’s control over the area couldn’t possibly be weak, and yet they actually opened the gates and surrendered!”","Wei Ping was just as excited as Cai Xian.","Zhang Zhongping couldn’t help speculating, “Could those people have been struck stupid by the rain? Perhaps they were so soaked that they mistook our army for Nanyue’s?”","Before Huo Ying could answer, Zheng Zicheng gave a mysterious smile and took up the explanation himself. “I happen to know a little about the answer to your questions, gentlemen.”","Wei Ping was the most impatient of them all. “Lord Zheng, stop keeping us in suspense. Hurry up and tell His Majesty and the rest of us.”","Since Wei Ping had even invoked the emperor, Zheng Zicheng no longer delayed. “According to my men, the squad guarding Ye City’s gates initially opened them on the pretext that the army attacking the city was a relief force sent by the Nanyue court to provide disaster aid!”","Cai Xian’s eyes widened. “Are you saying, Lord Zheng, that those soldiers guarding the city actually knew our Dayan army had arrived?”"]},{"number":520,"title":"Chapter 520: If Only You'd Made a Bar Chart or a Pie Chart","paragraphs":["Zheng Zicheng stole a glance at Emperor Mingxi, who was listening intently with his ears practically perked up, then nodded firmly. “My men were hidden nearby and saw everything clearly. They knew that the army arriving was indeed our Dayan army.”","“How could a few city guards have pulled this off?” Zhang Shangshu still found it hard to believe.","Zheng Zicheng shook his head with a smile. “Minister Zhang, it wasn’t just a few. Of the hundred or so men stationed on the walls at the time, along with the city defense troops below, more than half already knew what was going on.”","Minister of Revenue Dong Qianli gripped the victory report and looked at Huo Ying and Zheng Zicheng. “Although our army has never suffered a defeat wherever it has gone, its reputation has spread far and wide, and the might of gunpowder has shaken the Five Nations, surely there must be more to this bloodless surrender?”","He had seen the situation clearly. Although the Nan Yue army had resisted after opening the city gates, the casualties among their soldiers had been the lowest since the war began.","They had taken a major city of an enemy state in a single day. Who would believe that if they told the story?","Zheng Zicheng smiled confidently. “Minister Dong, have you forgotten that one of the matters keeping your ministry busy lately has been sending disaster relief grain to several cities in Nan Yue?”","Dong Qianli nodded. “Of course not. That request came from the Grand Mentor herself.”","Their Ministry of Revenue had been busy for nearly half a month. The relief grain had already been on its way before the heavy rains began in Nan Yue.","“Those Nan Yue soldiers are human too. They need food, and they have families at home who are starving!”","“Are you saying they surrendered because of the relief grain, Minister Zheng?”","“Not entirely. More of them were moved by the Grand Mentor’s rainmaking in Feng City and other places, as well as her having diverted the heavy rains elsewhere.","“They are all believers in the Divine Maiden. They heard her say that they, too, were people of Dayan. Because of that, the Divine Maiden would offer them some protection.”","Everyone present, Emperor Mingxi included, nodded in unison. “That makes sense!”","“Yes, I knew there couldn’t be such a good thing without a reason. It turns out they were doing it for our Grand Mentor’s sake!”","“Elder Yu, has the Grand Mentor said when she will return to the capital?”","Ling Yinghua nodded repeatedly as well. “Indeed, Minister Yu. With the Grand Mentor away from the capital, I can never settle down. I can’t eat or sleep properly!”","Emperor Mingxi nodded furiously inwardly. He suffered from the same affliction as Minister Li. If not for the calming incense Fuguang had given him, he probably wouldn’t have managed a single night of sound sleep.","“Fuguang’s dispatch two days ago said that she should be returning to the capital within the next three to five days.”","The next time the girl went out, she would have a flying carriage, so there would be no need for the army to accompany her as an escort.","Emperor Mingxi’s eyes lit up at once. He leaned forward, barely able to contain himself. “Minister Yu, is Fuguang returning with the escort force this time, or will she come back ahead of them?”","Everyone’s hearts stirred at the question, and all eyes turned in unison to the three members of the Yu family.","There was a world of difference between returning with the guards and returning alone.","Yu Chongshan bowed. “Your Majesty, judging by what Fuguang said, she should be returning ahead of them. In the future, she may not need the army to accompany her when she travels.”","When Emperor Mingxi heard that Yue Fuguang would be returning ahead of the others, his eyes narrowed into a delighted smile. Xie Zhiyan’s gaze shifted, and he naturally understood exactly what his imperial father was so happy about.","Everyone present wore a grin from ear to ear for the same reason: the Divine Maiden’s flying carriage!","They had only heard reports from every region, making them the last people to see it in person. How could they not be curious?","Take the memorial submitted by Huang Xie, the prefect of Yingchuan. It was more than two thousand characters long, and two thousand of those characters were devoted to describing the flying carriage, the flying horses, and the Grand Mentor’s impressive bearing.","In the apology memorial submitted by Deputy Prefect Zhou of Flower City, he had used a five-thousand-character essay to give a detailed account of the Grand Mentor descending upon Flower City in her flying carriage, as well as the scene that night when she punished the commoners who had abused private justice.","There wasn’t a single person at court who didn’t want to see it for themselves.","“Where should we go to welcome Little Aunt when she returns to the capital?” Emperor Mingxi gave his eldest son an approving look when he heard the question.","That was exactly what he wanted to ask as well. The Grand Mentor had worked for the nation and its people; as emperor, he should naturally leave the city to welcome her and demonstrate his respect.","Yu Chongshan’s expression grew troubled. “Your Majesty and Your Highness know that Fuguang will be returning in the flying carriage. She can enter the city directly, so there should be no need to—”","“No, no, no! The Grand Mentor’s return to the capital is a momentous occasion. We must leave the city to welcome her with due ceremony!”","Emperor Mingxi shook his head like a rattle. Without even thinking, he knew that with Fuguang’s temperament, she was very likely to land her flying carriage directly at the Yu residence’s Brightmoon Pavilion. If that happened, he, the emperor, might not even get to see her.","Quite apart from how unwilling he was to miss the chance to see the flying carriage, if the Divine Maiden returned and the imperial court made no gesture at all, the common people and officials would surely find out. He wouldn’t even need the censors to impeach him for failing to reward a meritorious subject or show respect to the Divine Maiden. Those eager to curry favor would be the first to drown him in abuse.","In a single day, the common people could curse away all the popular support he had worked so hard to build and turn him into a foolish ruler.","Emperor Mingxi continued shaking his head. He truly could not afford that!","Seeing the emperor’s expression, the sweat on Yu Chongshan’s forehead nearly began to pour. He sighed inwardly and ventured, “How about I ask Fuguang what she thinks?”","If his granddaughter genuinely refused to cooperate with His Majesty’s performance, they could hardly force her, could they?","Emperor Mingxi gave a reserved nod, while Xie Zhiyan smiled obediently. “Thank you for your trouble, Elder Yu.”","Yu Chongshan hurriedly said that it was no trouble at all.","“All right. Now that Fuguang’s matter has been settled, let’s discuss how we should fight this war against Northern Li and Western Qiang.”","“And as for the commanders, does anyone have suitable candidates?”","[Host, another dispatch has arrived from the Yu residence? What does it say? Is it related to the war?]","The system had become incredibly lazy lately. It could have processed the data and found the answer itself, yet it insisted on asking Yue Fuguang.","“Grandfather says the emperor wants to leave the city and welcome us just like last time.”","[He’s putting on another show! What do you think, host? Are you going to play along with him?]","“It wouldn’t hurt.”","[Huh? Host, have you changed your temperament? This isn’t like you at all... Wait, there must be something in it for you, right?]","“System, haven’t you noticed that you’ve been getting rather lazy lately? You don’t even analyze the data anymore. If you had made a bar chart or a pie chart, you would have been able to see the pattern in the growth. Every time I make an appearance, that’s when the incense-and-faith points increase the fastest.”","Yue Fuguang rolled her eyes. “If you’d so much as made a bar chart or a pie chart, you would have been able to see the pattern in the growth.”"]},{"number":521,"title":"Chapter 521: These Little Bastards Have Only Just Had a Few Decent Meals","paragraphs":["The System was trying to recall the past. Afraid of being discovered by the Main System, it refused to alter any data unless the mission required it, hoping to coast all the way to victory.","【So the reason you like appearing in public so much isn’t to show off, but to gather incense offerings and faith?】","Yue Fuguang’s old face flushed at the System’s use of “show off.” She coughed twice, then asked defensively, though her bravado was clearly forced, “What else could it be? I’m doing all this for our mission!”","The System’s data flickered on and off. It still felt that something was off. Its host had always been a bit of a slacker who disliked meddling in other people’s affairs, and that tendency had already infected its current self.","But its host also loved showing off and enjoyed receiving praise and attention. No one could fool it about that. Supposedly, this had something to do with her upbringing and family environment. The System didn’t understand such things, but that didn’t stop it from cooperating enthusiastically out of a strong instinct for self-preservation.","【Host, you’ve really worked hard. To complete the mission, you’ve sacrificed so much and endured things no one of your station should have had to endure...】","“All right, System. That’s enough,” Yue Fuguang interrupted its stream of flattery.","“Lord Feng, write back to my grandfather. Tell him that our air carriage will descend in front of the city tower at Xuanwu Gate at the hour of Chen three days from now.”","Beyond Xuanwu Gate lay Xuanwu Avenue, the main thoroughfare of the capital and one of its busiest streets. Since she was going to appear in public, Yue Fuguang decided to let everyone see just how impressive her air carriage was.","Ever since Emperor Mingxi received the message, he had made no attempt to keep it secret. Even without his orders, the people of the capital had learned that the Divine Maiden who had saved them from the drought was returning to the city.","They had taken to the streets of their own accord and cleaned every road the Grand Preceptor might pass through. Some had even been tempted to take rags and wipe the streets down themselves.","“Mother, stop wasting your time. I heard the Divine Maiden is coming back in an air carriage. She won’t even need to use our street!”","A woman in her forties struck her son with a broom. “I’ll do what I please! Even if the Divine Maiden doesn’t come down onto our street, she’ll have to fly over it, won’t she? How could we let some filthy road offend the Divine Maiden’s eyes?”","An old man nodded in agreement. “Mistress Wang is right. We’re people from the Divine Maiden’s hometown. We can’t bring shame upon her!”","Mistress Wang nodded. “Old Brother Wu is right. These little whelps have only enjoyed a few full meals, and they’ve already forgotten the Divine Maiden’s kindness!”","As she spoke, Mistress Wang raised her broom again, intending to strike her son.","He was nearly twenty and would soon become a father himself. He protested aggrievedly, “Mother, you’re accusing me unfairly! When have I ever forgotten the Divine Maiden’s kindness?”","Unable to help himself, he lightly slapped his own mouth. “It’s all your fault. Why does your mouth always run ahead of you?”","Their home was on a small side street. Who was to say that the Divine Maiden couldn’t pass by there?","“Mother, I’m going to help my employer clean his shop on Xuanwu Avenue. The Divine Maiden is sure to pass that way.”","“All right, go on, then. Remember to work hard.”","As he spoke, his mother resumed sweeping the ground in front of their home.","Scenes like this continued to unfold throughout the capital. Three days passed in the blink of an eye, and with the joint efforts of the officials and the common people, the capital had taken on an entirely new appearance.","Even Yue Fuguang, seated in the slowly descending air carriage, noticed the difference.","“Hmm? Little Zhu, is it just my imagination, or does the capital seem much cleaner this time we’ve returned? Look at the tiles on the houses atop the city gate tower. They look as though someone deliberately scrubbed them.”","Feng Tang, who knew the truth, smiled faintly. His Majesty and the people of the city had not gone to all that trouble for nothing. The Grand Preceptor had noticed it all.","Emperor Mingxi and the others had been waiting on the city tower for nearly half an hour. Naturally, they too saw the air carriage slowly descending, and heard Yue Fuguang’s thoughts.","“She’s here! The Grand Preceptor is here!”","No one knew who shouted it from within the crowd. The moment they saw the carriage flying out from the clouds, he had been unable to contain himself.","Xuanwu Avenue had originally been quiet, with crowds lining both sides of the road to welcome her. But at the sight of the air carriage, the people erupted into complete excitement.","“The Divine Maiden! It really is the Divine Maiden!”","“Those flying horses really have wings! They’re so long and white!”","“The Divine Maiden’s immortal carriage is beautiful!”","“Is that an immortal carriage made of emerald jade?”","“The bells on the carriage sound so lovely!”","“Yes, listening to them makes my heart feel so light.”","“Are you sure your heart feels light because of the bells, and not because you’ve seen the Divine Maiden?”","The avenue below the city tower was bustling with excitement. On the city wall, the officials of the Great Yan court stretched their necks and rose onto their toes, all trying to get a better look.","Yue Fuguang’s air carriage descended incredibly slowly, giving everyone ample time to admire it.","The more they looked, the more envious they became. In particular, when they saw their colleague Feng Tang sitting on the driver’s bench, their envy and jealousy reached its peak.","Even Emperor Mingxi was no exception. He practically wished he could fly up, drag Feng Tang down, and take his place himself.","At last, after swaying through the sky for nearly the time it took to burn a tea stick, Yue Fuguang’s carriage slowly landed on the city tower.","“Your Majesty!”","“Fuguang, you’re back. You’re safe and sound—that’s all that matters!”","Yue Fuguang was still standing on the driver’s bench, but Emperor Mingxi and the others swarmed around her without even waiting for her to climb down and offer them the proper greeting.","It wasn’t that they had abandoned all dignity. The carriage, along with the winged horses pulling it, looked far too much like the divine beasts and celestial vehicles described in the legends of immortals.","The “special effects” surrounding the carriage were still active. Spiritual light shimmered, and the occasional phantom of an immortal beast or celestial plant appeared and vanished. Emperor Mingxi had reached out to touch the carriage wall, but quickly withdrew his hand.","For the first time in his many years as a man, Emperor Mingxi felt deeply inadequate.","“Fuguang, is this your new carriage? It’s truly beautiful!” Compared with it, his jade palanquin seemed utterly inferior.","“Your Majesty, this air carriage is not only beautiful but fast as well. Without it, I wouldn’t have been able to return so quickly.”","“On behalf of the people of the realm, I thank you, Fuguang.” Emperor Mingxi bowed to Yue Fuguang. “Without you, Great Yan would be no better off than the several nations bordering us.”","Now that Yue Fuguang no longer concealed her identity as the Divine Maiden, he could, as ruler of the empire, properly bow to her as such.","Yue Fuguang had never publicly acknowledged that she was The Immortal Lord, but neither had she denied it. That was effectively an admission.","Seeing that His Majesty had offered his respects, the assembled officials did not hesitate either.","“We thank the Grand Preceptor for your assistance!”","Yue Fuguang had no sense that their gratitude was undeserved. Given her status, she could not be excessively humble and cautious; doing so would only diminish her dignity.","She lifted her chin slightly and accepted their homage with her hands clasped behind her back. Her voice, however, held a touch more warmth.","“Your Majesty, and all of you, there is no need for such formalities.”"]},{"number":522,"title":"Chapter 522: Prince, you come over here too","paragraphs":["With a faint smile tugging at the corners of her lips, she said to Emperor Mingxi, “The rain that has fallen across Dayan this time was mostly transferred from the skies above the few cities in Southern Yue that our army recently conquered. It certainly took me quite a bit of effort.”","“Fuguang, you’ve worked hard. Will you be able to rest at home for a few days this time?” Emperor Mingxi took a glass of juice from the tray Qian Gui was holding behind him and handed it to her.","“According to the memorials sent in from all over the empire, Dayan’s drought has been greatly alleviated. Fuguang should take a good rest.”","“That’s right, Grand Preceptor. Not only has this year’s summer harvest escaped the effects of the drought, but thanks to your efforts, it is expected to increase by more than thirty percent.” Wang Shouchen, Minister of Agriculture, was brimming with excitement. The old man’s face had gone red, though no one could tell whether it was from excitement or the heat.","War was ultimately a battle of logistics. After two years of careful development, Dayan had finally built up some reserves, which was why they had dared to launch an attack on Southern Yue.","Their confidence and strength had both come from Yue Fuguang. With money, grain, and Yue Fuguang on their side, Dayan’s emperor and ministers would not be afraid even if Northern Li and Xiqiang joined forces to attack them.","Yue Fuguang smiled lightly. “I can stay for seven or eight days this time. Dayan is doing fine for now and is basically not short of water. However, we can’t neglect the newly conquered territories. Otherwise, the people’s loyalty will crumble, and it will make things difficult for Your Majesty to govern.”","She had moved the rain clouds away from the skies above the cities of Southern Yue, but given the current conditions, it would take less than ten days for more rain to gather there. Even if she did nothing, the heavy rains would continue to fall.","Upon hearing Yue Fuguang’s words, tears immediately welled up in Emperor Mingxi’s eyes. If he had not still been concerned with preserving the dignity of an emperor, he would have burst into tears on the spot.","“Fuguang, you have considered both me and Dayan in every way, yet I have nothing with which to repay you!”","The others nodded as well. “We are ashamed that we cannot share His Majesty’s burdens as the Grand Preceptor does!”","“Your Majesty and all the ministers are too kind.” She turned to Emperor Mingxi. “Your Majesty needn’t think about how to repay me. Govern the realm well and do not mistreat the people. That would be the best repayment you could give me.”","After all, this affected the evaluation of her final mission rank. Whether the realm was governed well or poorly made a considerable difference, most directly reflected in the points she would receive.","System: This is such a touching moment, and you’re being so practical!","Yue Fuguang: If you’re not practical, then give me all your points!","System: Never mind. Forget I said anything!","Emperor Mingxi nodded solemnly. “Fuguang, rest assured. I know deeply that the people are the foundation of a state, and when the foundation is firm, the state will be peaceful. I shall inherit and protect this realm, and I swear to practice benevolent governance with a benevolent heart.","“Whenever an imperial decree is issued, I shall ensure that it brings tangible benefits to both officials and commoners. Should I betray these words, let Heaven and Earth bear witness to the responsibilities of a ruler!”","Yue Fuguang nodded, then looked past Emperor Mingxi at the Crown Prince. “You are the heir to the throne, so you must also remember what His Majesty has said today.","“The ruler is a boat, and the common people are water. Water can carry a boat, but it can also overturn it.”","“Yes, Aunt Fuguang. I, Zhiyan, will remember both your words and Father’s and will never dare forget them!” Upon hearing this, Xie Zhiyan was deeply shaken. By identifying him as the heir to the throne in such a public setting, Yue Fuguang had effectively placed an armor-like layer of protection around him.","Even his father could no longer shake his position as Crown Prince. He was now unquestionably the next emperor. Not even his fifth brother’s marriage to a daughter of the Yu family could threaten him in the slightest.","He was also stunned by those words: “The ruler is a boat, and the common people are water. Water can carry a boat, but it can also overturn it.” This was the first time he had ever heard someone explain the relationship between ruler and people so thoroughly in just two short sentences.","Xie Zhiyan was not the only one. Emperor Mingxi and all the ministers were equally shocked, and their feelings were even more pronounced.","For a long time, everyone had suspected that although the Grand Preceptor had presented them with many books, some of those books revealed traces of a literary tradition she had never mentioned.","They had no idea why the Grand Preceptor had never shown any intention of revealing it. Could it be that they still had not done well enough?","Yue Fuguang had no idea what they were thinking. Once their shock had passed, her gaze returned to the flying carriage.","Some people’s eyes were practically glued to it, as though they wanted to pry it apart and take it home. Her eyes flashed. “Your Majesty, would you like to take a ride in the flying carriage?”","“Fuguang!” Emperor Mingxi’s voice rose several pitches in excitement. “Are you serious?” His eyes nearly popped out of his head. “I can really ride in this flying carriage?”","Yue Fuguang nodded with complete confidence. “If I say you can, then you can.”","She raised a hand. “Your Majesty, please!”","At that, Emperor Mingxi hesitated instead. Yue Fuguang thought he had frozen because he was afraid of heights, but then she heard him muttering under his breath, “Should I step in with my right foot first, or my left? The left is the honored side!”","And so Yue Fuguang watched as Emperor Mingxi decisively stepped in with his right foot.","She nearly burst out laughing.","“Your Majesty, take it slowly!” Qian Gui hurried over to support him.","“Grandfather, Father, Second Uncle, you should come too!” Naturally, his own family had priority.","As for Yu Qinchun, who was standing among the crowd, Yue Fuguang maintained that there were simply too many people and she had not seen him.","“Fuguang!”","The father and two sons of the Yu family slowly climbed into the carriage beneath the envious, reddened gazes of all their fellow officials.","At last, Yue Fuguang stood on the carriage platform and turned to give the envious-looking Xie Zhiyan a faint smile. “Crown Prince, you should come over too!”","“Yes, Aunt Fuguang!” Xie Zhiyan grinned and took several steps before climbing into the last carriage bound for the Sky Station.","“Aunt Fuguang, I’ll drive!” Xie Zhiyan had long envied the position Feng Tang had occupied before. Although the flying horses did not actually need him to rein them in, he still liked the driver’s seat more and more the longer he looked at it.","It was much like driving a luxury car in a later age. Personally taking the wheel and sitting in the passenger seat simply felt different.","“It’s flying! Quick, look—the carriage is flying again!”","The commoners below the city wall had no idea what the goddess and the honored guests above had been discussing. Now the carriage had taken flight once more. Was the goddess returning to her residence?","Some people were already preparing to run toward the Yu residence, only to discover that the flying carriage began slowly circling above them.","“Look! Is that our Crown Prince driving the carriage?”","The commoners might not recognize Xie Zhiyan, but they recognized his clothes. Who else could be so young and wear a robe embroidered with dragon designs, other than the Crown Prince?"]},{"number":523,"title":"Chapter 523: Old Cai, tell us quickly, how does it taste","paragraphs":["The princes all wore python robes.","“Judging by the patterns on that robe, it really is our Crown Prince.” This was spoken by someone well-read, who recognized at a glance the style of embroidery on the robe.","“His face confirms it too—it’s definitely our Crown Prince. They say the Divine Maiden favors His Highness the Crown Prince. Looks like it’s true.” This was someone who had seen the Crown Prince before and enjoyed listening to the rumors circulating in the streets.","“If only I had an aunt like that!” This came from a family with nothing but sons and not a single daughter.","“I have an aunt, but my aunt doesn’t have a flying carriage!” This was a brazen, thoughtless child who failed to notice that his ten-year-old aunt had already silently picked up her little whip.","Below the city tower, the common people were buzzing with discussion. Above it, Emperor Mingxi and Yue Fuguang were nowhere to be seen, and the officials had begun talking among themselves as well.","Wei Ping and several of the ministers in particular craned their necks, gazing enviously at the carriage in the sky, which shimmered with flowing light as a galaxy flashed around it.","“Do you think that once His Majesty and the others come down, Grand Tutor Yue might let us take a ride too?”","“I doubt it. Grand Tutor Yue must be exhausted. She may simply return to her residence afterward.”","“Then do you think Grand Tutor Yue will take the flying carriage to court over the next few days?”","“Exactly! Grand Tutor Yue hasn’t attended court in so long. I feel that court is nowhere near as interesting when she isn’t there!”","“Grand Tutor Yue is truly terrifying when she attends court, but when she’s absent, it really does feel as though something is missing!”","Gossiping was entertaining, but being frightened was genuinely frightening too. Many times, they had felt they knew far too much and might lose their heads over it.","“So... do we still have a chance to ride in it?”","The men looked at one another, silently assessing just how much weight they carried in Yue Fuguang’s eyes and whether they had any hope of getting a ride.","As for attending court, their wish actually came true. Three days after Yue Fuguang returned to her residence, she really did take the flying carriage to court.","At that moment, Yue Fuguang sat inside the carriage. Emperor Mingxi was on her left, and Yu Chongshan on her right. Seated below them were the brothers Yu Zhongchun and Yu Shuchun.","Emperor Mingxi held a cup of fragrant tea in his hands as he gazed at the scenery outside. The wind and clouds were so close that they seemed within reach.","Every so often, birds swept past in the distance. They were now flying higher and farther than the birds themselves.","Below them, the capital of Shangjing grew smaller and smaller, while the people of Dayan were reduced to tiny black specks.","The green mountains and vast stretches of land beneath them also dwindled into insignificance. Without realizing it, everyone’s hearts seemed to open up.","To see all the mountains below from such a lofty height—to stand at an altitude they had never even imagined and take in the scenery of the world—filled them with an inexplicable surge of heroic spirit, along with the complicated realization that they were so very small.","Supreme shock and fear intertwined in their hearts, eventually transforming into boundless joy and reassurance. After all, when they turned their heads, they could see the Divine Maiden Yue Fuguang, the pillar that stabilized all of Dayan.","Once Emperor Mingxi and the others had settled their emotions, Yue Fuguang brought out some food for them as well. With a trace of regret in her voice, she said, “It’s a pity the timing isn’t right today. Watching the sunrise from the flying carriage is an experience unlike any other.”","“This is already more than enough. I never dreamed that one day I would be able to drink tea and admire the scenery in the sky!”","Emperor Mingxi chuckled. “And it’s so steady, too. Even my imperial carriage can’t compare!”","Yue Fuguang smiled as well. “Now that Your Majesty is flying through the heavens, is it different from what you imagined?”","Emperor Mingxi nodded with a smile. “I never imagined we could fly higher than the birds. I never knew the clouds in the sky would look like mist, and as for the land below...”","Emperor Mingxi went on for quite some time. At that moment, he was like a curious old child. Every time Emperor Mingxi said something, the three members of the Yu family nodded along.","Whether or not the emperor had voiced exactly what was in their hearts, the father and sons provided emotional support with remarkable enthusiasm.","They drank tea and admired the scenery as they traveled through the sky for quite a while. Then Yue Fuguang thought of the people of Dayan still waiting below, and her eyes shifted.","Seeing her host purchase yet another attention-grabbing item from the system shop, the system couldn’t help grumbling, [Host, do you really love showing off that much?]","Yue Fuguang retorted, refusing to admit the accusation in the slightest. “System, I’m doing all this for the mission. The mission!”","With that, she stopped paying attention to the system. As the flying carriage slowly descended, she reached her hand out of the window and snapped her fingers at the empty air.","In an instant, the wind and clouds began to surge, and seven-colored light appeared on the horizon.","Everywhere the flying carriage passed, petals sprang into existence and drifted gently downward.","“Quick, look! The Divine Maiden’s flying carriage is coming back! And what’s that?”","“Are those flower petals?”","“Flower petals? Like the petals from Nanyue?”","“Nanyue? What do you mean, brother? Tell me about it!”","“You’re not from Shangjing?”","“I’m from Liuping County. I only just arrived in Shangjing.”","“Then let me tell you...”","While everyone was talking animatedly, the petals high in the sky finally began to fall in thick, snowlike flurries.","“Catch them! Catch them!”","Some people stretched out both hands to catch them. Others even opened their mouths, while some took off their clothes entirely.","The civil and military officials standing atop the city tower, waiting for His Majesty and Grand Tutor Yue to return, did not remain dignified for long either.","Because they stood higher than the common people, they were the first to reach out and catch the falling objects.","Wei Ping examined the petal resting in his palm. It looked neither quite like a flower petal nor a drop of water, but rather like some strange, jade-green object. Cai Xian held one in his hand as well, and it was exactly the same.","“Old Cai, want to taste it?”","The two had worked together far too many times. They possessed a tacit understanding that others could never match.","“Let’s taste it! We’ll see if it’s better than those flatbreads!” Cai Xian carefully popped the tiny object in his hand into his mouth.","He smacked his lips twice with great concentration. Wei Ping watched his reaction curiously, but when Cai Xian remained silent for some time, he couldn’t help urging him, “Old Cai, hurry up and tell us—how does it taste?”","“It tastes like the meat pies I love. After eating just one, my whole body feels warm. My stomach was a little empty a moment ago, but now I actually feel full!”","“It can do that? Really?” Huo Ying leaned over. He, too, had one cupped in his hand.","“You’ll know once you try it, won’t you?”","“True. Then I’ll give it a taste too!”","Huo Ying was a straightforward man. He tossed it directly into his mouth, but before he even had time to smack his lips twice, the thing had already slipped down his throat.","Wei Ping leaned over again. “Well? How is it?”"]},{"number":524,"title":"Chapter 524: Little Aunt, Please Spare Me JPG","paragraphs":["“I didn’t have time to savor the flavor, but Old Cai was right. My whole body feels warm and cozy. These past few months, I’ve been so busy with the war that my meals have been irregular, and my stomach hasn’t been doing well. I already feel much better.”","Many others shared the same experience as Cai Xian and Huo Ying. They were all impatient by nature, and because they trusted Yue Fuguang completely, they swallowed the flower petals they received without letting them linger for even a moment.","“Mine was sweet. Huh? My back feels better!”","“Mine was spicy. Eh? My legs, which have been cold and aching for twenty years, feel much better too!”","“My presbyopia...”","“Mine was a golden peanut! Hahaha, now I can afford to buy my daughter some flowers to wear!”","“Mine was a golden peanut too! I’m going to enshrine it properly!”","After Yue Fuguang flew her vehicle once around the capital and harvested another huge wave of faith points, she directly took Emperor Mingxi, his son, and the father-and-son duo from the Yu family back to the Yu residence.","Standing atop the city wall and watching the flying vehicle disappear into the distance, the assembled officials exchanged glances. They knew their Grand Preceptor far too well.","As expected, the ancestor was too lazy to come down again and had simply abducted His Majesty and the Crown Prince to her home.","Time passed slowly as the women of the Yu family insisted that Yue Fuguang had lost weight and needed to be properly nourished—and immediately put that conviction into action.","For the next two days, a steady stream of food and other treats was sent to the Brightmoon Pavilion. Even the Empress Dowager and the Empress came along to join in the fun.","Yue Fuguang ate and drank to her heart’s content while the system watched enviously.","【Host, where exactly have you lost weight? Could it be that you’re simply growing? With how much you’re eating, aren’t you afraid of actually getting fat?】","Yue Fuguang tossed another candied peanut into her mouth and mumbled, “I have slimming pills. What’s there to fear from a little indulgence? If I really do get fat, I’ll just take a pill and lose the weight painlessly.”","【If the folks back home heard you say that, they’d drown you in spit!】","Yue Fuguang rolled her eyes without the slightest trace of grace. “System, if you don’t sell me out, who’s going to find out?”","“Also, are we really going to expose him at court tomorrow?”","She hadn’t expected to return home and spend only two lazy days lounging around before the system handed her another mission. Sure, it was giving her points for free, but its inexplicable insistence on not letting her relax made her want to quit on the spot.","【It’s a system mission, and the points are free. How can we refuse them?】","“It’s only the eighth year of the Yuankang era. Why are we in such a hurry to deal with him?”","【Because we’re about to find the lair of Panshan, and it’s time to pull out the mole in Dayan too.】","“How come you didn’t notice there was something wrong with him before?”","【It seems his identity was hidden by the workings of fate, so the Gossip-Eating System didn’t detect anything suspicious about him at the time.】","Perhaps it was precisely this hidden identity that had caused so many transmigrators to fall.","Even the two of them had almost misjudged him, treating him like some insignificant nobody.","“All right, then. It’s been a long time since I’ve given Dayan’s ruler and his officials some gossip. This time, let’s give them a big one.”","The system was getting excited too. It hadn’t accompanied Dayan’s ruler and officials in a gossip session for several months, and it was genuinely looking forward to seeing their reactions when they heard this huge, thoroughly confirmed piece of news.","【Master, it’s been months since you attended court, but the emperor and the officials are still exactly the same!】","Yue Fuguang once again sat in her usual spot, with tea, fruit, and pastries carefully selected to suit her tastes by Eunuch Qian arranged before her.","The moment the system began, the emperor on the Dragon Throne and the officials below all felt that familiar sensation.","“Of course they are. What changes did you expect them to make?”","【There have been some changes. That shower of flower petals you sent down a few days ago helped cure or ease quite a few people’s old and new ailments. Look at the man in the green robe, third from the left in the second-to-last row. I’ve always suspected he was nearsighted. Now look at his eyes today. Aren’t they much clearer?】","“You spent all that time describing his location, when you could’ve just said he’s the man behind my big brother, Yu Qingyu.”","【Hehe, you were about to fall asleep, so I thought I’d liven things up a little!】","The green-robed junior official whom the system had appraised had a flushed face. Though he had been reduced to a mere member of the atmosphere-setting team, he was inexplicably thrilled.","All of them, including his fellow graduates—and Yu Qingyu, the Grand Preceptor’s own elder brother—had spent three years compiling books in the Hanlin Academy before finally earning the right to attend court.","Unfortunately, their timing had been poor. Just as they became qualified to participate in court, the Grand Preceptor had left the capital to oversee flood relief, so they had never had the chance to see her at court.","Only today, upon meeting her for the first time, did they learn that the secret concealed by the entire court was actually...","“Little Zhu, you’re right. This morning court is just as boring as ever. I’m practically falling asleep listening to it!”","【Master, would you like to hear some gossip to wake yourself up?】","“Gossip? Whose?”","At the mention of more gossip, some people grew excited, while others wore worried expressions.","Whenever the Grand Preceptor indulged in gossip, it inevitably dragged a whole string of incidents into the light. The problems were indeed solved, but each time, the officials genuinely felt as if they had taken a stroll around the gates of the King of Hell.","Wei Ping and Cai Xian exchanged a knowing glance. The same three words were written all over both their faces:","We’ve got work!","【It’s royal gossip. Want to hear it?】","When Emperor Mingxi and his officials heard the words “royal,” their hearts sank completely.","Emperor Mingxi couldn’t help tightening his grip on the armrest of the Dragon Throne. The divine artifact had nearly stripped him down to his underwear already—what other gossip could there possibly be left in the royal family?","The Crown Prince and several of the other princes were likewise filled with apprehension. The second, third, fifth, and sixth princes each carefully thought over their recent actions. Even during the months when the Grand Preceptor had been away from the capital, they had behaved themselves quite well.","The only difference was that the Fifth Prince had recently started hovering around several members of the Yu family, acting so obsequiously that he seemed to have forgotten he was a prince.","There was also the Sixth Prince’s wedding to the princess of Nanyue, which had proceeded in a perfectly proper and conventional manner.","The Seventh and Eighth Princes, who had only recently begun attending court and participating in government affairs alongside Yu Qingyu and the others, silently leaned closer together, looking weak, helpless, and pitiful.","Seventh Prince: Auntie, please let us off! [Picture of a pleading expression]","“Royal gossip? Of course we have to hear that!”","Yue Fuguang’s excitement nearly burst through the roof. Emperor Mingxi silently rubbed his forehead, thinking that this ancestor had probably forgotten she herself now counted as half a member of the royal family.","【Master, do you remember who Dayan’s last ruler was—the one who led it to ruin?】","Gasp!","Hiss!"]},{"number":525,"title":"Chapter 525: This sounds like it's going to be quite a show","paragraphs":["Some newly appointed officials who had never seen much of the world stirred slightly at those words. Fortunately, two senior officials were currently engaged in a “friendly” debate over how to govern the newly conquered territories.","They were practically spitting in each other’s faces, and the officials throughout the hall followed their rhythm, quietly discussing matters among themselves. The unnatural expressions that flashed across some faces did not seem particularly conspicuous.","Emperor Mingxi and the ministers who had weathered countless storms, however, suddenly felt as though they had been transported to another lifetime when they heard Yue Fuguang and the others mention the fallen ruler once more.","The question that had lingered in their hearts for four years was finally about to be answered.","Emperor Mingxi and his assembled officials did not have to wait long. Yue Fuguang promptly provided the name.","“Of course I remember. Wasn’t the fallen ruler of Dayan none other than the Eighth Prince, Xie Zhilian?”","Yue Fuguang wore a nostalgic expression. “I still remember the first time we attended the emperor’s birthday celebration. You pointed at the princes and princesses of the six kingdoms in the hall and asked me to guess who would ascend the throne.”","[Exactly. There were more than a dozen princes and princesses from the six kingdoms combined, yet only that Xie Zhilian eventually became emperor—and he became the ruler who lost his kingdom.]","“I never figured it out. At the time, Dayan’s Crown Prince was dead, the Second and Third Princes were crippled, the Fifth and Sixth Princes were barely clinging to life, and the Seventh Prince was dead as well.”","With every sentence Yue Fuguang spoke, the emperor’s and the princes’ expressions grew grimmer.","“The emperor’s Fourth and Ninth Sons were still alive, and behind them stood Northern Li and Southern Yue. So how did the insignificant Eighth Prince end up ascending the throne?”","Indeed—how had the Eighth Prince ended up ascending the throne?","As the person involved, Xie Zhilian very much wanted to know the answer himself. The moment Yue Fuguang revealed his name, the people around him began looking at him strangely.","Before today, he had never imagined that he would become the ruler who lost his kingdom. How could it possibly be him?","[Because when it came to backing, the Eighth Prince’s supporters were no weaker than those two!]","Eighth Prince: How did I not know my backing was that powerful?","The other princes: Little Eighth, you’ve been hiding your strength! If you’re so capable, why have you been pretending to be innocent?","“There was something like that too? Hurry up and tell me what kind of force stood behind him. If it was so powerful, how did he still manage to destroy Dayan?”","Emperor Mingxi and his officials: Exactly! If you had such powerful backing, how did you still lose the kingdom?","[Master, is it possible that the very purpose of pushing Little Eighth onto the throne was to speed up Dayan’s collapse?]","“Little Eighth’s ascension could accelerate Dayan’s destruction? Is he really that capable?”","The Eighth Prince, utterly despairing: Auntie, if you had this kind of ability, would you want it?","[Master, the force behind Little Eighth was Panshan, an organization devoted to overthrowing dynasties and replacing them with new ones. In their eyes, although Dayan had been founded only a little over a century ago, it was already corrupt and declining. They felt it was time for someone else to take its place.]","“I’ll admit that it was corrupt. After all, among the six kingdoms, it had the most severe land monopolization and the greatest number of powerful aristocratic clans.","“But if you wanted to replace it, then replace it. How did you end up plunging the world into chaos?”","[Is it possible that they accidentally lost control of the situation? Originally, the Xie family’s dynasty was supposed to be replaced by the Sima family. But something went wrong along the way, and the Sima family ended up controlling only half the empire.","“Then that half of the empire kept changing hands. The other kingdoms under their control also descended into internal disorder, and the heirs they had favored failed to ascend the throne.","“While attempting to ‘restore order,’ they managed to get the emperor killed. After that, the entire realm fell into chaos!]","“So most of the blame for the chaos that engulfed the world should fall on Panshan? Isn’t their organization supposed to be deeply entrenched, with influence everywhere, and constantly boasting about how powerful they are?","“And they still managed to lose control? Their abilities and methods aren’t all that impressive, are they?”","[Master, Panshan’s strength lies in the wide distribution of its influence, but that is also the source of its downfall!","“Panshan is like a dynasty in its own right. It is made up of people, and wherever there are people, there will be personal agendas and individual preferences.","“Once those exist, disagreements will follow. And once there are disagreements, there will be struggles.”]","Yue Fuguang nodded. “Take Southern Yue, for example. Two or three factions within Panshan were maneuvering behind the scenes over the throne. On the surface, it looked like the Gan family was fighting among itself, but in reality, it was Panshan’s own people battling one another. When all was said and done, it was nothing more than a struggle for profit.”","[That’s right. At the time, Dayan’s emperor and Crown Prince had both died, while the adult sons who remained were either dead or crippled.","“Several important ministers who were loyal to the emperor had either been forced out of court or met with violent deaths. Most of those left behind were sycophants concerned only with their own advancement.","“During the struggle among Northern Li, Southern Yue, and Panshan, Panshan emerged victorious in choosing the successor. Xie Zhilian, who represented their interests, ascended the throne.","“His mission was to bring the Xie dynasty to an end, become a sinner against the Xie family, and rule as the emperor who lost his kingdom.”]","The hearts of Emperor Mingxi and his officials were shaken to the core. Xie Zhilian’s face, in particular, had gone so pale that not a trace of color remained.","If the Seventh Prince had not still cared enough about their brotherly bond—and if he had not wished to keep Yue Fuguang from noticing that something was wrong—and thus done his utmost, together with the Third Prince, to support him, Xie Zhilian would have collapsed long ago.","The Third Prince, too, stared at his Eighth Brother in bewilderment. The divine artifact had said that the younger brother with whom he was closest would eventually ascend the throne. So it had been Little Eighth all along. Yet their relationship was only ordinary at present. How had they later grown so close?","“Did Xie Zhilian know about his historical ‘mission’? No matter what, he was still a member of the Xie family. How could he destroy the foundation his own family had built?","“Anyone would have to suffer brain damage for ten years straight to do something like that!”","Emperor Mingxi nodded furiously inwardly. Forget ten years—even twenty years of brain damage would not be enough to make someone do such a thing.","If his abilities were lacking and he lost the kingdom because he could not govern it properly, that would be a matter of competence. It would be a fatal flaw, but there would be nothing to say.","But if he had set out from the very beginning with the intention of bringing about the kingdom’s downfall, then the problem lay with his principles!","He narrowed his eyes as he scrutinized his eighth son. The boy was nearly fifteen this year. How had he failed to see earlier that he was a menace?","[By the timeline, in the eighth year of Yuankang, he still didn’t know. At that point, he didn’t even know that he carried Panshan blood.]","“Panshan blood? What does that mean?”","[Master, guess this: among all his brothers, the Eighth Prince was unremarkable in every way. Why was he chosen to inherit the throne?","“Although I said that the original purpose of placing him on the throne was to bring about a change of dynasty, there were people among those who pushed him forward who did not share that intention.”]","“You mean Xie Zhilian was chosen by Panshan for some particular reason, and the people who supported his ascension eventually split into factions?”","[That’s right. The divisions within Panshan were actually even greater than those among the officials in the imperial court. When Xie Zhilian ascended the throne, some wanted him to send Dayan to its grave, while others hoped he could secure his position as emperor and use Dayan’s existing framework to establish a dynasty of their own.]","“That sounds like quite a spectacle!”"]},{"number":526,"title":"Chapter 526: Are the People of Panshan Trying to Be Parasites","paragraphs":["【Exactly! The one who wanted Dayan destroyed naturally supported the faction backing the Sima family, while those who hoped Xie Zhilian would secure the throne were his maternal relatives.","But judging by the outcome, Xie Zhilian’s maternal family clearly failed!","Still, the faction supporting the Sima family didn’t win outright, either.】","“Why does this struggle for the realm look more and more like an internal power struggle within Panshan?”","The others had the same feeling. They had always considered themselves clever and exceptional, but now it seemed that an entire group of them had been toyed with by Panshan. Even the imperial family had been unable to escape its grasp.","“And you said Xie Zhilian’s maternal family? Consort Qin’s family has ties to Panshan as well? To be able to support their own grandson in ascending the throne, they must have held a fairly high position within Panshan!”","【Master, the Eighth Prince wasn’t Consort Qin’s biological son at all. When the Eighth Prince was born, his birth mother, Noble Lady Hu, died in childbirth. At the time, Consort Qin and Noble Lady Hu’s mother lived in the same palace and had a good relationship, so the emperor had Consort Qin adopt Xie Zhilian.】","“What sort of background did the Eighth Prince’s birth mother have?”","At that moment, Xie Zhilian stared at Emperor Mingxi in disbelief, hoping to see a denial on his face.","Emperor Mingxi simply gazed back at him, rigid and silent. Xie Zhilian’s heart lurched.","So it was true. He really wasn’t his mother’s biological child!","【Master, the palace records for Noble Lady Hu state that her father was Hu Zhongting, a minor sixth-rank official in the Ministry of Rites, and her mother was Lady Jiang.","But in truth, she wasn’t the Hu family’s biological daughter.】","“So this is another case of a switched child?”","【Not exactly. Noble Lady Hu was an adopted daughter of the Hu family. Hu Zhongting and Lady Jiang had been married for five years without having any children.","Afterward, he took two more concubines, but the result was the same.】","“So the problem with their infertility lay with Hu Zhongting.”","【Later, they heard someone say that adopting a girl would bring them a son, and that was how they came to have Noble Lady Hu.】","“Was the ‘someone’ they heard that from a member of Panshan? Did they start laying their plans this early?”","【Your guess is correct, Master. The Hu family was a household Panshan had carefully selected, and they were the ones who caused Hu Zhongting’s infertility.","As a result, within half a year of Noble Lady Hu entering the Hu family, Lady Jiang became pregnant and gave birth to a son.】","Yue Fuguang and the system discussed the matter in a calm, matter-of-fact tone, but Emperor Mingxi and the assembled officials were trembling with fear.","Panshan was not only deeply entrenched, with members from every walk of life. They were also masters of long-term schemes, making them nearly impossible to guard against. To uproot them completely would be an exceedingly difficult task.","Yue Fuguang: It’s not difficult. If it were, I wouldn’t have gone straight for their lair long ago!","【And this kind of scheme involved far more than just Noble Lady Hu, and far more than just one country.】","The system’s data shifted. It decided to use this opportunity to reveal to the ruler and officials of Dayan the locations of several important Panshan strongholds that they knew about.","【Look. Panshan’s stronghold in Southern Yue is located right in its capital, Gancheng. The one in Nanzhao is in Baihua City. Dayan’s isn’t in the capital, Shangjing, but it isn’t far away, either. It’s in Pingliang County, about a hundred li from here...】","The system proceeded to recount everything they had learned from searching the souls of Consort Liang, the old nanny by her side, Zhao Quanan, and several others regarding the locations of Panshan’s strongholds.","The minor official disguised as a palace recorder was writing so furiously that sparks seemed to fly from his brush. There was no helping it—the divine artifact had provided far too many details.","It had clearly explained who belonged to Panshan, exactly where the strongholds were, what mechanisms and traps they contained, where their treasure vaults were hidden, and how many people guarded them.","Emperor Mingxi and his officials exchanged a glance. If they simply followed the divine artifact’s instructions, how much trouble would they be spared?","Yue Fuguang: I don’t know whether the emperor and the others will have an easier time, but not having to do anything myself certainly makes things easier for me.","“All right, I don’t want to hear any more about that. Let’s get back to Little Eight and continue digging into the imperial family’s secrets.”","System: Pretend all you like. If you didn’t want to know, you wouldn’t have waited until I finished before telling me to stop!","【Master, Noble Lady Hu was able to enter the palace and become one of Emperor Mingxi’s consorts because Panshan exerted influence behind the scenes. At the time, the old emperor was on the verge of death. He doted on Prince Rong and wanted to give him the throne.","In the end, however, he failed to outmaneuver the Crown Prince—the current Emperor Mingxi.","In fact, both of them had members of Panshan backing them at the time. Although the Panshan faction behind Prince Rong failed to defeat the emperor, they still preserved a bloodline for him when he fell.","As for the Panshan faction behind Emperor Mingxi, this was when they sent Noble Lady Hu into the palace.】","By now, Emperor Mingxi and the officials were not only trembling with fear—they were breaking out in cold sweats.","Never in their wildest dreams had they imagined that Panshan had also meddled in Dayan’s struggle for the throne. Their unseen hands truly reached everywhere.","“Panshan really is impossible to shake off. It’s as though the imperial authority of all six states lies beneath their enormous shadow.”","【Isn’t it? They have long controlled the succession struggles of every country, and this has caused many members of Panshan to develop delusions and selfish ambitions.","They want the one who controls the world to be their own descendant. It is another form of usurping imperial power from within.】","“Are the people of Panshan trying to become parasites?”","【More or less. Noble Lady Hu came about in precisely this way. Unfortunately, she died in childbirth when she gave birth to Xie Zhilian after becoming pregnant through fertility medication. Otherwise, Xie Zhilian would never have grown up as an unnoticed nobody among the imperial princes.】","“If Noble Lady Hu had lived, wouldn’t the imperial harem of Dayan have been even livelier?”","Emperor Mingxi: Who would want that kind of liveliness? Whoever wants it can have it. I certainly don’t!","【After Noble Lady Hu died, the newborn Xie Zhilian was adopted by Consort Qin. The people of Panshan then went into hiding and waited for him to grow up.","Some waited for him to seize the throne and take control of the government. Others waited for him to seize the throne and send Dayan to its destruction.】","“When did Xie Zhilian learn all this?”","【According to the timeline, it should have been when he turned fifteen. That’s only a few months away.】","“He believed it so easily? And what did he do after learning about his true origins?”","【His birth mother, Noble Lady Hu, had been adopted, and the circumstances of his birth were no great secret. Anyone could discover the truth with a little investigation.","Besides, the first people to approach him were his maternal grandfather and uncle. A nephew takes after his uncle, and Xie Zhilian looked very much like his maternal family.","Moreover, Panshan’s notorious reputation had yet to be exposed at that time. His maternal relatives were all old-timers within Panshan, and in terms of influence, they were far more useful than the Hu family.","Unfortunately, he didn’t know that his maternal grandfather’s family had few heirs. Though they were considered Panshan veterans, their actual influence was limited.","That was also why Dayan ultimately fell instead of Xie Zhilian truly securing the throne.】","Yue Fuguang glanced at Xie Zhilian, whose face had already gone deathly pale and whose entire body was trembling.","“However, according to the historical records, during the two years after Xie Zhilian ascended the throne, his actions didn’t exactly resemble those of someone who wanted to secure his position.”","Seeing Xie Zhilian’s expression, Yue Fuguang ultimately swallowed the words “what a foolish emperor” that had nearly escaped her lips."]},{"number":527,"title":"Chapter 527: This... is really hard to judge","paragraphs":["【Well, for one thing, it’s because of Xie Zhilian himself. He was never raised to be the crown prince, so it’s perfectly normal that he lacks ability.","For another, he wasn’t merely incompetent—his character was poor as well. He had only just taken the throne when his maternal grandfather’s family was wiped out from within Panshan.","After that, he listened to the slander of the other side and did everything that rulers of fallen kingdoms tend to do. Of course Dayan was doomed!】","Xie Zhilian could bear no more. He collapsed onto the floor.","【Master, what’s wrong with Xie Zhilian?】","Before Yue Fuguang could say anything, Emperor Mingxi slammed his hand against the armrest of the imperial throne and shouted, “Xie Zhilian, the evidence is conclusive. Your maternal grandfather, Hu Zhongting, was on intimate terms with the Prince of Beili and is suspected of treason and collusion with the enemy. You still want to plead for him?”","「Little Zhu, I was so engrossed in the gossip just now that I missed something. How did Hu Zhongting suddenly become a traitor?","And he was on intimate terms with the Prince of Beili? Which prince—Beiyue or Bei Ye?」","【No idea! I wasn’t paying attention to what Minister of Rites Zhang Zhongping and Court of State Ceremonies Minister You Mingmin were saying earlier, either.】","「Forget it. It doesn’t matter. The crown prince is alive now, and Dayan is growing stronger by the day. Even if Xie Zhilian’s maternal grandfather comes looking for trouble, he won’t be able to cause any real waves.」","【That’s true, but we still need to find an opportunity to tell the crown prince about the eunuchs and palace maids his maternal grandfather’s family planted around him.","Especially Yang Fu. He deserves enormous credit for the fall of Dayan!】","Yang Fu. Emperor Mingxi, his sons, and all the civil and military officials repeatedly turned that name over in their minds.","As for the Eighth Prince, Xie Zhilian, they had no idea whether His Majesty intended to execute him or confine him.","But Yang Fu would not live to see another sunrise.","Yue Fuguang and the system finished their gossip and sauntered away, leaving the ruler and officials of Dayan with a mountain of work.","It took the court more than a month before that work finally began to wind down.","That day, Yue Fuguang sat atop a cloud, gazing down at the people of Dayan as they busily gathered the harvest. She felt an inexplicable sense of accomplishment.","In the fields, every farmer was drenched in sweat, yet the joyful smiles never left their faces. Those smiles smoothed away the wrinkles carved into their features by years of hard labor.","There was light in their eyes, and hope for a better life.","【Host, are you suddenly feeling that all your hard work over the past few months was worth it?】","Yue Fuguang rested her chin in her hand and nodded slightly. 「It does seem to have been pretty meaningful!」","【Then I’ll give you a few more pieces of good news.】","【Within Dayan, the Panshan organization has been destroyed by the imperial court by eighty percent over the past month. At this rate, more than ninety percent should be dealt with before the end of the year.","As for Southern Yue, the Dayan army has already advanced to Gancheng. The Southern Yue court has now split into two factions: the faction advocating resistance and the faction advocating surrender.】","「Is Gan Sheng dead yet?」 Wasn’t this man’s life a little too tough? Even with the medicine Zhao Quan’an found to alleviate the poison, he was enduring far too well.","「Gan Chengyuan is useless. He’s been on the throne for two months, yet he still hasn’t dealt with the previous emperor.」","【He thought Gan Sheng was about to die, but who could have expected him to hold on for so long? If Gan Tang’s people hadn’t sent him on his final journey, he probably could have lasted another ten days or half a month. By then, he might even have lived to see Southern Yue’s capital fall into Dayan’s hands.】","「You mean Gan Sheng is dead—and Gan Tang’s people killed him?」","【He breathed his last early this morning. The moment he died, his several children ‘disappeared.’】","「Did they really disappear, or did he send them away?」","【Of course he sent them away. Gan Sheng was afraid that his children would eventually fall victim to Gan Chengyuan’s schemes. He was even more afraid that, once Southern Yue was destroyed, Dayan would wipe out the imperial family.】","「He had so little confidence in Southern Yue?」","【If he truly had confidence, whose kingdom would lose most of its territory to an enemy in less than half a year?】","Yue Fuguang nodded. Even she had not expected the Dayan army, armed with gunpowder, to be so terrifyingly formidable. It seemed she might be able to complete her mission two or three years ahead of schedule.","【Oh, right, Master, I have one more piece of news. Beili had barely gone to war with Dayan when Dayan’s spies exposed the true relationship between Imperial Noble Consort Rong and Chancellor Wei.】","Yue Fuguang flashed a mischievous smile. 「Bei Ji’s expression when he learned the news must have been priceless!」","【Naturally. Apparently, he replaced the furnishings in his bedchamber several times. For several days in a row, he didn’t go near that mother and son at all.","The consorts and princes in the Beili imperial palace seem to have sensed that something was wrong and began secretly tripping up that mother and son at every turn. Guess what happened?】","「What? It didn’t work?」","【Not exactly. I don’t know whether Bei Ji was too busy fighting Dayan and simply turned a blind eye to their little schemes, but the Eighth Prince was injured because of them a few days ago. Bei Ji didn’t even go to see him, unlike in the past.】","Yue Fuguang fired off three questions in succession. 「Has he truly come to hate that mother and son because of this? And what about Wei Qingyi’s military authority? Is Bei Ji really comfortable leaving it in his hands?","And Bei Ye—has he succeeded after all this time? It’s been more than a month!」","【Rather than hatred, it would be more accurate to call it fury at discovering he had been deceived, humiliation and embarrassment at having been kept in the dark, and fear at how narrowly he had escaped losing the throne.","Bei Ji knows very well how capable Chancellor Wei is, as well as how deeply rooted his influence is throughout the court.","After learning that Imperial Noble Consort Rong is Chancellor Wei’s biological younger sister, Bei Ji naturally became afraid.】","「Afraid that Chancellor Wei would join forces with that mother and son, get rid of the father, and keep the son?」","【Once the Eighth Prince truly ascended to the position of crown prince and gained the legitimate right of succession, what use would there be for Bei Ji?】","「For someone like Chancellor Wei, who has someone he loves in his heart—a white moonlight—an emperor’s ambitions would be a nuisance. And once you eliminate the person creating the nuisance, the problem no longer exists.」","【That’s why Bei Ji is afraid now. An irreparable rift has formed between ruler and minister. His actions are meant to test whether Chancellor Wei will step in to protect the Eighth Prince.】","「Why would he even need to test that? Anyone with a brain knows that Imperial Noble Consort Rong and Chancellor Wei must be colluding.」","【That’s the thing. Although they’re both well into their years, Bei Ji still has personal feelings for Chancellor Wei. Those feelings make him unwilling to give up until he sees the truth for himself.","And it’s precisely because of those feelings that Wei Qingyi remains commander of those one hundred and fifty thousand troops. Bei Ji merely replaced the deputy general with one of his own trusted men.】","「Bei Ji is quite a complicated person—devoted and ruthless at the same time.」","【Isn’t he? He’s ruthless toward the sons he doesn’t value, devoted to his old lover, and even extends that affection to the people around him!","But he doesn’t know that one of his pawns is plotting to rebel against him.】","「You mean Bei Ye succeeded?」","【Mm-hmm. The backup pawn, Bei Ye, has successfully taken Wei Qingyi.","In the Dayan army’s forward camp, the Dayan and Beili forces are fighting fiercely.","In the rear camp, Bei Ye and Wei Qingyi are fighting just as fiercely.】","「This... is hard to comment on!」"]},{"number":528,"title":"Chapter 528: The Nanzhao Cannot Return","paragraphs":["【Indeed. They had thought Beili would be a tough nut to crack, but who could have guessed that their commander and prince would do something so absurd and practically deliver their heads to Dayan?","Wei Qingyi’s army of one hundred and fifty thousand and the army of one hundred thousand under the command of Marquis Wuying of Beili were both thoroughly crushed by the Dayan army—or rather, by Dayan’s firearms—in their very first battle.】","“Firearms and cold weapons aren’t even in the same league. If Dayan couldn’t win by an overwhelming margin under these circumstances, they’d be utterly useless.”","【Of all their opponents, the Dongyi people are still the easiest to deal with. Dayan had barely more than thirty thousand naval troops, yet they chased the Dongyi army of over a hundred thousand all over the mountains and plains.","Now all four islands belong to Dayan. Even today, the other four kingdoms still haven’t learned that Dongyi has been destroyed. That is the advantage of being isolated on an island—the news is difficult to get out.】","“Since Dayan has taken Dongyi, it’s time to dig up the gold mine!”","To this day, Yue Fuguang still had not told the officials of Dayan where Gaozu’s treasure was hidden. She felt that Dayan was wealthy enough for now and truly had no need to touch that reserve fund.","【War is ultimately a contest of money and logistics. It hasn’t even been half a year, yet Dayan’s overflowing treasury has already been drained considerably. You have no idea—recently, all of Emperor Mingxi’s anxiety has been caused by his worries over money.】","Yue Fuguang divided the bright red apples on the table between Toffee and Milk Tea. “Dayan’s treasury can hold out for another six months of war. Isn’t he panicking a little too early?”","【Let him panic. It’s not as if he dares come ask Master.】","“I’m not actually going to leave him without military funds. The sooner they unify the continent, the sooner we can complete our mission.”","It was a mutually beneficial arrangement. Yue Fuguang had no intention of deliberately making things difficult for Emperor Mingxi, nor did she want to let the soldiers fighting for their lives on the front lines suffer.","【There’s also trouble brewing in Nanzhao.】","“What happened? Tell me quickly.” Life was so comfortable now. When she did not have to run around acting as a human sprinkler, her days were filled with the simple joy of teasing cats and playing with foxes.","【Nanzhao’s new emperor has ascended the throne and immediately carried out a massive purge of the court, uprooting the forces of the other princes and princesses.","Lan Xuancheng slaughtered so many people in the capital of Nanzhao that the streets nearly ran red with blood. Behind his back, the people of Nanzhao have taken to calling this month the Blood Moon.】","“Did the other princes and princesses simply let him kill them without resisting?”","【Of course they resisted. That is why the streets ran red with blood. Every side suffered casualties. But in the end, the emperor possesses the moral high ground. Regardless of how he came to power, most people will still support the emperor as the legitimate ruler.】","“What happened to those princes and princesses?”","【The new emperor originally intended to send them away to take up their fiefs. Now, however, they have all either been thrown into the imperial prison or placed under house arrest in their own residences.】","“With Nanyue on the verge of destruction, Nanzhao should be thinking about how to save itself. Yet the first thing this new emperor did after taking the throne was eliminate his rivals. This emperor... is difficult to assess! Still, his rise to power is good news for Dayan.”","News of Nanzhao’s Blood Moon soon reached the ears of Dayan’s court as well. Lan Xuan'er, who had already been preparing to return to Nanzhao, hesitated when she heard it.","Gan Tang, now the Sixth Princess Consort of Dayan, heard the news from the Sixth Prince. She did not dare delay for even a moment and hurried to the diplomatic residence at the Office of State Ceremonies.","“Xuan'er, listen to me. You cannot return to Nanzhao.” Gan Tang pulled her down to sit and earnestly tried to persuade her. “Once you go back, even if you have no desire for the throne, do you think the new emperor will believe you?”","Lan Xuan'er shook her head. “My second brother appears broad-minded, but in truth, he is extremely petty and vindictive. Mother has always favored me, and I’m sure he has kept that resentment in his heart.”","Gan Tang wore an expression that said she had expected as much. “Exactly. If you go back, you’ll either be thrown into the imperial prison or placed under house arrest.","“And you actually believed the edict summoning you home?”","Lan Xuan'er continued shaking her head. “If I had truly believed it, I would have returned the moment I received it. Why would I have waited until now?”","Perhaps Mother really had wanted to summon her home, but someone had clearly tampered with the matter. Although the edict was convincing enough to pass for genuine, Lan Xuan'er had still noticed something amiss. That was why she had delayed her departure until today.","“But Sister Tang, the world doesn’t know the edict is false. If I refuse to obey it, what will the people of Nanzhao think? How will the historians record it?” If they accused her of colluding with Dayan and plotting treason, the charge would be too grave for her to bear!","“If I don’t go back, won’t that simply prove the accusation true?”","Lan Xuan'er wanted to live, but she did not want to spend the rest of her life bearing such a disgrace. She would rather die with her innocence intact.","Gan Tang glared at her and lightly tapped her on the forehead. “You fool! You’re willing to throw your life away for a little empty reputation?","“History is written by the victors. Lan Xuancheng can write you down as a traitorous princess only if he manages to become the victor!”","A mocking smile curved Gan Tang’s lips. “Nanyue is about to fall. Tell me, how long do you think Nanzhao can withstand Dayan’s gunpowder?”","At the mention of gunpowder, Lan Xuan'er’s face instantly turned deathly pale. She had personally witnessed the destructive power of an explosion.","“My people in Nanzhao...”","She covered her face, tears spilling through the gaps between her fingers. “They had only just managed to survive the drought and the floods. And now they must suffer the devastation of war!”","Gan Tang gently patted her shoulder. “You should be grateful that the Divine Maiden ultimately took pity on the suffering people of Nanzhao. Otherwise, many would have died either in the floods or from the epidemic. How could there have been any chance for them to endure the suffering of war afterward?”","Lan Xuan'er nodded. Whenever she thought about it, her feelings were complicated. Yue Fuguang had always watched coldly from the sidelines as Nanzhao endured drought and floods.","Yet, in the end, she had still been unable to remain completely unmoved. Before the great rains came, she had issued a warning. Though no one knew who had first spread it throughout Nanzhao, it had truly saved many lives.","Then, once the floods had receded and an epidemic was about to break out, she had sent down sweet dew that cured disease. She had shown Nanzhao great kindness.","Gan Tang handed her a silk handkerchief. “Listen to your sister. Don’t go back. In the end, Nanzhao will certainly follow in Nanyue’s footsteps—and may fall even faster than Nanyue did.”","Lan Xuan'er stared at her with wide eyes. She saw little regret on Gan Tang’s face. In the end, she held back a sigh and had to admit, “The Nanzhao army is somewhat lacking.”","It could not compare with Nanyue’s, much less with the army of Dayan as it was now."]},{"number":529,"title":"Chapter 529: The Two Countries Are Bound to Go to War","paragraphs":["Gan Tang shook her head. “It’s not just a matter of military strength. There’s also the people’s support.”","She glanced at Lan Xuan’er. Seeing that her emotions had stabilized somewhat, she continued, “The people of Nanzhao no longer stand with the Nanzhao court. Their hearts belong to Dayan. After the floods and the Divine Maiden’s descent of healing dew, who do you think the people of Nanzhao will believe now?”","“You’ve forgotten that before the rains came, the court issued an edict ordering every city to close its gates and forbidding the people from going outside. How many people died because of that decree?”","“That edict... it definitely wasn’t issued by Mother Empress. Judging by the timing, she should still have been ill then! My mother was always compassionate toward her people. She would never...” Lan Xuan’er desperately tried to defend her late mother.","Gan Tang gently patted Lan Xuan’er’s hand, soothing the agitated girl. Her voice was tender. “Silly girl, when did I ever say that the edict was issued by Her Imperial Majesty? According to the information my people gathered, control of the government had already fallen into the hands of several of your older siblings by then.”","“But the world doesn’t know that. The people don’t know. My mother will never be able to shake off the blame!”","Gan Tang gave a confident little laugh. “Who says she can’t? As long as you live well, you can plead with the Divine Maiden someday to set the record straight. Wouldn’t that be resolved with a single word from her?”","“Didn’t I just tell you? The people of Nanzhao stand with Dayan. Nanzhao won’t merely fall—it will fall soon. Lan Xuancheng himself is a loser. As for the historical records concerning your mother, they will certainly be written by Dayan!”","“So you have to stay alive. You have to live well! For the sake of your mother’s reputation after death, you absolutely cannot let anything happen to you.”","Lan Xuan’er, who had been unable to make up her mind, finally settled on an answer. After drinking a cup of hot tea, she felt much more at ease. It seemed that she had once again found a reason to stay and keep living.","She carefully studied Gan Tang’s complexion. Her skin was fair, her cheeks rosy, and her eyes and brows were filled with smiles. “Sister Tang, it seems your husband really is just as wonderful as the rumors say.”","Lan Xuan’er was genuinely happy for Gan Tang. Although their marriage had begun because the former emperor of Nanyue had harbored ulterior motives and forcibly made Gan Tang marry him, judging from the situation now, his ill intentions had accidentally resulted in something good.","Gan Tang smiled. “My husband and I don’t have to worry about state affairs. After all, His Majesty, the Crown Prince, and the Divine Maiden are all holding up the sky in Dayan. Even if it collapses, someone will shield us from the storm.”","She playfully winked at Lan Xuan’er. “These days, deciding what to eat has become the biggest problem I face!”","Lan Xuan’er cupped her face and looked her over from side to side. “You really have filled out a little!”","Gan Tang lightly slapped her hand away. “Why are you stating such an obvious truth?”","She had heard their prince say that the Divine Maiden possessed a kind of weight-loss pill. He had told her to eat without worry—if she really grew too fat, he would kneel and beg the Divine Maiden to grant him one.","To win the Divine Maiden over, he had already begun secretly collecting all sorts of exquisite treasures.","While things were harmonious between Gan Tang and Lan Xuan’er, the Xi brothers sat facing each other next door, the atmosphere heavy and tense.","“Are you really going back?” Xi Ling poured Xi Yuanshan a cup of water.","Xi Yuanshan gave a helpless, bitter smile. “Father has summoned us. This is already the third letter urging us to return. We can’t delay it any longer.”","Xi Ling’s expression darkened. “He just wants to drag us back there to serve as... cannon fodder. Yes, cannon fodder!” That was the inner voice he had heard the last time he met Goddess Yue.","After witnessing the power of Dayan’s gunpowder, Xi Ling had to admit that the comparison was painfully apt.","Xi Yuanshan treated the tea in his cup like wine meant to drown his sorrows and downed it in one gulp. “What difference does knowing that make? We are his sons and his subjects. How could we disobey an order from our royal father?”","“Why couldn’t we?” Xi Ling slammed his fist onto the table. The teapot and teacups rattled with a crisp clatter. “If you ask me, you’re just too honest!”","He looked at this nominal older brother—his actual cousin—with an exasperated, frustrated expression. “He may be your father, but he gave you barely any parental care. Though you are a prince, you have neither military power nor the emperor’s favor. What can you do if you go back?”","“Become some minor official and lead a group of cannon fodder into battle?” Xi Ling sneered. “By the time you get there, you probably won’t even touch the hem of a Dayan soldier’s robes before you’re killed by their gunpowder!”","When Xi Yuanshan lowered his head and said nothing, Xi Ling continued driving the point home. “If you die, that’s the end of it. But what about your mother and your uncle? You’re their only child.”","“But don’t worry. If the worst comes to pass, I’ll support them in their old age!” Both their families had few children. Xi Ling had only two full siblings.","“Nanzhao...” As a former citizen of Nanzhao, Xi Yuanshan knew the strength of the Nanzhao army all too well. Nanyue would be followed by Nanzhao. He felt a pang of regret. “I should have brought them out sooner.”","He glanced at Xi Ling. “And... Uncle and Aunt...”","Seeing his cautious expression, Xi Ling smiled. “Did you really need to ask? I had already secretly brought them to Huacheng. Did you think I would let them keep soaking in floodwater?”","“When did this happen? Why has Mother never mentioned it in her letters?” Xi Yuanshan was so excited that he nearly jumped out of his chair.","Seeing that Xi Yuanshan finally no longer looked so lifeless, Xi Ling calmly smiled. He slowly finished his cup of tea before saying, “I told Aunt not to mention it.”","He raised an eyebrow at Xi Yuanshan. “Your side isn’t exactly clean. If someone who shouldn’t hear about it happened to learn the news, we’re thousands of miles apart. We might not be able to protect them.”","He had never dared underestimate Xi Yan’s methods. Their father, like Bei Ji, was a shrewd and calculating emperor.","By comparison, Emperor Mingxi of Dayan seemed much more simple-minded.","Emperor Mingxi: “You’re calling me simple-minded? Your whole family is simple-minded!” [Image of a screaming marmot]","“So you really intend to go back and serve as cannon fodder for that so-called father of yours?”","Xi Yuanshan nodded. “One of us has to return. Given your identity... I have no choice but to go.”","“Xiqiang hasn’t declared war on Dayan yet. As long as Father insists, Emperor Mingxi can’t very well force us to stay.”","Dayan had no reason to clash head-on with Xiqiang over the two of them at this critical juncture. It simply wouldn’t be worth it!","Xi Ling’s face was full of indignation. “Who doesn’t know that war between the two countries is inevitable?”"]},{"number":530,"title":"Chapter 530: Returning to One's Country and Returning Home","paragraphs":["“Before we completely fall out, we still have to keep up appearances. Neither of us has much real power in our hands. We don’t even qualify to be pieces on the chessboard.”","Especially after spending more than a year in Dayan, the two brothers had been deliberately—or perhaps unintentionally—excluded from the center of power by the imperial court.","Whenever they thought about it, both brothers felt stifled. Hadn’t they stayed in Dayan because they were following their imperial father’s secret order? And now they had been mercilessly abandoned.","Xi Ling had once been the emperor’s most favored son. At the thought of this, his face flushed red. “Why didn’t I seize more power back then?”","He had plenty of capable people under his command, but most of them had been given to him by the emperor. Now, those people had become swords hanging over his head—harbingers of his doom.","He had no idea how many of them were truly loyal to him. After confirming his identity, he had spent the past few months distinguishing between and purging those who had once followed and protected him, but might now silently take his life to save themselves.","Seeing that he could not persuade him otherwise, Xi Ling could only say, “Then when are you planning to leave? I’ll see you off.”","Xi Yuanshan hurriedly waved his hand. “Don’t! Since you’re pretending to be ill, you should make it convincing. Half a month is nowhere near enough. Ideally, you should keep pretending until Xiqiang goes to war with Dayan.”","Xi Ling smiled bitterly and nodded. “I understand. Take care on the road, and don’t trust anyone too easily.” Including that father of ours.","Thinking of the ambitious Princess Consort Yi still residing in his cousin’s princely estate, Xi Ling knew it would be difficult for him to remain completely uninvolved. He could not help warning him, “That Princess Consort Yi of yours is up to no good. If...if you really can’t keep her under control, then find someone else to share your bed.”","A flash of coldness passed through Xi Yuanshan’s eyes at the thought of the troublesome woman in his estate. Although he was in Dayan, he was still the master of Prince Yi’s estate. As long as he wanted to know what was happening there, nothing could escape his notice.","Everything that woman had done was pushing the entire estate toward destruction!","“I know what I’m doing.” Xi Yuanshan’s voice was deep and heavy as he continued drinking cup after cup of tea. Seeing him like this, Xi Ling suddenly lost the desire to continue the conversation.","“What? Xi Yuanshan has returned to his country too?”","Yue Fuguang was on her way back to Dayan at that moment. In another half a day, she would arrive at the capital, Shangjing.","[He just set out. Xi Yan has urged them to return several times already. It would be difficult to justify staying any longer. Xiqiang hasn’t gone to war with Dayan yet, so he can’t do what Beiyue did.]","“Xi Ling didn’t return with him?” Thinking of his background, Yue Fuguang wondered if Xi Yuanshan and Xi Ling were the real and fake princes who had been switched at birth.","“Does Xi Yan already know Xi Ling’s identity?” Over the past two years, she had watched coldly as Xi Yan’s affection for this son diminished year by year.","[He probably found out. For the sake of his reputation, Xi Yan could keep Xi Ling alive as long as he denied him any power. But now that the world is in chaos, he wants to eliminate every destabilizing factor within the country.]","Yue Fuguang tossed a grape into her mouth. “So Xi Ling is one of the destabilizing factors that needs to be eliminated?”","[After so many years as father and son, Xi Ling understands Xi Yan. Before Xi Yan could make a move, Xi Ling had already purged everyone he had placed around him.]","Yue Fuguang nodded. She did not ask whether any innocent people had been caught up in it all. There was no point. None of it had anything to do with them.","[Now that you’re returning to the capital, can you take some time to rest?]","With her host’s lazy temperament, it was already impressive that she had managed to focus on one task for several consecutive months. Constantly flying from place to place was no easy feat.","“This time, I won’t be needed until the people have planted the new crops.”","When Old Madam Yu and the others asked her about it, Yue Fuguang gave them the same answer she had given Little Zhu.","The wrinkles on Old Madam Yu’s face seemed to multiply from her smile. “That’s good, that’s good!”","She pulled Yue Fuguang down to sit beside her. “Your grandmother specifically asked the farmers on the estate. Because of our Fuguang, the fields aren’t short of water anymore, and the crops have only just begun to be harvested. It’ll take at least a month to plant all the new crops.”","Madam Zhang took Yue Fuguang’s right hand. “That’s wonderful. You’ll be able to stay home for a while this time. Your mother and grandmother can make sure you’re properly nourished.”","She stroked the small hollow between Yue Fuguang’s fingers, which had almost filled out. “My poor child. You’ve suffered so much. You’ve lost weight.”","There was no solution to the problem of a mother believing her daughter looked too thin. Even now that Yue Fuguang had firmly established herself as the Divine Maiden, she could do nothing but softly reassure her, “Mother, I’ve grown taller. I haven’t lost weight.”","She pointed at Cuizhu. “If you don’t believe me, ask Cuizhu. I’m actually eating half a bowl of rice more than I usually do.”","Old Madam Yu immediately said, “As long as you can eat, that’s what matters!”","She glanced at Yu Ningxuan and the other girls in the main hall. “The first priority for the girls of our family is to stay healthy. It isn’t worth starving yourselves just so outsiders can praise you for being as delicate as a willow in the breeze or for having an elegant figure!”","Yue Fuguang was surprised. “Grandmother, has someone been dieting to look pretty?” Her gaze swept over the sisters of the Yu family. “I have slimming pills. Eat to your hearts’ content. If you really gain weight, just take one pill and you’ll slim right back down.”","“As for those men who value thinness above all else, they aren’t worthy of the girls of the Yu family.”","Old Madam Yu’s expression turned solemn as she addressed the girls. “Did you all hear what your younger sister said? The girls of our family have their maternal family to rely on. You don’t need to humble yourselves or make things difficult for yourselves just to please your husbands!”","“If you grovel and lower yourselves, you’ll only bring shame to Fuguang’s reputation!”","The girls immediately agreed. The eldest, Yu Ningxuan, spoke up first. “Grandmother and Sister, don’t worry. We sisters have our pride. We would never do such things.”","“Grandfather’s last letter said he had found a potential match for Second Sister—the eldest son of the Feng family. How did it go?”","“Little Zhu, did you find anything suspicious in Feng You’s life from the time he was born until now?”","[No. He was raised according to the model of a refined young nobleman. He’s talented, courteous, devoted, and not at all chauvinistic. His character is quite good too. He genuinely cares for your sister.","As far as I know, when he learned that he was going to meet your second sister, he was so happy that he couldn’t sleep for several nights. As a result, he showed up to meet her with dark circles under his eyes!","He still hasn’t received a reply from the Yu family, and he’s regretting everything now. He thinks he must have made a poor impression and that the Yu family didn’t approve of him. Ha-ha! At the moment, he’s wondering whether he should ask his father, Feng Tang, who has just returned home, to sound out your opinion.]"]},{"number":531,"title":"Chapter 531: Goddess Temple","paragraphs":["“Sound you out?” Yue Fuguang stared blankly. “It’s my second older sister who’s going on a blind date with him. Why would he need to sound me out?”","【Because your second older sister is a total sis-con! She announced ages ago that she wouldn’t marry unless you approved.】","Everyone else merely covered their mouths and chuckled at the system’s words, but Yu Ningxuan actually blushed shyly. From the flush in her cheeks, Yue Fuguang could tell that she was satisfied with Feng You and was only waiting for her to return and give her approval.","Second Aunt Yu picked up the conversation with a beaming smile. “We all think the young man seems quite decent, but we still weren’t entirely at ease, so we thought we’d wait until Fuguang came home before making a decision.”","Yue Fuguang nodded. “I don’t know Feng You well, but both Feng Xiu and Feng Tang are good men. I imagine Feng You is probably a good person too.”","【Master, if you didn’t already know how things turn out, that would be a terribly irresponsible thing to say!】","“You said it yourself—I already know how things turn out. Since everyone at home thinks he’s suitable and we haven’t found any problems, I can say whatever I like. In any case, Second Aunt and the others simply want some reassurance.”","【That’s true. Your family is more meticulous about choosing husbands for its daughters than the Crown Prince’s family is about choosing a wife for him. Finding someone like Feng You, who is suitable in every respect, really is an opportunity they can’t afford to miss.】","“My sisters deserve that kind of consideration, of course. But what kind of life they lead in the future will still depend on themselves.”","【Feng Tang and Lady Feng are both your staunch supporters, so they certainly won’t mistreat their eldest daughter-in-law. Feng Xiu is your study companion and Yu Ningxuan’s classmate. In the future, even after he marries, the sisters-in-law in the Feng family should get along well enough.】","“That’s also why I insist on finding them the right people instead of simply choosing families with impressive status. We’ll have to leave eventually!”","People’s hearts were fickle. The families who married her sisters only because of Yue Fuguang’s influence could not be relied upon forever!","This was when Yu Chongshan and his sons arrived. After hearing from the servants that the Seventh Young Miss had returned, they had happily hurried toward the rear courtyard.","Who would have thought that, the moment they entered the old madam’s courtyard, they would hear Yue Fuguang saying that they would eventually leave? The smile on Yu Chongshan’s face, which had creased it with countless lines, instantly froze. His leg even stumbled mid-step.","“Father!”","Yu Zhongchun, who was walking behind him, quickly caught hold of him. “Slow down, Father. Just because you heard your granddaughter was home doesn’t mean you should get so excited that you forget your health.”","“That’s right, Father. You’re not young anymore. You can’t be so reckless.”","“You little rascals! How dare you turn things upside down and start lecturing your father?”","Their playful banter eased some of the sorrow in their hearts.","Yue Fuguang and the others naturally heard the commotion in the courtyard and went to greet them at the door.","“Grandfather, Father, Uncles, you’re all off duty.”","Yu Chongshan’s face crinkled with an enormous smile. “Fuguang, when did you get back? If your grandfather had known you were home, I would have come back even earlier.”","“I only got back a little while ago.” Yue Fuguang helped Yu Chongshan sit down. “I’ll be staying home for quite some time this time, so we’ll have plenty of time to see each other.”","“Really?” Yu Chongshan’s eyes lit up at once. “That’s wonderful! Wonderful!”","“In a few days, when you’re all free, let’s take the whole family to my estate for a visit.” The weather was still a little hot, and it was also the season when the fruit at her estate was ripening.","Yu Zhongchun clapped his hands. “That’s an excellent idea, Fuguang. The chickens and ducks on the mountain should be nice and plump by now, and the mushrooms are in season too. Pine mushrooms are at their best around this time.”","“Father understands me.” Yue Fuguang nodded. “The wine I brewed last year should be ready to drink now as well. It’s good for the body, so Grandfather and Grandmother can drink it without worry.”","Seeing his eldest and youngest sons chatting animatedly, Yu Chongshan swallowed the scolding he had been about to give his gluttonous son and instead said, “Then it’s settled. Grandfather will look forward to enjoying a life of luxury with my granddaughter.”","Old Madam Yu was smiling as well. “Now that you mention it, Grandmother has been craving that fine wine you brewed yourself for ages. At last, I’ll finally get to taste it.”","“Grandmother, I guarantee that once you’ve had some, you’ll want more.”","【Of course she’ll want more! You used nothing but the finest ingredients. It’s mild and gentle, without any harshness, and extremely nourishing for an ordinary person’s body. Master, did you brew it especially for the elders in your family?】","“You think I was joking when I said I’d help them live to a hundred?”","The Yu family members exchanged glances. Their hearts somehow felt even more miserable.","As a result, what Emperor Mingxi saw at court the next morning was the four Yu men wearing dark circles under their eyes—darker even than those beneath the eyes of the eldest son of the Feng family.","What had happened? Fuguang was back, so they ought to have been overjoyed. Why did every one of them look as though they hadn’t slept well?","Emperor Mingxi kept his doubts to himself throughout the morning court session. Finally, after court was dismissed, he summoned the Yu family’s men and several other important ministers to the Imperial Study.","“Minister Yu, what’s the matter with all of you? Shouldn’t you be happy that Fuguang is back?”","Emperor Mingxi was worried that something might have gone wrong with Yue Fuguang.","She was now the pillar supporting the heavens of Great Yan—more important even than the emperor himself. If anything happened to her, the entire realm of Great Yan would tremble.","The Crown Prince also looked anxiously at Yu Chongshan. “Grand Minister Yu, is something wrong with my maternal aunt?”","Seeing that the imperial father and son had misunderstood, Yu Chongshan hurriedly waved his hands. “Your Majesty, Your Highness, Fuguang is perfectly fine. Aside from being a little thinner and looking somewhat tired, there’s nothing wrong with her.”","As for whether she was truly thinner or genuinely tired, the entire Yu family had unanimously decided that their child was simply tired and had lost weight.","“Last night, my sons and I were so happy that Fuguang had returned that we drank a few extra cups. We didn’t sleep well afterward, which has made us look foolish in Your Majesty’s eyes.” A trace of embarrassment appeared on Yu Chongshan’s face.","Embarrassment was contagious. After hearing Yu Chongshan’s explanation, Emperor Mingxi couldn’t help feeling guilty. Yue Fuguang had done all this for whom, if not for the stability of the House of Xie and the empire?","Ahem! Any disappointment and displeasure he had felt at not being informed of Yue Fuguang’s return immediately were completely replaced by guilt.","“Fuguang has indeed made tremendous sacrifices for Great Yan.”","He glanced at the people in the room. “Some time ago, General Xu reported that he had obtained a fine piece of jade. I intend to use it to carve a jade statue of Fuguang, so that the people may worship her.”","As soon as he heard this, Yu Chongshan stepped forward. “Your Majesty, do you mean to build a temple for Fuguang?”","“I have long intended to do so. Although there are already several temples dedicated to Fuguang in the mountains around the capital, they are ultimately too simple.”","He patted the stack of papers on his desk. “I had this plan several years ago: to build a magnificent Divine Maiden Hall dedicated solely to her.”"]},{"number":532,"title":"Chapter 532: Count My Family In","paragraphs":["“That’s why it took several years to gather all the materials.” Eunuch Qian distributed the papers on the table among the assembled officials.","“These are the architectural plans and the materials required, all of which the Crown Prince and I organized. We spent these past several years collecting the rarest materials. A few of them were even found in several cities of Southern Yue.”","Only after examining the various architectural drawings and lists of materials did everyone finally understand why their wealthy Emperor had needed several years to gather everything required to build a temple for the Grand Preceptor.","Even the various rare woods alone were worth a fortune and nearly impossible to obtain. The stone was all the finest jade-bearing rock, while the floor tiles were golden bricks that took several years to fully form.","The Emperor had said he had been preparing for several years, and he truly had not exaggerated in the slightest!","Receiving his father’s cue, the Crown Prince took over. “After several years of gathering materials from various sources, most of what we need has already been prepared. We are only waiting for the Directorate of Imperial Astronomy to select an auspicious day before officially beginning construction.”","He turned to Lu Qi, Minister of Works. “Minister Lu, this matter will require your careful attention.”","Lu Qi accepted the order excitedly. “Your Majesty, Your Highness, rest assured. This humble official will certainly not disappoint the Divine Maiden!”","This was a temple being built for the Divine Maiden. What an immeasurable merit it would bring!","Such an enormous opportunity had landed right in his lap. Of course he would hold on to it with all his might!","Yu Chongshan, Yu Zhongchun, and the other members of the Yu family also stepped forward together and bowed. “This humble official and his sons thank Your Majesty on Fuguang’s behalf for Your Majesty’s gracious favor!”","“Your Majesty, looking at the plans, the Divine Maiden’s statue will be about three meters tall. Will the piece of jade General Xu obtained be large enough? If it is not, my family has another fine piece of material. Perhaps—”","“Why not use my family’s?” Wu Yuanjing’s father, Wu Yong, had not even finished speaking when Minister of Rites Zhang Zhongping interrupted him and directly suggested using his own family’s jade.","“Minister Wu, what do you mean, use your family’s? Who among us hasn’t seen that piece of yours? The material is good, but it’s far too small. It simply isn’t worthy of the Divine Maiden!”","When it came to competing for the honor of providing the jade for the Divine Maiden’s statue, Wu Yuanjing was not the least bit intimidated by Zhang Zhongping, whose official rank was higher than his.","His son had once ridden in the Divine Maiden’s flying carriage. Naturally, he had to do everything he could to contribute to the construction of the Divine Maiden’s temple.","“Can yours really be larger than the piece His Majesty recently acquired?” As Minister of Rites, Zhang Zhongping had now completely forgotten all about etiquette.","Contributing to the Divine Maiden’s temple was a great deed that would earn blessings for one’s descendants. At a time like this, who still had the leisure to worry about etiquette?","The others also came to their senses amid the two men’s quarrel. While secretly cursing them for their cunning, they all began declaring that their own families possessed fine materials and were willing to contribute a share toward the Divine Maiden’s statue.","In their eyes, taking part in the construction of the Divine Maiden’s temple was already a tremendous merit. But providing the material for the statue was an even greater merit within that tremendous merit.","Even if it meant incurring the Emperor’s displeasure, they were determined to get involved. With so many people speaking up, His Majesty could hardly refuse them all.","“You...” Emperor Mingxi was rendered both exasperated and amused by the faces of his trusted ministers. They were all old foxes, after all. Since he had taken the lion’s share, he did have to leave them a little broth to drink.","“Your Majesties—His Majesty and I are aware of the several ministers’ desire to contribute to the Divine Maiden’s temple. However, as for the statue...” He glanced at Emperor Mingxi before continuing, “The piece of material General Xu obtained in the mountains of Ye City is just large enough.”","This was something he had secretly written to his maternal uncle about shortly before the two nations went to war, asking him to keep an eye out in Southern Yue. Of the Six Kingdoms, if one were to speak of where jade was most plentiful, Great Yan could rank among the top three.","But if one were to speak of where the finest jade came from, then Southern Yue was unquestionably the best.","“This...” As soon as they heard this, everyone refused to accept it. What did he mean, just large enough? Wouldn’t a three-meter Divine Maiden statue be far less imposing than one four or five meters tall?","Xie Zhiyan raised a hand, signaling them to calm down. “Several ministers, please hear me out.”","He pointed to the drawing of the statue. “The jade for the Divine Maiden’s statue is sufficient, but the lotus pedestal beneath her feet still requires a considerable amount of fine jade.”","“Your Highness, my family has a piece of emerald-green jade, translucent and delicate in texture. It would be most suitable for making the lotus pedestal.” Cai Xian was the first to step forward, having learned his lesson.","Wei Ping followed close behind. “Your Highness, my family possesses a piece of white jade as smooth and fine as mutton fat. It is exceptionally warm and lustrous, making it ideal for the lotus petals.”","“Your Highness, my family’s piece is a smoky violet color. Count my family in for the petals.” Wu Yuanjing thought to himself that if he could not have the meat, he absolutely had to get a taste of the broth.","Zhang Zhongping’s thoughts were no different. “The piece in my family is ice-blue and as clear as frozen water. It would be most suitable for the petals of the lotus pedestal beneath the Divine Maiden.”","“My family has a piece of pale jade passed down from our ancestors. Count us in for one of the petals as well.” Ling Yinghua cupped her hands toward the Crown Prince. In order to be selected, she had even brought out an heirloom passed down through the generations.","“My family...”","One voice followed another. Before the Yu family’s father and sons could even speak, the lotus pedestal beneath Yue Fuguang’s jade statue had already been assembled from nine different colors.","Yu Chongshan said, “Your Majesty, shouldn’t the Divine Maiden’s statue be holding a precious orb? My family will provide the orb.”","Emperor Mingxi nodded in agreement. He could refuse the others, but he had no way to reject the Yu family.","“Your Majesty, regarding the carving of the Divine Maiden’s statue, this humble official dares to ask: Which master sculptor have you invited?”","Yu Chongshan was deeply worried that the sculptor Emperor Mingxi had chosen might not be able to capture even a fraction of his granddaughter’s spirit.","At the thought of what Fuguang had said the previous evening, he imagined that, in the future, whenever the Yu family’s younger generations wished to admire the bearing of their Immortal Great-Aunt, they would have one more place to visit besides the portraits preserved in the family collection.","Emperor Mingxi smiled faintly. “You all know this person.” He gestured toward the only person present who had not been competing to offer up his family’s treasured collection. “Master Xuanmingzi, tell the several ministers about it.”","“Yes. In my youth, I studied stone carving for several years.” He nodded slightly to everyone, particularly the members of the Yu family. “My teacher, Master Gu Yang, should be on his way to the capital by now. Judging by the time, he should arrive within the next day or two.”","Everyone understood.","So that was why Xuanmingzi had seemed so unconcerned earlier. They had thought him aloof, but it turned out he had accepted an assignment that would earn even greater merit.","Xuanmingzi cupped his hands toward Emperor Mingxi. “We are deeply honored by Your Majesty’s favor. My teacher and I will devote every skill we possess to restoring even a fraction of the Divine Maiden’s magnificence. We only ask that we do not tarnish the Divine Maiden’s illustrious name.”","Yu Chongshan nodded slightly. With Gu Yang—the finest sculptor in all of Great Yan—working on the statue, his family’s Fuguang was certain to be immortalized properly. However...","“Master Xuanmingzi, if I remember correctly, Master Gu Yang put away his carving knife several years ago because of his poor health.”"]},{"number":533,"title":"Chapter 533: I Have to Go There Myself","paragraphs":["“The statue of the Divine Maiden will be a massive undertaking. Even with your assistance, can his body really withstand it?” Senior Mr. Yu was worried that the statue might not be finished before the sculptor himself passed away. That would only damage his granddaughter’s reputation, wouldn’t it?","“Senior Mr. Yu, please rest assured. My master is in excellent health and will certainly complete the statue of the Divine Maiden on time.” He had begged His Majesty for this assignment and even invoked his master’s name to secure it.","According to his junior fellow disciple’s letter, his master—the old man—had been so delighted to hear that he would be carving a statue for the Divine Maiden that he had nearly jumped three feet into the air.","Just moments earlier, someone had offered a hefty sum to commission a small piece from him, only to be refused on the grounds that he was advanced in years and no longer had the stamina. Master Gu had already put away his carving tools for good.","Yet the moment he heard that he was being invited to the capital to carve a three-meter-tall jade statue of the Divine Maiden, his master—who had been lying in bed drinking medicine—recovered before he had even finished the dose.","He had not waited a single day before packing up his belongings and hurrying toward the capital. If he knew that he had nearly lost the assignment because of concerns over his age and strength, he would probably have dropped dead on the road!","Afraid that Senior Mr. Yu might not believe him, Xuanmingzi continued explaining, “Although my master has lived in seclusion in the mountains these past years, several of his disciples still receive his instruction from time to time. His skills have not diminished in the slightest.”","Yu Chongshan nodded. “It seems this old man was worrying needlessly!”","He then asked about another matter. “Your Majesty, has the site for the Divine Maiden’s temple been decided?”","Emperor Mingxi and the Crown Prince exchanged a glance. The Crown Prince took over, saying, “Senior Mr. Yu, you may not know this, but Father has selected several possible sites. As for where it will ultimately be built, Father believes we should ask my maternal aunt.”","“Ask me?”","As soon as he had finished his duties for the day, Yu Chongshan had rushed straight to Yue Fuguang’s Brightmoon Pavilion and handed the final decision regarding the temple’s location to her.","Yue Fuguang had not expected Emperor Mingxi to be so thoughtful. He had even remembered to build her a temple so that she could be worshiped. She simply did not know whether she would still be able to enjoy the offerings of incense after leaving this world.","Even if she could not, however, she had left behind a legend in this world. The Divine Maiden’s temple would be the best proof of that. And that... was not bad at all.","Faced with the question Emperor Mingxi had thrown her way, Yue Fuguang pondered only briefly before saying, “Grandfather, tell His Majesty that the temple should be built on Lotus Mountain.”","“It’s only ten or twenty li from the eastern gate of the capital. It’ll be convenient for the people to leave the city and come up the mountain to offer incense.”","That place not only had beautiful scenery, but was also fairly close to her estate.","Since it was her temple, she naturally had to make certain arrangements to protect it and establish its sphere of influence. Even after she eventually left, her temple should stand unshaken through the passing of time and the changes of the world, becoming a true divine relic.","“Lotus Mountain?” Yu Chongshan considered the location, then nodded with a smile. “That’s a fine place. The mountains are lush, the waters clear, and it’s peaceful too.”","Yue Fuguang then took out two small jade bottles. “Grandfather, please deliver these two bottles of pills to Master Gu Yang.”","She pointed to the green jade bottle. “This is a Vitality-Nourishing Pill. It’s highly effective for those who are elderly and physically frail.”","Then she pointed to the white jade bottle. “This bottle contains Body-Strengthening Pills. With these two medicines, Master Gu should be able to complete the statue without any trouble.”","She had also felt that her grandfather’s concern was justified. Master Gu seemed to be nearly seventy years old. Asking an old man with one foot in the grave to undertake such a physically and mentally demanding task made her worry that something might go wrong and he might die before finishing it.","Her temple did not need to bear that sort of karmic burden. “Consider them an advance payment for their work.”","Yu Chongshan felt a pang at the thought of his granddaughter giving away such precious things, but he also felt that her action was prudent. It would help ensure the statue’s completion and win her an even better reputation.","“Your grandfather has seen the temple’s plans. Construction will begin this year, but it will probably take at least a year or two to complete.”","“That’s fine. Slow work produces fine results. Tell the Ministry of Works to take their time. There’s no need to rush.” Judging by the current progress of the Great Yan campaign, it would take more than two years to conquer all five kingdoms.","And that was only the occupation of their lands. Occupying them alone would not complete her task.","After all, the six kingdoms had only just been forced together. They could fall apart again at any moment. She still had to watch over their integration and turn them into one family.","That was the truly difficult part. She needed to think of a way to accomplish it.","Just as Yue Fuguang was pondering this, an opportunity soon presented itself.","“What? You’re saying that the Great Yan army has already fought its way into Gan City today?” Yue Fuguang’s hand paused as she carried a bowl of porridge. She had not even taken a bite of breakfast when the system brought her the excellent news that Gan City had fallen into Great Yan hands.","【That’s right, Host! When we went to Gan City last time, I set up an anchor point in the imperial palace. So even though we’re thousands of li away, I can still receive news from there promptly. You can rest assured—the information is completely reliable. Even the emperor doesn’t know yet!】","“System, you’ve really grown capable!” Yue Fuguang gave the system a big thumbs-up. “How are the casualties on both sides?”","【The Great Yan army used gunpowder to blast open the way, and suffered more than four thousand casualties in the battle. As for the Southern Yue army, more than thirty thousand were killed or wounded, while over seventy thousand were taken prisoner. Half of those surrendered voluntarily.","【Great Yan’s gunpowder was so terrifying that it scared the soldiers witless. They all shouted that the Divine Maiden had sent down heavenly thunder. Of course they surrendered!】","As Yue Fuguang ate her steamed buns, she asked the system, “What do you think? Should we give those who surrendered voluntarily a chance at wealth and glory? It could also help with the integration of the various kingdoms.”","【You mean have them join Great Yan and earn military merits alongside its army?】","“Look at it this way. Although Great Yan has taken the Southern Yue capital, a small portion of Southern Yue’s territory is still in the hands of the Southern Yue imperial family and its generals.","“Whether Great Yan’s army fights to take that land or the surrendered Southern Yue soldiers do it, the result will feel different to some of the Southern Yue civilians.”","War would inevitably cost lives. Rather than let the people of Southern Yue direct their hatred toward Great Yan, they might as well direct it toward their own countrymen.","The system clearly saw the ruthlessness behind Yue Fuguang’s plan. 【The Host’s idea is excellent. This may speed up the process of national and ethnic integration.】 Even if it failed to achieve that, Great Yan would lose nothing.","“There’s more. People from the same land understand one another best. Who knows? This surrendered army might bring us some unexpected gains.”","Yue Fuguang finished her breakfast in two or three bites. “No, I have to make the trip myself.”"]},{"number":534,"title":"Chapter 534: Can you see it too","paragraphs":["“Something like this—you could have just sent Wei Shouyi a telegram. Why make the trip yourself?”","“This is one of those matters where my personal presence will have the best effect. First, it will reassure them; second, it will serve as a warning. Since I’m giving them gunpowder, I have to make sure they use it for the right purposes.”","Yue Fuguang rose and headed outside, instructing Cuizhu as she went, “Cuizhu, go tell Grandmother and Mother that I have some business to attend to and will be away for a few days. I’ll be back soon, so they don’t need to worry.”","She also tossed her a hastily written letter. “Give this to Grandfather. He’ll know what to do.” She couldn’t be bothered to go to the palace herself to explain her plans to Emperor Mingxi. Whatever she decided, the emperor wouldn’t oppose it anyway.","She was informing them because the Ministry of Revenue and the Ministry of Works would need to guarantee these men’s logistical support, as well as arrange their future military merits and rewards.","Cuizhu followed her into the courtyard. When a flying carriage suddenly appeared before them, she couldn’t help asking, “My lady, where are you going? Shall I pack some things for you?”","Yue Fuguang waved her off. “No need. I’ll be back in two or three days.”","Turning around, she said to He Jin and Shen Chunying, “Only the two of you are coming with me this time.” Her carriage wasn’t large, and there was no need to bring anyone else.","Out of the corner of her eye, she spotted Dai Yuxing and Luo Shendong hurrying over. She waved at them. “You two stay behind and look after the place.”","She waved to everyone and departed in the carriage with a carefree flourish.","Dai Yuxing watched the flying carriage recede into the distance. Turning to Luo Shendong, he complained, “I’ve been held back by my gender! If I were like He Jin, could I follow the lady around all day too?”","“The lady treats the few of you better than she treats Yu Huaixian and the rest of us old men. Don’t you think that counts as gender discrimination?”","Luo Shendong gave him a light, disdainful look and said with her chest puffed out, “We’re more favored than you men. So what? The lady likes us. Do you dare object? If you want, I can mention it to her when she gets back.”","Dai Yuxing hurriedly shook his head and waved his hands. “I wouldn’t dare! Auntie, I was wrong. Please, whatever you do, don’t tell the lady.”","Seeing the two of them, Cuizhu smiled, shook her head, and went off to attend to her own tasks.","Inside the flying carriage, Shen Chunying’s eyes gleamed. “My lady, you’ve noticed too, haven’t you?”","Yue Fuguang gazed out at the cloudless blue sky and deliberately asked, “What do you mean?”","The smile on Shen Chunying’s face widened. “I mean my Shendong and Lord Dai...”","Yue Fuguang put on an expression of sudden realization. “Oh, that. Yes, I’ve noticed something going on.”","“Then, my lady, do you approve?”","“Me?” Yue Fuguang looked baffled. “It’s their business. As long as they both agree, that’s all that matters. They don’t need to ask me.”","She had no experience with romance, after all. If the two of them had fallen for each other and wanted to marry, she wouldn’t stop them. They were all her subordinates, and letting them pair off among themselves was rather convenient—at least the good water wouldn’t flow into someone else’s fields.","Shen Chunying looked troubled. “If they really get married, will they still be allowed to remain by your side?”","That was why Dai Yuxing and Luo Shendong had hesitated to make their feelings known even after realizing how they felt about each other.","Neither of them wanted to leave the lady’s side, but they were also in love.","Yue Fuguang paused. That was indeed a problem. Once people married, they were no longer solitary souls who only had themselves to worry about. “What do they want? Do they want to stay, or should I find Shendong another position?”","Whether she placed them in the civil administration or the military, it would only take a word from her. Both of them were capable, and they could make a name for themselves anywhere.","Shen Chunying hurriedly shook her head. “Naturally, they want to stay by your side. They don’t want to go anywhere else!”","She quickly stole a glance at Yue Fuguang’s expression. “Are you going to send them away, my lady?”","Seeing how cautious and worried she looked, Yue Fuguang chuckled. “I’ve grown accustomed to having all of you around. As long as you don’t want to seek opportunities elsewhere, I won’t drive you away.”","She wouldn’t be staying in Dayan for more than a few years anyway. There was no need to find another group of unfamiliar guards and make trouble for herself. What a hassle!","Shen Chunying and He Jin’s eyes lit up at the same time. “My lady, we’ll remember those words. You can’t go back on them!”","Yue Fuguang smiled and accepted the tea He Jin handed her. “This lady always keeps her word. Once spoken, even a galloping horse can’t catch it. The lot of you can rest easy and start families.”","“There is one condition, though. If you have children, you must let me decide what to do with them.” She couldn’t very well have the children grow up neglected while their parents were away.","[Host, we can only stay here for a few more years. There’s no chance of any latchkey children. And see? I told you those two had something going on, but you didn’t believe me.]","“I just don’t have any experience. How was I supposed to notice?”","[You may lack hands-on experience, but don’t you have theoretical knowledge? Did you waste all those romance novels and television shows?]","“Fictional romances aren’t the same as real life. Isn’t it perfectly normal that I couldn’t tell when they hid it so well?”","“My lady, we’ve arrived.”","He Jin’s soft voice roused Yue Fuguang from sleep. Her old habit from her previous life had never changed: she always got drowsy in a vehicle. She had been arguing with the system earlier, but at some point, she had fallen asleep without realizing it.","“He Jin, how long was I asleep?” Yue Fuguang lifted her head and looked out at the rising sun. After flying for more than ten hours, they had finally reached the skies above Gancheng.","“You slept for three and a half shichen.” As she helped Yue Fuguang wash up, He Jin asked, “My lady, shall we have breakfast at General Xu’s residence, or would you like to eat now?”","Yue Fuguang brushed her hand across the tabletop, and a spread of steaming hot Western and Chinese breakfast dishes appeared. “The food at their place may not be as good as what I brought.”","At General Xu’s residence, General Xu nervously rubbed his hands together. “Brother Wei, do you think the Grand Preceptor will come to the general’s residence for breakfast?”","He glanced outside once again. “By my reckoning, the Grand Preceptor should have reached Gancheng by now!” No one knew how many times that morning he had looked toward the courtyard entrance.","Wei Shouyi, who was more familiar with Yue Fuguang, remained as steady as an old hound. He picked up the bowl of porridge on the table and took a large gulp.","“Hey! The Grand Preceptor hasn’t arrived yet, and you’re already eating?” General Xu reached out dramatically. If the porridge hadn’t already gone down Wei Shouyi’s throat, his expression suggested he might have tried to claw it back out.","“Do you know this is a grave offense?” General Xu had spent years stationed at the border. Although he had met Yue Fuguang only a few times, he knew quite a bit about her deeds."]},{"number":535,"title":"Chapter 535: You too are the people of my Great Yan Kingdom.","paragraphs":["Especially regarding the matters of the crown prince and the queen, he and the entire Xu family were no less grateful to Yue Fuguang than the royal family. They even regarded her as more important than the emperor, which led to that disrespectful remark.","Wei Shouyi was nodding while munching on a soft bun. \"I know, I know. But look at the time outside. It's long past the time for the Grand Tutor to have his meal.\"","With a beaming smile on his face, he said, \"You know I've been by the Grand Tutor's side for quite a while. If he doesn't come at this time, he must have eaten on his own.\"","\"You really understand me, Minister Wei.\" Yue Fuguang's voice suddenly rang in their ears. General Xu was so startled that he jumped to his feet.","The bun in Wei Shouyi's hand dropped to the ground. \"Grand Tutor!\"","General Xu took the lead and rushed outside. Before he even caught a glimpse of Yue Fuguang, he was walking quickly while bowing with his hands clasped. \"Your subordinate, Xu Su, is late to welcome you. Please forgive me, Grand Tutor!\"","\"General Xu, there's no need for such formalities.\" Xu Su only heard Yue Fuguang's voice. He looked around the courtyard of the General's Mansion but couldn't see Yue Fuguang and his entourage anywhere.","\"General, look! The Grand Tutor is in the sky!\" Wei Shouyi, who followed out later, clearly had more experience in finding Yue Fuguang.","The two bowed respectfully towards the beautiful carriage floating in the void. But their ears were filled with the shouts of the nearby villagers. \"The Divine Maiden! It's the Divine Maiden!\"","\"The Divine Maiden has finally come to Gan City!\"","\"Welcome, Divine Maiden!\"","Nearby were the rapid breathing sounds of the soldiers of the Great Yan Army. The moment they saw the carriage in the air, all the soldiers of the Great Yan Army stationed in Gan City, regardless of what they were doing the moment before, sheathed their swords, tidied their uniforms, and then knelt on one knee solemnly and shouted in unison, \"Greetings to the Grand Tutor!\"","Their actions made the surrendered soldiers from the Southern Yue Army envious. Some smart ones had already started to follow the example of the Great Yan Army and shout.","\"Liu Qi, what are you getting involved for?\" Some of them were captives, and some had surrendered voluntarily. Although they were now half part of the Great Yan Army, they still felt inferior to the Great Yan soldiers psychologically.","The young man named Liu Qi, although looking haggard, had bright eyes. \"Squad leader, we are also people and soldiers of the Great Yan. Isn't it right to pay respects to our own Grand Tutor?\"","\"Well... it seems to make sense!\" The squad leader seemed to be easily convinced by the young soldier named Liu Qi.","The big - bearded man beside the vice - squad leader mumbled in a low voice in agreement, \"That makes perfect sense.\"","Saying that, he changed from kneeling on both knees to kneeling on one knee. \"Wu Dayong, a surrendered soldier from the Southern Yue, greets the Grand Tutor.\"","Liu Qi gritted his teeth silently. Why was this guy adding extra drama to himself?","The vice - squad leader rolled his eyes. \"Yao Facai, a surrendered soldier from the Southern Yue, greets the Grand Tutor!\" Yao Facai felt a bit ashamed for the first time in his life when shouting his own name.","Yao Facai thought: Yao Fugui would have been more reserved and decent than Yao Facai!","\"Surrendered soldiers from the Southern Yue...\" In an instant, a large group of soldiers in Southern Yue military uniforms knelt down. Yue Fuguang could see it all clearly from the flying carriage.","This trip of hers was precisely aimed at these people.","\"The villagers down there are so enthusiastic to see the Grand Tutor. They're no less enthusiastic than the people of the Great Yan,\" Shen Chunying said, looking out of the window.","She could faintly see that the villagers below had started to burn incense candles in their direction. The flames passed through the morning mist and caught the eyes of the three of them.","Yue Fuguang put down her teacup. \"I'll go and meet the people of Gan City in the Great Yan and all the soldiers.\"","\"Look! It's the Divine Maiden! The Divine Maiden has come out!\"","\"The gaze of the gods is finally upon us!\" Yue Fuguang's appearance pushed the enthusiasm of the villagers below to a climax. Amid the curling smoke, they saw the Divine Maiden stepping on the illusory shadow of a lotus flower, coming down step by step from above.","\"Woo! Woo! Thank you, Divine Maiden!\"","\"Thank you, Divine Maiden!\"","\"If it weren't for the Divine Maiden, my son would have been taken away by the plague two months ago!\"","\"My little girl is only three years old. If it weren't for the Divine Maiden, our family's precious darling would be gone!\" The couple had given birth to five sons before having this little daughter. The child was delirious with fever at that time. If it had been a little later, the father and daughter would have been separated by death.","\"If it weren't for the Divine Maiden, our whole family would have perished!\" As Yue Fuguang walked down step by step, she felt a pure and strong power of faith filling her body. She felt that at this moment, even without wearing the Boots of Lotus Steps, she could fly in the air without any hindrance.","[Host, you've become stronger again! You're not human! Not human at all!]","Yue Fuguang resisted the urge to roll her eyes and gritted her teeth. [System, don't you understand? It's extraordinary! Extraordinary!]","Although this ability couldn't be taken with her when she was born or when she died, she could enjoy the moment. Yue Fuguang was still very happy in her heart. But it was a bit too much for the system to say that she was not human!","Yue Fuguang waved her sleeve gently, and a huge Dharma image appeared behind her. The Dharma image lowered its eyes, as if looking at the villagers of Gan City below.","At the same time, her voice also drifted over Gan City. \"I, Yue Fuguang, have received your gratitude.\"","She raised her right hand slightly. \"Get up and speak.\"","\"Thank you, Divine Maiden!\" The deafening shouts echoed over Gan City, spreading far and wide and startling countless birds in the forest.","But just as the birds flew into the air, they all fell back to the ground one after another. They lowered their heads human - like, touching the ground with their beaks, as if they were also paying respects to Yue Fuguang.","[Host, did you do something to these birds?]","Yue Fuguang resisted the urge to roll her eyes again. [Do I look like such a boring person to you?] She herself was also very puzzled by these submissive birds.","Could it be that the \"overbearing\" aura on her body couldn't be hidden anymore? Even the birds could smell it!","This thought flashed through her mind for a moment. She stopped dwelling on it and turned to business. \"Now Gan City is the land of the Great Yan. You are all the people of the Great Yan.\""]},{"number":536,"title":"Chapter 536: Is That It","paragraphs":["Yue Fuguang looked down at the devout people of Gancheng. When she told them that they, too, were now citizens of Dayan, there was no disturbance of the sort she had expected.","Some people looked unhappy, but judging by their clothes, Yue Fuguang chose to ignore them. What she saw on the faces of the vast majority was joy. They did not reject their new identity—in fact, some even seemed excited.","She continued, “Whatever the people of Dayan have, you shall have as well.”","The implication was obvious. Sure enough, one of the sharper-minded villagers immediately summoned his courage and asked, “Goddess, does that mean we’ll be able to plant the high-yield crops from Dayan, too?”","A few people whispered among themselves, “Sweet potatoes, potatoes, corn... If we can plant even one of those, we’ll never have to worry about starving again!”","“Exactly! I never even dared dream that we’d be able to grow those crops so soon.”","Only after the people below had gradually quieted down did Yue Fuguang speak again. “As I said, you are now citizens of Dayan. Naturally, you may plant every crop that the people of Dayan possess.”","“Not only high-yield sweet potatoes, potatoes, and corn, but also the tastier fruits and vegetables—as long as you are citizens of Dayan, you will all have the opportunity to grow them.”","Newly conquered territories would be given new land policies on a trial basis. With these benefits dangled before them, the people would naturally stand on the side of the imperial court.","As for the wealthy and nobles who opposed them, if they dared make trouble, cutting down a few of them to establish authority would be just fine.","Sensing a fleeting murderous intent from its host, the System changed the admonition it was about to make into: 【Host, is Dayan’s supply of improved seeds sufficient?】","「This year’s harvest was abundant. It should be enough to plant in Nanyue.」 Not all the land would be used for those three crops, after all. Rice was still the staple grain here.","【Was adding something to the rainwater all in preparation for this?】","Although this year had supposedly brought drought, once the grain harvested across Dayan had been weighed and calculated, the total had already far surpassed that of any previous year. It was truly a bumper harvest!","「Otherwise, why would I do it? Adding those ingredients costs points!」 Yue Fuguang tightened her grip on her purse. Spirit-infused liquid filled with vitality was painfully expensive.","Boom!","At her words, the people below erupted completely. Weeping, shouting, and laughter blended together—a full display of the many flavors of life.","Yue Fuguang paid no further attention to the people who were happier than if they had picked up a fortune. Instead, she turned her gaze toward the military camp stationed outside the city.","The troops below soon sensed her attention as well. Xu Shu and Wei Shouyi had already galloped to the camp and received word of her arrival. They bowed toward Yue Fuguang and said, “My lady, please give us your orders. This subordinate and our brothers will do whatever it takes—even give our lives—to fulfill your wishes!”","“We are willing to die for you, my lady!”","“We are willing to die for you, my lady!”","Yue Fuguang nodded. “Now, most of Nanyue’s territory has already fallen under Dayan’s rule. However, the people of Fu City, Yi City, and Jiang City are still suffering.”","“General Xu, you must rescue them as quickly as possible.”","Yue Fuguang’s words sounded lofty and righteous, but the System could not help mocking her. 【Host, that was so hypocritical. Far too hypocritical!】","「Are you saying the people of those three cities aren’t suffering?」","Faced with that question, the System genuinely had nothing to say. The Nanyue royals and nobles who had fled had all poured into those three places. The local people were now suffering one hardship after another and were practically on the verge of rebellion.","“Yes! We shall obey your command. We swear to take the three cities, even at the cost of our lives!”","“We swear to take the three cities!”","“We swear to take the three cities!”","Yue Fuguang put on an expression of great satisfaction. “General Xu, the surrendered soldiers are now soldiers of Dayan as well. You will treat them equally and grant them the same benefits as the soldiers of Dayan.”","Xu Shu deliberately asked, “What exactly do you mean, my lady?”","“Build merit, establish a career, and earn honors for your wives and children.”","Yue Fuguang’s eight words rang across the skies above Gancheng like thunder, echoing through the hearts of the soldiers and civilians of Nanyue.","Build merit, establish a career, and earn honors for your wives and children!","Even as surrendered generals and soldiers, they could still build merit and establish careers just like the army of Dayan, earning honors for their families!","A young general with a resolute face suddenly stepped forward. Dropping to one knee, he proclaimed, “My lady, I am You Minzhi, formerly a Nanyue general and now a surrendered officer. I am willing to serve as vanguard and assist the army of Dayan in taking the remaining three cities of Nanyue!”","Yue Fuguang raised an eyebrow. “You’re from the You family?”","The young general paused. He had not expected the Goddess to know of the You family. Overcome with excitement, he replied, “Yes. I am You Minzhi, from the second branch of the You family!”","Yue Fuguang nodded. “General Xu, did you hear that? Your vanguard commander has volunteered for battle. The You family is a renowned military clan. I imagine Young General You will not disappoint me.”","You Minzhi excitedly cupped his fists. “I swear to take the three cities and will not let you or the general down!”","Yue Fuguang shook her head slightly. “The remaining three cities are merely small places. Young General You, do your best, but there is no need to risk your life! Your lives are of great importance to Dayan. We still have Nanzhao, Beili, and Xiqiang to deal with.”","“General Xu, when attacking the cities, lead with explosives and do everything possible to minimize casualties among our troops!”","Upon hearing this, not only You Minzhi and the other members of the You family, but also the ordinary soldiers of Nanyue and the troops of Dayan, were moved to the point of secretly wiping away tears.","They had assumed that even if they were given the chance to build merit and establish careers, they would have to exchange their lives for it. Who could have known that the Goddess had never intended to use their lives as cannon fodder?","Explosives—they had personally experienced their power. With such weapons, what city could they possibly fail to take? If there truly was one, then they could only blame themselves for being useless!","“Dayan will not let down those who do not let down Dayan.” The words were both a warning and a reassurance, meant to put their minds at ease.","【Host, is that it?】","The System stared blankly as Yue Fuguang climbed back into her flying carriage and lay down again. They had flown for more than ten hours, yet Yue Fuguang had appeared for less than half an hour—and had already won over both the hearts of the people and the loyalty of the army.","How did it know? A large amount of faith value was spilling out from Yue Fuguang and being picked up by the System, allowing it to repair its damaged data. The process was slow, but effective.","「What else should I do? Stay behind for a banquet?」 Xu Shu and Wei Shouyi had genuinely wanted to throw her a grand feast, but Yue Fuguang had refused.","「I forgot to ask you—how did Prince Cheng... no, Emperor Chenghe, die?」","The army of Dayan had stormed into Gancheng. The emperor was dead, while the imperial family and several high-ranking officials and nobles had fled. After Gan Sheng’s death, several of his children had also disappeared."]},{"number":537,"title":"Chapter 537: Are You Trying to Smear Their Reputation","paragraphs":["These nobles posed a threat to the future unified Dayan. She did not want Dayan to become another Great Qin.","How could she win the hearts of the six kingdoms...? The methods from her homeland were not entirely suited to this world, where productivity was low and the people’s thinking was comparatively rigid. More importantly, the kingdoms were already divided, and their people had not yet suffered enough. Rapid integration would be difficult—extremely difficult.","[He was ultimately ambushed and killed by men left behind by Gan Sheng when Gan City fell.]","[At the time, Emperor Mingxi’s reach had not yet extended to certain areas of Gan City. A force from Panshan still operated there, though it had originally been suppressed by the people behind Gan Sheng.","Who could have expected Dayan to begin clearing out Panshan’s strongholds along the border between the two countries, allowing some surviving fugitives to slip into Gan City and reinforce the faction supporting Gan Sheng?","When the Dayan army arrived, they did not think of defending the city. Instead, they killed the emperor first!]","“So that indirectly helped Xu Shu and the others? At least it saved quite a few soldiers on both sides.”","“Are the people supporting Gan Sheng’s faction in league with Zhao Quan’an?” Yue Fuguang suddenly thought of a question. “Then are they currently supporting Gan Minghao’s succession, or do they want Gan Mingyu on the throne?”","Although they were both sons of Gan Sheng, the difference between them was considerable.","[Host, neither Gan Minghao nor Gan Mingyu will be able to take the throne.]","Yue Fuguang’s fingers, which were holding a grape, paused. “Why? Did the empress still make a move against Gan Minghao?","“And what about Consort Liang’s son? Didn’t you say that Emperor Chenghe, Gan Chengyuan, ultimately refrained from killing Gan Mingyu because of their agreement, even after Gan Mingyu lost the protection of his birth mother?”","[Host, refraining from killing him and not making a move against him are two different things. By my calculations, neither of them has many days left to live.","“Although it feels somewhat cruel, their survival truly is detrimental to Dayan’s unification.”]","The system’s merit data shifted again, but was quickly overwritten by the gossip system’s data.","Even the system now understood that, for the sake of lasting peace and stability for the vast majority of people, this was no time for mercy.","Upon hearing the news, Yue Fuguang did not discuss the matter further. Whether Panshan wanted to put one of them on the throne or the other, both would ultimately perish.","“System, spread the news that Gan Chengyuan was killed by Panshan’s people, along with everything Panshan has done over the years—how they manipulated the governments of Southern Yue and the other kingdoms and exploited the common people.","“The more they try to hide it, the more determined I am to put them before the eyes of the entire world.”","[Host, you want to ruin their reputation and turn Panshan into a despised target that everyone wants to stamp out?]","“Would that be a bad thing? The common people will hate them, while the imperial court and the nobility will be wary of them. Let’s see how they survive after that.","“System, from now on, any newly emerging organization with ties to the criminal underworld is to be labeled a Panshan offshoot.”","[Wouldn’t that be rather arbitrary?]","“So what? Organizations involved in the criminal underworld aren’t exactly good things to begin with. Dayan must ban Panshan just as my homeland banned drugs. Anything that changes its name but not its nature deserves to be destroyed!~”","[If you really manage to accomplish that, Panshan will unquestionably become an evil organization—feared by the people and viewed with suspicion by those in power.]","“Have you heard? The emperor of Southern Yue was actually killed by an organization called Panshan!”","“Panshan? What kind of organization is that? It can even kill an emperor?”","“Exactly! Is it true? I heard the emperor of Southern Yue was executed by the Dayan army after they stormed the imperial city.”","In a teahouse in the capital of Southern Zhao, groups of three or five Southern Zhao citizens gathered around tables, drinking tea and chatting.","Ever since Southern Zhao had suffered drought, followed by floods and an epidemic that had nearly spread on a massive scale, how long had it been since these moderately wealthy merchants had been able to gather for tea and idle conversation?","Today, the Restful Tea House had finally reopened, drawing in a large number of its old customers. As soon as they opened their mouths, they began discussing the latest rumors from their neighbor’s household.","After all, discussing current affairs in their own country carried risks. There was no such concern when discussing sensational news from the neighboring kingdom.","“That could hardly be false!” A well-fed, comfortably dressed man in his forties waved his folding fan and spoke with certainty. “The news has spread throughout Southern Yue. We’re simply farther away, so quite a few people haven’t heard it yet.”","Seeing everyone around him prick up their ears, he immediately became even more eager to tell the story. “I heard this came straight from the Southern Yue imperial palace. There were quite a few people beside His Majesty when he died.”","He pointed his folding fan toward Southern Yue. “They’ve already confirmed that the ones who carried out the attack were people left behind by the late emperor. Those two—uncle and nephew—paid for one life with another. You could say they’ve settled the score.”","He shook his head. “But these people from Panshan have reached far too deep. They even dare interfere in imperial affairs. We ordinary folk had better stay well away from people like that.”","The gray-robed man seated across from him nodded in agreement. “Brother Liao is right. Panshan’s people are truly despicable.”","He placed his teacup heavily on the table with a crisp clack, drawing everyone’s attention toward him. “I also heard that the death of Southern Yue’s Crown Prince Xuanhe was connected to Panshan. And it seems that even some people from our...”","He pointed upward. “Our own side may have been involved as well. Her Majesty the Empress... Ah, what a pity!” His voice grew quieter and quieter, but everyone at the table could still hear him.","The claim was undeniably bold. As expected, the people nearby drew sharp breaths.","Hiss!","Those who were old enough still remembered the Crown Prince Xuanhe. He had been a benevolent and gentle heir, and even the people of Southern Zhao had heard of his good reputation.","What a pity that he had died of illness at such a young age, before he could ascend the throne. Everyone had said that Heaven was jealous of his talent.","Now they were learning that the prince’s death was connected to an organization called Panshan—and even to their own empress... The others discreetly glanced at the unfamiliar-looking gray-robed man. Just as he had said, what a pity.","“Brother Xu, is this really true? Did Panshan interfere in imperial affairs all those years ago?” Someone could not resist asking, despite the taboo surrounding the subject.","“Of course it’s true. Everyone here has heard of Panshan before.” He paused deliberately, teasing them with a little suspense before continuing to enlighten them. “The Longevity Sect in Southern Yue is a branch of the Panshan organization.”","“The Longevity Sect? Wasn’t it said that the late emperor of Southern Yue, Gan Chengjiang, died because he took their pills? Was that Panshan’s doing as well?”","Everyone’s eyes widened. The gray-robed man continued piling on the revelations.","“And that’s not all. The Phantom Assassination Hall in Southern Zhao, the Pingliang Sect in Dayan, the Blood Blade Hall in Northern Li, and the Iron Hand Gang in Western Qiang—all of these organizations, whether they still exist or have already been wiped out by their respective emperors, are branches of Panshan.”"]},{"number":538,"title":"Chapter 538: The One Who Came to Borrow Troops","paragraphs":["Someone seemed to have reacted and couldn't help shouting loudly, \"So, Panshan is not only involved in the affairs of the royal family, but also has its influence in the lives of ordinary people like us!\"","The small lobby of the teahouse was immediately ignited by this remark. Everyone started chattering like a boiling pot. These words were quickly spread by different people, and even the imperial palace in Nanzhao caught wind of it.","\"How is it possible? How could the Phantom Assassination Hall be a branch of Panshan?\" Lan Xuancheng, who had just ascended the throne, looked utterly incredulous.","The Phantom Assassination Hall was clearly established by him. The current hall master was the leader of his personal secret guards. He was the behind - the - scenes financial backer of the Phantom, and even the name \"Phantom\" was written by his own hand. How could it turn out to be a branch of Panshan now!","Lan Xuancheng ordered the shadowy corner of the palace hall, \"Come, summon Zhao Shanhu to see me!\" Zhao Shanhu was now the nominal hall master of the Phantom. He had to summon the man to ask if there was a problem with him or if there was a problem with the assassination hall itself.","Lan Xuancheng was naturally suspicious. Now, when he thought carefully about the past situations, it was also impossible for Zhao Shanhu to play any tricks.","He was usually busy with power struggles and didn't pay much attention to the affairs of the assassination hall. If there was really a problem in the hall, he might not necessarily notice it.","Although he said he didn't believe it, his body was very honest. The first person he began to suspect was his own secret guard leader.","\"Yes, Your Majesty!\" As Lan Xuancheng finished speaking, a black - clothed man suddenly appeared from the darkness. He bowed to Lan Xuancheng and then quietly left just as he had appeared.","\"It seems that I have to speed up. I must never give those people a chance to fight back against me!\"","Lan Xuancheng murmured to himself. He didn't know how much his siblings knew about the fact that he was the financial backer of the Phantom Assassination Hall. But no matter how much they knew, they could take advantage of this matter to make a big fuss.","Lan Xuancheng tightened his grip on the pen in his hand. Since he couldn't solve the problem, he would solve the people who might create the problem. In this world, only the dead could keep secrets!","\"People died? How many?\" After several consecutive autumn rains in Yue Fuguang, which relieved the drought, she resumed the habit of going to court.","However, Emperor Mingxi took pity on her for her consecutive days of hard travel and didn't require her to go to court every day.","She only needed to go once every few days. With her around, the court officials were much more at ease and well - behaved.","In Chongshan's words, with Yue Fuguang in the Dayan court, the colleagues became more civilized, and even the work efficiency had improved a lot.","Today was another day for her to go to court. Half - asleep and half - awake, leaning on the chair in a daze, the system came to give her bad news again.","[All of the empress's children, except the one on the throne and Lan Xuan'er who stayed in Dayan, are dead!]","The system didn't expect that in this otherworld, they would encounter an emperor who would wipe out his own family. If it weren't for the strict protection in Dayan, Lan Xuan'er would also have been doomed.","Yue Fuguang was a bit stunned. She thought she was having an auditory hallucination because she hadn't woken up yet. \"What do you mean by 'all the others are dead'? I remember that among the empress's children, except for Lan Xuan'er, who was obsessed with Prince Ming and had been delaying her marriage, the others were all married and had their own children.\"","[Master, 'all are dead' means that even their children are dead!]","Hiss! This Lan Xuancheng is really ruthless!","\"Little Pearl, when did this happen? Was it Lan Xuancheng who did it?\"","Apart from him, who else had the ability to wipe out all the empress's children within the territory of Nanzhao? You know, there were quite a few guards around these people. Even Panshan didn't have the ability to attack several people at the same time and wipe them all out.","[You're right, Master. It was Lan Xuancheng. He had been planning to deal with his siblings for a long time. But after hearing the rumors about Panshan and fearing that they would use this matter to attack him, he accelerated his plan.","Well, he started to close the net three days ago. The eldest princess, who held on the longest, died at dawn today. Among the empress's children in the capital, except for Emperor Lan Xuancheng, the others were all dead.]","\"Does Lan Xuan'er know about this?\" She was probably the most affectionate one among the empress's children. If she hadn't met that scumbag Prince Ming when she was young, been blinded by his good looks, coaxed by his sweet words, and manipulated by his tricks of playing hard - to - get, she should have had a better life.","[When Lan Xuancheng was plotting against the princes and princesses, they actually had already noticed it. After all, he had just ascended the throne and didn't have a good grip on the dynasty yet.","The eldest princess and the others also took counter - measures. But since he started to close the net three days ago, the third prince was stabbed to death in the street first, and the eldest princess sent a flying pigeon message to Lan Xuan'er.","She already knows that the third prince, the fourth prince, and the fifth princess are dead.]","\"So, at the latest by tomorrow, she will know that her eldest sister is also dead. Her brothers and sisters were all killed by her second brother. What do you think she will do?\"","[Naturally, she will ask the emperor to lend her troops to launch a campaign against Lan Xuancheng.] The system said confidently and affirmatively.","\"Are you so sure, Little Pearl?\" Yue Fuguang glanced at the Dayan court officials who seemed to be seriously discussing the war with Beili. \"Dayan is in the middle of a war and may not have any extra troops to lend her.\"","[But if Lan Xuan'er is really allowed to lead troops into Nanzhao, isn't it a good thing for Dayan? It can save Dayan from having to take action itself.","Maybe, considering her status as a Nanzhao princess, there will be less resistance, and both sides will have fewer casualties.]","\"A war between two countries can be described as an 'internal dispute' within the Nanzhao royal family with such a maneuver.\" This statement is a bit shameless, but as the saying goes, history is written by the victors.","Is there anything wrong with saying so!","Emperor Mingxi, Huo Ying and others all nodded secretly. The words of the divine artifact master and the junior master really resonated with them.","[Master, Lan Xuan'er, who is coming to borrow troops, is almost outside the palace hall. Do you want to plead for her later and ask the emperor to lend her some troops?]","Yue Fuguang thought for a moment. It would be a good thing for her if Lan Xuan'er could capture Nanzhao for Dayan. It was obvious to everyone that once Nanyue fell, Nanzhao would sooner or later become part of Dayan."]},{"number":539,"title":"Chapter 539: So What Do You Want","paragraphs":["However, if she were the one to carry out this task, it would be a good thing for both Dayan and the people of Nanzhao.","“It’s a pity that the Yue Army is still on the battlefield in Beili and can’t be withdrawn for the time being. Otherwise, having them march south with Lan Xuan’er to establish their merit would be an excellent choice.”","Yue Fuguang’s words amounted to an agreement to lend Lan Xuan’er troops. Not only that, she seemed quite optimistic about her prospects.","The eyes of the officials whose young descendants had yet to find an opportunity to enter the imperial court began to shift, and their minds grew active as well.","“Your Majesty, Princess Xinmin of Nanzhao has come to court bearing the Secret Insignia Gold Plaque and requests an audience with Your Majesty. She is waiting outside the hall. Shall Your Majesty summon her?”","Qian Gui, who had been standing behind Emperor Mingxi, had apparently slipped out at some point. Upon returning, he brought Emperor Mingxi the news of Lan Xuan’er’s request for an audience.","After a brief moment of consideration, Emperor Mingxi nodded slightly. “Since Princess Xinmin has come to see Us bearing the token of diplomatic relations between our two countries, she must have an important matter to discuss. Let Us meet with her.”","Yue Fuguang had not yet finished a piece of osmanthus cake when Qian Gui led Lan Xuan’er, her face streaked with tears, into the main court hall.","With reddened eyes, Lan Xuan’er looked past the crowd and saw Yue Fuguang, a bit of dried osmanthus still clinging to the corner of her mouth.","When she saw that Yue Fuguang was looking back at her, the tears she had managed to hold in suddenly burst forth, blurring her vision.","She mechanically followed Qian Gui to the front of the hall and stopped at the spot nearest to Emperor Mingxi and Yue Fuguang where a court official could stand.","Before she could say anything, she heard Yue Fuguang’s familiar, slightly childish voice.","“Eunuch Qian, bring Princess Xinmin a handkerchief.”","She was crying so hard that she had practically become a tearful mess. She must truly be heartbroken. If she knew that her eldest sister was gone too, perhaps she would fight even more fiercely once she reached the battlefield.","“Xuan’er thanks Grand Preceptor Yue and His Majesty the Emperor of Dayan!”","She wiped the tears from her face but said nothing. Instead, she stared at Yue Fuguang with those deer-like eyes, looking at her again and again.","“Little Zhu, what’s wrong with Lan Xuan’er? Didn’t she come to borrow troops? Why does she keep staring at me? It’s not as if I have any soldiers for her to borrow on my face!”","[Master, you don’t have any on your face, but you do have them in your hands!]","“Then if she doesn’t say anything, how am I supposed to know she’s here to borrow troops?” Asking for something too eagerly would only weaken one’s bargaining position. Although she did look rather pitiful crying like this, when it came to the interests of herself and Dayan, the terms still had to be negotiated.","“Your Majesty, Grand Preceptor Yue, I have come to ask for your help.” Having heard Yue Fuguang’s thoughts, Lan Xuan’er understood that there was hope and finally explained why she had come.","“If Princess Xinmin has something to ask, you may as well tell Us. Although our kingdom is burdened with affairs of state and is currently at war with Nanyue and Beili, your mother and I have been friends for many years. Whatever We can do to help, We will do our best.”","As for what We could not do, that would be another matter entirely!","Lan Xuan’er naturally understood the implication behind his words. At present, aside from the emperor, the only other person in Dayan with the authority to make decisions was the Goddess Yue. If she agreed to something, Emperor Mingxi would not truly oppose it.","So long as she offered a sufficient price, borrowing troops should be assured.","She bowed deeply and said sorrowfully, “Your Majesty, I have received definite word that my two elder brothers and one elder sister have all been killed by the new emperor.”","Her tears began to fall again. “I have come to ask Your Majesty to lend me troops so that I may punish the Emperor of Nanzhao, Lan Xuancheng, and rescue my eldest sister!”","[It’s too late. Your two elder brothers, two elder sisters, and all of their children have already died at Lan Xuancheng’s hands.","[Members of the Lan imperial clan and relatives from the families of their husbands and wives were involved as well. Otherwise, Lan Xuancheng, who had only just secured the throne, could never have carried out the massacre so cleanly. Not one survivor was left behind.]","Two elder brothers, two elder sisters? Not one survivor?","Lan Xuan’er’s vision darkened. Her mind went completely blank, and an icy shiver ran through her entire body. If not for her formidable willpower, she would have collapsed unconscious in the middle of the hall.","She dug her fingers into her arm to force herself to remain calm. She could not fall. With her eldest sister gone, she had to lead the troops into Nanzhao even more.","Lan Xuancheng and the Lan imperial clan had to pay the price. Blood debts must be repaid in blood!","With her mother and brothers and sisters gone, what meaning did Nanzhao have anymore?","“Borrow troops to attack Nanzhao?” Emperor Mingxi wore an expression of difficulty. “Princess Xinmin knows that our dynasty is fighting on two fronts. We truly have no troops to spare for another war against Nanzhao.”","Hearing this, Lan Xuan’er knew it was time to raise her offer.","She bowed and said, “Your Majesty, I ask Dayan for only thirty thousand troops to help me seize Fen City. Once that is done, I will be able to recruit Nanzhao citizens into the army and continue the advance south myself.”","Seeing that Emperor Mingxi was still hesitating, she continued to increase the stakes.","“I guarantee that I will lead the combined armies of Dayan and Nanzhao all the way to Nanzhao’s capital, Phoenix City!","“All the land, and all the people living upon it, will belong to the Great Yan Dynasty.”","Emperor Mingxi regarded her solemnly. “And what do you want in return?”","“I want only Lan Xuancheng’s head, to offer it in sacrifice to my brothers and sisters.” She paused, then turned her gaze toward Yue Fuguang. “In addition, I hope that the people of Nanzhao can receive the same treatment as the people of Dayan and enjoy the protection of the Goddess.”","“Why is this my concern too?”","[Master, with you here, being a citizen of Dayan is far better than being a citizen of Nanzhao. If Lan Xuan’er can secure this guarantee, recruiting troops and raising an army in Nanzhao will become much easier.]","Under the expectant gazes of the officials of Dayan and Lan Xuan’er, Yue Fuguang nodded slightly and said calmly, “As long as it is Dayan’s land, its people will naturally be treated equally. Whatever the people of Dayan possess, the people of these new lands will possess as well.”","“Did the Goddess really say that? Princess Sixth didn’t deceive us, did she?” a young man from Nanzhao asked a scholar dressed in a student’s robe.","The scholar pointed amiably at the notice posted on the city wall. “It’s written there in black and white. It even bears the private seal of the Sixth Princess and the official seal of the Fen City government office.”","“Scholar, is it really true that we can live just like the people of Dayan?” someone asked, still unable to believe it.","They lived closest to Dayan, with only a great river separating the two countries. They knew better than anyone what kind of life the people of Dayan enjoyed now.","“The Goddess’s exact words were: ‘As long as it is Dayan’s land, all its people will be treated equally.’”"]},{"number":540,"title":"Chapter 540: How do you think they should be rewarded","paragraphs":["“Now that we’re under Great Yan’s rule, doesn’t that make us people of Great Yan too?” A woman looked hopefully at the scholar.","Meeting her hopeful gaze, the scholar nodded reflexively. “This auntie is right. The troops stationed in Fen City are now all soldiers of Great Yan. We can indeed be considered people of Great Yan.”","As for the Sixth Princess still in the city, everyone unanimously forgot that she was originally a princess of Southern Zhao. She had personally led troops against Southern Zhao’s cities, after all—clearly, she stood on Great Yan’s side.","Upon hearing that they too were people of Great Yan, a little girl of six or seven asked her weathered-looking father innocently, “Father, does that mean we’ll be able to eat our fill from now on? When there’s drought, the Divine Maiden sends rain. When there’s flooding, the Divine Maiden drives the rain away. Even if there’s an epidemic, the Divine Maiden can bestow sweet dew that cures illness!”","Her father did not answer. Instead, he turned to look at the scholar.","The scholar: Why are you looking at me again? If I knew the answer, I wouldn’t have been standing here studying the notice for so long!","Face flushed red, the scholar turned to look at the two Great Yan soldiers guarding the notice, who stood there as silent and motionless as carved stone statues.","Soldier B glanced at Soldier A. Soldier A cleared his throat and called out loudly, “Everything written in the notice is true! Fellow townsfolk, the Grand Preceptor of our dynasty personally told the Sixth Princess that so long as it is land belonging to Great Yan, She will treat everyone equally. Whatever the people of Great Yan have, the people of newly acquired lands will have as well!”","The crowd immediately erupted at the soldier’s words.","Some shouted that they would now have high-yield grain to plant. Others cried that they wanted to enlist in the army, earn military merit, and win themselves a future like the soldiers of Great Yan.","In Great Yan’s imperial court, the ministers held their breath.","Today, Minister of War Huo Ying seemed distinctly different. He held a memorial in his hands, his face unable to conceal his delight.","Yue Fuguang swept her gaze over the emperor and the assembled ministers. Recalling the victory report the system had told her about early that morning, the corners of her lips rose unconsciously as well.","“Your Majesty, this minister Huo Ying has a memorial to present!” At the very beginning of the grand court session, Huo Ying stepped forward and stood beneath the imperial dais. His expression was more solemn than at any previous morning audience.","The memorial in his hand bore three seals of wax. On its cover were written the two bold characters: “Victory Report.” Every civil and military official had naturally seen it, and they all began speculating over where another battle had been won.","Emperor Mingxi raised his head from behind the imperial desk. His eyes fell upon the memorial, and the corner of his lips lifted almost imperceptibly. “Proceed!”","Huo Ying took a deep breath, unfolded the silk document, and read aloud:","“Your servant, General Xu Shu, Conqueror of the South, kowtows and respectfully reports to Your Majesty: Since receiving the imperial command to campaign southward this year, I have led two hundred thousand soldiers... Now, all the lands of Southern Yue have been incorporated into our dynasty. I humbly petition Your Majesty to lavish rewards upon the meritorious officers and men, that those who follow may be encouraged. I risk death in submitting this memorial.”","The hall fell silent for three full breaths.","Then it exploded into uproar, with excited discussion breaking out everywhere. Some stroked their beards and laughed in delight. “Splendid! Splendid! Splendid!”","Others stared at one another in utter shock. “It isn’t a victory report from Northern Li? Great Yan conquered Southern Yue so quickly? Southern Yue... that land...” He swiftly glanced at the Grand Preceptor, who appeared to have known everything all along.","Any matter concerning land still had to be arranged by that personage. Not even His Majesty could make all the decisions alone!","Others gave no thought to such matters. They simply began counting on their fingers, calculating how vast that territory was.","Nine hundred and forty li from east to west—an expansion of territory unlike any Great Yan had achieved since its founding.","Receiving Emperor Mingxi’s look, Qian Gui immediately called out, “Silence!”","Although Emperor Mingxi had learned of the news slightly earlier than the ministers below, hearing it again now still made it impossible for him to suppress the joy in his heart. He gave Yue Fuguang an almost imperceptible smile.","More clearly than anyone else, he understood that without this venerable ancestor, forget expanding the empire—even the ancestral realm would have been impossible to preserve.","Emperor Mingxi accepted the memorial Eunuch Qian handed to him, his gaze lingering for a moment over the line: “Nine hundred and forty li east to west, and more than six hundred li north to south.”","“Huo Ying, Generals Xu and Wei, together with our two hundred thousand soldiers of Great Yan, have expanded our borders and rendered an extraordinary service to the dynasty,” the emperor said, his voice calm and measured. “How do you believe they should be rewarded?”","Huo Ying bowed and replied solemnly, “In response to Your Majesty, this minister believes that every word in General Xu’s report is true. The two generals have now helped Great Yan seize Southern Yue’s territory—this is a tremendous achievement and should naturally be rewarded generously!”","If they were not richly rewarded, not only would the officials of the entire court object, even the Grand Preceptor would not approve.","Emperor Mingxi gave a slight nod and turned his gaze toward the ministers. “Huo Ying speaks reasonably. General Xu has expanded our territory by nine hundred and forty li and slain countless enemies. Such merit deserves proper reward. My lords, discuss how the soldiers at the front should be rewarded.”","The Minister of Revenue was the first to step forward. “Your Majesty, expanding the realm is an achievement for the ages. Yet the newly acquired territory must be provided with officials and garrisons; roads must be built and cities fortified. The cost of this...”","“I asked how the soldiers should be rewarded,” the emperor interrupted, his tone mild but beyond dispute. “I did not ask about expenses.”","Even so, he was calculating how much remained in his private treasury and the national treasury. War truly did consume an enormous amount of money, but with such a vast territory now in their possession, the expense was well worth it.","Besides... Emperor Mingxi’s eyes flickered. More than a month ago, Fuguang had given him a sea chart showing the locations of the gold and silver mines.","Only after seeing the chart had he and the ministers understood that the “gold mountains and silver mines” truly meant mountains of gold and mines of silver—it was not that the silver mine itself was named Gold Mountain!","Their sovereign and ministers had made fools of themselves, but that day had also been the day they laughed most freely.","Minister of Revenue Dong Qianli withdrew awkwardly. He knew his words were unwelcome at such a moment, but the national treasury had truly been reduced by half. It pained him to see it!","It had only just been replenished, yet so much had already been spent. If he did not speak up, His Majesty would surely begin spending lavishly again.","Minister of Rites Zhang Zhongping stepped forward and bowed. “Your Majesty, this minister believes the rewards should be determined by distinction. Those who were first to scale the walls in an assault, who slew enemy generals and captured their banners, or who captured the enemy king—these are the highest merits. They may be granted titles, land and residences, and rewards of gold and silver.","“The remaining soldiers should receive silver and silk according to whether their military achievements are ranked Grade A or Grade B. Compensation for those killed in battle should be doubled.”","He bowed toward Yue Fuguang. “This official has heard that the Grand Preceptor once told the soldiers of the Yue Army that monuments to heroes would be erected for those who died in battle, with their names and deeds inscribed upon them.”"]},{"number":541,"title":"Chapter 541: Dingyuan Stele","paragraphs":["\"Your Majesty, the imperial court could follow this example and set up 'Boundary - Stabilizing Stele' in the newly acquired territories, engraving the names of meritorious soldiers for future generations to remember.\"","\"Minister Zhang makes a good point,\" the emperor nodded and then looked at Yue Fuguang, who was playing with the 'Boundary - Breaking Pearl', and asked gently, \"Fuguang, what's your opinion?\"","Yue Fuguang thought to herself, \"What a familiar 'What's your opinion'!\"","Sitting there, Yue Fuguang heard Emperor Mingxi's question. She just lowered her eyes and thought for a moment, then said, \"Your Majesty, I think it's not enough.\"","As soon as these words were spoken, all the court officials were stunned. Not enough? For opening up new frontiers, granting fields, houses, and titles, this was already an extremely high reward. Did the Junior Grand Tutor still think it was not enough?","Huo Ying seemed to have been prepared. He stepped forward and said in a solemn voice, \"Your Majesty, Junior Grand Tutor, I have something to say, but I'm not sure if I should.\"","\"Speak.\"","\"After General Xu Shu conquered the Southern Yue, he wrote me a private letter.\" Huo Ying took out a snow - white letter from his sleeve.","\"He said in the letter: 'I'm not a person greedy for merit, but there's something I have to say. Since our troops left Louguan Pass, there have been soldiers who haven't taken off their armor for a single day. There's Lieutenant Zhao Hu...'\"","What Huo Ying read were all the words General Xu Shu used to state the achievements of his subordinates, without mentioning his own merits at all. He put away the letter, looked up at the emperor, and said, \"Your Majesty, Junior Grand Tutor, I think when rewarding soldiers, we can't just count the number of enemy heads cut off or the number of cities captured.","When those soldiers fought with their lives, they didn't think about titles and fields. However, whether the imperial court rewards them and how to reward them determines the hearts of the people across the country.\"","The hall fell silent for a moment.","Yue Fuguang stood up, walked to the front of the hall with her hands behind her back. The morning light poured in from outside the hall, shining on her prince's robe. The gold patterns on the robe glistened in the sunlight.","Suddenly, she smiled, turned around, and spoke in a low but clear voice that reached everyone's ears, \"Your Majesty, those who have made contributions should be rewarded. From top to bottom, all soldiers of the Great Yan Dynasty, regardless of their ranks, should be bathed in the imperial grace. Let everyone remember that Your Majesty sees their sacrifices of blood and lives for the Great Yan Dynasty.\"","Emperor Mingxi also nodded with a smile, \"Fuguang speaks reasonably!\"","He said to Zhang Zhongping, \"Pass on my imperial edict. All soldiers who followed General Xu Shu on the southern expedition and have made contributions will be rewarded without exception.","The military achievements are divided into five grades. Those of the highest grade will be granted the hereditary title of Yunqiwei, given a hundred mu of perpetual - use farmland, and rewarded with two hundred taels of silver; those of the second grade will be given gold and silk, and their households will be exempted from corvée and taxes for three years; for the third to fifth grades, the rewards will be determined according to their merits. The Ministry of War and the Ministry of Revenue should work out the detailed rules within three days.\"","He paused for a moment, scanned everyone with his eyes, and finally fixed his gaze on Huo Ying.","\"As for Generals Xu and Wei, they will be granted the title of Marquis, given five thousand mu of land, and a lot of wealth...\" The emperor listed a series of rewards. Huo Ying's eyes were slightly red, touched by the emperor's grace.","Dong Qianli's eyes were red too, but it was because he felt heart - ache seeing the money in the national treasury flowing out like water!","All the court officials in the hall bowed their heads together and shouted long live, \"Your Majesty's imperial grace is boundless!\"","However, the emperor didn't stop there. He picked up a pen and wrote an imperial edict, then handed it to Xie Zhiyan, \"Prince, you go and handle this personally. Send it to General Xu Shu with the fastest relay of horses.\"","\"Yes, Father!\" The prince took the edict with both hands and looked down. He saw the following words written on the edict: \"General Xu, I've learned all about the soldiers' contributions. Two million taels of silver will be sent to the southern region immediately, and five hundred jars of imperial wine will be used to reward the troops. For the fallen soldiers, a stele named 'Boundary - Stabilizing Stele' will be erected in the newly acquired land, and they will enjoy seasonal sacrifices.","All your requests are approved, and those things that you didn't request but I've thought of will also be carried out. In addition, I bestow the title 'Pacifier of the South' on you to commend your achievements in opening up the frontiers.","I hope you can take good care of the soldiers and consolidate our new territory. I'm waiting for your return in the capital city.\" At the end of the edict, the emperor added a line of small characters, the ink of which was obviously lighter than the previous part. 'Tell those soldiers for me that they've opened up more than nine hundred li of new territory for the Great Yan Dynasty. The Great Yan Dynasty won't forget them, nor will I.'","The prince held the edict in his hands, feeling happy for his uncle and those soldiers. He saw Yue Fuguang smiling at him, and he felt at ease. Although his uncle's achievements were so great that they might overshadow the emperor, with the Junior Grand Tutor around, there wouldn't be any problems!","That night, the post - horses galloped out of the west gate of the capital city. The sound of the horses' hooves shattered the moonlight over the capital city.","At the foot of Taibai Mountain, Xu Shu had just finished inspecting the wounded soldiers' camp. He sat in the tent, with a sheepskin map spread out in front of him. The newly marked territory on the map still had the wet ink smell.","Suddenly, the hoarse singing of the night - watch soldiers came from outside the tent. Someone started the song, and the rough tune was like the once - dried and net - like land of the Southern Yue. The song gradually spread.","\"A man should bear a sword in his life, To seize the fifty states of the frontier...\"","Xu Shu listened for a while and exchanged a smile with Wei Shouyi, who had just come back from outside. \"This is a poem written by the Junior Grand Tutor.\" It's a pity that the frontier is over there in Beili. Otherwise, it would be more appropriate now.","Wei Shouyi nodded. \"I happened to be there when the Junior Grand Tutor wrote this poem. I remember I asked the Junior Grand Tutor what a Wu hook was at that time.\"","\"What did the Junior Grand Tutor say?\" Xu Shu put down the map in his hand and became interested.","\"Pointing to the battle - knife on his waist, the Junior Grand Tutor said that a Wu hook was a kind of weapon.\"","\"And about the Lingyan Pavilion, the Junior Grand Tutor said that a similar one would be built in the Great Yan Dynasty in the future, and the meritorious officials of the Great Yan Dynasty would be enshrined in it, just like those hero steles, to be respected by future generations.\"","Xu Shu's eyes flickered slightly. He had opened up new frontiers for the Great Yan Dynasty. There should be a place for him in the Lingyan Pavilion, right?","Wei Shouyi also thought so. He didn't dare to be sure before, but now that they had captured the Southern Yue, he thought his name should be on it.","Thinking like this, he looked out of the tent and said with a soft laugh, \"These young fellows are homesick!\"","Xu Shu also said, \"When the emperor's rewards arrive, it will be really glorious for them to return home in glory. It won't be in vain for them to have fought on the battlefield!\"","Wei Shouyi nodded. \"The Junior Grand Tutor is still in the capital city. There won't be any problems. Maybe the emperor's reward edict is already on the way.\"","Thinking of that person, Xu Shu also felt at ease. \"The war on our side is basically over. The rest is the business of the civil officials.\"","He then shifted his gaze back to the map. \"I wonder how the battle is going in Beili now.\""]},{"number":542,"title":"Chapter 542: Even Wrapped in Horsehide, One Can Return Home","paragraphs":["“I know Shen Jian’s methods well enough. With gunpowder clearing the way, Beili will belong to Dayan sooner or later—and it can belong only to Dayan!” Through their use of gunpowder and coordination with the soldiers, they had already worked out a complete and practical strategy, and had passed their experience along to the troops operating on the Beili front.","Wei Shouyi spoke with absolute confidence and boldness, because he vaguely felt that the Grand Preceptor thought the same way.","No one could defy the Grand Preceptor’s will.","“General, what we need to consider next is how to take Nanzhao.” Wei Shouyi’s large hand tapped a spot on the map. “Although the Sixth Princess of Nanzhao is leading the charge, we can’t simply stand by and do nothing. His Majesty would never let her conquer Nanzhao’s territory on her own.”","Whether they could succeed or not was one thing, but it would hardly sound good if word got out.","“Not sound good? I think it sounds great!” Yue Fuguang held up the words she had written herself—“The Heroes of Dayan Shall Live Forever”—along with the inscription beneath them. She looked at them from left to right, then right to left, and found them flawless.","[Host, where is “Heroes’ Memorial Stele” supposed to sound good? Don’t you think it’s too blunt and completely lacking in refinement?]","“System, I wrote this for ordinary people. They haven’t studied much and many of them can’t read. Only straightforward wording like this will let them understand at a glance why the monument was built.”","The system had no way to argue with her. Then it remembered that things seemed to be done the same way in her hometown, so it decided to let her have her way.","News that the imperial court would erect a monument to the soldiers who had died in the wars quickly spread throughout Dayan and across the entire military.","At first, the matter was merely a hot topic among the common people.","“Have you heard? The court is going to erect a monument for the soldiers who died in battle. They say it’s to commemorate how they fought for the country, shedding blood and sacrificing their lives, and to honor their contributions to expanding our borders.”","“I know, I know.” A lively young man in his twenties immediately chimed in, determined not to let the other man’s words fall flat.","“I heard that from now on, these men will receive offerings from all the people. Does that mean that even if they left behind no descendants, they won’t lack incense in the underworld?”","After all, many soldiers were still very young, and plenty had died before marrying or having children.","A middle-aged man with a beard smacked his lips. His robe was worn, but it had been washed fairly clean and was still neat. “That’s not all!”","The young man hurriedly asked, “Scholar, what else is there? Are there other benefits too?”","Being addressed as “Scholar” clearly pleased the middle-aged man. He cleared his throat. “They say this was first suggested by our Divine Maiden.”","He pointed toward the sky. “Since it was something the Divine Maiden proposed, how could the imperial court fail to handle it properly? As for the materials used for the monument, although they won’t be as fine as those used for the Divine Maiden’s Temple on Lotus Mountain, they certainly won’t be cheap.”","He gently stroked his beard. “A thousand years from now, who knows whether our graves will still exist? But their names will be known, remembered, and worshiped by later generations.” The more he spoke, the more envious he became.","Someone couldn’t help clicking his tongue. “Surely the court isn’t erecting a separate monument for every single person? How much would that cost? And there wouldn’t even be enough land!”","The people of the capital, born beneath the Son of Heaven, received news more quickly than others. They had heard that the Heroes’ Monument would be built beside Lotus Mountain, on Great Azure Mountain. After all, every part of the green hills was meant to be a burial place for loyal bones.","Unfortunately, Great Azure Mountain was all sheer cliffs and precipitous slopes. There weren’t many places where people could actually be buried.","The middle-aged scholar shook his head. “It won’t be one monument per person. Their names will be carved onto a wall, to be passed down forever.”","When he said “passed down forever,” he emphasized each word. If he hadn’t already been in his forties, too old for the army to accept him, he might well have gone to the battlefield himself for the sake of such a name.","His heart was full of regret, and even his voice was heavy with longing. “What a pity. If I were ten or fifteen years younger, I’d go fight on the battlefield too. If I died, my name would be carved onto the Heroes’ Wall, and later generations would offer me incense. If I were lucky enough to survive, I could at least carve out a future for myself.”","He had spent nearly twenty years taking the examinations and was still only a licentiate. He might never advance any further in this life. Compared to that, it really would be better to risk everything on the battlefield.","While he lamented his own circumstances, someone else took his words to heart.","“The court will really record the name of every soldier who dies in battle?”","“Ergou, if it were you, it might be better not to have your name recorded!” someone teased when he heard the young man named Ergou ask the question.","“Shanzhu, is your name any better?” Ergou naturally refused to back down in the face of a personal attack.","“Shanzhu sounds mighty and imposing!” Liu Shanzhu retorted. He had recently learned the phrase from his younger sister, who attended school. He liked the words and had committed them to memory.","“Hmph! So what if my name is Ergou? If it can be remembered by later generations, who cares?” Ergou very much wanted to curse and rant, but in the end he held his tongue.","He planned to go enlist that very day. He didn’t want to waste too much time arguing with Liu Shanzhu.","“Are these all the names of the soldiers who died in battle?” The news that the imperial court intended to erect a monument for the fallen had spread among the common people, but those in the army had heard it earlier and knew more details.","As soon as they received the news, they passed it down through every army. For soldiers who had already fought on the battlefield—as well as those preparing to do so—this news was even more inspiring than receiving a few extra taels of compensation.","The black-faced general nodded firmly. “Your Excellency is wise. As soon as we received the news, the military overseers, record keepers, and others began compiling the rolls of our fallen brothers.","“Not a single one will be omitted, and not a single name will be entered incorrectly.”","The deputy general beside him added, “From the very beginning, we followed the Grand Preceptor’s orders and created detailed registers for every man. Their names, native places, and home addresses are all recorded clearly.”","Because of this, even the armies that did not belong to Yue’s Army felt indebted to the Grand Preceptor.","With these records in place, even if a man met an unfortunate end on the battlefield, his remains could ultimately be sent back to his hometown. That, too, was something the Grand Preceptor had required. Even if they died wrapped in their armor, they would still be returned home.","It was precisely because of this that the brothers on the battlefield were willing to fight without fear for their lives. They all knew that even if they died, they would still have a place to return to.","The minor official in green robes smiled and nodded. “The Grand Preceptor truly had the foresight. Thanks to him, we’ve been spared a great deal of work verifying these records.”","Their arrival immediately attracted the attention of the soldiers in the forward camps. News that the imperial court had sent people to reward the army and take away the registers of the fallen spread like wildfire.","In the battles against the Beili army that followed, morale rose even higher. Even without relying on gunpowder, the Dayan army drove the Beili forces back again and again.","The Beili army fled ahead, while the Dayan army pursued close behind."]},{"number":543,"title":"Chapter 543: It is a capital crime","paragraphs":["“Qingyi, you’re injured?” Bei Ye, who had been hiding in the Northern Li great general’s tent all along, looked up to see Wei Qingyi being helped inside by his personal guards, his battle robes stained with blood. He was so startled that the teacup in his hand slipped and clattered to the ground.","Wei Qingyi’s face was somewhat pale. Seeing the worry in Bei Ye’s eyes and his faintly trembling hands, he gave him a reassuring smile. “A-Ye, there’s no need to worry. They’re only minor wounds. It’s nothing serious. I’ll be fine after a few days of rest.”","Bei Ye waved away the two guards and personally took up the medicinal powder to treat Wei Qingyi’s wounds. “Did the battle not go well?”","Wei Qingyi frowned before giving a slight nod. “I don’t know what happened today, but the Great Yan troops were unusually spirited. Our army suffered a heavy defeat.”","Bei Ye’s hand paused as he applied the medicine. “Unusually spirited? Ever since Great Yan took Southern Yue, the fighting in Southern Zhao has also gone smoothly for them. When have the Great Yan troops ever lacked morale?”","What he did not say was that the Northern Li army was also facing Yue Fuguang’s Yue forces. Though they had not directly clashed with Wei Qingyi’s army of one hundred and fifty thousand, Bei Ye had heard plenty of reports. The forces led by the neighboring Marquis of Pacifying the West had encountered them and failed to gain even the slightest advantage, taking quite a beating instead.","It was said that whenever the Northern Li forces encountered Yu Boming, a member of the Yu Family, on the battlefield, they would take a detour. No one dared to kill him outright.","When the news reached the capital, that old bastard Bei Ji was so furious that he smashed a great many things. He even issued several successive reprimanding edicts, yet no one truly obeyed them.","After all, the emperor could kill them only once. But if the Divine Maiden’s second brother truly died at their hands, that would not be a matter of dying just once.","In an instant, Bei Ye’s thoughts raced through all of this. Wei Qingyi, however, shook his head firmly. “Today was different. Those men fought as if they had no regard for their own lives. The entire Great Yan army descended like ravenous tigers, killing until their eyes ran red.”","Bei Ye was clever, and he knew Wei Qingyi well. “You suspect that something has happened in Great Yan—something we don’t know about?”","Wei Qingyi nodded slowly. He clasped Bei Ye’s slender hand tightly. “A-Ye, I have a terrible feeling. I’m afraid that this time, Northern Li... may suffer the same fate as Southern Yue. We may be doomed.”","Bei Ye let him hold his hand. A flicker of struggle crossed his face. “Qingyi, I understand the Goddess Yue’s strength and terrifying power even better than you do.”","He tried to tell him everything he knew, but he could not force out a single word. He nearly suffocated himself in the attempt.","“I originally thought that when Northern Li encountered Great Yan, we would have only two options: defeat or negotiation.” He gave another bitter smile and shook his head. “I was wrong. I failed to see the situation clearly and ignored Beiyue’s warnings.","“I truly believed that after Great Yan conquered Southern Yue, they would merely teach Northern Li a lesson and then withdraw.”","“Now it seems that Great Yan truly intends to unify the realm.” It was laughable that he had been blinded by the throne. Even after witnessing Yue Fuguang’s otherworldly, unfathomable methods, he still could not let go of his desire for that position.","He did not know whether this refusal to give up came more from his desire to sit upon that throne, or from wanting to prove himself to his imperial father—to make the old man realize that he had chosen the wrong person.","Whatever the reason, the moment he heard that Wei Qingyi was leading the army, Bei Ye had felt as though he had been possessed. He believed this was his chance to turn his fortunes around. Ignoring Beiyue’s advice, he had done everything possible to return.","But after several months of fighting between Great Yan and Northern Li, Northern Li had already lost two cities. They had fought battle after battle, both large and small, without achieving even a minor victory.","Wei Qingyi did not find this surprising. “If you and I were standing in Great Yan’s position, with such national strength and the Goddess as our powerful support, we would also fight to the very end.”","He shook his head. “Not to mention that Great Yan’s gunpowder strikes are like the wrath of the heavens. Their armor is stronger, their weapons sharper, and their equipment more advanced. We simply cannot compete with them.”","Though those words sounded like he was bolstering the enemy’s prestige and undermining his own, they were an undeniable consensus throughout the Northern Li army.","He drew the treasured sword at his waist. Its blade was covered with more than a dozen chips of various sizes. This was a priceless sword, yet when it met the blades wielded by Great Yan’s soldiers, it was no match for them either.","Reports of Northern Li’s successive defeats continued to reach the ears of Bei Ji and his ministers. Some officials even tried to blame every failure on Wei Qingyi.","“Your Majesty, I impeach General Wei Qingyi for shrinking from battle and missing critical opportunities, thereby causing our Northern Li army to lose three cities in succession. He deserves the death penalty!”","Bei Ji did not answer at once. Instead, his gaze swept across the ministers in the hall. Under the pressure of his stare, they all lowered their heads.","“Chancellor Wei, what is your view of Censor Cui’s impeachment?” His expression was calm and his voice solemn. Only when he thought of the three lost cities did his brows crease slightly.","It was impossible for Bei Ji not to feel pain and fury over the loss of those three cities. But he knew more than the ministers did, and what he knew disturbed him even more.","That was also why, despite the fact that Wei Qingyi had lost three cities and should technically have been executed, he had not punished him.","Chancellor Wei’s face remained composed. He stepped forward, bowed, and said, “Your Majesty, I believe Censor Cui’s impeachment is nothing more than baseless nonsense born of ignorance.”","He appropriately allowed a trace of grief to show on his face. “Your Majesty surely knows the situation at the front better than any of us. Great Yan has superior weapons and the might of gunpowder behind it. This... is not something our Northern Li soldiers can make up for simply by charging forward without fear of death.”","Northern Li had no steel. Nor did it possess a will as unyielding as steel. When faced with gunpowder powerful enough to destroy heaven and earth, even if his son exhausted every ounce of his ability, he could not carry the army along with him.","He quickly glanced up at the emperor seated upon the dragon throne. Their sovereign understood this better than anyone.","“When faced with the might of gunpowder, the harder our troops charge, the greater their casualties will be.” He took a scroll from his sleeve. “Your Majesty, this is a method my son Qingyi risked his life to devise for countering Great Yan’s gunpowder attacks.”","After Bei Ji had read it, Chancellor Wei continued, “Though it cannot fully neutralize the advantage of gunpowder, it should at least reduce the casualties among our soldiers to some extent.”","Bei Ji nodded slightly. “General Wei has been thoughtful.”","At those words, someone’s eyes flickered.","Their emperor had always favored Chancellor Wei and regarded Wei Qingyi as a nephew and younger member of the family. Even when Wei Qingyi and the Fifth Prince Bei Ye had caused such an indecent scandal, he had not punished him severely.","He had always called him Qingyi. Yet now he addressed him by his official title. Some people could not help but wonder whether this was truly a sign of the emperor’s respect for General Wei."]},{"number":544,"title":"Chapter 544: At That Time, He Died in His Arms","paragraphs":["At the thought of the rumors from several days ago, and seeing the expressions on His Majesty’s and Chancellor Wei’s faces, some officials felt that their opportunity had arrived.","“Your Majesty, even if General Wei has found a way to counter the Great Yan army’s gunpowder, that cannot make up for the crime of losing three cities in succession. General Wei may be spared the death penalty, but he must still face punishment. This minister proposes that Wei Qingyi be immediately escorted back to the capital to stand trial!”","“This minister seconds the motion. Wei Qingyi’s crimes are unforgivable. He ought to be investigated and dealt with.”","“This minister seconds the motion!”","“This minister seconds the motion!”","One official after another stepped forward in support, demanding that Wei Qingyi be prosecuted for losing the cities.","Bei Ji still did not speak at once. Instead, he lowered his eyes as though deep in thought, while the corner of his eye swept toward Chancellor Wei and several of the officials standing behind him.","“Your Majesty, I believe the words of these gentlemen are rather one-sided. As for Wei Qingyi...”","“What happened to Wei Qingyi?”","Sitting in the Great Yan court, Yue Fuguang was still able to learn of the developments in Northern Li in a timely manner, thanks to the system acting as her informant.","[He was suddenly stripped of his position as Left General today and is being escorted back to the capital to stand trial.]","“What’s the reason?”","[Counting the losses from the previous few days, Wei Qingyi has now lost four cities in succession. How could the Northern Li court possibly continue to tolerate him? They’ve been arguing in court for more than ten days, demanding that he be punished.","Actually, officials had already begun impeaching him after he lost the second city. But at that time, Bei Ji still didn’t know about the relationship between Chancellor Wei and his favored concubine.","Besides, he understood the might of Great Yan’s gunpowder. It was not something human strength could withstand, so he went out of his way to defend Wei Qingyi.","After the loss of the third city, Bei Ji had already grown suspicious of Chancellor Wei. When the court censors impeached Wei Qingyi again, Bei Ji stood by coldly and watched the Chancellor’s faction clash with the opposing side.","Although he did not strip Wei Qingyi of his position as Left General, he did issue an edict reprimanding him and sent several military supervisors to the front line.]","Yue Fuguang chuckled. “So after Wei Qingyi lost yet another city, Bei Ji decided to punish him?”","[Yes and no. If three more cities fell, the Great Yan army would be able to march all the way to Northern Li’s capital. Naturally, the court wanted to replace the commanding officers, so the impeachment of Wei Qingyi intensified. They weren’t only targeting Wei Qingyi; they had no intention of letting any of the generals on the front lines off the hook.","However, the reason Bei Ji finally acted against Wei Qingyi was that Chancellor Wei ultimately couldn’t resist secretly contacting the Noble Consort—and Bei Ji’s people found out.]","Yue Fuguang froze. She could easily imagine how chaotic the Northern Li court must be at that moment. The emperor had turned against the trusted and heavily relied-upon minister at his side, with a favored concubine and a prince caught between them.","The front lines were under pressure, while the rear was not only in crisis but also actively undermining itself. For Great Yan, this was the perfect opportunity—one that would certainly help them accelerate their conquest of Northern Li.","As it turned out, Yue Fuguang’s guess had been exactly right. In the early spring of the tenth year of Yuankang, two months after Great Yan captured Nanzhao, Northern Li also fell into Great Yan’s hands.","“Little Zhu, are you saying that Wei Qingyi and Bei Ye are both dead?”","The cherry in Yue Fuguang’s hand nearly fell to the ground. “Weren’t Zheng Feng and my second brother escorting them to the capital? How did they suddenly die?”","She felt that the two of them being dead was better than their being alive, but she had truly never imagined that anyone would make a move against them.","Yue Fuguang did not want to assume it was some conspiracy. Could Emperor Mingxi and the others have acted ahead of schedule?","[Master, after Wei Qingyi was impeached, Bei Ji ordered that he be escorted back to the capital. He was kept in Northern Li’s imperial prison the entire time. Later, Bei Ye returned to save him.","As a prince, he worked things out through numerous channels and managed to prevent Wei Qingyi from dying in prison. His health...]","Before the system could finish, Yue Fuguang interrupted it. “Wait. Why was it Bei Ye who went to great lengths to help him? What about his father, Chancellor Wei? Didn’t he care? And what about his aunt and cousin? They just stood by and let him die? Did they decide Wei Qingyi was a useless piece and abandon him? That’s awfully heartless!”","After all, Wei Qingyi’s predicament was inseparable from these people.","As it turned out, the general temporarily appointed to replace Wei Qingyi was no better than him. He failed to gain even the slightest advantage against the Great Yan army.","The cities that were destined to fall still fell. It was only thanks to the methods Wei Qingyi had previously devised for dealing with Great Yan’s gunpowder attacks that the Great Yan army’s progress in taking the cities was slowed somewhat.","The Northern Li court could not possibly have failed to notice this. Chancellor Wei could not have simply hidden his head in the sand.","[Chancellor Wei’s explanation was that there was already a rift between His Majesty and himself. If he stepped forward, it would only make His Majesty more wary of the Wei family.]","“Do you believe that?”","[I don’t, but that didn’t stop Bei Ye from believing it. So for more than half a year after returning, he had no time to fight for the throne at all. He spent all his time thinking of ways to rescue Wei Qingyi.","Unfortunately, before he could save Wei Qingyi, the Great Yan army broke through the capital and captured all of them. They had been perfectly safe on the road under escort, but no one knows why the Eighth Prince—who had already become a prisoner—still dared to attack Bei Ye in the chaos.","He had intended to poison Bei Ye without anyone noticing, then pin the blame on your second brother, Zheng Feng, and the others escorting them.]","“So Bei Ye was poisoned to death by the Eighth Prince, and Wei Qingyi committed suicide for love?”","When the ministers and officials of Great Yan heard Yue Fuguang’s guess that Wei Qingyi had died for love, their expressions shifted in complicated ways.","Perhaps Wei Qingyi would not have done such a thing in the past. But now that he had become a prisoner of Great Yan, with his future uncertain, it was entirely possible that he would choose to end everything himself.","As for the Eighth Prince’s attempt to use this as an excuse to shift the blame onto Yu Boming and the others, the officials of Great Yan paid it little mind.","Even if they had not known the truth, they would never have punished the heroes of their own nation over it. To them, the death of an enemy prince and a dismissed general was perhaps less important than the death of an ordinary citizen.","Besides, the army of the Grand Preceptor’s Yue clan was not something just anyone could order around.","[Master, you guessed wrong this time. The Eighth Prince poisoned Wei Qingyi, not Bei Ye. The poisoned chicken soup was originally meant for Bei Ye. But Bei Ye was worried about how badly Wei Qingyi’s health had deteriorated, so he tricked him by saying that he had already drunk it and gave all the soup that was meant for him to Wei Qingyi instead.","Wei Qingyi drank the soup, and before long, he stopped breathing. He died in Bei Ye’s arms.]","After capturing the Northern Li imperial family, Great Yan did not mistreat them. They were afraid that, having grown accustomed to comfort and luxury, the prisoners might die on the journey, so they occasionally gave them some extra food.","That was precisely what gave the Eighth Prince his opportunity.","Yue Fuguang thought about the scene and then considered the feelings between the two men. She felt that Bei Ye must have gone mad at that moment."]},{"number":545,"title":"Chapter 545: All dead","paragraphs":["Wei Qingyi had not only died in his place—he had been sent to his death by Bei Ye himself. The guilt and remorse he carried needed someone to bear the consequences, and they also needed blood to wash away his own guilt.","Someone also had to take the blame for him and Wei Qingyi.","“Then what happened? Did Bei Ye commit suicide immediately out of love, or did he take revenge first and then kill himself?” Given what she knew of Bei Ye, the Eighth Prince probably had not survived either.","The system’s next words confirmed Yue Fuguang’s guess, while going far beyond it.","【Bei Ye did not act immediately. Although he was not sure who had done it, the culprit could not have been anyone outside his brothers and sisters.】","Yue Fuguang nodded. That was true. Although Bei Li had perished, and this was not a matter of mortal enmity, no subject would attack their former ruler while they were all prisoners.","“What the Eighth Prince did is truly baffling.” The system had not explained why he had suddenly attacked Bei Ye, which meant it had not found out either.","Ignoring the remark, the system continued with its revelations.","【When night came and everyone had fallen asleep, Bei Ye began to act.","The first was the Eighth Prince. He was the person Bei Ye suspected most. Over the past few months, Bei Ye had been trying to find a way to save Wei Qingyi while also using the connections at his disposal to deal with the officials who had openly or secretly sided with the Eighth Prince. Quite a few people had been brought down by him during that time.","After that came Bei Ji’s remaining children. Before his death, Bei Ji certainly never imagined that the son he had once regarded as a spare pawn would wipe out all the children he had left in this world—all because of one man’s death.】","This time, the bright red cherry in Yue Fuguang’s hand really did fall straight to the floor. Eunuch Qian, standing nearby, immediately replaced it with another.","Every cherry had been carefully selected by him—large and fresh.","All of Bei Ji’s children were dead. It was not only Yue Fuguang who was shocked; Emperor Mingxi and his assembled officials were also taken aback. They exchanged a knowing glance and secretly breathed a sigh of relief.","It was good that they were dead. With them gone, Dayan no longer had to consider how to deal with them. To be honest, keeping them alive would ultimately have been a hidden danger. But for Emperor Mingxi, who wanted to be remembered as an enlightened ruler, it would have been impossible to kill them all so decisively while worrying about his reputation and the judgment of the historians.","More importantly, this era had not yet developed the custom of eradicating every last member of a defeated imperial family.","At this time, dynasties did not generally believe that one had to eliminate the roots to prevent future trouble. Most former royal families were simply confined for life and deprived of their freedom.","Had the Tong family's descendants not been bent on restoring their kingdom and causing trouble everywhere, thereby posing a serious threat to the Dayan dynasty, Emperor Mingxi would not have exterminated them either.","Of course, Yue Fuguang had no intention of being the one to set such a precedent and plant that poisonous seed.","Thus, Emperor Mingxi and his officials secretly breathed a sigh of relief, and Yue Fuguang did the same. If she had not known that Bei Ye had died as well, Emperor Mingxi would certainly have awarded him a merit for this.","“They’re all dead? Bei Ye is certainly ruthless. He wasn’t even sure who was responsible, yet he wiped them all out without exception! Bei Ji must never have imagined that the moment he went below, all his children would follow him one after another.”","Yue Fuguang paused, then said, “Wait, there’s still one person alive—Beiyue! Beiyue is still alive and well at the hostel of the Court of State Ceremonies!”","That was right. Only after Yue Fuguang reminded them did Emperor Mingxi and his officials remember that they still had a prince of Bei Li among them.","It had to be said that Beiyue had been far too well-behaved over the past year or so. His presence had faded day by day, and apart from You Mingmin, Director of the Court of State Ceremonies, nearly everyone had almost forgotten that he even existed.","【The Bei Li imperial family has only one member left, Beiyue. Nan Zhao has only Lan Xuan'er, Nan Yue has only Gan Tang, and Dong Yi has no one left at all.】","Each time the system mentioned another country, another measure of awkwardness appeared on the faces of Dayan’s officials. It was true that they had not caused these things deliberately, but no one could honestly claim that it would have happened without their tacit approval.","【Now, of the five kingdoms, only Xiqiang remains. Master, guess who will be the last person from Xiqiang to survive?】","Without giving it a thought, Yue Fuguang replied, “Little Zhu, is there really any need to guess? As long as Xi Ling doesn’t go looking for death, he definitely won’t die.","“After all, although he bears the title of the Xiqiang prince, everyone knows that he is not Xi Yan’s biological son.”","No one knew who had spread the story, but it had become common gossip—not only in the court, but among the people of both countries as well. Countless versions of Xi Yan’s amorous escapades and the tale of the true and false princes were circulating everywhere.","“However...” Yue Fuguang changed the subject. “Shouldn’t we be more concerned with how long it will take Dayan to conquer Xiqiang?”","The system did not seem particularly concerned about the question.","【Setting aside Dayan’s own generals, the surrendered commanders from Nan Zhao, Nan Yue, and Bei Li alone would be more than enough to defeat Xiqiang. As for how long it will take, surely it won’t drag on past the tenth year of Yuankang?】","At those words, Emperor Mingxi and Huo Ying felt the weight on their shoulders increase, and the pressure suddenly became immense.","The earlier kingdoms had been easy enough to deal with. As for Xiqiang, the problem was not that its soldiers and generals were especially formidable, but that the roads within the country were terribly difficult to traverse—more troublesome even than the mountainous terrain of Nan Zhao and Nan Yue.","War was a matter of logistics. In a campaign against Xiqiang, the greatest difficulty lay in transporting provisions.","In the past, they could have chosen to sustain the army through the war itself by collecting or seizing supplies from the areas they occupied in Xiqiang. But with the military code personally revised by the Grand Preceptor, Emperor Mingxi and his officials would rather proceed more slowly than cross the line.","The emperor and his officials exchanged glances. Although they worried that failing to conquer Xiqiang before the New Year might earn them a reprimand from the Divine Artifact, compared with violating the military code established by the Grand Preceptor, they could only resign themselves to being scolded.","Yue Fuguang raised an eyebrow. She was extremely satisfied that the system was openly urging Dayan’s officials to march westward, and she joined in, saying, “Conquer new territories, win noble titles, and rise to high office. Dayan is offering more than enough. There’s no need to worry that the soldiers at the front won’t fight desperately for the chance to advance their station.”","In the society of this era, there was no faster way to rise through the social ranks.","【Master, why did you refuse when the emperor wanted to make Yu Boming a Duke of State?】","“Because I think Marquis of Anguo is quite good enough. The higher one’s position, the greater the responsibility—and the greater the risks. It’s perfectly fine for the Yu family’s descendants to inherit a stable legacy. They don’t need to occupy too lofty a position, lest they attract unwanted attention one day and bring disaster upon themselves.”","【I’d like to see who would dare!】","When the system said this, everyone in the great hall felt as though they had been locked onto by an invisible killing intent."]},{"number":546,"title":"Chapter 546: Pre-War Preparations","paragraphs":["Everyone, including Emperor Mingxi, was so frightened that no one dared even breathe too loudly. For a moment, the great hall was so quiet one could hear a pin drop.","In the end, Emperor Mingxi gave a light cough and took responsibility for the matter. “My dear minister Huo is right. Xiqiang not only sent troops to support us when Dayan was at war with Beili, but also took advantage of the opportunity to harass our border regions repeatedly. If we do not attack them, the people will not be satisfied.","“But after such a long series of battles, shouldn’t we give our soldiers some time to rest and recover?”","Emperor Mingxi had set the tone for sending troops against Xiqiang. It would be easier to discuss the next steps with a justifiable cause for war. However, although Dayan’s military was at the height of its strength, gathering and transporting money and provisions would still take time. And then there was that godforsaken road in Xiqiang...","“My esteemed ministers, who do you think is capable of taking command of this great campaign?”","Emperor Mingxi and his ministers discussed which general should lead the army, how preparations for provisions were progressing, and the best time to launch the attack.","Meanwhile, Yue Fuguang had already begun complaining to the system.","“System, when it comes to shamelessness, no one beats politicians.”","She picked out a large, sweet cherry and popped it into her mouth.","“Anyone who didn’t know better would think Xiqiang had simply given Dayan its first border city.”","【After fighting major wars against several nations, the Dayan army’s morale is soaring. Wei Shouyi, Zheng Feng, and Yu Boming have all been ennobled as marquises. Even the surrendered generals from Nanyue and Nanzhao who fought bravely and achieved great merit were made earls or barons. Not to mention the soldiers of Dayan—even the surrendered generals are all rubbing their fists, eager for battle.","【And then there is Lan Xuan'er. Despite being a woman and the princess of Nanzhao, she was granted the extraordinary title of female marquis because of her military achievements. This demonstrates that Emperor Mingxi judges people not by their origins, rewards anyone who renders merit, and has greatly inspired the morale of the soldiers at the front.】","Yue Fuguang nodded. Emperor Mingxi certainly had a broad vision, and it had won him considerable praise.","“We’re getting closer and closer to completing our mission!” Such good days really did grow fewer with every passing day.","【Host, Dongyi, Nanyue, Nanzhao, and Beili have now all been incorporated into Dayan. Xiqiang has also lost three cities to Dayan. I don’t think it will be long before we reach their royal capital, Jincheng.】","The system’s voice was more cheerful than ever.","【Once Dayan takes Xiqiang, our mission will be almost complete!】","Infected by the system’s excitement, Yue Fuguang pushed open the window and gazed at the bright moon overhead.","“Yes. After more than two years of conquest, four of the five nations now belong to Dayan. It won’t be long before we leave.”","Yue Fuguang’s “it won’t be long” turned out to mean a very long time indeed. More than six months after Nanzhao and Beili had been absorbed into Dayan, only Xiqiang remained outside the territory of the Dayan Dynasty.","Three months earlier, the current Grand General, Shen Jian, had led Dayan’s soldiers and He Yan, one of the surrendered generals from Nanzhao, in gradually capturing the three Xiqiang cities of Dingyuan, Pingchang, and Gangu. Their army’s spearhead now pointed directly at Xiqiang’s royal capital, Jincheng.","But the army had come to a halt in Gangu. It was not because they could not defeat the enemy, but because their provisions could not keep up. Within Dayan’s territory, transportation was manageable. The deeper Dayan’s army advanced into Xiqiang, however, the more treacherous the roads became, turning the transport of supplies into a tremendous problem.","Shen Jian had once stared at the roads inside Xiqiang and gnashed his teeth.","“Damn it, I’ve never seen roads harder to travel than those in Xiqiang!”","He Yan nodded. “Even though Nanzhao is mountainous, it’s easier to travel there than here.”","At the time, Nanzhao had only recently been pacified. The blood in Beili’s capital had not yet dried, and the people had not fully submitted. The imperial court needed time to digest its newly acquired territories, comfort the populace, and, most importantly, implement the land policies promoted by the Grand Preceptor.","A handwritten edict from Emperor Mingxi arrived at the army camp. It contained only eight characters:","Preserve your strength and await the right moment.","That wait lasted three months.","Dayan had not been idle during those three months. Grain and provisions transported from every corner of the country had filled the twelve warehouses in Lianzhou. Horses from Beili arrived continuously to replenish the cavalry camps. Dongyi’s gold mines were being worked without pause, giving the sovereign and his ministers of Dayan the greatest confidence of all.","The Ministry of Works continued to improve its forging techniques, tripling weapon production.","By this autumn, Minister of Revenue Dong Qianli submitted a memorial and reported news that greatly heartened all the civil and military officials: Dayan had enjoyed a bumper harvest. Not only Dayan, but also places such as Nanzhao and Nanyue, which had benefited from the Grand Preceptor’s policies, had reaped abundant crops.","Dayan now had money, grain, weapons, warhorses, and manpower. Supplies had also been transported into the newly acquired cities of Gangu, Dingyuan, and Pingchang.","The foundation for the final decisive battle with Xiqiang had long been laid. All that remained was for the emperor to give the word.","Emperor Mingxi had waited for three months and no longer hesitated. Xiqiang’s terrain was high and cold, and winter warfare would disadvantage Dayan’s army. They had to capture Jincheng before winter arrived.","If they launched the campaign in August or September, the supply routes would remain clear. As long as the main fighting ended before November, the army could spend the winter in Jincheng.","On the third day of the eighth month, Emperor Mingxi summoned the most important ministers to the Hall of Supreme Harmony for a council of war.","On the sand table before the emperor, Xiqiang’s mountains, rivers, and cities were laid out in perfect detail. The entire nation was long and narrow, bordered by a desert to the north and snow-capped mountains to the west. The Huang River Valley ran from east to west through the country, with Jincheng situated in its middle reaches.","The three cities Dayan had already occupied—Gangu, Dingyuan, and Pingchang—were positioned at the eastern end of the valley, precisely where it lay closest to Lianzhou in Dayan. Together, they were like a wedge driven into Xiqiang’s gateway.","“Advance along three routes.” Zhou Xian, Shen Jian’s deputy, gestured over the sand table. “The central route will be our main force. We will advance westward from Pingchang along the Huang River and make straight for Jincheng.","“The northern route will set out from Gangu, cross the Huanglian Mountain Pass, and circle around to strike Xiqiang’s rear.","“The southern route will move south from Dingyuan and cut off Xiqiang’s connection with the Qiang tribes to the south. With the three armies surrounding it, Jincheng will be a turtle trapped in a jar.”","Shen Jian himself was still at the Pingchang military camp, but the strategic plan had already been sent to the emperor through confidential reports. After listening to Zhou Xian’s briefing, Emperor Mingxi did not immediately state his position. Instead, he turned to look at the Minister of War, Huo Ying.","Dayan’s successive foreign wars had clearly drained his energy. His once-powerful figure had grown somewhat gaunt, and the weariness on his face made him resemble another Wei Ping, who had gradually become haggard under the burden of Yue Fuguang’s revelations and the mountain of work they created.","Back then, Wei Ping had work he could never finish and documents he could never get through!","Now Huo Ying had wars he could never finish and battles he could never fight to the end!"]},{"number":547,"title":"Chapter 547: Faith","paragraphs":["Although he had grown somewhat thinner, his eyes still gleamed whenever he looked upon Dayan’s ever-expanding borders.","The emperor and his minister shared an unspoken understanding. When Emperor Mingxi glanced toward him, Huo Ying immediately braced himself against the edge of the imperial desk and rose, then walked over to the sand table. He studied it for a long while.","“Your Majesty, General Shen’s plan is sound.” Huo Ying paused before continuing, “But I have one concern.”","“Speak.”","“The people of the three cities along the western route.” Huo Ying pointed to the area west of Jincheng on the sand table. “Beyond the capital of Xiqiang lie the three cities of Huangzhong, Linqiang, and Poqiang. The people of these cities are deeply devoted to the God Shibi. They are unlike the people of Dayan.","“When we fought Nanzhao, Nanyue, Beili, and Dongyi, the people eventually welcomed us because many of them had secretly worshiped the Divine Maiden to begin with. The messages we spread among the common people traveled quickly, and the Divine Maiden would occasionally appear before them in person. The people believed that our dynasty would treat them well. Once we conquered their lands and they discovered that their lives were better than before, they naturally submitted. But Xiqiang is different.”","After a brief pause, Huo Ying continued, “Most of the people in those three cities belong to the Huaqiang tribe. They truly believe in the celestial god Shibi. In their eyes, the Dayan army is an army of heretics, come to destroy their god.”","The hall fell silent for a moment.","Everyone present was familiar with the Huaqiang branch of Xiqiang and its belief in the God Shibi.","Legend had it that several centuries ago, when the ancestors of the Qiang people rose in rebellion, a god descended upon the summit of Mount Luntai. Calling himself Shibi Tian, he bestowed three military manuals upon the ancestor of the Huaqiang and helped him pacify the realm.","After the founding emperor ascended the throne, he enshrined Shibi as the sole true god worshiped by the Huaqiang. To this day, temples had been built and sacrifices offered, with incense burning without end.","Even as dynasties rose and fell, faith in Shibi continued to spread among the people. Among the Huaqiang in particular, it had nearly become the spiritual anchor of every person.","The people of Xiqiang worshiped neither Buddha nor the Dao. They had once believed only in Shibi. But ever since Yue Fuguang emerged like a heavenly miracle, the faith within Xiqiang had split into two factions. Ordinary Xiqiang people had turned to worshiping Yue Fuguang. They called themselves the “Divine Maiden’s People,” and the first three cities conquered by Dayan had been populated mainly by them.","Throughout the war between the two nations, the people of Xiqiang had harbored complicated feelings toward Dayan—fear, closeness, and yet resistance all at once.","The other faction consisted of the Huaqiang. Even after hearing countless accounts of Yue Fuguang’s miracles, they remained convinced that Shibi Tian was the true god.","They feared that once the people of Dayan arrived, they would forbid them from worshiping Shibi Tian. As a result, their resistance was the fiercest. That was precisely what concerned Huo Ying most at this moment.","After listening to Huo Ying, Emperor Mingxi fell silent for a while.","“So in this battle,” he said, “the difficult part is not taking the cities. It is what comes afterward.”","“Your Majesty is wise,” Huo Ying said, bowing.","In the end, the decision remained unchanged: they would attack. No one would permit a single corner of Dayan’s territory to remain outside its borders. But before sending out the troops, Emperor Mingxi issued a personal order to Shen Jian. It contained only one sentence:","“After a city is conquered, Dayan’s soldiers are forbidden to enter the temples of the God Shibi.”","Emperor Mingxi was confident that once Xiqiang became part of Dayan, even the Huaqiang who worshiped only Shibi would willingly and sincerely offer their devotion to the Divine Maiden after witnessing her in person.","By the time the emperor’s handwritten order was carried by swift horse to the Pingchang encampment, Shen Jian was standing atop the city wall, gazing westward. The setting sun dyed the snowy peak of Mount Luntai a golden crimson. Beyond that mountain lay the heartland of Xiqiang.","After reading the order, he was silent for a moment before handing it to the military clerk beside him.","“Have three hundred copies transcribed and distribute them to every unit.”","The clerk accepted the order and glanced at it, hesitating to speak.","“Go on.” Shen Jian looked at him.","“General, the soldiers of our army firmly believe in the Divine Maiden. They worship her as the one true god. Some even think the Huaqiang are being deliberately obstinate. It would be one thing if they refused to worship the Divine Maiden, but they actually have the audacity to claim that Shibi Tian is the only true god who has ever walked among humankind.","“They... they all feel that the Huaqiang are using Shibi’s name to insult the Divine Maiden.” The clerk spoke carefully. “Will this order make the men think that...?”","“Think what? That I fear their god? Or that they should doubt my devotion to the Divine Maiden?” Shen Jian turned his head, his expression calm. “I am not afraid of their god. I am concerned about winning over their people. Remember this: taking a city is easy. The true measure of ability is making the people within it willingly become citizens of Dayan.”","The clerk said nothing more. He lowered his head and went to carry out the order, clearly not entirely convinced by Shen Jian’s words.","Shen Jian gazed out the window at the full moon hanging high in the sky. After the war in Beili, he had seen too many cities, too much blood, and too many flames.","He had also seen the Dayan army fight its way into Beili from the south. Every time they conquered a city, the hardest part was not the charge, but the first few days after occupation.","The people inside would be afraid, resentful, and desperate. If they were not told immediately that “your lives will not become worse now that Dayan has arrived,” then even ten times the effort later might not be enough to win them back.","“Fortunately, Dayan has the Divine Maiden.” Every time Dayan conquered a city, the Divine Maiden would personally appear and scatter her heavenly dew, ending the drought that afflicted the people. That was more effective than any number of reassuring words.","Xiqiang’s circumstances were even more unusual. Its people did not fear that the Dayan army would slaughter them.","After all, the Dayan army was famous throughout the wars of unification for its strict discipline. It did not massacre cities, loot, or kill surrendered soldiers. These rules were enforced more rigorously by the Dayan army than by anyone else.","Some of the people of Xiqiang feared that Dayan would destroy the beliefs they had held for centuries.","Shen Jian did not wish to destroy those beliefs. Not because he believed in Shibi, but because, like Emperor Mingxi, he was confident—in the Divine Maiden.","They believed that as long as the Divine Maiden appeared before the Huaqiang, no Shibi could prevent them from turning to worship her, the only living true god in this world.","Faith was more difficult to breach than city walls, but it was not impenetrable. The Divine Maiden was the crack in that fortress, the one through which centuries of devotion could collapse—and a new god could be rebuilt in its place.","That was his belief, and the emperor’s as well.","The expedition was scheduled for the twentieth day of the eighth month.","The troops had yet to move, but provisions had to go ahead of them. In the first half of the eighth month, Pingchang was a hive of activity. To secure the supply lines, grain and fodder continued to be transported into Xiqiang from increasingly distant regions. Wagons laden with provisions filled the official roads leading to every city in Xiqiang.","Meanwhile, the atmosphere in Jincheng was an entirely different matter."]},{"number":548,"title":"Chapter 548: I Had a Dream These Past Few Days","paragraphs":["King Xiyan of Xiqiang had not attended court for five days in a row. He had shut himself away in the innermost chambers of the palace and refused to see anyone.","Most of the meals sent in by the attendants were carried out untouched. The only thing that disappeared, time and again, was the wine.","The court had descended into uproar.","The Xiqiang court was divided into three factions. The war faction, led by General Feng Yuan, believed that although the Dayan army was powerful, Xiqiang held the advantage of terrain. The Huangshui Valley was narrow, making it difficult for Dayan’s vast army to deploy. By holding the strategic passes, they could still put up a fight.","“If the Dayan people want war, then let them come!” Feng Yuan had slammed his fist on the table in court. “The Huangshui Valley will be their grave! We, Xiqiang, have the advantage of terrain. We still have a chance to fight!”","The peace faction was led by Chancellor Zhao Chongli. They believed that Xiqiang had no chance of winning, and that clashing head-on with Dayan would merely mean using the lives of ordinary people to fill a hole that was doomed never to be filled.","After losing three cities and witnessing the superior weapons of Dayan’s elite troops, the civil officials had become even more aware that Xiqiang was far inferior to Dayan in military strength. Its people were reluctant to fight, making this a doomed battle.","“Dayan’s weapons and equipment are far superior to Xiqiang’s. Fighting them head-on would only bring about our own destruction.” Zhao Chongli’s recommendation was, “We still have bargaining chips with which to negotiate with Dayan. If we go to war again, we’ll lose those chips.”","He cupped his hands toward several of Xiyan’s sons, especially giving Xi Yuanshan an extra glance. “Submit as a vassal and pay tribute, while retaining the title of king and becoming a subordinate state of the Dayan court. That would not be a bad choice.”","Xi Yuanshan pretended not to notice. Throughout the entire session, he brought only his ears; as for his mouth, what right did he have to speak?","Apart from the war faction and the peace faction, there was a third group in the court that remained silent. These were the noble lords of Xiqiang. Each held his own territory, with soldiers and provisions at his command. If the court won, they would follow along and take a share of the spoils. If the court lost, they would surrender to Dayan.","In any case, they had already realized that Xiqiang’s chances of victory were slim. Even if they surrendered, Dayan would not kill them. It would merely grant them official positions, estates, and residences, allowing them to remain wealthy and honored for the rest of their lives. This idea had spread widely among the nobles of Xiqiang, and many had long since made their calculations.","Unfortunately, they had calculated everything except whether Dayan’s ruler and ministers would leave themselves such a massive source of trouble. They had also failed to calculate whether Dayan’s goddess would grant them a path to survival.","Xiyan was growing old, and his control over the court had weakened considerably. With a great war approaching, he was caught between two sides, unable to offend either.","The war faction held the troops; the peace faction held the money. He could suppress neither one. His refusal to attend court for several days was less an attempt to devise a countermeasure than an act of escape.","It was not until the seventeenth day of the eighth month, when news reached Jincheng, that he was forced out of his chambers.","The vanguard of the Dayan army had already left Pingchang.","Chancellor Zhao Chongli personally brought the news to the palace. The chancellor, now in his sixties, did not wait outside the hall as he usually did. Instead, he marched straight into Xiyan’s chambers. When the attendants tried to stop him, he sent them sprawling with a sweep of his sleeve. Though Chancellor Zhao was a civil official, he was by no means incapable of fighting.","It could be said that among the Six States, anyone who could stand in court knew at least a few martial skills. This was not an age that favored frail scholars who could not even lift a chicken. The mainstream ideal among learned men of the era was to wage war on horseback and govern from behind a desk. If one insisted on describing the difference, it was simply that, as with scholarship, some were stronger and some weaker, some more accomplished and some less.","“Your Majesty!” Zhao Chongli stood at the entrance to the chamber, his voice hoarse. “The Dayan army has already reached the Huangshui Crossing. How much longer do you intend to drink in here?” Even if he had given up on himself, he could not go this far. Was he truly planning to wait until the Dayan army came knocking at the gates?","In the past, their ruler had raised his sons like poisonous insects in a Southern Zhao gu pot. It was not that the clear-sighted officials had failed to notice. As chancellor, Zhao Chongli had repeatedly offered him subtle remonstrances.","Unfortunately, their ruler had once been a brilliant young sovereign, decisive and absolute in his authority. He believed in the law that the strong survived and the weak perished. How could he have listened to the cautious counsel of aging ministers?","Now, one prince had remained in Dayan for several years without returning. Another was as silent as a gourd with its mouth sawn shut. The remaining princes had certainly become more active over the past two years, but they were also capable of stirring up trouble. Many people had been dragged into the struggle of the succession because of them.","As chancellor, Zhao Chongli knew perfectly well that he himself was a succulent piece of meat, and that everyone wanted to drag him into their own bowl. He had been subjected to one attempt at recruitment after another by every faction, to the point of being thoroughly fed up.","Whenever he thought of the beautiful concubines and favored consorts that had appeared in his household over the past two years, Zhao Chongli frowned. How old was he now? Even if they gave him the finest beauties, he no longer had the teeth for them. His heart might be willing, but his body was powerless.","Xiyan raised his head from the couch. His eyes were bloodshot, and wine stained the corners of his mouth. He looked at Zhao Chongli for a long moment before finally recognizing him.","“Chancellor Zhao,” he said, as though his mouth were full of phlegm. “Has Dayan really attacked?”","Xiyan himself could not understand how matters had reached this point in little more than two years. The emperors he had known had died one after another, and nations had fallen one after another.","Now it was finally the turn of what remained of Xiqiang’s territory.","“It shouldn’t have happened like this!” He patted his head. “These past few days, I’ve had a dream. In the dream, it was clearly Dayan that was supposed to be devoured by several of us. It was clearly my Xiqiang that was supposed to swallow the whole of Lianzhou, as well as most of Yizhou and Quanzhou. How did it...”","Zhao Chongli was helpless. He did not believe a word of his ruler’s delusional rambling, yet he could not help sighing inwardly. With a touch of impertinence, he interrupted Xiyan in a grave voice.","“Your Majesty, dreams are always the opposite of reality!”","“The opposite?” A flicker of bewilderment crossed Xiyan’s increasingly aged face.","Looking at the king he had served for more than twenty years, Zhao Chongli suddenly felt a deep sorrow.","Their ruler was not truly trying to neglect his duties. He simply knew too well that Xiqiang could not win, especially after several other countries had fallen one after another. He had already prepared himself for that possibility.","But being prepared was one thing. Being unwilling to admit defeat and wanting to make one last desperate struggle, while also refusing to drag everyone else down with him, was another. The torment of being trapped between those two impulses was more agonizing than pure fear.","And most of all, Xiyan could not bring himself to admit defeat to that old acquaintance of his—to Emperor Mingxi Xie Fei, whom Xiyan had always believed inferior to himself.","“Your Majesty...” Zhao Chongli lowered his voice. “The Dayan army has already set out. This is no longer a question of whether we want to fight. It is a question of how we are going to fight.”","Or whether they should surrender outright. He wanted to say that, but before Xiqiang suffered its first defeat, their ruler might not be willing to listen."]},{"number":549,"title":"Chapter 549: I'm old, not crazy.","paragraphs":["Xi Yan closed his eyes and remained silent for a long time. Outside the hall, the wind swept past, setting the bronze bells beneath the eaves tinkling in a delicate burst of sound.","They were wind chimes unique to the Xiqiang royal palace. It was said that the Huajiang tribe’s ancestors had passed down the craft, and that every peal of the bells represented the gods’ protection. But at this moment, the sound seemed especially hollow.","“Summon Feng Yuan,” Xi Yan finally said, his aged voice seeming to drift from somewhere far away. “And summon all the tribal lords as well—especially Huajiang. At tomorrow morning’s court, anyone who fails to appear need not come again.”","Zhao Chongli accepted the order and withdrew. When he reached the hall doors, he heard their emperor’s voice sound once more behind him, soft as a mutter to himself.","“Minister Zhao, do you think the appearance of that Goddess Yue at this particular moment is suspicious?”","Zhao Chongli stopped but did not turn around.","“Your Majesty, Goddess Yue... whether we want to acknowledge it or not, she is the goddess of Dayan. Her origins can be verified.”","Xiqiang gave no reply. Once again, he thought of the fragmented dreams he had been having after getting drunk these past days. Yet none of them contained Yue Fuguang.","A great drought had ravaged the world for three years, killing countless people. Like Dayan and Beili, Xiqiang had been severely weakened by the prolonged disaster.","But thanks to the arrangements he had made in advance, he had successfully joined forces with several kingdoms to drain Dayan, which possessed the best land in the Central Plains, and use it to replenish their own countries.","He clearly remembered succeeding. They had spent several years wearing Xie Fei down before dividing Dayan’s territory among themselves. In the years that followed...","Xi Yan collapsed heavily back onto the bed. He stared blankly at the canopy, murmuring, “Yue Fuguang! Yue Fuguang! It shouldn’t have turned out like this. There shouldn’t have been...”","By the time Zhao Chongli left the palace, dusk had already fallen. There were few pedestrians on the streets. Occasionally, a few carriages hurried past, loaded with household belongings and heading out of the city.","The wealthy families in the city had already begun fleeing in secret, taking their gold, silver, and valuables to hide at the foot of the snow mountains to the west. Ordinary citizens had no way to escape. All they could do was burn incense at home and pray for their Goddess Yue to protect them.","He had even heard that some commoners were secretly hoping Dayan would conquer Xiqiang as soon as possible.","Zhao Chongli watched the departing carriages. This was their last chance. Once tomorrow passed, the city would probably be sealed off.","“System, what do you mean? What does it mean that Xi Yan has begun awakening memories of his previous life?”","[Host, I’m not entirely sure either. I only detected abnormal fluctuations in Jincheng, the capital of Xiqiang.] The system felt a pang of pain whenever it spoke of this.","[I spent quite a bit of energy conducting a careful scan and discovered that the problem originated with Xi Yan. Through his dreams, he has been recalling fragments of the history we know.]","Yue Fuguang rubbed the fluffy little creature in her hands. “The two countries are so vastly different in strength now. So what if he remembers? It shouldn’t have much impact on the overall situation.”","Yue Fuguang was brimming with confidence. With the unification of the world down to its final push, Xi Yan was like a mantis trying to stop a chariot before Dayan’s advance. As far as the grand scheme was concerned, he could not cause much trouble.","[Host, have you forgotten? I told you that after Dayan fell, the other kingdoms benefited at first, but they later declined one after another, leading to those three hundred years of chaos.]","Otherwise, the destruction of a single Dayan would never have plunged the world into such a dark age.","The previous hosts had not initially chosen Dayan, the first kingdom destined to fall. They had failed, while her host was on the verge of succeeding.","Whether the problem lay in their choices or their methods was anyone’s guess.","“So?” Yue Fuguang finally became a little more serious, though she still did not take her hands off Caramel and Milk Tea.","After being constantly fed by her, the two black-and-white fluffballs had become just as clever as Taxue and Wuhen, who perched in the peach tree at Mingyue Pavilion.","Still, they were often tricked by the three foxes. If not for their larger size and overwhelming physical strength, they probably would have been led straight into a ditch by those three.","With her current identity, everyone around her was a “good person,” leaving her no opportunity to witness palace intrigues or household dramas.","Yet these past few days, the animals around her had been putting on a domestic power struggle every day. Once the little creatures started competing for attention, no one else had anything to do.","The system glanced at the way its host stroked the black-and-white fluffballs—one pat at a time, nearly rubbing them bald—and desperately wanted to say that it really was unnecessary. Even if Dayan unified the entire world tomorrow, they would not be leaving this realm anytime soon.","They were a proper system, after all, complete with after-sales service!","[So, Xi Yan has recalled the events of the past. Xi Yan, whose paranoia has only worsened with age, still possesses some influence in Xiqiang. And though he is old, his methods remain ruthless.","Host, guess what he’ll do next?]","The system was asking her to guess again. It had been playing this guessing game since the very first chapter and still wasn’t tired of it.","Yue Fuguang rolled her eyes. “Could he really slaughter the people who would later destroy the Western family’s dynasty, even with a great war about to begin?”","Yue Fuguang had read the complete history of the Six Kingdoms. Xiqiang was a dynasty composed of numerous tribes, and more than half of those who held the greatest power came from noble families.","The strongest tribes were the Xiqiang tribe under Xi Yan’s control, followed by Huajiang and Qingqiang.","The collapse of Xiqiang would owe much to those two tribes and the various nobles.","[Why not? If he can’t kill off Dayan, can’t he send those people to their graves first?]","They were all going to die anyway. With Xi Yan growing increasingly deranged, he was perfectly capable of taking revenge and settling old scores.","[Besides, I wouldn’t mind wasting a little energy to physically liberate those nobles who devour human flesh and drink human blood, all without getting my own hands dirty.]","“Didn’t you say he only dreams of his past life after getting drunk? Who would believe things they saw in a dream, let alone act on them and sabotage their own people at such a crucial moment?”","Xi Yan was merely old, not insane.","[Where there’s a will, there’s a way.]","Wasn’t this simply a matter of adding a little fuel to the fire? The system was an expert at that. If it could eliminate all those bloodsucking nobles without dirtying its own hands, it did not mind spending a little energy.","Xi Yuanshan was certain his father had gone mad. These past few days, Xi Yan would often ask who he was, and even say such chilling things as that he should never have existed.","If the two of them had not looked three or four parts alike, Xi Yuanshan would have suspected that his father might depose him.","“My lord, are you truly planning to sit here and wait for death?” Xi Yuanshan no longer knew how many times Xie Zhiyao had questioned him about this in recent days."]},{"number":550,"title":"Chapter 550: I Thought You Would Show Some Tenderness","paragraphs":["“His Majesty is clearly senile. He can’t even recognize his own son—what on earth is he trying to pull? Can’t you see it, Prince?”","Xi Yuanshan also thought his father had gone a little mad, but he had no intention of taking up Xie Zhiyao’s words. The two had been married for several years, yet they had never been close.","Neither of them was the sort to lose their head over love. Feelings had never been their priority. In the past, he had still pretended to be devoted in front of other women, but ever since returning from Dayan, he had rarely visited the women’s quarters.","Seeing Xi Yuanshan play dead again, Xie Zhiyao was furious. Her aggressive questions came one after another. “When he’s sober, he knows you’re his son. Once he’s drunk, he says you shouldn’t even exist. Do you have any idea what people outside are saying about you?”","“What are they saying?” Xi Yuanshan asked indifferently. “Let them say whatever they want. Anyone with a mouth can talk.” As for the future, they would have to live long enough to see it.","Based on the things his father had been saying bit by bit lately, Xi Yuanshan actually felt that some of them sounded strangely familiar. He had racked his brains but still couldn’t figure out why. “Could Father really have gone senile?” he muttered inwardly.","“Prince, do you truly not care at all? Even if you won’t think of yourself, shouldn’t you think of your children?”","Xi Yuanshan had one son and two daughters. His eldest son, who was three and a half years old, had been born to Xie Zhiyao and was her greatest source of confidence in Prince Yi’s residence.","If the child had not been so young, and if his uncles had not each been so capable, Xie Zhiyao would not have pinned her hopes on her husband becoming a great man. She would have pinned them on her son becoming one instead!","“It’s precisely because we’re doing this for their sake that we can’t act rashly. At the very least, you’re the Commandery Princess of Dayan. Even if we...”","“Stop talking. My father died at the hands of Xie Fei and Yue Fuguang. I will fight them to the death!”","Unlike Xi Yuanshan’s decision to lie low, Xie Zhiyao was an aggressive advocate of war. She had even met Feng Yuan in secret and revealed everything she knew about Dayan and Yue Fuguang to him and the other hardliners.","Xi Yuanshan was not surprised by her reaction. In fact, he thought her choice was perfectly understandable. The vengeance owed for a murdered father could never be forgotten.","But as he had said, Xie Zhiyao’s decision to fight Dayan—and especially that goddess—to the bitter end was destined to lead her down a dead end.","Yet when he thought of all the secrets he had heard in Dayan, and of the things his wife had done to that goddess, Xi Yuanshan could not help sighing deeply inwardly.","Though they had married with their own agendas and shared no real affection, they were still bound together by their children. He did not want her to walk into a dead end, but he had no way to pull her back.","“Can’t you do it for the children...”","His words were interrupted by Xie Zhiyao once again. “Prince! I, Xie Zhiyao, would rather die than bow my head to the emperor or Yue Fuguang!”","She gazed out the window, her voice revealing neither joy nor sorrow. “If I die, I hope the Prince will treat Little Ping well and protect him until he grows up safely.”","Xi Yuanshan did not know exactly how many times she had tried to harm Yue Fuguang behind the scenes. But he knew that even after coming to Xiqiang, his wife had never stopped. Not only had she stirred up the already murky waters of Xiqiang’s succession struggle, she had also continued trading information about Dayan for personal gain.","Whether he had benefited passively or actively, he was, in truth, one of the beneficiaries.","“Don’t worry. As long as I’m alive, nothing will happen to the children.”","If Goddess Yue truly possessed such extraordinary abilities, she must know everything happening here. How could she possibly let Xie Zhiyao off?","“Let her go? Naturally, that’s impossible. But from the looks of things, she’ll walk herself to her own doom without us having to lift a finger.”","Over the past few years—especially during the period when Xi Yuanshan had lived in Dayan for an extended time—Xie Zhiyao had used Prince Yi’s residence to cause no end of trouble throughout Xiqiang. It was no wonder Yue Fuguang had spared her back then.","Xie Zhiyao was capable enough that even Xi Yan had once exchanged benefits with her.","She was also on good terms with the Feng family, the Huaqiang Tribe, and the various noble clans. She had even considered arranging a betrothal for her son, who was only two or three years old, in order to win over the military powers. At the time, even though Xi Yuanshan was not in Xiqiang, he had still found a way to stop her from becoming any more deeply entangled.","Now that Dayan’s army had reached the city gates, her status as the Commandery Princess of Dayan had made her a welcome guest in the homes of those who remained uninformed. But which of those people was truly easy to deal with?","[I thought you would be the type to show mercy to a beautiful woman.] The system felt that it had indeed been overthinking things. Its host was still the same person who cared only about profit and gave no thought to the lives of men, women, or children. Clearly, it had chosen the right person from the beginning!","“System, don’t get your hopes up about me. For the sake of obtaining my own body, beautiful women and handsome men will receive the same treatment. I won’t hesitate to send any of them on to the next life.” Besides, these people harbored such deep malice toward her. Was she supposed to keep them around so they could bring trouble upon the Yu family? She would be patting herself on the backside and leaving soon enough. She could hardly leave others with a mess to clean up.","[So why haven’t you detoxified Beiyue yet?]","“A half-dead Prince of Beili makes a better subject. Besides, he won’t die anytime soon.”","[Why don’t you just admit that while he won’t die, it will affect his life expectancy?]","Yue Fuguang waved her hand dismissively. “System, haven’t you heard? Everyone dies eventually. It’s only a matter of when.","“Beiyue doesn’t like women, so he’s destined to have no descendants. Once he’s gone, there won’t be any legitimate members of the Beili imperial clan left. Isn’t that wonderful?”","[It is. For Dayan and for the common people who want to live peaceful lives, it’s certainly good news.]","Yue Fuguang and the system were chatting animatedly when she suddenly seemed to hear someone, somewhere far away, murmuring prayers to her.","The Goddess Hall of Dayan was still under construction, but at the foot of Lotus Mountain, the people had already begun offering incense and worshiping from afar, facing the unfinished hall and the statue of the goddess.","She had gone to see the statue herself. Although it was only half completed, the jade likeness of the goddess already resembled her by eight or nine parts out of ten.","For that reason, Yue Fuguang decided to leave it a great gift when she departed.","“System, I think I’m hearing someone murmuring in my ear again. It’s too far away—I can’t make out the words.” Since she could not hear clearly, she first ruled out the people of Dayan.","At that very moment, in a temple in the northern part of Jincheng, Xiqiang, the temple was packed with people. Men and women, old and young, filled the hall like a sea of black, all kneeling, kowtowing, and praying."]},{"number":551,"title":"Chapter 551: Too Late","paragraphs":["The incense at the temple was so thick it made the throat burn. Dense smoke poured from the main hall, hanging over the shrine like a gray cloud. An old woman sobbed and shouted in the midst of the crowd, her voice piercing the evening sky.","“Divine Maiden! You are the Divine Maiden of Dayan, but you are also the Divine Maiden of our Qiang people! You can’t protect only the people of Dayan—you have to protect us too!”","Both of her sons had gone to the front. Her husband, already in his forties, could very well be dragged off to fill the trenches if the fighting went badly. Three grown men from their family—surely they couldn’t all be sacrificed to this war!","With all the men gone, wouldn’t the rest of the family be bullied to death?","Her wailing was scattered by the northwest wind into the ash-filled air. No one answered her, because every family kneeling there was in the same dire situation.","The wind chimes beneath the temple eaves rang out, their sound just like the bronze bells in the palace—fine, cold, and distant, like a sigh drifting from somewhere very far away.","No one knew what deity this temple had once enshrined, but that was all in the past. Now it housed a small statue of Yue Fuguang. Judging from the surrounding furnishings, the temple had evidently been chosen in haste.","On the day Shen Jian led the central army out of Pingchang City, dawn had barely broken.","Forty thousand infantry, eight thousand cavalry, and three thousand crossbowmen, along with the supply train and civilian laborers, stretched for more than twenty miles. The military banners snapped in the morning breeze, embroidered with Dayan’s emblem: a crescent moon cradling a long sword.","This was the symbol of Yue Fuguang, a design the officials and sovereign of Dayan had debated repeatedly before finally settling on it. The Dayan army had only recently begun using these banners.","On the lands of Western Qiang, the emblem represented two things: the Dayan army, and Yue Fuguang’s protection. When those two things became one, the people of Western Qiang found their will to resist subtly shaken. They no longer knew exactly whom they were fighting.","Shen Jian rode a tall, powerful horse in the middle of the column. His armor looked ordinary at first glance, no different from that of any other general, but a closer look revealed its distinctive features.","It was the latest creation of the Ministry of Works—what the Grand Preceptor called “cutting-edge technology.”","The army advanced westward along the Huangshui River valley. Scattered fields and villages dotted the slopes on either side, their barley already harvested at this time of year, leaving only knee-high stubble.","The poplars along the field paths had begun to shed their leaves, and golden foliage carpeted the roads. This was the finest season in Western Qiang: high skies, sparse clouds, clear river water, and distant snowcapped mountains gleaming white beneath the sun.","Yet the villages were deserted.","No one came out to watch the army pass. Doors were shut and windows closed. The only sound was the occasional bark from some courtyard, quickly muffled by a terrified owner.","Shen Jian ordered the messenger beside him, “Pass it down. No noise when we pass through the villages. Do not touch so much as a blade of grass belonging to the common people. Anyone who dares violate military discipline will be executed without mercy!”","The messenger accepted the order and hurried off to relay it.","News that all three armies had begun their advance reached Jincheng almost simultaneously. The northern Dayan army had set out from Gangu and crossed the Huanglian Mountain Pass; its vanguard had already reached Haoyuan.","The southern Dayan army had departed Dingyuan and was advancing west along the Tao River, closing in on Yongshi River.","The central army, Shen Jian’s main force, had already passed Wuyi and was less than two hundred and fifty miles from Jincheng.","The three armies converged like three pincers, closing from the east, north, and south. Jincheng was the walnut caught between them; no matter how hard its shell, it could not withstand pressure from three directions at once.","Xi Yan finally began to act like a king. At court, he announced three decisions.","First, he appointed Feng Yuan commander-in-chief and ordered him to lead fifty thousand troops from the defenders of Jincheng to meet the enemy outside the city and hold the narrowest point of the Huangshui Valley—the Jishi Gorge.","Second, he ordered the urgent conscription of troops from all the tribes of Western Qiang, requiring them to assemble in Jincheng within three days.","Third, he sent envoys west to seek aid from the Hua Qiang tribes, offering them large sums of money and land in return.","Each of the three decisions was sound, but every one of them had come too late. In fact, three months earlier, before Dayan had shown any clear intentions, Xi Yan and his chancellor, along with the other senior ministers, had already considered mobilizing the various tribes.","The idea itself was sound. But times had changed. If they had moved two years earlier, the troops could have been mobilized simply by issuing Xi Yan’s imperial decree.","But now... who would come and throw themselves into the pit for them?","The defensive fortifications at Jishi Gorge should have been built six months ago, yet they were only being reinforced now, with the Dayan army nearly at the gorge. The order to mobilize the tribal forces had been issued a month earlier, but Dayan’s three armies were already advancing from three directions, and those who had received the summons still had not moved. At the time, the factions advocating war and peace had still been arguing among themselves.","As for seeking aid from the Hua Qiang tribes in the west, it would take their riders at least five or six days to reach Jincheng. By then, the Dayan army would have surrounded the city. Besides, the Hua Qiang were fond of sweeping only their own doorstep clean, and even more fond of adding flowers to brocade—helping the strong rather than the desperate.","But not everyone could see that these decisions had come too late. Some officials at court breathed a sigh of relief, believing that since His Majesty was finally willing to fight, Western Qiang might yet be saved. More remained silent, already calculating the losses in their hearts.","After the court session, Feng Yuan summoned his subordinates to his home to discuss military affairs. This Western Qiang general, in his early forties, was broad-shouldered and powerfully built, with a full beard and a voice like a booming bell.","Among the nobles of Western Qiang, he was the best fighter after the Marquis of Changxin. Although he had ultimately been forced to retreat during the previous struggle for the three cities, he had caused the Dayan army considerable trouble. Shen Jian had mentioned him specifically in his battle report, describing him as “bold in the face of battle and well versed in military strategy.”","Yet at this moment, the situation shown on the sand table before Feng Yuan was undeniably grim.","“The central army of Dayan numbers roughly fifty thousand, all seasoned troops under Shen Jian,” his deputy said, pointing at the sand table. “The northern army has forty-five thousand men, commanded by He Yan, a surrendered general from Nan Zhao. They’ve reportedly crossed the Huanglian Mountain Pass already. The brothers defending Haoyuan probably won’t be able to hold out.”","He lowered his voice slightly. “As for the southern army, it numbers thirty thousand and is led by a general named Zhang Fang.”","“Oh? Tell me more.”","“According to the information we’ve gathered, he once served as the captain of the Goddess Yue’s guards.”","Feng Yuan glanced at him in surprise. Upon hearing that Zhang Fang had once been a guard captain, even he had to admit that the man clearly had a powerful patron.","He drew a deep breath and raised a hand to stop the deputy from continuing. Instead, he fixed his eyes on the sand table and stared at it for a long time."]},{"number":552,"title":"Chapter 552: The playing style is almost too \"flexible\"","paragraphs":["“How many troops can we still muster, and how many days can Jishi Gorge hold?” he asked.","Dayan was well equipped, and its soldiers were of decent quality. They could deploy more than a hundred thousand men at a time. On their side, they would need to gather as many troops as possible—without splitting their forces too thin—before they had any chance of meeting the enemy head-on.","“At most, a hundred and fifty to a hundred and sixty thousand in the short term,” the deputy general replied cautiously. “If we can repair the fortifications, we should be able to hold for seven or eight days with the troops we have.”","“But the Dayan army has thunderclap bombs. The rubble walls at the gorge entrance may not withstand them.”","Thunderclap bombs were a siege weapon unique to the Dayan army. No matter how thick a city wall was, once those things were brought against it, breaching the wall was only a matter of time. Over the past two years, they had attacked several neighboring countries, and not a single city had managed to hold out against them.","“Seven or eight days will be enough,” Feng Yuan said. “The reinforcements from the various divisions can arrive in five days at the earliest. With the Qiang cavalry joining us, we won’t be outnumbered. As long as we hold Shen Jian at Jishi Gorge and wait for the reinforcements to arrive, we can encircle the Dayan army from three sides. Then they’ll be like half-cooked rice in a pot—neither edible nor salvageable.”","He spoke with great confidence, but no one in the tent responded. Everyone present was a seasoned veteran. They knew perfectly well that whether the reinforcements and Qiang cavalry arrived on time depended entirely on whether the various lords were willing to come.","Those lords all had their own calculations. The Dayan army had not yet reached their doorsteps, so who would be willing to send their own soldiers out to die?","The group fell silent for a while. Then a young officer spoke softly. His voice was not loud, but in the quiet tent, every person heard him clearly.","“Great General, I heard that the Dayan army has been stationed around Gangu for three months. They haven’t slaughtered or pillaged the people. In fact, you could say they’ve been more disciplined than the soldiers of our own army.”","Feng Yuan’s expression changed immediately. He knew better than anyone what the Dayan army had done. In that regard, the Western Qiang army truly could not compare with them. But asking him to impose strict military discipline would be even more difficult than waiting for the various divisions to send reinforcements.","“What are you trying to say?”","Seeing Feng Yuan’s dark expression, the young officer hurriedly lowered his head. “This subordinate meant nothing.”","But he had already said it, and everyone in the tent had heard him. The men exchanged glances, then quickly looked away.","What the young officer had said was simply a fact. After Gangu, Dingyuan, and Pingchang fell into Dayan hands, the Dayan army had not harmed a single hair on the heads of the local people.","There were even rumors that those regions would receive Dayan’s high-yield grain varieties the following year. As a result, the wavering hearts of the people in those three cities were slowly being won over.","If Dayan fulfilled its promise the next year, those three cities would truly become part of its territory.","Some even began to think that Dayan now had more money, lower taxes, more honest officials, and a more disciplined army. What was the point of following Feng Yuan into a battle they were certain to lose?","Such thoughts spread like weeds across the Western Qiang lands. No one voiced them aloud, but everyone was quietly leaving themselves a way out.","On the thirtieth day of the eighth month, the vanguard of Dayan’s central army reached Jishi Gorge.","Jishi Gorge was the narrowest section of the Huang River valley. Steep mountains rose on either side, and the river narrowed here to only a few dozen yards across.","The Western Qiang army had built a stone wall at the eastern entrance of the gorge, taking advantage of the terrain. Behind the wall were ballistae and catapults, while archers had been stationed on the hilltops on both sides. From the front, it was indeed a formidable defensive line, easy to defend and difficult to attack.","Shen Jian did not rush to attack. He rode to a small hill two li outside the gorge entrance and spent a long time studying the defenses through a spyglass. Then he summoned several generals to his side.","“A direct assault would cost us too many men.” He looked down at the map of Jishi Gorge he had just drawn. “The defenders at the gorge entrance can strike at us, while we can’t reach them. The terrain is against us.”","“Then does the general intend to wash the ground with gunpowder first?” asked Vanguard General Huo Sui.","During his years at Sancha Pass, he and the others had absorbed every offhand remark Yue Fuguang had made, along with all his shameless tactics. They had even developed a habit of drawing inferences and improving upon them.","His father, Huo Ying, the Minister of War, had been a brilliant and resourceful commander on the battlefield in his youth. He never could have imagined that one day his second son would fight with such audacity—such downright unconventional methods!","Huo Sui, along with Cai Bing and Wei Yan, had also taken part in the campaign against Beili. They had earned considerable military merit, and once the Western Qiang campaign concluded, they might very well be granted noble titles if they performed well.","Shen Mu did not answer directly. Instead, he pointed at the map.","“Jishi Gorge has more than one route in. Look here.”","His finger traced a line along the mountains south of the gorge entrance. “This valley can be used to circle around from the south. Once we cross this ridge, we can cut directly into the rear of the gorge. The defenders’ supply route and escape route are both there.”","Huo Sui leaned closer to study the map, frowning. “General, cavalry can’t pass through this valley. The path is too narrow. Even infantry will have to go through one at a time. And if we cross the ridge, we won’t be able to bring the baggage train with us.”","His eyes shifted as an idea came to him. “How about I take some men over there and lay a batch of land mines? Then we can block the passage without even having to go all the way through. That way, we can seal off their escape route without losing too many men.”","Shen Jian could not help glancing sideways at him. Huo Sui was under his command, while Wei Yan and Cai Bing were leading the other two armies. If this fellow was already like this, then the other two were probably no less troublesome.","“All right. Take a team and find some men who know what they’re doing. Get it done quickly, so the enemy doesn’t grow suspicious while we’re wasting time here.” Shen Jian looked at Huo Sui. “Huo Sui, you’re going there to lay land mines, not to launch a surprise attack. Don’t do anything unnecessary.”","It wasn’t that he didn’t trust Huo Sui. The truth was that all those who had come out of Yue Fuguang’s army—generals and soldiers alike—had minds that were far too active, and their methods were far too... “flexible.”","In any case, Shen Jian had experienced it several times. Their methods were always unexpected. Especially in small-scale operations, even a force of a thousand men might be beaten senseless by a hundred of them without ever managing to catch so much as a glimpse of their attackers.","Huo Sui gave an honest, sheepish smile, dimples appearing at the corners of his mouth. “Don’t worry, General. Huo Sui knows where to draw the line.”","Shen Jian grumbled inwardly, You know where to draw the line? If I hadn’t warned you, who knows what kind of trouble you’d have caused.","Who would have thought that this young man, who looked rather honest and even had adorable dimples when he smiled, could suggest burying land mines, loading explosives into catapults, and then washing the area with white phosphorus? No one knew who he had learned such ruthless tactics from."]},{"number":553,"title":"Chapter 553: My Fragile Heart of Glass","paragraphs":["Yue Fuguang, who was having an immersive experience petting pandas in the faraway Shangjing City, suddenly had an itchy nose and sneezed.","\"Could it be that I'm allergic to panda fur?\" This was already her third sneeze today! Not only was she sneezing, but her eyelid also kept twitching.","Was something going to happen?","On the side of Jishi Gorge, Huo Sui received the order and led two hundred elite soldiers on a night - time march. These two hundred men were the best field soldiers in the Yue Army. Each of them was an expert at climbing slopes and crossing gullies. Besides their swords, spears, bows and crossbows, each carried a bag containing black iron lumps.","Shen Jian stood on the city wall and watched them disappear into the night. The mountain wind was strong, making the military flags flap loudly.","On the second day of the ninth lunar month, the Dayan Army launched a frontal attack on Jishi Gorge.","Although Shen Jian verbally showed disdain, his actions were honest. He used Huo Sui's battle plan without any hesitation, first testing the mettle of this Western Qiang army.","To preserve the combat - effective strength of the Dayan Army, he immediately used catapults to launch explosives at the ambush locations of the Western Qiang troops.","The catapults were pushed by eight men in rotation, with two more to load the ammunition. Each group consisted of ten men, advancing forward while bombarding.","Behind them were the archers, and at the end were the ordinary soldiers with swords and spears.","The Dayan Army used bows, crossbows and catapults to suppress the Western Qiang Army, attacking rhythmically in waves, leaving no chance for the Western Qiang Army to catch their breath.","The canyon was filled with the rumbling of catapults all day long. When the explosives hit the stone walls, gravel flew everywhere and dust filled the air. The explosions could be clearly heard from several miles away, and the Western Qiang soldiers were extremely frightened.","Feng Yuan personally supervised the battle at the gorge entrance. He stood on the highest point of the stone wall. Arrows from the Dayan Army occasionally flew over his head. A personal guard beside him raised a shield to protect him, but he pushed it away.","\"The Dayan people have a limited supply of gunpowder,\" he shouted to the soldiers around him. \"As long as we endure this wave, we can hold on. Once we hold on, we have a chance to counter - attack!\"","The morale of the Western Qiang Army was shattered by the explosives, and their courage was also shaken to pieces by the continuous rumbling sounds.","If it weren't for Feng Yuan's high prestige in the army and the fact that the defenders knew that behind them was Jincheng and they had nowhere to retreat, they would have fled long ago.","At the end of the day, the Dayan Army suffered more than a hundred casualties, while the casualties of the Western Qiang Army were incalculable. Some were directly blown to death, and some were buried in the gravel. The battlefield was a bloody mess, but fortunately, the defense line had not been completely broken.","After nightfall, Shen Jian summoned the middle - route army generals for a meeting. Dozens of candles were lit in the tent, illuminating it brightly. Shen Jian sat in the main seat, with a pot of tea in front of him. He took a sip and glanced at the generals in the tent.","\"How many casualties were there today?\"","\"Twenty - three were killed and eighty - two were wounded,\" reported the deputy general.","Shen Jian nodded. This number was within his expectations. The defense of Jishi Gorge was more solid than expected. A frontal attack was indeed difficult. If it weren't for the Dayan Army having gunpowder as a powerful weapon, when faced with such a terrain that was easy to defend but difficult to attack, there would be no better way than to engage in a bitter battle and sacrifice lives.","Next, Shen Jian began to arrange the subsequent tasks. Through several attacks today, he had figured out the general situation of the Western Qiang Army. He adjusted the subsequent deployment. \"Huo Sui, I order you to be the vanguard...\"","\"System, what did you say? Shen Jian and Huo Sui's troops are using infantry - tank coordination?\" Goodness me, Yue Fuguang was truly shocked.","It was just that she had casually complained to the Yue Army generals during the last meeting. How could they implement it so quickly?","[Host, isn't this what you wanted?] The system rolled its virtual eyes. If you didn't want it, why were you complaining to me in your heart?","It remembered very clearly that its host had shouted \"Little Zhu\" when complaining.","Yue Fuguang coughed lightly in embarrassment. She took a sip of water and then said with a smile, \"Well, I knew there were no tanks here, so I just wanted to show off a bit. Who would have thought that Huo Sui could draw inferences from one example? Hehe...\"","Before Yue Fuguang's embarrassed laughter could end, the system added insult to injury. [Host, who says only Huo Sui did this? Wei Yan, Cai Bing, and even the most well - behaved Lin Huaijing have been influenced by you. He's not only the military advisor among them but also like a glutinous rice ball filled with black sesame paste.]","The system had a gloating tone. [These people regard you as their teacher, believe in you, and revere you! Aren't you happy?]","\"Happy my foot!\" At this moment, Fuguang finally understood the weight of the words that Patriarch Bodhi once said to Sun Wukong: \"One day when you cause trouble, just don't bring me into it.\" And the weight was still increasing.","[Host, why do you look like you never smile? Is it a natural trait?]","Seeing that the five kingdoms were about to be unified, the system was so happy that it forgot its place. [Host, although you will leave in the future, your ideas will continue here, and your mark will be engraved throughout the future history of Dayan. Shouldn't you be happy?]","Yue Fuguang threw the pastry in her hand into the jade plate, rolled up her sleeves, and said, \"System, my will already covers all the lands of Dayan. My ideas have already been integrated into the books printed by the publishing houses. Do I still need those young guys to inherit them?\"","She clenched her fists. \"Moreover, with those books, those factories, those technologies, those schools, and the immortal Divine Maiden Hall, the marks of my existence are so deep that even if I wanted to erase them, I couldn't!\"","These things would not disappear from the long river of history even if Dayan perished and the dynasty changed one day.","\"They will be remembered, improved, but never forgotten. Humph! I think you're getting carried away and need a beating!\"","[Host, have you forgotten that there was an \"evil - clearing\" incident in your hometown? You should be on guard against such things. Those technologies, those books...]","Yue Fuguang waved her hand, interrupting the system's words that might be harmful to \"unity.\" \"I've already taken precautions against a similar situation here.\"","[So, are those formation - arranging materials you're going to buy from the system store for the Divine Maiden Hall?]","\"Otherwise? Although I'm borrowing this body now, I can't stand the thought that one day someone will destroy my shrine and steal my statues in a place I can't see. Then they'll say in front of the Divine Maiden Hall, 'The Divine Maiden is nothing special. She can't even protect her own shrine!' With my sensitive heart, I'd be so angry that I'd die!\""]},{"number":554,"title":"Chapter 554: The Host Has a Conscience, but Not Much","paragraphs":["The System thought about its host’s pettiness and figured that if something like that really happened, she would probably turn evil once she found out.","[Cloth! Lots and lots of cloth! I’ll go ask the Main System for a discount!]","The moment Yue Fuguang heard that, she almost asked: Aren’t you a nobody with no official registration? Weren’t you supposed to keep yourself hidden? How did you get in touch with the Main System again? Just what kind of relationship do you two have, anyway?","But for the sake of the discount, she silently reined in her curiosity. She could save the gossip for later—the System wasn’t going anywhere, after all. Discounts, on the other hand, didn’t come around every day.","There were plenty of things she wanted to buy. Since there was a sale this time, she might as well stock up on everything.","[System, hurry, hurry! The size of the discount depends on you!]","The instant the thick smoke rose into the sky, the morale and fighting spirit Feng Yuan had struggled to rally scattered in the blink of an eye.","First, the soldiers at the far southern end began running down. Then the ones in the middle followed, and finally the entire defensive line collapsed. No one shouted for a retreat, and no one ordered them to flee, but everyone was running.","Every soldier understood one simple truth: their retreat had been cut off. If they stayed, they would only be walking toward certain death. What was more, the Dayan army had not only used gunpowder to blow them up—they had also launched a fire attack.","They had not used the white phosphorus Huo Sui had mentioned to wash the battlefield clean, but flaming oil was still more than enough to make things unbearable for ordinary flesh and blood.","Looking at the defeated Western Qiang army, Huo Sui regretted that they had not managed to overhear the Grand Preceptor’s method for making white phosphorus. If they had, these people would not have had even the chance to run.","Yue Fuguang: With all those hands-on, experiment-loving murderous talents around, do you think I’d dare say that? Leave people a way out, will you?","System: The host has a conscience, but not much of one!","Feng Yuan drew his blade and cut down two deserters who ran past him. His eyes bulged with fury, and even his beard trembled. But his sword could not stop the flood of fleeing soldiers. They surged past him, forcing him backward, and he was swept along by the press of bodies, retreating from the stone wall against his will.","The stone wall was empty.","When the Dayan infantry saw the defenders break and flee, they launched their charge without waiting for orders. Shield-bearers led the way, spearmen followed close behind, and archers and crossbowmen provided cover from the rear.","The distance from the stone wall to the Dayan army’s position was only two hundred and fifty paces. They covered it in less than the time it took to burn half an incense stick.","Huo Sui’s men were at the very front. They had fought all day and were utterly exhausted, but the sight of the retreating Western Qiang army filled them with renewed energy. Shouting like madmen, they charged into the camp at the mouth of the gorge.","Under the protection of his personal guards, Feng Yuan fought his way through and retreated toward Jincheng with fewer than three thousand men.","Behind him stretched a sea of routed soldiers, while the iron hooves of the pursuing Dayan cavalry thundered in pursuit. His warhorse ran until white foam poured from its mouth. Fury and despair mingled in his eyes, scorching his entire face with heat.","They raced out of the mountain pass, thinking they had finally escaped with their lives, when explosions that seemed capable of destroying heaven and earth erupted all around them...","The Battle of Jishi Gorge lasted less than three days from the moment the Dayan army launched its formal assault to the complete collapse of the Western Qiang forces. More than eight thousand Western Qiang soldiers were wounded, while the number killed could not be determined. Over thirty thousand were taken prisoner, and most of the stragglers who fled were swallowed by that final explosion.","The Dayan army suffered roughly four hundred casualties, fewer than two hundred of whom died in battle.","From a tactical standpoint, the battle was hardly worth recording in the annals of war. It had been nothing more than a standard tactic: opening the way with gunpowder, followed by coordinated action among the troops.","Its significance, however, lay in the fact that once Jishi Gorge fell, the eastern gateway to Jincheng was completely exposed. From Jishi Gorge to Jincheng, the road ahead was flat and unobstructed, with no natural defenses to hold.","The news reached Jincheng late at night on the seventh day of the ninth month.","Zhao Chongli heard it in the prime minister’s residence. He remained silent for a long while before weakly waving a hand at the scout who had delivered the message.","“I understand. Go down and get some rest.”","After the scout left, Zhao Chongli sat alone in his study, a map of the entire Western Qiang territory spread out before him. Candlelight flickered, casting his shadow onto the wall, where it grew and shrank with every tremor of the flame.","He was sixty-five years old that year. He had served two generations of Western Qiang kings. He had witnessed Western Qiang at the height of its power, commanding a hundred thousand mounted archers and inspiring awe across the land. He had also watched the nation decline step by step.","Its decline had not begun with Dayan. It had begun when the country slowly rotted from within.","When Dayan had suddenly risen to prominence several years earlier, he had known that a war between the two countries was inevitable.","But he had never expected the day to come so soon. He always felt that someone had been pushing events along from behind the scenes, forcing that day to arrive before Western Qiang—or any of the other countries—had time to prepare.","Yue Fuguang: Old Zhao, you’ll never understand the heart of a mission-taker eager to complete her assignment.","Life here was comfortable, but Yue Fuguang had not forgotten her original purpose. She had not been dazzled by wealth or personal adoration. She gave herself a mental thumbs-up. JPG.","His heart felt terribly heavy. It was not fear, nor was it sorrow. It was more like relief—the relief of finally facing what was coming instead of anxiously waiting for it.","He spread out a sheet of paper and began to write a letter. It was addressed to Shen Jian, and its wording was earnest without being servile.","In the letter, he wrote that Western Qiang and Dayan had originally shared the same roots, and that the Goddess Yue was the patron deity common to both countries. Now that Dayan intended to unify the realm, Western Qiang was willing to submit, so long as the lives of its people were spared. If Shen Jian was willing to grant that request, he would persuade Xi Yan to open its gates and surrender.","Once the letter was finished, he summoned the household servant he trusted most and instructed him, “Leave the city after dawn and head east. When you see the Dayan army’s banners, hand this letter directly to General Shen. Remember—you must place it in his hands yourself.”","The servant accepted the letter and carefully tucked it inside his robe.","Zhao Chongli added, “If our own people stop you along the way, tell them you’re going east to investigate the battle. Keep the letter hidden. Don’t let them find it if they search you.”","The servant nodded and withdrew.","Wind rose outside the window, making the poplar trees in the courtyard rustle loudly. Zhao Chongli walked to the window and gazed at the half-moon in the sky.","The moonlight was bright, spilling across the roofs and courtyard and cloaking everything in a layer of cold, pale light. Suddenly, he remembered the sight of his little granddaughter offering incense with his wife in the family’s small Buddhist shrine.","The tiny girl had knelt on the prayer mat beside her grandmother, palms pressed together, bowing with devout sincerity.","At the time, as the prime minister of Western Qiang, he had neither stopped nor encouraged them. His wife and the younger members of the family all assumed that he knew nothing about their household’s worship of the Goddess Yue.","But the only things his old wife and granddaughter prayed for were the safety of their family and a peaceful, stable life."]},{"number":555,"title":"Chapter 555: Let Me Surrender — Is That What You Call Magnanimity","paragraphs":["Can war truly bring peace and stability?","No.","Then we can’t keep fighting. The blade of Dayan’s unification was something Western Qiang could not withstand. There was no reason to keep using the people’s lives to fill the gap.","Some of the defeated soldiers from Feng Yuan’s army gradually made their way back to Jincheng, bringing news of the defeat at Jishi Gorge—and two even more alarming reports.","The first was that General Feng Yuan had disappeared, presumably blown to death by the Dayan army’s gunpowder, leaving no remains behind.","As for the second, the Dayan army had not killed any prisoners at the gorge entrance. Not only had they spared them, they had also given the surrendered Western Qiang soldiers dry rations and water. They had not released them to go home, but neither had they taken their lives.","Thanks to the radio, news of the great victory at Jishi Gorge reached Dayan even faster than it reached Jincheng.","“It ended that quickly?”","[What else did you expect? With gunpowder clearing the way, even a naturally defensible place like Jishi Gorge couldn’t withstand coordinated infantry-and-tank operations!]","“It looks like the war will be over soon. We need to start preparing for what comes next.” Their work was not over just because the war had ended. Only after the territory had been reclaimed and unified, and the people’s hearts had been won, could they truly consider their mission complete.","[As long as the army continues its advance and takes Jincheng and the Huaqiang tribes, Western Qiang will have been completely incorporated into Dayan.]","“Jincheng? The Huaqiang tribes? That won’t take long either.”","Yue Fuguang’s words proved prophetic.","After the defeat at Jishi Gorge, the morale of the troops on Jincheng’s walls visibly plummeted. The soldiers keeping watch atop the walls looked listless, the patrol formations had become lax, and officers had to shout several times before anyone responded when they ordered a change of guard.","More than ten thousand men had died in the battle at Jishi Gorge. The scattered soldiers who fled back kept talking about how powerful the Dayan army’s thunder bombs were and how swift its cavalry was. Their words spread through the garrison like a plague, inflicting more damage than any attack by the enemy.","Xi Yan heard the news of the defeat at the palace. He smashed his teacup on the spot and cursed Feng Yuan—who was already dead and reduced to bones—as a useless pretty face. He spent a full quarter of an hour pouring out every insult he knew without pause.","But once he had finished cursing, he realized there was very little he could actually do.","Jincheng’s garrison had originally numbered fifty thousand. Feng Yuan had taken thirty thousand with him, and fewer than three thousand had returned. Including the troops stationed in the city and the private forces contributed by the various families, there were fewer than thirty thousand men in total.","Not a single reinforcement force had arrived. They had not been delayed on the road—they had never set out in the first place.","After hearing that Jishi Gorge had fallen, those lords became even more determined to remain on the sidelines.","The Dayan army was already at their doorstep. Sending troops now would simply be sending them to their deaths, wouldn’t it?","The Huaqiang tribes to the west did send someone, but not to offer support. They had come to name their price. Their representative said, “Your Majesty, if you want us to send troops, please deliver the gold you promised first.”","Xi Yan was so furious that he wanted to have the man beheaded, but ultimately restrained himself. He ordered the treasury to provide three hundred taels of gold and sent the man away.","He knew that even after receiving the gold, the troops would never come. The Huaqiang people would only play tricks. They were even more shrewd than the Western Qiang nobles and would never place a bet on a battle they were certain to lose.","Sure enough, after waiting several days, Xi Yan saw no sign of them. He was so enraged that he fell ill.","However, the gossip circulating through Jincheng claimed that their king had not fallen ill from anger. His health had already been poor, and being provoked by the Huaqiang tribes had merely pushed him over the edge.","The princes, including Xi Yuanshan, therefore entered the palace to attend to the ailing king and were kept there. Meanwhile, Xie Zhiyao, who was still at the Prince Yi’s residence, took advantage of the opportunity to leave the estate, slip out of Jincheng, and head toward the Huaqiang territory.","By the time Xi Yuanshan received the news and sent people after her, she had already vanished without a trace.","After several days of rest, Shen Jian’s army arrived at the eastern outskirts of Jincheng on the fifteenth day of the ninth month.","More than forty thousand soldiers formed ranks outside the city, their banners blotting out the sun and their weapons standing like a forest of steel.","The catapults were pushed to the front lines, thunder bombs loaded onto them and aimed directly at Jincheng’s eastern gate. The cavalry spread out on both wings. The horses snorted, pawed at the earth, and kicked up clouds of dust.","The infantry formed ranks that stretched from outside the eastern gate all the way to the distant riverbank.","Shen Jian sent a master archer to shoot a letter onto the city wall. Its contents were simple: the Dayan army would not slaughter the city or kill surrendered soldiers.","If Jincheng opened its gates and surrendered, both the officials and the common people within the city would be spared. They had one day to respond. If they refused to surrender after that deadline, the army would attack, and the Dayan army would not be responsible for civilian casualties within the city.","The letter was delivered by the defending soldiers to Xi Yan. Chancellor Zhao Chongli, who had also received Shen Jian’s reply, was in the palace at the time.","Still lying in bed, Xi Yan finished reading the letter. His hand trembled slightly—not from fear, but from rage. Yet he did not know whom to be angry with. Dayan? Shen Jian? Feng Yuan, who had died in defeat? The tribal leaders who had refused to send reinforcements? Or himself?","He handed the letter to Zhao Chongli.","“Minister Zhao, you should read it too.”","Zhao Chongli took the letter and read it from beginning to end. His expression did not change in the slightest. He placed the letter on the table and said calmly, “Your Majesty, Shen Jian’s terms are already quite generous.”","“Generous?” Xi Yan’s voice suddenly rose. “He has marched all the way to my city and is ordering me to surrender. You call that generous?”","“Your Majesty, you should be able to imagine what the situation will be if you refuse and the city falls.” Zhao Chongli ignored his king’s unreasonable outburst, his voice remaining calm. “The Dayan army maintains strict discipline within Dayan’s borders. But if we truly follow the Princess Consort Yi’s suggestion and incite the people to resist, then once the city falls, no one can guarantee that the Dayan army will continue to refrain from harming even the smallest thing.","“Shen Jian is Emperor Mingxi’s nephew. Even if he fails to follow military orders, His Majesty the Emperor would likely overlook it.”","Seeing that the king, who had been persuaded by the Princess Consort Yi the previous day, remained unmoved by his words, he gave Xi Yuanshan a subtle glance.","Xi Yuanshan pressed his lips together. Knowing that this was his own princess consort’s fault—and that he would have to bear the consequences—he spoke up. “Father, Xie Zhiyao has disappeared. Her words cannot be trusted, and neither can her plan.”","He glanced at his father, who had lowered his eyes, and continued, “If things truly unfold as Chancellor Zhao says, then once the city falls, the people within it will suffer, the imperial family and royal kinsmen will suffer, and the common people will not be spared either.","“If we surrender now, the terms Shen Jian has personally offered will serve as our protection. He is the emperor’s nephew, so he can be trusted. Therefore, Father, this really does count as generous.”"]},{"number":556,"title":"Chapter 556: Have You Got a Virus","paragraphs":["“I’m not entirely sure either. However, the device we placed on her was expelled from her body after she gave birth. Otherwise, we could have used it to locate her.” Its data was limited, and the images it transmitted were somewhat blurry.","Yue Fuguang saw that the system truly could not give her a definite answer, so she stopped dwelling on it. “Forget it. Even if she isn’t dead, she won’t be able to stir up much trouble.","“But just in case, I should still give the royal father and son a heads-up. They should keep an eye out regardless. Her husband and son are still alive, after all.”","Half a month later, Emperor Mingxi and the Crown Prince watched as the final missing corner of the Great Yan map was filled in. Needless to say, their hearts surged with excitement and pride.","The Great Yan court remained in a celebratory uproar for several days before the sovereign and his ministers finally managed to calm down.","Once they had regained their composure, the next matters on the agenda were rewarding those who had contributed and deciding how to govern such a vast nation. More importantly, they had to determine how to win the people’s hearts.","That would require institutions—and... time.","As for Yue Fuguang, events unfolded exactly as she had anticipated. Although Great Yan had achieved unification, the progress bar for their mission still had not reached completion.","“System, Great Yan has been unified for more than a year now. Why is the progress bar still stuck at ninety-nine percent? Could it be broken? Or have you caught a virus?”","At the mention of a virus, the system discreetly rolled its eyes. 【Host, there is no way I could be broken! Could the reason our mission still hasn’t been completed be that there are issues with the integration of the peoples from the various nations, or some other hidden danger?】","“What hidden danger could there be? Haven’t we already spent more than a year making the people of the various nations identify themselves as Great Yan citizens?”","【They do identify with it, but some people of Great Yan inevitably look down on others, believing that as native Great Yan citizens, they are superior.","“Although they are only a minority, once people with ulterior motives spread and magnify their views, they could stir up the resentment buried deep in the hearts of the people from the five other nations. The consequences would be extremely harmful. Besides, some people still feel uncomfortable knowing that their former country was destroyed by Great Yan.”】","“How serious is the impact?”","At that moment, Emperor Mingxi and his ministers in the Hall of Diligent Governance were discussing the same issue.","Looking over the reports from various regions, Emperor Mingxi frowned and could not help asking Zheng Zicheng, Great Yan’s “thousand-mile eyes and ears.” Regional discrimination was a serious problem. If it was not resolved, the foundations of Great Yan would become unstable, and this newly united nation could easily fall apart.","For now, with the Divine Maiden holding everything in check, no major disturbances were likely to arise, so he and the Crown Prince did not need to worry too much.","But what about in the time of their grandchildren and great-grandchildren?","They all knew that the Divine Maiden would leave one day. She could not remain Great Yan’s pillar of stability forever.","Zheng Zicheng glanced at the Crown Prince before saying to Emperor Mingxi and the other ministers, “Your Majesty, according to the information I have received, people in many regions have already begun discussing this matter in private.","“The people of Bingzhou, Xingzhou, and Yizhou—regions that were originally close to the borders—have reacted especially strongly.”","Emperor Mingxi tossed the report Zheng Zicheng had given him onto the table and looked at the several high ministers standing below. “Do any of you have a good solution?","“The people are the foundation of a nation. If the people’s hearts are unsettled, the state cannot remain at peace. Great Yan has been unified for barely a year, and now this has arisen. It strikes at the very foundations of our dynasty. We cannot afford to ignore it!”","“Your Majesty is right.” Dong Qianli stepped forward first. “However, the people of the six nations have always differed greatly in customs, food, language, and habits. Now that they are living together, friction is inevitable. Could it simply be that too little time has passed? If another generation or two were to pass, might the situation improve?”","Fortunately, although the six nations spoke different languages, they all used the same written script. Otherwise, their troubles would have been even greater.","Only now did everyone truly understand the old saying: conquering a realm was difficult, but protecting it was even harder. Governing it into the kind of strong nation united in spirit that Grand Preceptor Cheng had described was harder still.","Wei Ping shook his head. “Once a conflict arises, eliminating it later requires far more time and effort. If we do not handle this carefully now, it may affect the next generation and the generation after that. By then, matters will be even more troublesome.”","Resentment could cause serious upheaval if it was allowed to accumulate for too long. The only reason the people remained so peaceful now was because of Grand Preceptor Cheng’s presence.","Cai Xian added, “Minister Wei is right. The problems our generation can resolve should not be left for future generations.” There might not necessarily be another Divine Maiden to keep matters under control by then.","Yu Chongshan hesitated before speaking. “The people of the six nations may differ in customs and language, as Minister Dong said. However, they do share one thing in common. Perhaps we can make use of it.”","The Crown Prince’s eyes lit up. “Senior Mr. Yu, are you referring to Little Aunt? Most of the people in the six nations worship Little Aunt.”","Yu Chongshan nodded. “That is precisely what I mean. The people of the six nations all worship Fuguang. That is what they have in common.”","He bowed to Emperor Mingxi. “Your Majesty, could we use this as a starting point and create more things they share? In time, they may gradually forget that they were once people of Southern Zhao, Southern Yue, Western Qiang, Northern Li, Eastern Yi, or even... Great Yan?”","His words plunged the entire hall into silence. Everyone, including Emperor Mingxi, lowered their heads and began considering whether Yu Chongshan’s proposal was feasible.","As for making the people forget that they were Great Yan citizens... that was not important. So long as they remained his subjects, what harm was there in forgetting?","The six nations were now joined together. Although people had been relocated and communities had become intermixed, their long-established habits would not be easy to change. Creating new common ground would be even more difficult.","Yet everyone also understood that Yu Chongshan’s idea was viable. The question of where to begin would require careful planning by the sovereign and his ministers.","“Your Majesty!”","Wei Ping’s eyes suddenly shone with astonishing brightness. He gazed at Emperor Mingxi with an expression that clearly said he had something to propose, yet was unsure whether he should say it.","Emperor Mingxi waved a hand. “Minister Wei, speak freely. I absolve you of any offense in advance.”","With the emperor’s assurance, Wei Ping no longer hesitated. After carefully choosing his words, he said, “Your Majesty, the people of Southern Zhao, Southern Yue, and the other five nations identify as Great Yan citizens largely because of the kindness Grand Preceptor Cheng showed them in the early days. Deep down, however, they are still accustomed to calling themselves people of Southern Zhao or Southern Yue.”","Everyone nodded. If not for Grand Preceptor Cheng, even the people of Southern Yue and Southern Zhao—who were the most obedient—would never have become what they were today.","“So...” Wei Ping quickly glanced at Emperor Mingxi’s expression. Finally, he shut his eyes and voiced the bold idea he had been considering. “Should we change the name of the country?”"]},{"number":557,"title":"Chapter 557: Change the Dynastic Title","paragraphs":["“What? Change the dynastic name?” The hall erupted at once. The voices of a dozen officials sounded louder than a crowd of several dozen.","By contrast, Emperor Mingxi and the Crown Prince—the imperial father and son—were surprisingly not the most agitated.","Emperor Mingxi frowned. Rather than flying into a rage, he pondered for a moment before asking cautiously, “Lord Wei, why do you have such an idea?”","Wei Ping bowed and replied, “In response to Your Majesty, this humble servant believes that since some among the people of Great Yan hold themselves above the people of the other five states, thinking themselves a cut above them—then what if Great Yan were to cease to exist?”","Wei Ping had truly thrown caution to the wind this time. The moment they heard him say that Great Yan should cease to exist, Cai Xian and the others broke into a cold sweat for him, afraid the Emperor would lose his temper.","Yet Emperor Mingxi did not grow angry as everyone had expected. His brows merely knit tighter, and his voice gave no hint of pleasure or displeasure. “Go on.”","Seeing this reaction, Wei Ping relaxed somewhat. “This humble servant was thinking: since that is the case, why not adopt an entirely new dynastic name? Let the people of all six states begin anew. Then, in a certain sense, would they not be starting from the same place?”","Wei Ping straightened. “From then on, there would no longer be any distinction between the people of Great Yan, Southern Yue, Southern Zhao, Northern Li, Western Qiang, and Eastern Yi. From that day forth, everyone would be equal.”","He cupped his hands in salute. “This is merely this humble servant’s foolish suggestion. Whether it is feasible still requires Your Majesty and my fellow officials to deliberate upon it.”","Deliberate? Everyone turned to look at their Emperor. A matter as momentous as changing the dynastic name was not something they could decide.","Great Yan had been named by Emperor Gaozu himself. In the end, whether they could defy the laws and traditions of their ancestors had to be decided by Emperor Gaozu’s descendants.","When Emperor Mingxi saw the looks his trusted ministers were giving him, he nearly laughed in exasperation. You’re afraid Emperor Gaozu will come knocking on your doors in the dead of night—do you think I’m not afraid too?","He was not afraid of his own father, but he was afraid his imperial grandfather might pay him a midnight visit and call him an unfilial descendant.","Still, Wei Ping’s proposal had stirred his heart in a most shameful way.","He glanced at his fine eldest son, who was looking at him as well. If he did not do it himself, he could hardly leave this hidden danger for his descendants to deal with. He had Fuguang as his backing; his sons and grandsons might not have the same advantage.","In a sense, he himself was the founder of this newly unified realm. And as its founder, what was there that he would not dare to do?","At last, Emperor Mingxi came to a decision. Yet he still asked, “What do you all think of Lord Wei’s proposal?”","The officials looked at one another. Finally, Yu Chongshan stepped forward and said, “This humble servant believes Lord Wei’s words are sound. Even if the dynastic name is changed, the country will remain the same country, and the realm will still belong to the Xie family. That will not change in the slightest.”","The others nodded in agreement. “Senior Mr. Yu speaks wisely. We will still be Your Majesty’s subjects. We simply wonder what the Grand Preceptor thinks. Should we not also ask the Grand Preceptor’s opinion regarding the adoption of a new dynastic name?”","“Ask me?” The moment Yue Fuguang arrived at court, Emperor Mingxi and his ministers tossed this question her way.","Her face was full of helplessness. She was hopeless at naming things—what good suggestion could she possibly have?","But then... Yue Fuguang rubbed the teacup in her hands. “System, you know, Wei Ping’s idea might actually increase the people’s sense of belonging. At the very least, as subjects under a new dynastic name, the six states would all be equal.”","The system data flickered rapidly. 【Host, according to the system’s calculations and assessment, this method has a sixty percent chance of succeeding.】","Sixty percent was not bad!","And even if it failed, it probably would not have any terribly adverse effects on Dayan, would it?","All at once, she understood why the ruler and ministers of Dayan had asked for her opinion. They wanted to make use of her influence among the common people!","Emperor Mingxi would bear the blame for changing the dynasty’s name, while she would be responsible for choosing the new one. That did not seem so bad.","“Your Majesty, my lords, have you truly decided to change Dayan’s national title?” Yue Fuguang asked again for confirmation.","If the ruler and ministers of Dayan had truly set their hearts on it, she would not come up with a name herself—but she could copy one. What harm was there in helping them plagiarize an impressive new national title?","“After discussing the matter with the ministers, we all believe this would be a feasible way to erase the divisions among the people of the various former states. What does Fuguang think?”","Within Xuanzheng Hall, candlelight gleamed upon twelve folding screens depicting rivers and mountains. The screens had been made recently, painted with the former territories of the five states. The ink was still fresh, carrying the faint scent of pine soot.","After Dayan had destroyed the five states and unified the realm, Emperor Mingxi had indeed discussed changing the national title with his ministers several times in private. Yet no matter how many candidates they had in mind, everyone in the Dayan court shared an unspoken understanding: the person who would make the final decision was not their emperor, but the Grand Preceptor.","Yue Fuguang nodded in agreement. “I also think Your Majesty and the ministers have a good idea. As for the name, what do Your Majesty and my lords have in mind?”","She did not believe they had no ideas of their own.","Emperor Mingxi smiled helplessly. “Yesterday, while you were absent, the court debated the new national title for an entire hour.”","Yue Fuguang took a bite of her apple. “Oh? Then let us hear it. What brilliant opinions do you all have?”","Ever since the five states had been unified, Yue Fuguang had become increasingly casual in both word and deed. As she crunched away at her apple, an elderly Hanlin scholar with a grizzled beard stepped forward first, entirely unfazed by her manner.","“Reporting to the Grand Preceptor, this humble official believes we should choose the character ‘Yong.’ Yong signifies harmony—may the realm prosper in harmony.”","Before the old scholar had even finished, a younger Hanlin scholar stepped forward.","“This humble official believes that, with the five states only recently pacified, we should choose the character ‘Zhen,’ to establish our might!”","Yue Fuguang shook her head inwardly. Setting aside whether the purpose of changing the national title was to project military might, the name Great Zhen simply did not sound very good.","“Improper, improper! Such a name runs contrary to the original purpose of changing the national title. This servant believes we should choose the character ‘Zhao,’ to proclaim Heaven’s mandate!”","Yue Fuguang did not even need to reject it before someone else leapt forward in opposition.","“Your Majesty, this servant believes we should—”","“Improper, improper. This servant believes—”","The voices gradually grew clamorous, like a pot of porridge brought to a rolling boil. When it came to voicing their opinions, not a single civil official lacked a sharp tongue.","Seeing that the scene had once again become exactly like yesterday’s, Emperor Mingxi frowned slightly. He raised a hand, and the hall fell abruptly silent.","“This matter still requires the Grand Preceptor’s final decision,” he said, his tone leaving no room for dispute.","The ministers came to their senses. In the heat of the argument, how had they forgotten that the Grand Preceptor had been meant to serve as judge from the very beginning?","No matter how fiercely they argued, if the Grand Preceptor did not approve, even the most reasonable justification would be futile.","In the vast Xuanzheng Hall, no one spoke again. All eyes turned toward Yue Fuguang, who was watching their quarrel with keen interest."]},{"number":558,"title":"Chapter 558: China has great rites and etiquette, hence it is called Xia.","paragraphs":["Some faces had flushed without their realizing it. Had they not, just moments ago, resembled common folk haggling over the price of vegetables in a marketplace?","Yet when facing Yue Fuguang, Emperor Mingxi’s imposing majesty gradually softened, leaving behind a warmth and patience he showed no one else.","“Fuguang, do you have any thoughts on the new dynastic name?”","Privately, he hoped that Yue Fuguang herself would choose the new name, rather than having one selected from the officials’ discussion. Only then, perhaps, would she feel a little more attachment to Great Yan.","It could be said that Emperor Mingxi spared no effort in tying Great Yan and Yue Fuguang together, hoping to win a little more of her favor.","Perhaps he had sensed something.","Yue Fuguang was called upon once more. After giving it serious thought, she reflected that names such as Great Tang, Great Han, and Great Ming had never existed in this era. They had also all belonged to powerful dynasties of antiquity; any one of them could have been used for Great Yan.","Yet what came out of her mouth was, “‘Yong’ is too rounded and gentle. It is a good name, but it does not suit Great Yan’s present circumstances.”","She tapped the tabletop.","“As for ‘Zhen,’ it is too sharp. Great Yan is changing its dynastic name in order to bring people together, not to intimidate anyone. It is not aimed at any particular party; it is meant to unite everyone.”","Yue Fuguang lifted her gaze and proceeded to comment on He, Zhao, Ding, Cheng, Xuan, Jing, Shun, and the rest, one by one.","Seeing Emperor Mingxi nod repeatedly, she suddenly asked, “Does Your Majesty have a character you favor?”","Emperor Mingxi did not answer immediately. He rose and walked to the twelve folding screens. His fingertips gently brushed across one of them—a map of the territory of Western Qiang, the last of the five kingdoms to fall. The ink looked as fresh as if it had not yet dried.","“I have shed too much blood,” he said, neither loudly nor softly. “The blood of the five kingdoms has stained half the Cang River. If the dynastic name were to include a character like ‘Zhen’—or ‘Wei’...”","He paused, turned to look at her, then shifted his gaze to the assembled officials. Daylight streamed in from outside, flickering in his eyes.","“Never mind what later generations may say of me. Even the people of the five kingdoms, at this very moment, surely only wish to recover and live peaceful lives.”","Yue Fuguang said nothing. She knew that Emperor Mingxi still feared the judgment of history—the endless voices of centuries to come. After all, not everyone could see the benefits of unification. All they would see was how many people had died in this war of unification.","And there was gunpowder. Much of the credit for unifying half the realm so swiftly lay in its power. It had terrified too many people and killed too many as well—and most of those people had not been citizens of Great Yan. Naturally, the common people harbored resentment and feared Great Yan’s imperial court.","But fear alone could not sustain a nation. It also needed love—or, more precisely, a sense of belonging.","Emperor Mingxi returned to the imperial desk.","“Fuguang, my ministers and I both know that Great Yan has reached its present heights entirely because of you. Therefore...” Emperor Mingxi looked at her, his tone sincere and earnest. “Half of this realm is yours. The dynastic name should, of course, be yours to decide.”","Yue Fuguang did not refuse.","She walked to the imperial desk and accepted the brush. Upon the snow-white paper, she wrote two characters.","She did not trace them or sketch their outlines. Her brush fell decisively, the words formed in a single sweep.","Great Xia!","Emperor Mingxi stared at those two characters. His brows shifted slightly.","The entire Xuanzheng Hall fell so silent that everyone could hear their own hearts pounding.","Yue Fuguang took a brief moment to admire her own calligraphy. Her efforts of the past few years had not been in vain—at last, her handwriting was presentable!","“Xia.” She heard Emperor Mingxi slowly pronounce the character. His voice trailed through the vast hall in a long, lingering echo. For some reason, it brought a faint ache to Yue Fuguang’s heart. It was the homeland to which she could never return.","Yue Fuguang turned around, her back to the imperial desk, facing the twelve-panel screen of mountains and rivers. At that moment, her silhouette overlapped with that of the newly completed statue of the Divine Maiden in the Hall of the Divine Maiden. Yet her voice was as light as a breeze brushing across the river’s surface.","“Does Your Majesty know what Xia means?”","Emperor Mingxi rose as well and stood at her side. Together, they gazed upon the immense map of the realm.","“All the ministers have searched through the classics, citing text after text, and proposed dozens of auspicious characters.” Yue Fuguang’s gaze settled upon the land that had once belonged to the Five Kingdoms.","Through the ink and painted lines, she seemed to see the mountains and rivers, the fields and villages she had once nurtured.","“And yet not one of them mentioned this character.” She raised her hand, her fingertips lightly tracing that vast expanse of territory in the air.","“Xia means greatness. It is the very first entry in a book I once read, called the *Erya*. Your Majesty, my lords—Xia means great. The various Xia are the people of the Central Realm. Is that not precisely what unified Dayan is today?”","“Three hundred years ago, this land was originally one Xia.” Yue Fuguang’s voice gradually deepened, like moonlight sinking into a still pool. “Dayan, Nanyue, Nanzhao, Beili, Xiqiang, and the Eastern Yi spoke different languages, yet shared the same writing and similar rites. Their people traveled and traded freely among one another. Only later did war arise, and the land remained divided for three hundred years.”","Three centuries were enough for most people to forget that they had once belonged to the same country. So much time had passed that, if they had not still used the same written language, Yue Fuguang could imagine that she might have had to follow King of Qin’s path once more.","Her gaze fell upon the famous mountains and great rivers she had once traveled through.","“Xia has another meaning,” she said, suddenly turning to face the assembled civil and military officials.","“Hua,” said Yue Fuguang. “In another book I once read, the *Zuo Commentary*, there is a passage: ‘The Central Realm possesses the grandeur of ritual, and is therefore called Xia; it possesses the beauty of its garments and adornments, and is therefore called Hua.’ Xia means greatness; greatness is Hua. Xia is Hua, and Hua is Xia.”","Her voice softened, like a fine string lightly plucked. Her eyes turned toward the hall’s open doors, as though she were looking toward some place unimaginably far away.","In the end, she still missed home. No matter how well she lived here, she still longed for it.","“Your Majesty has taken the Five Kingdoms. There is no need to distinguish one from another any longer. They are people of Xia, and so are you. From this day onward, this land shall have only one name: Xia—the Great Xia.”","Sunlight streamed in from outside, leaving half the great hall bathed in light and shadow. Everyone present, including Emperor Mingxi, was deeply shaken by Yue Fuguang’s words:","‘The Central Realm possesses the grandeur of ritual, and is therefore called Xia; it possesses the beauty of its garments and adornments, and is therefore called Hua.’ Xia means greatness; greatness is Hua. Xia is Hua, and Hua is Xia."]},{"number":559,"title":"Chapter 559: Happy or not, surprised or not","paragraphs":["They hadn't read Erya and Zuo Zhuan, but it didn't stop them from thinking that the name \"Xia\" was beautiful and grand, and it was very suitable for the Great Yan at this time.","\"Great Xia,\" everyone murmured these two characters over and over again.","\"Since Your Majesty asks for my opinion, I think this character is excellent,\" she said, with a rare sly smile in her eyes. \"If Your Majesty and the gentlemen don't like it, then we can think of another one.\"","\"No, no, no. The word chosen by the Young Master Instructor is excellent!\" Elder Wang Shouchen stepped forward first.","He also didn't forget to give a wink to the emperor, as if to say, \"Your Majesty, don't mess this up. Hurry up and agree!\"","Emperor Mingxi blushed. He had just been lost in thought and got distracted, which made Yue Fuguang misunderstand.","He cleared his throat and said in a loud voice, \"Our Great Yan is originally the central country in the world, a unity of the center, orthodoxy, civilization, and territory.\"","They had seen the world map that Yue Fuguang had shown. No matter how much land there was outside of Great Yan, the emperor and his officials all agreed that Great Yan was the center of the world.","The other places were all uncivilized barbaric lands.","\"The people of our Great Yan have lived in the center of the world for generations, so it is the Central Country. It has great etiquette and beautiful clothing. 'Xia' means great, and 'great' means 'Hua'.\"","He also looked outside the hall, as if he could see his vast territory. \"From now on, there will be no more divisions between Great Yan, Southern Yue, Southern Zhao, Northern Li, Western Qiang, and Eastern Yi on this land. From now on, there will only be one name, which is 'Xia', Great Xia.\"","He picked up the imperial seal and firmly stamped it on the two characters \"Great Xia\" written by Yue Fuguang.","The cinnabar spread, and the seal characters were clearly visible.","Outside the Xuancheng Hall, the sun was rising slowly. The golden sunlight shone on the owl-shaped ornaments on the roof ridge, as if gilding an ancient country with a new and golden dawn.","The name of Great Xia spread out at the fastest speed. \"System, the task progress bar has finally moved!\" Yue Fuguang looked at the task progress bar on the system panel, which had reached 99.5%. A big burden in her heart was finally eased a little.","Although it wasn't 100%, at least it was no longer stuck at 99% for nearly a year. It was obvious that changing the name of Great Yan was the right move.","[Host, we're almost there! Just a little bit more and we'll succeed!] The system was also very excited. It had actually suspected that there was something wrong with itself.","[It's probably because the time is too short and many common people don't know the name of Great Xia yet. Great Xia was named by the host. With the common people's pious belief in you, it won't take long for us to complete the task.]","The system's prediction came true. It had only been a little over a month since Yue Fuguang proposed the name of Great Xia at the court meeting. One sunny afternoon, she was lying in the corridor, admiring the beautiful spring scenery.","Surrounded by cute little ones like Treading Snow Without a Trace and Caramel Milk Tea, she was in the midst of petting the cats when suddenly she heard a ding.","It was the same sound as when she first bound the system.","[Ding! Congratulations to the host, Yue Fuguang, for successfully completing the main task of this world. Task rating: S-level. The task reward has been issued. Please collect it yourself!]","\"Zero-Seven, Zero-Seven, did you see that? We've completed the task!\"","[Host, Tongtong saw it. Not only did we complete the task, but we also got the highest rating!] The system was even more excited than Yue Fuguang.","\"By the way, system, how long can we stay in this task world after completing the task?\"","[Ten days, host. After ten days, we'll enter the next task world.]","\"Little Zhu, do you mean that Master will come to pick me up in ten days?\" The next day at the morning court, Yue Fuguang let out the news about her leaving through her thoughts.","What? The Young Master Instructor's master would come to pick her up in ten days?","Emperor Mingxi and the civil and military officials looked at each other, not understanding what this meant for a moment.","Seeing that the emperor and the officials seemed not to understand, the system continued to chat with Yue Fuguang. [Yes, master. The Divine Venerable said that because you've prevented a century-long catastrophe of massacres in this world. You've saved countless lives, which is a great merit.","Master, you can end your mortal training ahead of time and return to Lingxu Mountain! Aren't you happy and surprised?]","Happy and surprised?","The emperor and his officials didn't know if the Young Master Instructor was happy and surprised, but they were really surprised and not at all happy.","They even felt a sense of dizziness as if the sky was falling.","In Emperor Mingxi's eyes, the whole world was gray at this moment, and only Yue Fuguang sitting below him was a vivid color. But this bright color was about to leave him, leave Great Xia!","Emperor Mingxi covered his chest and looked down pale - faced. What he saw were the officials who were also covering their chests and gasping for breath.","The hall suddenly fell into a dead silence. Elder Wang Shouchen, who had been talking non - stop about the newly added cultivated land this year, suddenly seemed to have his throat grabbed and could only make hoarse sounds.","Out of the corner of her eye, Yue Fuguang was really afraid that the old man, being of such an advanced age, couldn't hold on and would faint. Fortunately, in the past two years, she had secretly and openly taken good care of their health. Look, even after such a shock, he could still stand there with his eyes wide open.","\"It is a bit of a surprise. I thought I'd have to wait until I was old and gray to go back,\" Yue Fuguang said cheerfully. Anyone could tell that the Young Master Instructor was happy.","Sure enough, the sorrows and joys of humans and gods are not the same!","They were extremely sad, but the Young Master Instructor was just thinking about going home. They had really misjudged the situation after all!","[If master had let things go and allowed this world to develop according to its original historical trajectory, you would indeed have to complete eighty years of training.","Now that master has changed history and let this world regain its vitality, the Heavenly Dao is rewarding you with great merit. It's time for you to return to Lingxu Mountain.]","After hearing what the divine artifact said, the emperor and his officials felt mixed emotions.","If the Young Master Instructor hadn't taken care of them, they would all have died. But by taking care of them, the price they had to pay was to lose her protection ahead of time. This...","\"Ten days isn't a long time, but it should be enough for me to make proper arrangements and leave without any worries. I hope my grandparents won't be too sad.\"","At this time, Yu Chongshan's heart was bleeding. How could he not be sad?","[What does master need to arrange? Now Great Xia is thriving and full of vitality. There shouldn't be anything for master to worry about.]"]},{"number":560,"title":"Chapter 560: Not Leaving Them Anything to Survive On","paragraphs":["Yu Chongshan’s heart was already bleeding. How could he not be heartbroken?","[What is Master planning to arrange? Great Xia is flourishing and full of vitality now. There should be nothing left for Master to worry about.]","[As for the Yu family, even without Master, the imperial family surely won’t mistreat them, right? After all, Master’s physical body still belongs to the Yu family.","The Xie family’s rule has been able to continue only because of Master’s efforts. This is karma the Xie family owes the Yu family. If future rulers mistreat or persecute the Yu family when they have committed no wrongs, then an unstable realm and the dynasty’s downfall will be the retribution they deserve.","Master isn’t planning to remind the emperor and the crown prince, is she?]","Emperor Mingxi and the crown prince exchanged a glance, cold sweat quietly creeping up their backs and dampening their underclothes.","They believed that, given the father and son’s feelings for Yue Fuguang, they naturally would not mistreat the Yu family. But what their descendants would do was truly uncertain.","Emperor Mingxi secretly ground his teeth. It seemed he would have to leave a confidential document for his descendants, warning future emperors to show the Yu family special favor as long as they had committed no wrongs.","“Reminding them is out of the question. I trust the emperor and the crown prince’s character. With the two of them around, as long as the Yu family doesn’t bring disaster upon themselves, they naturally won’t mistreat them.","“As for future rulers, that will be up to fate. However, I will leave a message for the Yu family’s descendants: they must remain loyal to the sovereign and devoted to their country, must not oppress the common people, and must never proclaim themselves kings or emperors under any circumstances.”","[Won’t you leave them something to protect their lives, such as pills or magical artifacts?]","At these words, the hearts of Emperor Mingxi and the crown prince settled back into place. They were almost flattered by Yue Fuguang’s trust in them.","If Yue Fuguang had not said that the Yu family’s descendants could never proclaim themselves kings or emperors, Emperor Mingxi might even have considered whether to make her princely title hereditary for the Yu family’s men.","Since they could not become princes, granting the Yu family’s main branch a hereditary marquisate that would endure alongside the nation would be quite suitable. Two marquises in one Yu family would be an honor in itself.","When they heard about pills and magical artifacts, everyone pricked up their ears. Over the years, many of them had received pills bestowed by the Grand Preceptor on their birthdays or during festivals, and they knew better than anyone else how beneficial such pills were.","“There’s no need to leave those things behind. They likely wouldn’t be able to protect them. Besides, I have secretly nourished and strengthened the family’s health over the years. They are all healthy and free of illness or pain, and living into their eighties or nineties will be no problem.","“Anything more would only bring them harm, not benefit.”","[You’re not leaving them a single thing? Aren’t you afraid they’ll be bullied by some blind fool in the future?]","“Don’t worry. I will lay down a protective formation around the Yu family. In a moment of life or death, it will ensure that the Yu family’s descendants remain safe.”","Yue Fuguang’s voice was icy, carrying a faint trace of killing intent. Everyone who heard her understood that the Grand Preceptor’s formation would certainly be far more than merely protective.","Yue Fuguang did not want to threaten people in this way, but everyone in the court knew her “origins” and just how many treasures she possessed.","If she did not make things clear, someone might truly assume that she would leave the Yu family a great many valuable items.","Perhaps no one in this generation would dare make a move out of consideration for their personal ties, but what about the generations to come? Her possessions were exactly the things these people needed—treasures that could extend one’s life, strengthen the body, cure illnesses, and save lives.","She did not want the Yu family’s descendants to suffer the disaster of their entire clan being wiped out because of her.","Hearing that she would leave them nothing, the father and son of the Yu family did not find it inappropriate. They had thought farther and more deeply than Yue Fuguang had.","Even if they used up everything Fuguang had given them or offered it all to the imperial family, people would still assume that the Yu family had more in reserve.","As long as the Yu family continued to exist, there would always be people watching them. That was unavoidable.","When they heard that Fuguang would set up a formation to ensure the safety of the Yu family’s descendants, they could no longer hold back their tears. They streamed down their faces in torrents.","Their fellow officials could do little more than help conceal their distress. They had no idea how to comfort them.","If this had happened to their own families, they would probably have cried themselves to death.","That day’s morning court ended amid gloom and sorrow, while suppressed sobs could be heard from several places in the rear residence of the Yu household.","Yue Fuguang was helpless and could only pretend not to hear them.","By evening, several of her married elder sisters had returned with their entire families. Judging by the trunks they had brought, they intended to stay for quite some time.","Although they desperately forced smiles when they saw Yue Fuguang, the reluctance in their eyes shimmered with tears that they could not hide.","Yue Fuguang could only pretend to amuse the children, chatting with her sisters now and then. “Ever since you got married, when have all of you ever gathered together like this outside of the holidays?”","As she spoke, she glanced at Yu Ningxin, whose belly was large with eight months of pregnancy. “Fourth Sister, you’re so far along. Why didn’t Xie Zhiquan come back with you?”","Yu Ningxin naturally could not say that, after hearing her little sister was leaving, she had run back ahead of her prince without waiting for him.","She gently stroked her belly and said with a smile, “I asked His Highness to buy the pastries you like best. He’ll be here later.”","Yu Ningxuan also smiled and joined in. “We heard that the fine wine Fuguang brewed is ready to drink, so we arranged to come and ask our little sister for a cup.”","Yu Ningxuan wore the coy, catlike expression of a glutton, just as she had back home. It was clear that she had been living well after marrying Feng You.","Yue Fuguang could not resist pinching the tender, chubby cheek of the one-and-a-half-year-old Feng Yao in her arms. “A-Yao, look. Your mother is even more of a glutton than you.”","Feng Yao, who was nibbling on a hibiscus pastry, raised his chubby little hand upon hearing this. “Mama eat!”","Then he picked up another piece with his other chubby hand and offered it to Yue Fuguang. “Yiyi eat!”","Smack! Yue Fuguang kissed his little cheek. The toddler could not even pronounce “Auntie” properly, yet he already knew how to show filial respect to his elders. Yue Fuguang adored him.","It had to be said that, regardless of whether they were boys or girls, the children of this generation all seemed to have good dispositions from a young age.","“A-Yao is such a good boy! When you grow up, you have to become a real man and protect your mother, understand?”","A-Yao nodded his round little head vigorously. “A-Yao protect Mama, protect Yiyi, protect...”"]},{"number":561,"title":"Chapter 561: A... Chicken No, It's a Bird","paragraphs":["This little guy had a high emotional quotient and counted all the elders he knew in the room.","\"A-Yao is so well-behaved. Auntie will give you a little toy to play with.\" As she said, Yue Fuguang waved her hand, and a pair of 'golden bracelets' appeared in her hand.","She put one on Feng Yao and handed the other to Yu Ningxuan. \"Fourth sister, keep this one for my unborn niece.\"","\"No need. Give them both to Young Master Yao,\" Yu Ningxin declined. \"You can give her a gift when she is born.\" As Yu Ningxin said this, her heart ached with a twinge of bitterness. She still couldn't accept the fact that her younger sister was leaving and was still trying to test her with words.","Yue Fuguang stuffed the bracelet into her hand. \"A-Yao only needs one. Remember to put this on the child after she is born. And here is this peace amulet. I'll give it to you now too.\"","Yue Fuguang took out a fine little jade plaque and gave it to Yu Ningxin as well. She also joked, \"The things I give to the children, you adults mustn't embezzle them. Remember to put them on the children and don't take them off without good reason. Otherwise, I won't give them any more in the future.\"","Old Madam Yu and Mrs. Zhang exchanged glances and also sensed that there was something special about the 'golden' bracelets. Given Fuguang's generosity, she wouldn't be stingy with a pair of gold bracelets. It could only be that these bracelets, like the peace amulet, were not ordinary items.","Everyone in the Yu family had a peace amulet. They heard from Fuguang that it was a magical item to protect people's safety. As for these bracelets...","[Master, after you leave, you won't be able to give them anything anymore! But with the jade plaque and the bracelets, one for attack and the other for defense, these little kids will be safe. You should feel at ease.]","Yue Fuguang had never felt this way before, but now that she was about to leave, she actually felt a sense of reluctance.","The Yu family members also thought as expected. Yu Ningxin, who had originally wanted to decline, didn't refuse anymore. \"Then I'll thank the child's Seventh Auntie on her behalf first.\"","Yue Fuguang said to Old Madam Yu with a smile, \"Grandmother, it's rare for our family to gather so completely. How about we go to my manor and have a good time there for a few days tomorrow?\"","Old Madam Yu smiled. She never refused her granddaughter's requests. \"Okay. We'll all listen to Fuguang. Let's go to Fuguang's manor and relax for a few days.\"","\"Madam, are you going to abandon your husband and go to enjoy yourself with the granddaughters alone?\"","Just as the old madam finished speaking, they heard Yu Chongshan's voice coming from outside the door. Truly, his voice arrived before he did.","All the younger generations stood up to greet him. Old Madam Yu blamed him affectionately, \"Isn't Master supposed to be on duty? No one is saying we won't take you. But we can't all stay at home just because of you.\"","Yu Chongshan poured himself a glass of water on his own. \"Who said I'm going to be on duty? I've already asked for leave from the emperor. I'll be staying at home these days.\"","His granddaughter was about to leave. Even if he was extremely busy, the emperor wouldn't deny their family the last time to spend with their granddaughter. If there weren't any precedents, the emperor himself would have wanted to stay in the Yu Mansion for a few days.","\"Grandfather, have you remembered everything I said?\"","Yu Chongshan had imagined for many years the time he could spend alone with his granddaughter, but he never expected it to be like this.","The whole family followed Fuguang's suggestion. The next day, including the married daughters, they all came to Fuguang's manor without exception to stay for a short time.","During the day, the family went up the mountain to pick fruits and dig wild vegetables, trying their best to look happy in front of Fuguang.","At night... at night, he was taken by his granddaughter to a secret chamber under a remote courtyard at the left rear of the manor.","This secret chamber was close to the mountain foot. It was specially and secretly built by his subordinate when the courtyard was being constructed. There were not only several secret chambers here but also a secret passage leading to the mountain.","Apart from himself, the only people who knew about this secret chamber were his eldest son and his granddaughter. As for that subordinate of his, according to his granddaughter, the memory about this place had been erased by her using a secret method.","He looked up at this secret chamber, which was a little smaller than his small study in the Yu Mansion, and slowly nodded. \"Fuguang, don't worry. I've remembered everything you just said in my heart.\"","Yue Fuguang looked at this little old man who was raising his head and trying hard not to let the tears flow down. She thought of her grandfather in her previous life. After her parents got remarried respectively, all her care came from her grandparents.","So in the past few years in the Yu Mansion, she had always treated Yu Chongshan and Old Madam Yu differently.","\"You can also rest assured. As long as there are descendants of the Yu family, this manor will surely be protected.\" Besides setting up a defensive formation in the Yu family's ancestral hall, Fuguang also left a way out for them in this manor.","These were all the legacies left by Fuguang for the descendants of the Yu family, the trump cards for survival. Naturally, the descendants of the Yu family would do their best to protect them.","\"Grandfather, I'll spread the news that I haven't left any items for the Yu family later.\" She pointed to an ordinary plain-colored purse on the table. If there was any difference, there was a... chicken? No, it was a bird embroidered on each side of the purse!","On the other side, there were two lotus flowers embroidered. There was no doubt about this. Even if the person who embroidered them was very unskilled, no one would mistake a highly recognizable flower like a lotus.","\"Grandfather, there are life-saving pills and other things I've left for the Yu family in here. You must hide it well. Don't use it unless it's absolutely necessary.\" Using it would leave traces, and it was hard to guarantee that smart people wouldn't notice something fishy.","This seemingly ordinary purse was actually a storage pouch customized by Yue Fuguang. It had similar functions to a storage bag, but it didn't need to recognize the owner by dripping blood to be used. In this way, it was also convenient for the Yu family to pass it down from generation to generation.","The only drawback was that its space was small, only twenty cubic meters. But its advantage was obvious: it was cheap!","Inside, there were not only pills but also two semi-spiritual artifacts, one for attack and the other for defense. In addition, there were several boxes of gold and several boxes of precious jewels and jade, which were some of the better collections in Yue Fuguang's warehouse.","She stroked the storage ring on her hand, which was filled with all kinds of treasures and things bought from the system mall.","The things in the storage pouch and in this secret chamber, as well as the things she left for each branch of the Yu family, were all the leftovers from her warehouse that she couldn't take away."]},{"number":562,"title":"Chapter 562: On Comforting Others: Not My Strong Suit","paragraphs":["Yu Chongshan nodded repeatedly as he gazed at the “purse” on the table. In the end, he still couldn’t stop his tears from falling. Yue Fuguang handed him a handkerchief and comforted him softly. “Grandfather, all good things must come to an end. Your granddaughter has completed her mission and is returning to Heaven to enjoy her blessings. You should be happy for me.”","As he took the handkerchief and wiped away his tears, Yu Chongshan nodded again and again. “Fuguang is right. I was thinking too narrowly. My granddaughter is going to enjoy her blessings. As her grandfather, I should be happy.”","He raised his head, clearly intending to prove that he really was happy. Unfortunately, he failed rather spectacularly. The smile on his face was more sorrowful than a cry.","【Host, aren’t you asking a little too much? Who could possibly be happy in a situation like this?】","The System had watched everything from the sidelines over the past few years. Its host had suffered only a little hardship at the beginning; after that, her days had been nothing but sweetness.","Although she was the Yu family’s greatest support, according to the System’s data, the Yu family’s feelings toward her were completely genuine.","Its host was truly lucky. After spending these years together, the Yu family regarded her as their pride. They had never abused her influence to throw their weight around, nor had anyone in the household schemed against her. Even Yu Ningrong, who had opposed her at first, had not turned out to be ungrateful.","It was easy to see how heartbroken the Yu family would be upon learning that Yue Fuguang was leaving. The System almost wanted to tell its host that the members of the Yu family, who claimed they were going to bed, had all secretly cried themselves hoarse in their rooms.","Yue Fuguang sighed. 「You know comfort isn’t exactly my strong suit.」 Speaking without having experienced another person’s suffering was easy—it would only sound like empty advice from someone standing outside the problem. Besides, she was the reason this had happened in the first place.","At that moment, she even indulged in a rather narcissistic thought: If she had a relative who treated her so well and was also an invincible source of support, only to leave her one day, she would probably cry herself to death too!","The next day, Yue Fuguang acted as if she hadn’t noticed the Yu family’s swollen eyes. She spent five “pleasant” days with them at the estate before finally setting off for the capital.","In those few days, news of her departure spread throughout the upper echelons of Dayan as well. Emperor Mingxi and his ministers waited for her return with eager anticipation.","“Your Majesty the Dowager Empress, Your Majesty the Empress, Fuguang will be leaving in a few days. I’ll have to trouble the two of you to look after the Yu family in the future.”","On the second day after returning to the capital, Yue Fuguang attended court and announced her departure before the assembled civil and military officials.","According to the System, the scene at the time was nothing short of a grand funeral.","When old men cried, women truly had no chance of competing with them. The senior officials had completely abandoned their dignity. Knowing that no matter how desperately they pleaded, they could not keep Dayan’s strongest backing—the thickest, most powerful support in existence—one by one, they were overcome with grief. They cried with complete sincerity, every tear representing genuine sorrow.","The military officers were especially emotional. Grown men wept silently, and Yue Fuguang found the sight almost unbearable.","The entire court was filled with sobbing. With Yue Fuguang and Emperor Mingxi seated above them, they looked almost like two memorial tablets awaiting worship. Even Emperor Mingxi, who was crying along with everyone else, failed to notice how... inauspicious the scene was.","After calming the civil and military officials of Dayan, she hurried straight to the inner palace.","The Dowager Empress and the Empress had both treated her well over the years. Naturally, she had to come in person to say goodbye before entrusting the Yu family to their care.","The Dowager Empress and the Empress each took one of her hands, tears streaming down both their faces. Yue Fuguang couldn’t help remarking, 「Little Zhu, I’ve lived for so many years, yet in these past few days I’ve seen more tears than I did in all the thousands of years before them combined!」","【That’s because everyone loves my master so much that they can’t bear to part with her. When you left Lingxu Mountain and descended into the mortal realm to suffer, the Divine Venerable secretly shed tears too.】","“Fuguang, those people have made you suffer.” The Dowager Empress squeezed her hand, speaking with heartfelt sincerity. Yet Yue Fuguang felt her face grow slightly warm.","In her previous life, she had also been born into a wealthy family. But if one truly compared the quality of their lives, aside from the conveniences of modern society, she had actually lived more comfortably here.","She had lacked neither material comforts nor emotional care.","She couldn’t let her carefully maintained persona collapse!","I must not break character! I must not break character! Yue Fuguang repeated to herself as she comforted the Dowager Empress. “Fuguang doesn’t feel that she has suffered. I’m simply returning home to the Upper Realm. Your Majesty needn’t be so sad.”","The Dowager Empress nodded slowly. “You’re returning to the Upper Realm to enjoy your blessings. I should be happy for you.”","She wiped the tears from her face. “But whenever I think that I’ll never see Fuguang again, my heart aches terribly.”","She pressed a hand to her chest. It genuinely hurt—not just at that moment, either. The dull ache in her heart had begun five days ago, when she first learned that Fuguang was leaving.","The imperial family understood better than anyone how different the world and the court would be with Yue Fuguang here—and without her.","The Empress nodded repeatedly. “Mother is right. My heart...” Empress Xu pressed a hand to her chest like the sorrowful beauty Xi Shi, tears glistening in her eyes. The sight was enough to make anyone’s heart ache.","Yue Fuguang produced two exquisite wooden boxes. She handed one to the Dowager Empress and the other to the Empress, who had begun crying again. “Please don’t cry. When you miss me in the future, just look at what’s inside these boxes.”","After ending the morning court session, Emperor Mingxi hurried over with Crown Prince Xie Zhiyan. He had barely stepped into the Dowager Empress’s Palace, the Palace of Benevolent Peace, when he saw his mother and the Empress crying while Fuguang comforted them and placed gifts in their hands.","Emperor Mingxi, whose eyes were still slightly red, strode in. Before he had even sat down, he asked hoarsely, “Fuguang, what treasures did you leave for Mother and the Empress?”","【Exactly, Master. You didn’t leave anything for the Yu family, so why are you acting like a gift-dispensing immortal in the palace?】","「They’re just little trinkets. I’ve already given the Yu family protective items before, which is why I said I wouldn’t leave them anything else after I departed.","But...」","【But what?】","「But everyone looked so miserable today that I changed my mind. I decided to leave the Dowager Empress and the Empress a few little trinkets to remember me by.」","“Your Majesty, they’re nothing more than little trinkets.”","“Mother, open it and let your son have a look.” Although Emperor Mingxi said this to the Dowager Empress, he had already taken the small box from the Empress’s hands, unable to contain his curiosity."]},{"number":563,"title":"Chapter 563: How are we supposed to make a living under their thumb from now on","paragraphs":["The Empress Dowager's box contained a jade bead necklace with one hundred and eight beads. It looked like jasper, but with its translucency, no one would mistake it for jasper.","Apart from the bead necklace, there was also a small white jade bottle.","\"They say jade nourishes the body. Your Majesty the Empress Dowager, wearing this jade bead necklace more often in the future will be good for your health.\" Her implication was quite obvious, and the four people in the hall clearly understood it.","She pointed at the jade bottle in the box. \"These are the pills I've left for Your Majesty the Empress Dowager. Take one if you don't feel well.\"","The contents in Empress Xu's box were similar to those of the Empress Dowager's, both having a bottle containing five pills. However, the difference was that Empress Xu's was a watermelon - red jadeite bracelet. In terms of material, the jade bracelet was of lower quality than the bead necklace. Well, one was the Emperor's mother and the other was the Emperor's wife!","It wasn't that Yue Fuguang was being discriminatory; she was actually trying to protect Empress Xu. Yue Fuguang thought she was truly considerate!","Emperor Mingxi was eyeing the things in the box enviously. Yue Fuguang resisted the urge to roll her eyes and took out two more boxes, giving them to Emperor Mingxi and Xie Zhiyan respectively.","The gifts for the four most powerful members of the royal family were generally the same, except that Emperor Mingxi's jade pendant was obviously one size larger than the Crown Prince's jade plaque.","After presenting gifts to the four most powerful people in the royal family, Yue Fuguang visited several high - ranking officials' mansions one after another in the following days.","These were all her loyal followers. In the court, they either had a say in political affairs or held military power. Yue Fuguang had to pay them a visit before leaving.","Even for those families she didn't visit, she sent someone to deliver gifts. She truly managed to treat everyone equally. As the system put it, [Host, you seem to be giving everyone benefits, but you really look like an air - conditioner trying to keep everyone cool evenly. It's just like the behavior of a typical playboy.]","Since the people of the Great Xia Empire learned that their Divine Maiden was going back to the upper realm, they were even more distraught than the civil and military officials in the court.","In the past few days, upon hearing the news, people from far and wide dragged their families to the capital city.","On the cement - built roads, as the system described, it was more crowded than the highways during the Spring Festival in later generations.","\"Dad, is the Divine Maiden really going to abandon us?\" A five - or six - year - old little girl stared at her father with eyes as black as grapes.","Her father wiped the sweat off his face and gently said to his daughter, \"A - Yan, the Divine Maiden isn't abandoning us. She... she's just going back to her own home.\"","\"Dad, isn't the Divine Maiden the Divine Maiden of the Great Xia Empire?\" The little girl didn't understand why the Divine Maiden had to go home.","\"Sister is right. The Divine Maiden is the Divine Maiden of the Great Xia Empire. Even the name 'Great Xia' came from the Divine Maiden's mouth. Why does she still want to leave us?\" A seven - or eight - year - old boy beside the little girl showed the same puzzled expression as his sister.","The man didn't have much education and was left speechless by his children's questions. After frowning and thinking for a while, he pointed at the sky and said, \"The place where the gods reside is in the sky.\"","He sighed softly. \"The Divine Maiden has completed her mortal experience and naturally has to return to the sky.\"","He looked at his son. \"Da Wa, you study at the academy founded by the Divine Maiden. In the future, you can be a useful person. Don't disgrace the Divine Maiden's name and let down her kindness to our poor families.\"","The boy nodded vigorously. \"Dad, I'll remember.\"","Such conversations were taking place in different families. Even without inquiring, Yue Fuguang already knew from the system that the people coming to see her off had lined up from the city gate of Shangjing to beyond the Ten - mile Pavilion.","\"He Jin, inform the Capital Guards to strengthen patrols and ensure the safety of the common people. If any lawbreakers are found, deal with them quickly and severely!\"","\"Yes, my lady. I'll go and inform Minister Wei right away.\"","\"Not so fast.\" Yue Fuguang stopped her. \"I'm leaving the day after tomorrow. You several can go to your respective yamen to start work these days and get familiar with your duties. If there are any problems, I'm still here and can make decisions for you.\"","He Jin, Shen Chunying, and Luo Shendong exchanged glances, and there was a glint of moisture in their eyes. He Jin forced a smile and said, \"My lady, we want to see you off before taking up our posts.\"","Luo Shendong also said, \"Yes, my lady. We're your subordinates. Who would dare to make things difficult for us?\"","Everyone knew that as long as they didn't make mistakes, even after the Grand Tutor (Yue Fuguang) returned to the upper realm, no one would really target them.","Those officials in the court more or less had a connection with them.","Seeing their determination, Yue Fuguang didn't persuade them anymore, but only instructed, \"Remember, we don't cause trouble, but we're not afraid of it either. If there are any blind - eyed people who dare to bully you, use the whips I gave you to reason with them properly.\"","It was not easy for women to serve as officials. Yue Fuguang was afraid that they would be at a disadvantage, so she gave each of them a horsewhip early on. These whips were all registered with the Emperor. If any officials offended them, they could really whip them without consequences as long as they were in the right, and even the Emperor couldn't punish them.","[Host, you've arranged everything clearly for everyone related to you. Aren't you supposed to be a lazy person who doesn't care about things? Why have you been so worried these days?] The teasing in the system's words was almost overflowing from the screen.","Yue Fuguang rolled her eyes and let the system figure it out on its own. After arranging everything for everyone, on the last day, she sent off her beloved pets like Treading Snow Without a Trace and Caramel Milk Tea.","\"You should support each other and live well in the future.\" Yue Fuguang was worried that these few little guys, with their intelligence far exceeding that of their peers, wouldn't be able to integrate into the animal community after returning to the mountains and might not make friends, so she couldn't help but give a few words of advice.","[Host, you're just being over - worried. With the tempers and abilities of these guys, if you release them into the mountains, the real concern should be how the other animals in the mountains will survive under them.]","The little pets rubbed their heads against her hand, with tears in their eyes, knowing that their master was leaving them.","Yue Fuguang felt heart - broken when she saw this. \"Alright, alright, stop crying. If you miss me, just look at the necklaces I gave you.\" Each of them had a pendant around their necks, with her photo inside. This was the only thing she left for them to remember her by.","No matter how reluctant Yue Fuguang was, time had finally arrived at the day when she had to leave."]},{"number":564,"title":"Chapter 564: Does Heaven Send Me","paragraphs":["At noon in the capital city of Shangjing, Great Xia’s sacrificial altar was hidden beneath a forest of flags. After changing the nation’s name, Yue Fuguang had taken the opportunity to create a national flag for Great Xia as well.","Emperor Mingxi led the civil and military officials in offering three bows and nine prostrations. Three thousand Imperial Guards stood in rigid formation beneath the vermilion steps, clad in grim armor. Beyond the altar, the people knelt in wave after wave, like a surging tide. Hundreds of thousands of eyes held their breath as they gazed toward the figure atop the high platform.","[Host, there must be over a million people here!] the System exclaimed in amazement. Not only was the city packed with people—even those dozens of miles beyond the city walls had come. There were far more people than it had filmed two days ago.","That was because only a few days had passed since the news was released. Those living farther away had not yet received word and had been unable to make the journey in time.","[Host, so many people are here to see you off! You’ll be able to brag about this for several lifetimes!]","Yue Fuguang straightened her back and lifted her chin slightly. “Of course! System, remember to film everything from beginning to end. This is my moment of glory.”","[Host, you’ve had plenty of moments of glory.]","Yue Fuguang shook her head. “This time is different. It’s also the last time, so it’s worth commemorating.”","Yue Fuguang was dressed in white, her entire body shimmering with an aura like moonlight and starlight. She stood at the center of the stone platform for offering sacrifices to Heaven, her sleeves slowly lifted by an invisible current of air. Behind her, her hair streamed like dark clouds of ink.","Over the past two years, her bearing had already grown ethereal and otherworldly. At this moment, she seemed even more like an immortal or deity who might rise with the wind at any moment.","Above her head, multicolored clouds slowly drifted and flowed, each one radiating brilliant light. Something in Heaven and Earth was being drawn to her, gathering and surging toward her from every direction.","First, the wind changed.","It was not an earthly wind, but a current that welled up from the depths of the void, carrying a faint golden glow. Silently, it began to circle around her. At that very moment, the translucent phantom of a lotus slowly blossomed beneath her feet.","The civil and military officials below were the first to notice. The jade tablet in the Ministry of War’s hands began to tremble faintly. The ceremonial official’s hat fell from his head without a breeze. Even the beads hanging from the emperor’s crown started to strike one another softly, producing a clear, springlike chime.","Yue Fuguang raised her head.","In her eyes appeared a sight invisible to ordinary people: deep within the firmament, the River of Stars hung upside down. A pillar of light descended from beyond the ninth heaven, falling straight down to envelop her.","The light was faint and pure, almost transparent. Yet the instant it touched her body, her entire being began to change.","“System, I only bought a discounted item. Isn’t this a little over the top?”","The upside-down River of Stars was invisible to ordinary people, but her body—transformed by divine incense and already freed from its mortal nature—could see it clearly. This spectacle truly resembled the prelude to an ascension in those cultivation novels, when a great immortal rose into the heavens by day after surviving a tribulation of lightning.","“I don’t remember the item description mentioning anything like this.”","[Host, why can’t it be this world’s Heavenly Dao seeing you off as well? Our mission received an S-rank evaluation, which clearly shows how satisfied the Heavenly Dao is with it.]","“The Heavenly Dao is seeing me off?” Yue Fuguang gazed toward the depths of the sky, but unfortunately, she saw nothing. Perhaps this world’s Heavenly Dao was too weak to reveal itself yet.","Under the radiance of the pillar of light, Yue Fuguang’s entire body began to glow inch by inch, as though some bloodline were slowly awakening within her. Her body shone—not with the harsh brilliance of the sun, but with a purer, gentler light.","It was as if she were awakening from within a mortal shell. The divinity she had carefully restrained in the mortal realm could no longer be suppressed. It surged forth like a flood bursting through a breached dam.","“Look! The Divine Maiden... Divine Maiden Yue is glowing!”","Someone cried out in alarm.","The people below the altar raised their heads one after another. A moment later, gasps and cries of astonishment rose and fell throughout the crowd.","As Yue Fuguang’s figure gradually left the ground, phantoms of all kinds of spiritual flowers began to surge into being beneath her feet, swirling upward around her. Even the lotus beneath her seemed to float upon the River of Stars.","Indeed, as Yue Fuguang rose higher and higher, a silver river of stars slowly appeared beneath her feet. Even in broad daylight, it shone more brilliantly than the sun in the sky, yet its light was far gentler and less dazzling.","Her ribbons unfurled in every direction, as though countless invisible hands were pulling them at once—or as if a colossal white flower bud were blooming.","Light streamed from the lotus-shaped mark between her brows. Seven-colored radiance intertwined and coiled around her, enveloping her entire form in a pure, luminous halo.","Emperor Mingxi abruptly rose to his feet, his crown nearly tilting askew. He clenched his fists tightly, his imperial eyes wide with disbelief.","He gazed at Yue Fuguang, already dozens of meters above the ground, surrounded by radiance and flowers. Tears once again spilled from his eyes without his realizing it.","He, his ministers, and the people were all witnessing Fuguang’s departure together. A hundred conflicting emotions clogged their throats, leaving them painfully unable to breathe.","The civil and military officials prostrated themselves on the ground, the hems of their robes snapping in a wind that seemed to come from nowhere. Every one of them, like their emperor, gazed upward at the figure in the sky with tears in their eyes.","As Yue Fuguang climbed higher and higher, the realization that they were about to lose their Grand Preceptor—their pillar that steadied the realm—became all the more painfully real.","The Imperial Guards drove their spears into the ground and knelt on one knee to see their Grand Preceptor off. Their iron armor grated harshly in the wind.","Someone began the chant. Soon, the cry resounded across the altar:","“The earth bears the Four Seas; Heaven covers the Eight Wastes! Wherever the sun and moon shine, all is Xia soil! Majestic are our mountains and rivers, forged in blood and iron! Eternal is our foundation, firm from this day forth! When the winds rise, clouds gather; the dragon strides and the tiger advances! One wrathful roar, and all nations tremble; when we live in peace, the world is settled!","“Our land, our people, our blood, our bones! Whoever dares invade Great Xia—no matter how far they flee, they shall be destroyed!","“Beat the drums! Beat the drums! Let them thunder with the fury of our mountains and rivers! Raise the flags! Raise the flags! Let them proclaim the spirit of Great Xia! Majestic is our divine realm, forever guarding the heartland! For a thousand generations, for ten thousand years—let the songs and dances rise again and again!”"]},{"number":565,"title":"Chapter 565: Time to Return to the Upper Realm","paragraphs":["This military song, also created by Yue Fuguang, was flying in the air. Its sound shook the nine heavens, and its power split the vault of heaven. It was like ten thousand horses galloping on the raging waves, and like the clash of gold and spears in the raging fire. Wherever the song spread, its intention was for the mountains and rivers to remain safe.","Outside the altar, the common people were no longer kneeling on the ground. There seemed to be an invisible pressure on them. This pressure was not sharp; instead, it carried a kind of compassionate gentleness. However, it made people feel an impulse to prostrate and worship from the depths of their souls. But they couldn't kneel down and could only stand with their heads held high.","This pressure came from the slowly awakening Heavenly Dao consciousness in this world, and Yue Fuguang had straightened their backs before she left.","Yue Fuguang's figure had risen to a height of one hundred meters.","Her face became clear and bright in the light. It was no longer the face that an ordinary mortal woman could have, but the compassionate face of a deity that made people dare not look directly at it.","The lotus mark between her eyebrows was lit up, fully showing her divinity. She lowered her eyes and looked down, just like the eternal galaxy overlooking the ever - changing mortal world.","A voice suddenly echoed in the air, \"Master, it's time to return to the Upper Realm!\"","As the voice fell, a seven - colored pearl suddenly appeared above Yue Fuguang's head. There seemed to be patterned immortal beasts on the pearl, making it hard to see clearly.","\"System, you're adding extra drama to yourself again.\"","[Host, I'm the Boundary - Breaking Pearl. It's very reasonable for me to break through the void and take you back, isn't it?] Its part was an essential link.","Yue Fuguang didn't argue with it and continued the act following its script, \"Yes, it's time to return to the Upper Realm!\"","Her voice was not loud; in fact, it was gentle, but it clearly reached the ears of everyone within a hundred - li radius, regardless of the distance.","That voice was like the morning bell and evening drum, like the mountain stream in the deep forest, and like a kind of echo only existing in dreams.","\"Little Zhu, the matters here are settled. It's time to return today.\"","The moment the word \"return\" fell, the \"Boundary - Breaking Pearl\" shone brightly. Then, it seemed as if someone had forcefully torn a crack in the sky.","The blue sky really cracked open, like a huge silk ribbon being torn from the middle. What shone through the crack was neither starlight nor clouds, but a kind of light that mortal eyes had never seen before. The color of this light exceeded the color spectrum of the Three Realms. It was so brilliant that it didn't seem real, but it was more real than any real thing.","Facing this scene, the people on the ground were so shocked that they all fell backward. Someone exclaimed, \"The sky, the sky has cracked!\"","\"The Divine Maiden has made the sky crack!\"","A long step made of light hung down from the crack, step by step, extending to Yue Fuguang's feet. Each step was semi - transparent, with a miniature of the galaxy flowing inside. Every step on it was like stepping on and shattering a piece of the sky.","At this moment, Yue Fuguang's mortal body began to melt like snow, wither like a flower, and twinkle like a star with little stardust.","\"The Divine Maiden... has disintegrated her body through self - sacrifice!\" The young scholar who liked to read picture books knew very well what this scene represented.","The Divine Maiden's mortal body was the Yu family's Seventh Young Lady. Naturally, she wouldn't take her mortal body with her when she returned to the Upper Realm.","The disintegration of her body through self - sacrifice was both expected and unexpected by everyone.","The Yu family members were looking tearfully at Yue Fuguang, who was gradually turning into floating light from her feet. The elderly Yu lady couldn't hold back anymore. She raised her hand and cried out sadly, \"Fuguang, my Fuguang!\"","Her voice was choked and hoarse. \"Look at your grandmother. Look back at your grandmother again!\"","Woohoo! Woohoo! The Yu family women hugged each other and cried. Even Yu Chongshan and other Yu family men were as pale as death and were in floods of tears, unable to speak.","Yue Fuguang seemed to hear them. She turned around, lowered her head, and smiled with her eyebrows. \"Grandmother, I'm leaving. Take care of yourself!\"","After thinking for a while, she added, \"If you miss your granddaughter, go to the Divine Maiden Hall and have a look.\"","Her voice was still echoing in the air, but her figure was gone. The broken light transformed from Yue Fuguang did not dissipate. Instead, it fell from the high sky like the water of the Milky Way. Everyone watched helplessly as the stream of light fell into a certain place on Lotus Mountain.","\"Is this... the location of the Divine Maiden Hall?\" Someone ventured to guess.","Someone echoed, \"The Divine Maiden disintegrated her body through self - sacrifice. Naturally, she should fall into her dojo.\"","\"Didn't you hear? The Divine Maiden told the elderly Yu lady who missed her to go to the Divine Maiden Hall to see her. There must be a reason for it!\"","Everyone was guessing while crying. However, their guess was confirmed later.","The floating light after the Divine Maiden's self - sacrifice did fall into the Divine Maiden's dojo, precisely on the jade statue of the Divine Maiden. The statue, which was originally just made of high - quality jade, then seemed to be wearing a celestial dress with the light of the moon and stars.","It was resplendent and full of divinity. Even the statue had a kind of indescribable charm. From then on, for thousands of years, few of the sentient beings who came to worship the statue of the Divine Maiden dared to look directly into the eyes of the Divine Maiden.","The Divine Maiden Hall and the statue of the Divine Maiden stood majestically. They were not only built of bricks and wood but also the carriers of her legendary stories and profound thoughts.","And the legend and immortal thoughts she left in the mortal world built a spiritual monument that transcended time and space."]},{"number":566,"title":"Chapter 566: Farewell, Honored Goddess","paragraphs":["For thousands upon thousands of years, through the rise and fall of dynasties and the transformations of the world, her influence had never faded.","Military strategy had gained new variables because of her. Political structures had been shaped by her. Even in the economic lifelines and the livelihoods of ordinary people, the imprint of her wisdom could be found everywhere.","In the histories written by the official chroniclers of later generations, she was recorded under the divine title of the Divine Maiden and entered into the official annals in *The Chronicle of the Divine Maiden*.","Folk artists, meanwhile, spared no ink in depicting her deeds in illustrated books and weaving them into tales of legend. Amid the sharp crack of storytellers’ wooden clappers, she became an eternal white moonlight, shining upon generation after generation.","But that was all still to come. At this moment, Yue Fuguang’s voice vanished from the sky for an instant. Then the winds and clouds churned overhead. A gust swept past, and rain suddenly began to fall from the heavens—rain made of flowers.","Countless multicolored petals drifted down from the rift in the firmament, each carrying a faint, delicate fragrance. The moment they touched the ground, they dissolved.","When they landed on the iron armor of the Imperial Guards, the armor became smooth and lustrous, as good as new. When they fell upon the shoulders of the common people, their aches and illnesses seemed to ease in an instant.","When they settled in the trembling hands of the civil and military officials, the headaches, insomnia, and palpitations that had plagued them for years vanished as though they had never existed.","Emperor Mingxi stood rigidly in place, allowing the petals to cover him as he stared at the spot where Yue Fuguang had undergone her divine dissolution. There, he saw a phantom figure slowly beginning to take form.","“She... she’s the Divine Maiden!” This was the true Divine Maiden—not the fifteen-year-old Yue Fuguang they had seen before.","She possessed flesh and bone as white as jade, a bearing as serene as autumn waters, and eyes that seemed to hold ten thousand stars within them. Even the flower rain swirling around her lost its color before her beauty...","【Host, look! I created this body according to what you once described—bones of white jade, the spirit of autumn waters, stardust for eyes, and a countenance adorned with every flower. Isn’t it breathtakingly beautiful?】","Yue Fuguang nodded. “It’s insanely beautiful!”","She shouted, 【System, charge ahead—for the sake of both our bodies!】","This time, Yue Fuguang did not look back. Her pace was neither hurried nor slow. Each step landed upon empty space, yet sent out tangible ripples, one circle after another, spreading outward. They passed through the sea of clouds, through the palaces and towers of the imperial city, through the mountains and rivers, and onward toward the distant horizon.","In an instant, the skies above the entire imperial city were blanketed by a vast storm of petals.","At last, the people emerged from their shock at seeing the Divine Maiden once more. Some burst into loud sobs. Some knelt and prayed. Some frantically stretched out their hands, trying to catch the drifting petals. Most simply prostrated themselves again and again, knocking their foreheads bloody without seeming to notice.","“Farewell, Divine Maiden!”","“Farewell, Divine Maiden!”","“Farewell, Divine Maiden!”","The voices began in the imperial city and spread outward like ripples beyond the walls.","The overlapping cries, shouts, and prayers intertwined into a single immense sound, surging like a tide, each wave higher than the last.","Yue Fuguang stepped onto the final level of light.","The rift in the firmament widened further and further. Light poured through it like an inverted waterfall, enveloping her entire form.","At the very last moment, she could not resist turning back one final time.","“May Heaven and earth be prosperous and peaceful, and may all under Heaven unite in harmony. May Huaxia endure for countless generations, and may an age of peace never end. May the people live in comfort, and may every harvest be abundant.”","Yue Fuguang used every blessing talisman she had on her.","【Host, you just threw them all out there. Are you planning to live on air from now on?】","“Whatever happens later can wait until later. For now, let me be extravagant one last time.”","As for the twenty-four words she had left behind—how many of them would ultimately come true, and how long they would endure—those were no longer her concern.","Because, amid the radiance at its most brilliant, her figure grew nearly transparent. The boundary between her form and the light blurred more and more until, at last, she merged into that expanse of radiance, like a drop of water flowing into the sea.","The rift in the heavens began to close slowly. Starting from the lowest step, the staircase of light faded away, transforming into countless tiny points of light. They spiraled through the air like fireflies for a moment before gently drifting down toward the mortal world.","In scarcely any time at all, the final thread of light vanished from the horizon.","The sky returned to its clear blue. White clouds drifted lazily past, as though nothing had ever happened. Only the incense and candles still burning upon the Altar of Heaven, the multicolored petals scattered across the ground, and the tear-streaked faces of the hundreds of thousands gazing up at the sky bore witness to all that had taken place during that brief period—the time it took for a single stick of incense to burn.","“Your Majesty... I, Xie Fei, send off our dynasty’s... Divine Maiden with gratitude!”","Emperor Mingxi slowly knelt once more and bowed in solemn reverence. As emperor, he saw Yue Fuguang off with the utmost respect. He also thanked her for the final blessings she had bestowed upon Great Xia—blessings that kept him from falling into utter panic after suddenly losing the Divine Maiden’s protection.","At that moment, the civil and military officials could no longer withstand the weight of their grief and awe. Alongside their emperor, they dropped to their knees and bowed three times toward the empty sky.","The civil and military officials lowered their heads in silent obeisance, while the armored Imperial Guards knelt in unison with the clamor of ringing metal.","He rose to his feet. His knees trembled faintly, but he no longer accepted anyone’s help.","“Deliver my edict.” His voice was steady. “First: Grant a general amnesty throughout the realm and reduce taxes for three years, in gratitude for the Divine Maiden’s protection. Second: Establish shrines to the Divine Maiden in every province and prefecture. Offer sacrifices in spring and autumn, and let this be observed forever.”","The assembled officials stared in astonishment, then prostrated themselves and cried out in unison, “Long live Your Majesty!”","The people’s wails gradually subsided, transforming into a shared, ceaseless hum—something between a prayer and an expression of thanks.","The wind fell still.","Upon the altar, a golden petal drifted gently down and landed precisely on Emperor Mingxi’s still-upturned left shoulder. For a long while, it did not fade away.","The End"]}]);
